	]
	quest.02BFE6EA90831AED.quest_subtitle: "A Burden of Ten Thousand Jun"
	quest.02BFE6EA90831AED.title: "Oath of the Overburdened Mind"
	quest.02C5ECCA9010AEA1.quest_desc: ["{\"text\":\"\",\"extra\":[{\"text\":\"I know you might get a headache seeing this mod's \",\"color\":\"gray\"},{\"text\":\"eyes\",\"color\":\"red\"},{\"text\":\", but now they can all be \",\"color\":\"gray\"},{\"text\":\"crafted\",\"color\":\"green\"},{\"text\":\".\",\"color\":\"gray\"}]}"]
	quest.02C5ECCA9010AEA1.quest_subtitle: "Craftable"
	quest.02CBB1D9A926F86B.quest_desc: [
		"&6Table Cloth&r"
		""
		"&7A block that combines item display and trading functions. It can store and display four items; right-click to deposit or withdraw. When multiple Table Cloths are placed adjacent to each other, their textures connect automatically.&r"
		""
		"&6Shop Function&r"
		"&7Combined with the &eStock Ticker&r&7, it can build an automated shop to sell stocked items to other players and collect payment.&r"
		""
		"&6Setting Up Items for Sale&r"
		"&7To build a shop, follow these steps:&r"
		"&7Hold the Table Cloth and right-click the &eWarehouse Keeper&r.&r"
		"&7In the interface, select the item and quantity to sell, specify the destination for the goods, then click the &a\"Configure\"&r&7 button.&r"
		"&7Place the configured Table Cloth in a suitable spot to display the goods.&r"
		"&7Set the price for the goods on the side of the Table Cloth.&r"
		"&7Each sales Table Cloth can be configured with up to nine products, but only the first four can be displayed at the same time.&r"
		"&7Be sure to &clock the logistics network&r&7 in the top-right corner of the Warehouse Keeper interface to prevent goods from being extracted directly by others.&r"
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"&6Buying Items&r"
		"&7Point your crosshair at a sales Table Cloth to view trade details. If stock is sufficient, you can trade directly.&r"
		"&7Right-click a sales Table Cloth to obtain a &eShopping List&r&7, which records the currently selected goods. Holding the list lets you continue buying other goods from the same shop, and subsequent items are automatically synced to the record.&r"
		"&7Hold the Shopping List and right-click the Keeper to check out. The system automatically deducts the corresponding payment items from your inventory. The &eStock Ticker&r&7 then sends a request to extract the purchased goods.&r"
		"&7Payment from customers is temporarily stored in the Stock Ticker. The shop owner can right-click to collect it directly, or use components such as &eHoppers&r&7 to extract it automatically.&r"
		""
		"&8A line of small text beside the manuscript reads: Display, price, trade—everything comes down to a simple contract.&r"
	]
	quest.02CBB1D9A926F86B.quest_subtitle: "Table Cloth / Tabletop"
	quest.02CBB1D9A926F86B.title: "Shop"
	quest.02EBF147125789FB.quest_desc: [
		"&7When worn:"
		""
		"&7Enhances &#FFCC44Scythe&7 enchantments:"
		""
		"&7&#FFAA33Boomerang&7: Returns immediately upon hitting an entity. Return speed increased to &e2&7x, damage dealt increased to &e1.5&7x."
		""
		"&7&#88DDFFSurging&7:"
		"&7If in a &#66FF66sprinting&7 state, the player's horizontal velocity is -&e0.6&7x the view unit vector;"
		"&7Attack range reduced to &e2&7 blocks and offset &e2&7 blocks along the view direction, damage dealt increased to &e1.25&7x."
		""
		"&7Disables &#FFCC44Scythe&7 sweep attacks."
		""
		"&7The &#FFCC44Scythe&7 icon above the player's experience bar indicates charge progress. Full charge requires &e10&7 seconds."
		""
		"&7Once fully charged:"
		"&7When attacked by a creature, the &#FFCC44Scythe&7 icon lights up and the player gains a &e5&7-second &#CC6666Malicious Intent&7 effect. The base effect level is &eII&7. For every &e6&7 damage taken during this instance, the effect level increases by &e1&7, up to level &eXI&7;"
		""
		"&7While under the &#CC6666Malicious Intent&7 effect, attacking other creatures with a &#FFCC44Scythe&7 triggers a Chain Slash:"
		""
		"&7Cancels the current attack;"
		"&7The Chain Slash attack area is centered on the scythe boomerang or the attacker's position, within an &e8×8×8&7 range;"
		"&7Damage multiplier = clamp(attack speed, &e0&7, &e2&7) * (effect level * &e2&7 - &e1&7);"
		"&7Duration is &e25&7 game ticks. Each tick deals 原damage / duration * damage multiplier physical and magic damage to all creatures within the attack area except the attacker, ignoring invincibility frames;"
		"&7&#CC66FFSoul-Returning Edge Scythe&7 reduces the chance of granting the &#CC6666Soul-Returning Advent&7 effect to &e40%&7;"
		"&7Resets the required charge time to &e10&7 seconds."
		""
		"&7While charging, attacking other creatures resets the required charge time to &e15&7 seconds."
	]
	quest.02EBF147125789FB.quest_subtitle: "Scythe Authority"
	quest.02F458E4623EBD67.quest_desc: [
		"&7Right-click to &FFD700charge&7, producing &#CC99FFspear thrusts&7 at enemies along the charge path."
		"&7Sneak-right-click produces &#CC99FFspear thrusts&7 at nearby enemies."
		""
		"&7Thrust damage = &cmelee damage × 2.0&7."
		"&7Cooldown is dynamically determined by &6Silent Gear's&7 &eattack speed&7 attribute."
	]
	quest.02F458E4623EBD67.quest_subtitle: "Ever Onward!"
	quest.03639EDED6577831.quest_desc: [
		"&7&#66CCFFMelancholy&7  "
		"&7When casting spells:  "
		"&7Each spell cast grants 1 stack of &#66CCFF\"Arcane Brand\"&7, up to &#FFAA335 stacks&7, lasting &#FFAA3360 seconds&7  "
		"&7Each stack provides &#66FF66cast speed, cooldown reduction, and spell power&7  "
		""
		"&7When attacking a target with &#66CCFF\"Arcane Brand\"&7 (at 5 stacks):  "
		"&7Deals &#CC99FFextra spell damage&7  "
		"&7Applies &#66CCFF\"Arcane Brand stacks\"&7 to the target  "
		"&7Resets your own brand stacks  "
		""
		"&7When an enemy with &#66CCFF\"Arcane Brand\"&7 dies:  "
		"&7All players within &#FFAA3310 blocks&7 &#66FF66restore 15% max health and 200 mana&7"
	]
	quest.03639EDED6577831.quest_subtitle: "Melancholy Erosion"
	quest.03639EDED6577831.title: "Melancholy Erosion"
	quest.038444481D165CED.quest_subtitle: "Analysis Paralysis"
	quest.038444481D165CED.title: "Equipment Choice"
	quest.03D7343C57EF0A14.quest_desc: [
		"&7Prolonged contact with &#66FF99Spirits&7 seems to have made my mind somewhat disordered. I can even hear strange &#88DDFFcalls&7 ringing in my ears... No, that's not right"
		""
		"&7When holding the &#CC99FFSoulstone&7, the &#88DDFFcalls&7 become clearer. It seems to want to take me somewhere"
		""
		"&7The &#CC66FFEye of Ender&7 points to the entrance of the End. If the &#CC99FFSoulstone&7 is fused into the &#CC66FFEye of Ender&7, where would it point?"
	]
	quest.03D7343C57EF0A14.quest_subtitle: "Soul Resonance"
	quest.03D7343C57EF0A14.title: "The Call"
	quest.0401FD00A60774F8.quest_desc: [
		"&6Torreya Forest&r"
		"&7is one of the surface biomes of the Starlight Dimension."
		""
		"&7Torreya Forests usually generate along the &#5CACEEAether River&r&7."
		"&7The &#8B7355Torreya Trees&r&7 within are tall and dense, forming winding, narrow river channels together with the Aether River."
		"&7This also makes Torreya Forests very likely to border multiple different surface biomes."
		""
		"&7The high-brightness presence of &#5CACEEAether Fluid&r&7 and &#8B7355Torreya Vines&r&7 also greatly reduces monster spawning on the biome's surface."
	]
	quest.0401FD00A60774F8.quest_subtitle: "Crossing Paths"
	quest.0401FD00A60774F8.title: "Torreya Forest"
	quest.0422DD98B2548813.title: "Armor Equipment"
	quest.0429A6763D6D23B3.quest_desc: [
		"&7The &#66DDCCPigment Mixer&7 is a crafting block used to create pigments. By mixing dyes, materials, or other pigments, you can create pigments with &#66CCFFcustom colors&7, used later to dye tool and equipment parts."
		""
		"&FFD700Making Pigments&7"
		""
		"&7Place any amount of the following items into the &#66DDCCPigment Mixer's&7 input slots:"
		""
		"&7&#FFD700Input Items&7"
		"&7&#CC99FFDye&7: Provides that dye's color"
		"&7&#66CCFFPigment&7: Provides that pigment's color"
		"&7&#66FF66Material&7: Provides that material's color"
		"&7&#66FF66Slimeball&7: Used to increase output quantity"
		""
		"Since it's not very important, I won't go into detail here"
	]
	quest.0429A6763D6D23B3.quest_subtitle: "Dedicated equipment for making pigments"
	quest.0429A6763D6D23B3.title: "Pigment Mixer"
	quest.046E980EB69A1209.quest_desc: [
		"&6Miniature Totem&r"
		"&7Can be bound to a familiar, and a familiar can only be bound to one totem at a time. When that familiar dies and you don't have the mana to revive it, the bound totem will be consumed, causing the familiar to &arevive&r&7, and the totem is consumed as well.&r"
	]
	quest.047B4F4A0587C0B6.quest_desc: [
		"&7Flying creature, only performs melee attacks;"
		""
		"&7Its attacks can be blocked by a &#FFD700Shield&7. Upon death, it splits into &#FFAA331~2&7 &#66FF66Lesser Wisps&7;  "
		"&7&#CC99FFPhantoms&7 are immune to fire damage and the vast majority of projectile damage (projectiles pass straight through their body);  "
		"&7The only projectile attack that can hurt it is the &#55D5D5Spirit Arrow&7;  "
		"&7&#CC99FFPhantoms&7 die instantly upon contact with water (fluid water, splash/lingering water bottles), and continuously lose health when exposed to rainy weather;  "
		"&7&#CC99FFPhantoms&7 that die this way &#FF6666will not split into Lesser Wisps&7;  "
		"&7You can determine which personality variant a &#CC99FFPhantom&7 belongs to based on its movement range;  "
		"&7&#CC99FFPhantoms&7 summoned by the &#FFD700Cunning Candle&7 &#FF6666will not split into Lesser Wisps&7 upon death"
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"&7Except for the docile variant, which is neutral toward players, all &#CC99FFPhantoms&7 will actively attack players;  "
		"&7Different personality variants of &#CC99FFPhantoms&7 also have different top-priority attack targets."
		""
		"&7&#FF6666Angry&7: Players, &#CC99FFSkeletons&7, &#CC99FFStrays&7, &#CC99FFPiglins&7;  "
		"&7&#66FF66Docile&7: &#FFAA33Striders&7;  "
		"&7&#CC99FFShy&7: Players, &#FF6666Magma Cubes&7, &#CC99FFPiglins&7;  "
		"&7&#66CCFFSlothful&7: Players, &#FFAA33Blazes&7, &#CC99FFPiglins&7."
		""
		"&7Certain creatures killed by a &#CC99FFPhantom&7 will become a &#CC99FFPhantom&7 husk, transforming into a new creature;  "
		"&7Therefore, after a transformed creature is killed, there is a chance a new &#CC99FFPhantom&7 will spawn in its place (the respawn chance depends on the creature type and world difficulty);  "
		"&7&#CC99FFPhantoms&7 will also transform into specific creatures after approaching certain gargoyle statues within Sanctuaries (structures);  "
		"&7A &#CC99FFPhantom&7 that has transformed other creatures through the above mechanics cannot perform new transformations by killing creatures/approaching gargoyle statues within &#FFAA3360 seconds&7 of respawning;  "
		"&7During this period, they will also change their top-priority attack target to creatures other than the one it transformed before."
		""
		"&7For example, a &#CC99FFPhantom&7 that transformed a &#CC99FFSkeleton&7 into a Vessel will, within &#FFAA3360 seconds&7 after that Vessel is killed and it respawns, no longer prioritize attacking &#CC99FFSkeletons&7;  "
		"&7Instead, it will prioritize attacking players, &#CC99FFPiglins&7, &#FFAA33Blazes&7, &#FF6666Magma Cubes&7, and other targets."
	]
	quest.047B4F4A0587C0B6.quest_subtitle: "Whoa"
	quest.047B4F4A0587C0B6.title: "Observation: Phantom"
	quest.0490EDB36F1CF908.quest_desc: [
		"&7In theory, you could also get this from the equipment bag as early as Stage I."
		""
		"&mPut it on and I'll make you fly&r"
	]
	quest.0490EDB36F1CF908.quest_subtitle: "The Sky Is the Limit"
	quest.04DD58980F332FEE.quest_desc: ["&7Similar to the knife, with lower damage and attack speed than the knife, but more &#66DDCCdurable&7. A tool that can be used for cutting board crafting."]
	quest.04DD58980F332FEE.quest_subtitle: "Survivor's Essential"
	quest.04F1594414B048D0.quest_desc: [
		"&7Increases the number of stacked items in a single backpack slot. Each backpack can hold up to three stack upgrades, and multiplied together they can achieve an extremely impressive stacking cap."
		""
		"&7Stack upgrades also apply to tanks, increasing their storage capacity accordingly."
	]
	quest.04F1594414B048D0.quest_subtitle: "Stack a bit, stack a bit more, stack a billion more"
	quest.05499B6A45252488.quest_desc: [
		"&7Produced by throwing a pumpkin into the &#CC99FFVoid Well&7. Place it on &#55D5D5Soul Sand&7 and accelerate it with &#66FF66Bone Meal&7 to produce a &#FF6666Misery Heap&7."
		""
		"&7Plant a &#FFD700Pumpkin Seed&7 on &#55D5D5Soul Sand&7, and it will grow upward into a &#FF6666Misery Melon Plant&7;  "
		""
		"&7After growing to a certain height, the &#FF6666Misery Melon Plant&7 will produce a &#FF6666Misery Melon&7.  "
		"&7The &#FF6666Misery Melon Plant&7 grows upward over time;  "
		""
		"&7For every &#FFAA331 block&7 of natural growth, the &#FF6666Misery Melon Plant&7 has a &#FFAA331/5&7 chance to produce a &#FF6666Misery Melon&7;  "
		"&7When the plant has already produced a &#FF6666Misery Melon&7, the &#FF6666Misery Melon Plant&7 will &#FF6666stop growing&7 until that &#FF6666Misery Melon&7 is destroyed;  "
		""
		"&7Using &#66FF66Bone Meal&7 on the &#FF6666Misery Melon Plant&7 will only make it grow infinitely up to the build height limit;  "
		"&7(Each segment of) the &#FF6666Misery Melon Plant&7 has a chance to drop 1 &#FFD700Pumpkin Seed&7 when destroyed;  "
		""
		"&7When destroying a connected, lower &#FF6666Misery Melon Plant&7, the &#FF6666Misery Melon Plant&7 and &#FF6666Misery Melon&7 connected above it will also be destroyed together;  "
		"&7Players can also climb along the &#FF6666Misery Melon Plant&7 just like climbing twisting vines."
	]
	quest.05499B6A45252488.quest_subtitle: "I'm having such a hard time"
	quest.056130E2CD71DC75.quest_desc: [
		"&7This modpack has made numerous &#FFD700QOL tweaks&7 and optimizations to &#66CCFFSilent Gear&7. For detailed tutorials and blueprints, please refer to the &#66CCFFSilent Gear&7 chapter."
		""
		"Please be sure to check the side quests. The main questline only serves to guide the progression and contains nothing else!"
		""
		"&zYou can craft the Multi-Tool Pickaxe and the Wide-Area Mining Pickaxe to significantly improve your gameplay experience"
		"[ { \"text\": \"Click to jump to Silent Gear\", \"underlined\": true, \"color\":\"yellow\",\"clickEvent\": { \"action\": \"change_page\", \"value\": \"59FD6ADB15123223\" } } ]"
	]
	quest.056130E2CD71DC75.quest_subtitle: "The Root of All Evil"
	quest.056130E2CD71DC75.title: "It's Blueprints After All"
	quest.058E2E161B35737E.quest_desc: ["前期优秀的特性，受击可以召唤狼群"]
	quest.058E2E161B35737E.quest_subtitle: "群狼形态"
	quest.0594FF6909227B41.quest_desc: [
		"&6All&r material attributes can be checked in the &6Silent Gear catalog&r, and trait effects can be searched and viewed in EMI"
		""
		"&7Codfish isn't really good at writing quests... please forgive the parts that aren't well written..."
		""
		"It's fine, I'll help Codfish write it—oh wait, I'm bad at it too, sorry about that."
	]
	quest.0594FF6909227B41.quest_subtitle: "To view attribute rankings, check the Material Encyclopedia"
	quest.0594FF6909227B41.title: "Materials can be searched in EMI: Silent Gear Materials to view all materials"
	quest.059AFBCEE942C1B4.quest_desc: ["不论是魔法师还是纯战士都建议带一个，根据魔力条增伤"]
	quest.059AFBCEE942C1B4.quest_subtitle: "增伤类材料"
	quest.059D21A5F949C15C.quest_desc: [
		"&2Players can store enchanted books into it, converting them into corresponding enchantment experience. Enchantment experience can be used to split or merge enchanted books."
		""
		"&cWithdrawing an enchanted book consumes the corresponding enchantment experience, and the cost grows exponentially with level."
		""
		"&2This mechanic can reduce the number of equipment modifications. A top-tier piece of equipment might only need 1 modification instead of 4-5, significantly saving experience."
		""
		"&7Can be collected bare-handed; using a pickaxe speeds it up. Can be infused and upgraded into the Library of Alexandria."
		""
		"&eMining and upgrading will not lose stored enchantments."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"&7How to use: The box at the top of the GUI allows direct searching for the enchanted book you need. The three slots on the right, from top to bottom, are: the filter box (yellow), used to place enchantable items to display their supported enchantments; the input slot (blue), to store enchanted books into the library; the output slot (yellow), to withdraw the enchanted book with the selected enchantment. You can also place existing enchanted books in to continue selecting."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"&7Storage method: In this device, enchantments are stored as enchantment points. Enchantment points represent how many level-one copies of that enchantment there are. When withdrawing, the enchantment consumes the corresponding enchantment points according to the vanilla anvil calculation, but does not cause an enchantment penalty. This is because merging enchantments in the library greatly reduces the occurrence of enchantment penalties."
	]
	quest.059D21A5F949C15C.quest_subtitle: "Right here, may you find the book you seek"
	quest.059D21A5F949C15C.title: "A Brand-New Way to Store Magic"
	quest.059FEF132D3FF800.quest_desc: [
		"&7Right-click to block as a &#FFD700shield&7 (even though the animation looks like throwing the sword). Within &#FFAA332s&7 after a successful block, the next attack gains &#FFAA3350%&7."
		""
		"&7Can obtain &cknockback resistance&7 from materials."
	]
	quest.059FEF132D3FF800.quest_subtitle: "My Sword-Shield"
	quest.05A4F69164ABBCCA.quest_desc: ["&7Functions the same as a vanilla &#66CCFFbow&7."]
	quest.05A4F69164ABBCCA.quest_subtitle: "The Classic Long-Range Weapon"
	quest.05EA527792F0F44E.quest_desc: [
		"&6Rune of Scythe Might&r"
		""
		"&7The Rune of Scythe Might gives the wearer power at the cost of &8souls&r&7 taken by the scythe. For a period of time, each kill makes the &eweapon&r&7 in hand increasingly &apowerful&r&7.&r"
	]
	quest.05EA527792F0F44E.quest_subtitle: "Destroying the Shattered"
	quest.05F590213B78B32C.quest_desc: ["Charges over time when worn. Once fully charged, it plays a sound cue. At that point, pressing the corresponding keybind uses Adrenaline. While under Adrenaline's effect, damage dealt is multiplied by 2."]
	quest.05F590213B78B32C.quest_subtitle: "Adrenaline"
	quest.05F6670AAFE979C5.quest_subtitle: "Time to take a break, huh?"
	quest.05F6670AAFE979C5.title: "Playtime 4h"
	quest.063C503183780229.title: "Coating Parts"
	quest.065CA86479CA3AF9.quest_desc: [
		"&7&#FFD700Signal Wave Totem Control&7"
		""
		"&7When multiple rituals exist simultaneously, it is extremely difficult to keep the order in which they each take effect consistent."
		""
		"&7Normally, a Spirit ritual only activates after collecting sufficient energy from the spontaneous arcane flow within the world."
		"&7For the &#66CCFFSignal Wave Totem Base&7, however, this energy remains in a kind of \"&#FFD700preserved&7\" state until it receives a &#FF6666redstone pulse&7."
		"&7When organizing multiple rituals, you can use a &#FF8844Redstone Observer&7 to pinpoint the exact moment a Spirit ritual can be activated."
		""
		"&7The timing of sending a pulse to the &#66CCFFSignal Wave Totem Base&7 can be difficult to grasp."
		"&7Note that a sustained signal is not required; the internal circuitry of the base only recognizes the pulse at the start of the signal."
	]
	quest.065CA86479CA3AF9.quest_subtitle: "&6A Miracle Appears in the World"
	quest.065CA86479CA3AF9.title: "Totem Magic II"
	quest.06BE812E1FAAD2B2.quest_subtitle: "没有最大，只有更大！"
	quest.06BE812E1FAAD2B2.title: "更大的空间 ！"
	quest.06C2F1EFADAD809F.quest_desc: [
		"&7昂贵而强大的材料，秘银需要在-63到-38之间挖掘寻找，生成量相当少，在用幽冥锤开路的情况下会轻松一些，挖掘掉落受时运影响。雷电瓶需要使用玻璃瓶右键闪电苦力怕获得，也可以在铁魔法的特殊结构中开启隐藏箱子获取。"
		""
		"&7其强大之处在于奥术谐振4词条，玩家每拥有10点魔力可提供1%增伤，上限词条等级*20，也就是说雷霆织物握柄在魔力值充足的前提下可以提供80%的恐怖增伤。"
		""
		"&e如果不同装备上同时存在多个奥术谐振词条，增加法力值的效果可以叠加，但增伤无法叠加，以最高等级计算。"
	]
	quest.06C2F1EFADAD809F.quest_subtitle: "优秀的增伤类材料"
	quest.070C94F2F2F2D972.quest_desc: [
		"&6Mending Diffuser&r"
		""
		"&7The Mending Diffuser uses fresh flesh and blood as a sympathetic anchor for natural life recovery. After completing one &6Focusing Cycle&r&7, a crucible equipped with it has a chance to slightly repair any &eCatalyst Charm&r&7. However, it cannot save a Catalyst Charm that has already shattered.&r"
	]
	quest.070C94F2F2F2D972.quest_subtitle: "Dead Scar Tissue"
	quest.073C903793B7F71F.title: "Discover the Sunken City"
	quest.074B29C2B24651B9.title: "Pickaxe Equipment"
	quest.075AC794CF9E3665.quest_desc: [
		"# &eResource Pack Management &r"
		""
		"### &cResource Pack Path &r"
		"&7<Reverie Foundry>"
		"&7\\config\\\\paxi\\\\resourcepacks"
		""
		"### &6Recommended Actions &r"
		"&f- Delete resource packs you don't want at this path"
		"&f- &cSome resources also need to be deleted in kubejs &r"
		"&f- For GUI texture packs:"
		"  &7▪ &aStrongly recommend replacing rather than deleting outright &r"
		"  &7▪ Replacement avoids missing UI element issues"
		""
		"### &3Notes &r"
		"&7- Recommend backing up original files before making changes"
		"&7- Deleting some resource packs may cause display issues"
		"If display issues occur, delete resourcepack_load_order.json as well"
	]
	quest.075AC794CF9E3665.quest_subtitle: "PAXI"
	quest.078C80DB81D1640E.quest_desc: [
		"&6Modpack Command Quick Reference&r"
		"&7The modpack provides many custom commands.&r"
		""
		"&6Wendigo&r"
		"&7&e/rf wendigosystem toggle&r&7 - Toggle the Wendigo effect&r"
		"&7&e/rf wendigosystem status&r&7 - Check status&r"
		""
		"&6Ore Stage&r"
		"&7&e/rf orestage&r&7 - Check current stage status&r"
		"&7&e/rf orestage reset&r&7 - &cReset all data (use with caution)&r&7"
		"&7&e/rf orestage reload&r&7 - Reload the config file&r"
		"&7&e/rf orestage validate&r&7 - Validate config and auto-repair&r"
		"&7&e/rf orestage info&r&7 - Check detailed progress info&r"
		"&7&e/rf orestage kills&r&7 - Check kill statistics&r"
		""
		"&6Utility Features&r"
		"&7&e/rf entityclean&r&7 - Clears miscellaneous entities nearby; by default only clears some dropped items, arrows, and similar entities (configurable)&r"
		""
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"&6Additional Suffering&r"
		""
		"&6State Management&r"
		"&7&e/rf deathsystem toggle&r&7 - Enable/disable the death penalty system&r"
		"&7&e/rf deathsystem status&r&7 - Check death statistics and current status&r"
		""
		"&6Data Reset&r"
		"&7&e/rf deathsystem reset&r&7 - &cReset the death counter and restore max health on next respawn&r"
		""
		"&7&e/rf depression toggle&r&7 - Toggle depression (Additional Suffering)&r"
		"&7&e/rf depression status&r&7 - Check depression (Additional Suffering)&r"
		""
		"&6Item Grants&r"
		"&7&e/rf give randomenchanted&r&7 - Claim a random enchanted book&r"
		"&7&e/rf give randomscrollid&r&7 - Claim a random scroll&r"
		"&7&e/rf give drunkard&r&7 - Claim the &bDrunkard Set&r&7 (various drinks)&r"
		"&7&e/rf give traveler&r&7 - Claim the &bTraveler Set&r&7 (backpack + enchanted book)&r"
		"&7&e/rf give sorcerer&r&7 - Claim the &bSorcerer Set&r&7 (spell equipment)&r"
		"&7&e/rf give warrior&r&7 - Claim the &bWarrior Set&r&7 (combat equipment)&r"
		""
		"&6Admin Features&r"
		"&7&e/rf give <set name> <player name>&r&7 - Give a set to another player&r"
		"&7&e/rf give <set name> <player name> clear&r&7 - &cReset a player's claim limit&r"
		""
		"&7&e/wits&7 - Check the structure you are currently in"
	]
	quest.078C80DB81D1640E.quest_subtitle: "Got it"
	quest.078C80DB81D1640E.title: "Utility Commands"
	quest.07C86BA6CAFFD6C8.quest_subtitle: "View the enhancement effects your current familiars have obtained"
	quest.07E7C74E2EA9FB8E.quest_desc: [
		"&6Spirulina Forest&r"
		"&7is one of the ocean biomes of the Starlight Dimension."
		""
		"&7Spirulina Forests have vegetation coverage completely different from the Starlit Sea."
		"&7The main plants covering it are &#20B2AASpirulina Plants&r&7, &#98FB98Sea Candle Grass&r&7, and &#DB7093Sea Roses&r&7, rather than the usual &#9ACD32Abyssal Fruit Plants&r."
		""
		"&7Non-aquatic creatures can only spawn underground, dozens of blocks deep from the Spirulina Forest."
	]
	quest.07E7C74E2EA9FB8E.quest_subtitle: "An Eternal Feast"
	quest.07E7C74E2EA9FB8E.title: "Spirulina Forest"
	quest.07E84F32AFD0365F.quest_desc: [
		"&7Defeating the Primordial Fire-Bearer will unlock &#2EFFCCEnd Gober Ore&r."
		""
		"&7Additionally, the Broken Key dropped by the Primordial Fire-Bearer can open special vaults within the castle, which produce materials such as Blaze Gold Ingots."
	]
	quest.07E84F32AFD0365F.quest_subtitle: "\"And then, I will naturally show you what power truly means\""
	quest.07F1B2594FCCAF01.quest_desc: [
		"&6Rune of Agility&r"
		""
		"&7The Rune of Agility urges the mind to move and adapt in dangerous moments, increasing &amovement speed&r&7. The amount increases as the wearer's vitality drains, up to doubling movement speed.&r"
	]
	quest.07F1B2594FCCAF01.quest_subtitle: "A Pulse That Spurs Flight"
	quest.082F47A08B859C62.quest_desc: [
		"Can be summoned via the Altar; search Spawn: XXX in EMI to view the corresponding recipe"
		"{image:kubejs:textures/gui/spawn.png width:150 height:130 align:center}"
	]
	quest.082F47A08B859C62.quest_subtitle: "Stage 3"
	quest.085ED7F06792B829.title: "Frozen Man"
	quest.08600655258549DB.quest_desc: ["&7Too powerful—feed it and it eats instantly. Combined with high-saturation food, you become an undying demon, as long as you don't get one-shot..."]
	quest.08600655258549DB.quest_subtitle: "Someone come feed the young master some cake"
	quest.086482C52023DB55.quest_subtitle: "A handy tool for finding the nearest Underground Dragon Nest"
	quest.086F7ED726FBC65F.quest_desc: ["&7击杀龙族即可入手，前期亦可借助跑图拾荒提前获得。属性加成不俗，是贯穿前中期都极具实用价值的材料"]
	quest.086F7ED726FBC65F.quest_subtitle: "你是龙，也好"
	quest.08A257E690F34298.quest_desc: ["&7理论层面的超级耐活材料，可积攒能量并提供高额回血。击败死者之王后方可获取，是高难度战斗时极为可靠的续航材料。"]
	quest.08A257E690F34298.quest_subtitle: "理论耐活王"
	quest.08C5CE1D2BDAE5E9.quest_desc: ["&7After defeating it, you can craft the &#66CCFFTidal Claw Blueprint&7. Left-click to fire a homing abyssal tentacle at enemies, right-click to fire a chain that pulls you forward."]
	quest.08C5CE1D2BDAE5E9.quest_subtitle: "Kill kill kill"
	quest.08CE5969D7C39389.quest_desc: ["Unlocked after the Skeleton King"]
	quest.08CE5969D7C39389.quest_subtitle: "Basic Part"
	quest.08DB4D29BBE0A6CD.quest_desc: ["&7基础值优秀，星光亲和度极高，即便只吃词条效果也毫不逊色。入手不亏，泛用性极强。"]
	quest.08DB4D29BBE0A6CD.quest_subtitle: "星语之核"
	quest.08F9A6C96FD98212.quest_desc: [
		"&7Does not spawn naturally. Only has a chance to be summoned after a &#66DDCCSoul Tendril&7 is triggered (small/medium);"
		""
		"&7&#FFAA33Spirit-Tier Horrors&7 summoned by the &#FFD700Cunning Candle&7 are always medium-sized;"
		""
		"&7&#CC99FFPhantoms&7 will actively attack &#FF6666Magma Cubes&7. A &#FF6666Magma Cube&7 killed by a &#CC99FFPhantom&7 will always transform into a &#FFAA33Spirit-Tier Horror&7;  "
		"&7A &#FF6666Magma Cube&7 transformed this way will still split into smaller &#FF6666Magma Cubes&7 as it would on a normal death;  "
		"&7After a &#FFAA33Spirit-Tier Horror&7 is killed, it &#FF6666will never&7 cause the &#CC99FFPhantom&7 to respawn;  "
		"&7If a &#CC99FFPhantom&7 approaches a [Step] gargoyle statue, it will immediately transform into a &#FFAA33Spirit-Tier Horror&7 (always large)."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"&7Inherited traits (&#FF6666Magma Cube&7)  "
		"&7Moves by jumping. A &#FFAA33Spirit-Tier Horror's&7 single jump height is roughly equal to its own body height;  "
		"&7Immune to fire damage;"
		""
		"&7Basic attack (melee attack):  "
		"&7Melee attacks have &#FF6666no frequency limit&7, meaning they can deal damage every frame (or every game tick);  "
		"&7The damage immunity mechanic ensures its target only takes two consecutive hits after being struck (per second);  "
		"&7Blocking with a &#FFD700Shield&7 will not trigger the damage immunity mechanic and will rapidly consume shield durability! Be careful!"
		""
		"&7Burrowing  "
		"&7&#FFAA33Spirit-Tier Horrors&7 sometimes burrow underground to chase targets;  "
		"&7While burrowed, the &#FFAA33Spirit-Tier Horror&7 has no hit detection (but &#55D5D5Spirit Arrows&7/explosion damage can ignore this mechanic and deal damage normally);  "
		"&7The &#FFAA33Spirit-Tier Horror&7 will resurface after several seconds of burrowing, and by inheriting its traits, it can deal two consecutive hits of attack damage to targets it collides with;  "
		"&7The &#FFAA33Spirit-Tier Horror&7 stops chasing its target within &#FFAA332 seconds&7 before resurfacing;  "
		"&7While burrowed, the &#FFAA33Spirit-Tier Horror&7:  "
		"&7Moves in the same way as a &#CC99FFZombie&7, and can also climb vertically placed blocks like a spider;  "
		"&7A &#FFAA33Spirit-Tier Horror&7 that splits from a larger &#FFAA33Spirit-Tier Horror&7 upon its death will always open with a burrow attack;  "
		"&7Burrow skill cooldown is &#FFAA335 seconds&7 (large) / &#FFAA3310 seconds&7 (medium, small)."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"&7&#66FF66Frogs&7 will produce &#FFAA331~8&7 &#66DDCCFrog Haze&7 after eating a &#FFAA33Spirit-Tier Horror&7;  "
		"&7The color of the &#66DDCCFrog Haze&7 produced corresponds exactly to the texture color of that &#66FF66Frog&7;"
		""
		"&7When a &#FFAA33Spirit-Tier Horror&7 touches water (fluid), is exposed to rainy weather, or is hit by a splash/lingering water bottle:  "
		"&7It will immediately transform into a &#FF6666Magma Cube&7 and gain &#FFAA3310 seconds&7 of Nausea, &#FFAA335 seconds&7 of Weakness II, and &#FFAA335 seconds&7 of Slowness III."
	]
	quest.08F9A6C96FD98212.quest_subtitle: "Squish"
	quest.08F9A6C96FD98212.title: "Observation: Spirit-Tier Horror"
	quest.0919F71D241AFD81.quest_desc: [
		"&6Authority of the Gleeful Target&r"
		""
		"&7Your form is frozen in time—an anomaly detached from the world. The form does not age, nor can it perceive the outside.&r"
		"&7-All &chealing received&r&7 reduced to one quarter&r"
		""
		"&7Authority—the treaty between your form and the world itself.&r"
		"&7-When struck, the form enters a &6Stasis State&r"
		"&7-Under the &6Stasis State&r&7, all &epotion effects&r&7 pause their timers and do not expire&r"
		"&7-Effects requiring the flow of time, such as regeneration and poison, cease to function; those unaffected by stasis still apply&r"
		""
		"{image:kubejs:textures/gui/malum/authority_of_the_gleeful_target.png width:160 height:200 align:center}"
	]
	quest.0919F71D241AFD81.quest_subtitle: "Happiest in the World"
	quest.0919F71D241AFD81.title: "Authority of the Gleeful Target"
	quest.092C65BDEC1E30A4.quest_desc: [
		"&6Transmogrification Table&r"
		""
		"&7Worried your weapon looks too ugly?&r"
		"&7Worried it doesn't look cool enough?&r"
		""
		"&7The Transmogrification Table, your first choice! Whether you want to &aplay the fool to catch the wise&r&7 or &apretend to be a tiger to eat the pig&r&7! It's all up to you!&r"
		""
		"&7Place the &eweapon&r&7 to be transmogrified in the first slot, and the appearance you want it changed into in the second slot, then consume amethyst energy to transmogrify your weapon!&r&7&r"
	]
	quest.092C65BDEC1E30A4.quest_subtitle: "Ever-Changing"
	quest.092C65BDEC1E30A4.title: "Transmogrification Table"
	quest.0973A81F39964B58.quest_subtitle: "Familiar Summoning Ritual"
	quest.09BD7CB2DEA2CD89.quest_desc: ["Can customize the fired arrow's speed and accuracy"]
	quest.09BD7CB2DEA2CD89.quest_subtitle: "Custom Experience"
	quest.0A12067C6B752CAC.quest_desc: ["&7With the help of the most mysterious Heart of the Sea, the Ocean Bookshelf has completed its transformation. Its power is more surging, yet it has not become violent. The &aTier&7 and &5Arcana&7 this bookshelf provides are more than two or three times that of its predecessor. However, the Heart of the Sea's power is ultimately gentle, and it did not bring an extra &aTier&7 cap. After all, nothing is perfect—achieving this much is already impressive."]
	quest.0A12067C6B752CAC.quest_subtitle: "Mysterious Embrace"
	quest.0A12067C6B752CAC.title: "Embrace of the Heart"
	quest.0A13EAB37AB4ACEF.quest_desc: [
		"&6Familiar Trinkets&r"
		"&7Familiar trinkets are items that can be equipped in trinket slots, providing different buffs to the corresponding familiar.&r"
		""
		"&7&eMagic Leaf&r&7: Increases the &aspell power&r&7 of &bDruid&r&7 familiars. Can be found in &bJungle Temples&r&7.&r"
		""
		"&7&eHunter's Chain&r&7: Increases the &aspell power&r&7 of &bHunter&r&7 familiars. Can be found in &cEvoker Fortresses&r&7 or &bHunter Camps&r&7.&r"
		""
		"&7&eLich Emblem Necklace&r&7: Increases the &aspell power&r&7 of &cNecromancer&r&7 familiars. Can be found in &8Graveyards&r&7.&r"
		""
		"&7&eCrown of Oblivion&r&7: Increases the &aspell power&r&7 of &bEvoker&r&7 familiars. Can be found in &cAncient Cities&r&7.&r"
		""
		"&7&eShining Crown&r&7: Increases the &aspell power&r&7 of &6Archmage&r&7 familiars. Can be found in &6Archmage Laboratories&r&7.&r"
		""
		"&7&eGolden Bell&r&7: Increases the &aspell power&r&7 of &dIllusionist&r&7 familiars. Can be found in &bWoodland Mansions&r&7.&r"
		""
		"&7&eWizard Candlestick&r&7: Increases the &aspell power&r&7 of &eBlaze&r&7 familiars. Can be found in &cPyromancer Towers&r&7.&r"
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"&7&eBlessed Chalice&r&7: Increases the &aspell power&r&7 of &aCleric&r&7 familiars. Can be found in &aCleric Huts&r&7.&r"
		""
		"&7&eThunder Emblem Necklace&r&7: Increases the &aspell power&r&7 of &6Thunder Warlock&r&7 familiars. Can be found in &bMountain Towers&r&7.&r"
		""
		"&7&eFilthy Cheese Necklace&r&7: Increases the &aspell power&r&7 of &cPlague Doctor&r&7 familiars. Can be found in &bIce Spike Shipwrecks&r&7.&r"
		""
		"&7&eLost Melody&r&7: Increases the &aspell power&r&7 of &dBard&r&7 familiars. Can be obtained through the &eMysterious Orb&r&7.&r"
		""
		"&7&eFrostflower&r&7: Increases the &aspell power&r&7 of &bFrost&r&7 familiars. Can be found in &bIce Spider Nests&r&7.&r"
		""
		"&7&eDragon's Tear&r&7: Increases the &aspell power&r&7 of &6Dragoon&r&7 familiars. Dropped by the &cEnder Dragon&r&7.&r"
		""
		"&7&ePandora's Box&r&7: Allows up to 10 familiars to be &asummoned/dismissed&r&7 at the same time. Obtained by crafting.&r"
	]
	quest.0A13EAB37AB4ACEF.title: "Any Familiar Trinket"
	quest.0A1FF9CCFB4FEA6C.quest_subtitle: "Can't come home empty-handed, right..."
	quest.0A1FF9CCFB4FEA6C.title: "First Fish Caught"
	quest.0ABD1C741FFFC78C.quest_desc: [
		"&6Rune of Scorching Fury&r"
		""
		"&7The Rune of Scorching Fury functions similarly to the ritual of the same name, granting the wearer a half-strength &bScorching Fury&r&7 effect, slightly increasing &aattack&r&7 and &amining&r&7 speed.&r"
	]
	quest.0ABD1C741FFFC78C.quest_subtitle: "A Pulse That Grinds"
	quest.0AC4291DE561460A.quest_desc: [
		"&6Aether River&r"
		"&7is one of the rarer surface biomes of the Starlight Dimension."
		""
		"&7Just like rivers in the Overworld, it is usually a &8transitional biome&r that separates waterways within one biome or across multiple biomes."
		"&7Scattered &#E6E6FAQuartz Sulfur Blocks&r&7 have a chance to generate along the Aether River banks, for players to collect."
		""
		"&7&#5CACEEAether&r&7 itself is a very &cdangerous&r&7 high-brightness fluid, and it prevents any vegetation or creatures from spawning on its surface."
		"&7Creatures can only spawn underground, dozens of blocks deep from the Aether River."
		""
		"&7The area underground beneath the Aether River is the only region where &#E6E6FAQuartz Sulfur Geodes&r&7 can generate."
		""
		"&5CACEEAether&r&7 can be used as fuel in a furnace"
	]
	quest.0AC4291DE561460A.quest_subtitle: "Painless Death"
	quest.0AC4291DE561460A.title: "Aether River"
	quest.0ADEACC84320DCC0.quest_desc: [
		"&7The Precision Forging system is a &5advanced enhancement mechanic&7 for &6Silent Gear&7 equipment, raising its &aquality&7 through &bpractical wear&7. Each time the &cequipment breaks&7, it accumulates &eexperience&7. After reaching a certain count, the &dPrecision Forging level&7 increases, granting the equipment &3random attribute bonuses&7.&r"
		""
		"&7&lCore Mechanics:&r"
		"&7Precision Forging level can reach up to &6Level V&r"
		"&7Each Precision Forging level increase requires accumulating &especific break counts&r"
		"&7Any modification to the equipment reduces the Precision Forging level by &c2 levels&r"
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"&7Each trait is generated independently. Without &6Precision Forging Strength Correction&7, the bonus value randomly ranges from &a-25%&7 to &c+25%&7"
		""
		"&7The same attribute can appear repeatedly at &bdifferent levels&7, and the effects &estack&7"
		"&7Within the same level, &cno&7 duplicate attributes will appear"
		"&7Equipment can have at most &d5 different attribute&7 traits"
		""
		"&6Precision Forging Probability Modifier&7"
		"&7Some special materials can provide equipment with a &b\"Precision Forging Modifier\"&7, affecting the bonus range during Precision Forging:"
		"&aHigher positive modifier&7: higher chance of positive bonuses, higher bonus cap"
		"&cHigher negative modifier&7: higher chance of negative bonuses, lower bonus floor"
		"&7Modifier range: &e-50 ~ +50"
		""
		"&6Precision Forging Strength Modifier&7"
		"&7Some special materials can provide equipment with a &b\"Precision Forging Modifier\"&7, affecting the bonus range during Precision Forging:"
		"&aHigher positive modifier&7: higher cap for positive traits during Precision Forging"
		"&cHigher negative modifier&7: higher cap for negative traits during Precision Forging"
		"&7Modifier range: &e-50 ~ +50"
	]
	quest.0ADEACC84320DCC0.quest_subtitle: "Polishing Equipment"
	quest.0B0C47F37FDE6435.quest_desc: [
		"&7Soulwoven Silk is a light yet tough material, full of things like &6souls&r&7. Like the form itself, it is naturally able to block &darcane energy&r&7. Though other materials have this property too, &6Soulwoven Silk&r&7 is easier to work with—certainly much better than &8stone&r&7."
		""
		"&7Fragments of souls can glow, so souls can naturally glow too. Why not let the souls within the silk emit light?"
		""
		"&7I crafted several &bbanners&r&7 to test the effect, and borrowed various &ereagents&r&7 and &6Spirits&r&7 to design patterns. When infused with energy, they emit a &8dim light&r&7; infusing one more Spirit makes them &edazzling&r&7."
	]
	quest.0B0C47F37FDE6435.quest_subtitle: "Weaving Illusions"
	quest.0B33B7CF2E127A4F.quest_desc: [
		"&7Journeys often involve carrying a large number of items. While storing them in &#66DDCCChests&7 offers considerable capacity, it can be inconvenient in certain situations..."
		""
		"&f\"Come one, come all, don't miss out—you can't lose, you can't be scammed! Gently used by a girl, &#66CCFF99% New Storage Component&f, one set. Order now and get a &#66DDCC16K Storage Block&f free. Don't underestimate this &#66CCFFStorage Component&f—it's tiny in your bag, but plug it in and it grows big and tall. Store ores, store junk, store food, super convenient. Don't just stand there, come grab one!\""
	]
	quest.0B33B7CF2E127A4F.quest_subtitle: "Convenient and Quick"
	quest.0B33B7CF2E127A4F.title: "AAA Korindou Secondhand Wholesale"
	quest.0BA8FDE1647AA593.quest_subtitle: "Keep at it"
	quest.0BA8FDE1647AA593.title: "First Death"
	quest.0BABB13A3B9A5412.quest_desc: ["往其中写入合成表后放置在 自动合成仓 中实现自动合成物品"]
	quest.0BABB13A3B9A5412.quest_subtitle: "流水作业"
	quest.0BB5CE1550F46002.quest_desc: [
		""
		"When facing a quest you need to keep as an ongoing goal but are afraid of forgetting, you can click the spot shown in the image to pin it"
		"{image:kubejs:textures/gui/ftb_kjs2.png width:200 height:100 align:center fit:true}"
		""
		""
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"Successful example:"
		"{image:kubejs:textures/gui/ftb_kjs1.png width:80 height:100 align:center}"
	]
	quest.0BB5CE1550F46002.quest_subtitle: "What was I supposed to do again"
	quest.0BB5CE1550F46002.title: "Pinning"
	quest.0BCF6B18963AB88F.quest_desc: [
		"&7In the tomb of the &#FF6666King of the Dead&7, there is a special cell whose loot barrel contains a &#FFD700Summon King of the Dead&7 scroll. This scroll requires &#FFAA3315000 mana&7 to cast. Generally it cannot be cast through a spellbook, but holding the scroll directly to cast ignores the mana cost—though the scroll is &#FF6666consumed&7 upon casting."
		""
		"&7Please note that the &#FF6666Wrathful King of the Dead&7 summoned by this scroll is an enhanced boss, not a friendly unit."
		""
		"&7That dead monster, forcibly revived by some kind of magic, as if some will behind it is pulling the strings."
		""
		"&8\"A will forcibly stitched into a broken husk by necromantic magic. When this fragile seam snaps once more, the power it sustains—that which should not exist in this world—begins to unravel\""
	]
	quest.0BCF6B18963AB88F.quest_subtitle: "Power of the Dead"
	quest.0BCF6B18963AB88F.title: "Wrathful King of the Dead"
	quest.0C1EFCAED337180F.quest_desc: [
		"&6Aurora Deer&r&7"
		"&7Neutral creature. Fights back only when attacked itself. Can only spawn on the surface of the &#87CEEBStarlight Permafrost Forest&r&7;&r"
		""
		"&7This creature only performs melee attacks and has low aggression;&r"
		""
		"&7After being hit for a period of time, it lowers its head to charge up (if the player gets close to its head at this time, they will take its melee damage, which may also interrupt its charge-up);&r"
		""
		"&7After charging up, it &#00FFFFcharges&r&7 several blocks in a random straight-line direction, dealing melee damage to targets along the way;&r"
		""
		"&7All of the above attacks can be blocked by a shield.&r"
		""
		"&7&#FFA500Aurora Deer Antler&r&7 cannot drop when the Aurora Deer dies on its own;&r"
		""
		"&7If the Aurora Deer hits any kind of &#808080stone block&r&7 during its charge:&r"
		""
		"&7It will always drop one full-durability &#FFA500Aurora Deer Antler&r&7, and this Aurora Deer's model will also be missing one antler;&r"
		""
		"&7A single Aurora Deer can drop at most two &#FFA500Aurora Deer Antlers&r&7. Losing an antler does not affect its attack damage.&r"
	]
	quest.0C1EFCAED337180F.title: "Aurora Deer"
	quest.0C2F2186BE39605E.quest_desc: [
		"&6Hunter Camps&r"
		"&7Hunters live in groups, so they built camps along their main hunting routes, mostly in &bforest&r&7 areas rich with prey. These camps can also be found using the &eRolled-Up Map&r&7 obtained from the Origin Island.&r"
	]
	quest.0C2F2186BE39605E.quest_subtitle: "Discover a Hunter Camp"
	quest.0C2F2186BE39605E.title: "&6Hunter Camp&r"
	quest.0C95DCE08BB56AF5.quest_desc: [
		"&6Rune of Spirit Solidity&r"
		""
		"&7The Rune of Spirit Solidity does not enhance the form's abilities, but instead applies pressure to its arcane existence, increasing the capacity and firmness of the &eSoul Ward&r&7.&r"
	]
	quest.0C95DCE08BB56AF5.quest_subtitle: "A Pulse That Spurs Creation"
	quest.0CC6907B16C93F5E.quest_desc: [
		"&7Combines &FF6666killing&7, &#66DDCCchopping&7, and &#66FF66harvesting&7 functions into one.  "
		"&7Attack speed is slightly slow. Left-clicking crops performs &#66FF66area harvesting&7, but does not replant."
	]
	quest.0CC6907B16C93F5E.quest_subtitle: "Jungle Essence"
	quest.0CCFA64CA88D2D22.quest_desc: [
		"# &3Press R for one-click sorting (under default settings) &r"
		""
		"### &bNotes &r"
		"&7- By default, pressing R sorts in Creative Mode order&r  "
		"&7- Pressing Shift+R sorts by quantity&r  "
		"&7- Pressing Ctrl+R sorts alphabetically&r  "
		"&7- Pressing Alt+R sorts by ID&r  "
	]
	quest.0CCFA64CA88D2D22.quest_subtitle: "Plenty of Options!"
	quest.0CCFA64CA88D2D22.title: "R-Key Sorting"
	quest.0CD35DB0CA195AE0.quest_desc: [
		"&7The &#66DDCCMaterial Grader&7 can grade almost every material supported by &#66CCFFSilent Gear&7. Materials of different grades provide different improvements to the parts and equipment made from them."
		""
		"&7Different grades affect many parameters of the material. Grades include &#FFD700E, D, C, B, A, S, SS, SSS, MAX&7"
		"&mWho's legendary&r"
		""
		"&7The &#66DDCCMaterial Grader&7 requires a &#FFD700Grading Catalyst&7 to function."
		""
		"&7The second input slot of the Material Grader is for placing the catalyst. Grading consumes the catalyst and increases the &#FFAA33average grade&7 based on the catalyst's grade. In short, the better the catalyst, the higher the possible grading level."
		""
		"&7Placing an already graded material back into the Material Grader will &#FFD700re-grade&7 it. A higher grade obtained by the material replaces the original; if the grade is the same or lower, &#FF6666nothing changes&7, but the catalyst is still consumed."
		"{image:kubejs:textures/gui/silentgear/material_grader.png width:200 height:100 align:center}"
	]
	quest.0CD35DB0CA195AE0.quest_subtitle: "So It Was Inferior Material"
	quest.0CE3D98152F44B6E.quest_desc: [
		"&7Explosions caused by the wearer:"
		""
		"&7Have a &#66FF66Fortune III&7 effect;"
		""
		"&7Avoid destroying valuable drops (&#CC6666#malum:prospectors_treasure&7): ores, storage/compressed blocks, ingots, nuggets, gems, raw mineral resources, charcoal, metal nodes, crystal clusters."
		""
		"&7Netherite Scrap does not match this tag and will be destroyed by explosions."
	]
	quest.0CE3D98152F44B6E.quest_subtitle: "Blast Miner"
	quest.0CFA26B3944AAF49.quest_desc: [
		"&7To enhance weapon attributes, you can use the &#66CCFFStarlight Charger&7 for strengthening."
		""
		"&7Set up a &#FFAA337×7&7 area in an open-air environment, with the charger in the center and a two-block-tall pillar at each of the four corners. The block placed on top of the pillar determines the &#FFD700charge level&7:"
		""
		"&7&#FFD700Level 1&7: &#FF6666Crimson Steel Block&7.  "
		"&7&#FFD700Level 2&7: &#66CCFFAzure Amber Gold Block&7.  "
		"&7&#FFD700Level 3&7: &#FFD700Tyr Steel Block&7."
		""
		"{image:kubejs:textures/gui/starlight_charger.png width:180 height:100 align:center}"
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"&7A charged weapon gains a certain degree of attribute improvement, but the improvement manifests in &#FFAA33specific values&7—for example, 12 attack damage might increase to 13. Percentage-type attributes receive basically &#FF6666no improvement&7."
		""
		"&7The Starlight Charge level &FF6666decreases&7 as the weapon wears down, and the numerical bonus Starlight Charging provides to the weapon also &FF6666decreases&7.&m(Isn't this just a stun baton)&r"
		"{image:kubejs:textures/gui/silentgear/starlight_charger.png width:200 height:120 align:center click_action:none:}"
		"&7After placement, wait about &#FFAA3315 seconds&7 for the charger to recognize the environment. This device must be charged in an &#66CCFFopen-air nighttime environment&7 and consumes &#FFD700energy&7 while working."
		""
		"&7A higher-tier charger can use lower-tier catalysts, but the charge level is based on the catalyst's corresponding level."
	]
	quest.0CFA26B3944AAF49.quest_subtitle: "Twinkle Twinkle Little Star"
	quest.0D0DADF7C531B664.quest_desc: ["&7If you lack experience when enchanting, the Potion of Ancient Knowledge can solve most problems. Simply add a Bottle o' Enchanting to an Awkward Potion, and the potion will greatly increase the experience the player gains. If you add another Bottle o' Enchanting to the brewed potion, the effect stacks and increases dramatically."]
	quest.0D0DADF7C531B664.quest_subtitle: "A Tasty Little Drink"
	quest.0D134B44D9F3BA01.quest_desc: [
		"&6Pact of the Shield"
		"&7A hastened exterior and a fragile nature cannot be separated.&r&cSoul Ward firmness halved"
		"&7A hastened form of Soul Ward, turning peril into safety like timely rain.&r&aIncreases Soul Ward capacity&r&aSoul Ward recovery rate doubled"
		""
		"{image:kubejs:textures/gui/malum/pact_of_the_shield.png width:160 height:200 align:center}"
	]
	quest.0D134B44D9F3BA01.quest_subtitle: "Alert in Action"
	quest.0D134B44D9F3BA01.title: "Pact of the Shield"
	quest.0D1AFFB3C244802E.quest_desc: [
		"&6Portal Frame&r"
		"&7A functional block that helps mages create permanent portals.&r"
		"&7When first placed, the portal frame is just an empty shell; only its border has a collision box.&r"
		""
		"&7By casting the &bEnder Portal&r&7 spell on the portal frame using methods such as the &eCall and Response Wand&r&7, it becomes a portal usable for teleportation. It can only connect to another portal frame that has also been cast with the Ender Portal spell in order to teleport. These two portals have no distance limit between them and exist permanently.&r"
		""
		"&7Do not attempt to break this block after creating a portal, otherwise the model will disappear while the block still exists, until you connect it with another portal.&r"
		""
		"&7Players can dye an activated portal by consuming 1 of any dye, and the corresponding other portal will also be dyed automatically.&r"
		""
		"&8It yearns to be granted a paired destiny; until it obtains its other half, not even the void can erase it."
	]
	quest.0D1AFFB3C244802E.quest_subtitle: "Rapid Transit"
	quest.0D88330EEA17433A.quest_desc: [
		"&7Hold right-click to charge and fire. Charge time affects damage."
		"&7Fires &c3&7 homing projectiles each shot."
		"&7Projectile damage = &cranged damage × attack speed modifier × charge multiplier&7."
		"&7Attack speed modifier = &cattack speed ÷ 4&7, minimum &c0.1&7."
		"&7Cooldown = &c40 × (4 ÷ draw speed)&7, max &c60 ticks (3 seconds)&7."
		""
		"&7When the crosshair points at a creature, the projectiles will home in on that creature."
	]
	quest.0D88330EEA17433A.quest_subtitle: "Hacks!"
	quest.0DA24AFB83B99AA4.quest_desc: ["可以提升灵魂护盾的坦度以及攻速，当武器攻速较慢时推荐使用"]
	quest.0DA24AFB83B99AA4.quest_subtitle: "防御特攻"
	quest.0DDD36DA6EAB60C4.quest_desc: [
		"&6Dark Swamp&r"
		"&7is one of the surface biomes of the Starlight Dimension."
		""
		"&7The Dark Swamp is overall paved with &#4A331ANight Mud&r&7 and &#7FCC7FPhantom Grass&r&7 blocks. The terrain is relatively open, and many shallow puddles complement the ground."
		"&7Besides the standard Gloomstone layer and Voidstone layer, the Dark Swamp also generates a unique \"&#4A331ANight Mud Layer&r&7\" between the surface and the Gloomstone layer."
		""
		"&7The Night Mud Layer is mainly composed of &#4A331ANight Mud&r&7 and &#A0A0A0Night Mud Embryo&r&7. Most plants that can generate on the Dark Swamp surface can also generate in the Night Mud Layer (including wild &#FF9900Xin Fruit&r&7 crops)."
		"&7&#4A331ANight Mud Deep Silver Ore&r&7 or &#A0A0A0Night Mud Embryo Deep Silver Ore&r&7 has a chance to generate in the Night Mud Layer. These are unique variants of &#C0C0C0Deep Silver Ore&r&7 that can only appear in this biome."
		"&7Likewise, the underground of this biome is the only region where &#9A32CDMiasma Purple Stone Ore&r&7 can generate naturally."
		""
		"&7The main tree species of the Dark Swamp is the &#2F4F4FGloom Fig&r&7 (corresponding to the Overworld's mangrove)."
		"&7Compared to the Overworld's mangrove swamp, the tree generation spacing in this biome is &alonger&r&7, and players have a more &aopen&r&7 view within this biome."
		""
		"&7You can also find some unique plants in this biome: &#7FCC7FPhantom Grass&r&7, &#FF69B4Swamp Rose&r&7, &#9370DBFan Purple Flower&r&7, &#7FCC7FPhantom Fern&r&7, etc."
	]
	quest.0DDD36DA6EAB60C4.quest_subtitle: "Dark and Sticky"
	quest.0DDD36DA6EAB60C4.title: "Dark Swamp"
	quest.0DEE720101A5B8C3.quest_desc: ["唉唉唉唉唉唉唉唉唉唉唉唉唉唉唉唉唉唉"]
	quest.0E08AE1987B72D9C.quest_desc: [
		"&7Drops produced by explosions caused by the wearer are generated directly at the wearer's position."
		""
		"&7When the wearer holds an item in the off-hand, only drops matching the &#66DDCCoff-hand item&7 are generated at the wearer's position; other drops remain in place."
	]
	quest.0E08AE1987B72D9C.quest_subtitle: "Blast Miner"
	quest.0E31F8D2D8BAC8A5.quest_subtitle: "Right-click to summon random Eternal Gates nearby (usable only in the End)"
	quest.0E82AB0377376FBD.quest_desc: ["If you don't want to advance Apotheosis enchanting, you can craft the Raven Enchanting Table after defeating the Fire-Bearer. Click the UI to freely adjust each enchantment attribute"]
	quest.0E82AB0377376FBD.quest_subtitle: "I Have Ascended"
	quest.0EE6ADB913E3CF80.quest_subtitle: "Has both armor and a small amount of spell attributes—very popular"
	quest.0EF088CAC11B1AA7.quest_desc: [
		"&7After defeating it, you can craft the following blueprints:"
		""
		"&#66CCFFAnnihilator&7, has higher &#FFAA33critical damage&7 than other weapons. When dual-wielding, hold right-click to perform a &#FFD700Slam&7, dealing damage to nearby entities."
		""
		"&#66CCFFWar Halberd&7, right-click to &#FFD700Charge&7, producing &#CC99FFspear thrusts&7 along the charge path at enemies; sneaking and right-clicking produces &#CC99FFspear thrusts&7 at nearby enemies."
		""
		"&#66CCFFCursed Bow&7, fires homing &#66CCFFghost arrows&7 at enemies."
	]
	quest.0EF088CAC11B1AA7.quest_subtitle: "Kill kill kill"
	quest.0EF9389ADF9236E6.quest_desc: [
		"&6Magic Essence&r"
		"&7A consumable used to increase &bspell power&r&7 and &bspell resistance&r&7. Each type has 3 tiers and a usage cap. Obtained through the following methods:&r"
		"&7Power: Dropped by &emagic creatures&r&7, upgraded through &6rituals&r&7.&r"
		"&7Resistance: Obtained through the &eShrinker&r&7, upgraded through &6rituals&r&7.&r"
	]
	quest.0EF9389ADF9236E6.title: "&6Magic Essence: Resistance&r"
	quest.0F430864AB53FB98.quest_desc: [
		"&7A structure generated in the Overworld by the dissipation of &#66CCFFStarlight Power&7. It is the only way to reach the &#66CCFFStarlight Dimension&7 for the first time..."
		""
		"&7You found a... &#FFD700Gatekeeper&7? He doesn't seem to want to talk to you. Maybe you'll have to fight him..."
		""
		"&7The &#FFD700Gatekeeper's&7 attack order is completely random, but almost all of his attacks can be blocked by a &#FFD700Shield&7."
		""
		"&7The &#FFD700Gatekeeper&7 fights with a \"point-taken\" approach and will not actually kill the player (generally), nor can he be killed by the player."
	]
	quest.0F430864AB53FB98.quest_subtitle: "Find the Starlight Portal"
	quest.0F731D1ED5DD01BC.quest_desc: [
		"&6Pact of the Windswept"
		"&7The wind also brushes the face.&r&cThe greater the momentum, the stronger the knockback taken"
		"&7Running with the wind.&r&aSprinting accumulates momentum"
		"{image:kubejs:textures/gui/malum/pact_of_the_windswept.png width:160 height:200 align:center}"
	]
	quest.0F731D1ED5DD01BC.quest_subtitle: "One with the Wind"
	quest.0F731D1ED5DD01BC.title: "Pact of the Windswept"
	quest.0FE4EF207A6937B7.quest_desc: [
		"&7Opening chests/mining workstations in a village while being witnessed will lower your &#FF6666reputation&7. You can try blocking villagers' line of sight with blocks, &m or just kill them all&r."
		""
		"&7Each villager's &#66CCFFreputation&7 is independent. High &#66CCFFreputation&7 gives &#66FF66discounts&7 on trades, while low &#66CCFFreputation&7 causes them to &#FF6666refuse to trade&7."
	]
	quest.0FE4EF207A6937B7.quest_subtitle: "————Raid————"
	quest.0FE4EF207A6937B7.title: "Arriving at the Village"
	quest.0FF85A086C90BE5A.title: "Discover the Bitter Cold Prison"
	quest.1031E9949D709475.quest_desc: ["The End Bookshelf is a more advanced bookshelf made using the magic of infused Dragon's Breath. Although this bookshelf does not provide very high values, the &aTier&r cap it can provide is raised to 90."]
	quest.1031E9949D709475.quest_subtitle: "Approaching the Endgame of Enchanting"
	quest.1031E9949D709475.title: "Introducing the Power of the End"
	quest.1051CF07BFF75644.quest_subtitle: "举头望明月"
	quest.1063B9A89D3EE67C.quest_desc: [
		"{\"text\":\"\",\"extra\":[{\"text\":\"Holding and \",\"color\":\"gray\"},{\"text\":\"right-clicking\",\"color\":\"yellow\"},{\"text\":\" will cause a \",\"color\":\"gray\"},{\"text\":\"Cursed Eye\",\"color\":\"red\"},{\"text\":\" copy to fly from the player's hand toward the nearest \",\"color\":\"gray\"},{\"text\":\"Bitter Cold Prison\",\"color\":\"aqua\"},{\"text\":\", while the Cursed Eye in the player's hand enters a \",\"color\":\"gray\"},{\"text\":\"3s\",\"color\":\"yellow\"},{\"text\":\" cooldown.\",\"color\":\"gray\"}]}"
		""
		"{\"text\":\"\",\"extra\":[{\"text\":\"The flight function only works in the \",\"color\":\"gray\"},{\"text\":\"Overworld\",\"color\":\"green\"},{\"text\":\". It will not work in the \",\"color\":\"gray\"},{\"text\":\"Nether, End\",\"color\":\"red\"},{\"text\":\", or worlds without a Bitter Cold Prison.\",\"color\":\"gray\"}]}"
	]
	quest.1063B9A89D3EE67C.quest_subtitle: "Bitter Cold Prison"
	quest.11047BEDA6023228.quest_desc: [
		"&6Mysterious Orb&r"
		"&7Right-click to obtain the &eHarp&r&7 and &eLost Melody&r&7 trinkets. Obtained through the &6Island Ritual&r&7. To use the Mysterious Orb, you need to complete the taming progress of all &belemental familiars&r&7 (except the Bard familiar).&r"
		"&5Or simply perform the ritual crafting to skip the tedious taming process"
	]
	quest.110C8BBFDBFBA375.quest_desc: ["Creature health and armor are modified to 30x, 15x armor toughness, 10x attack"]
	quest.110C8BBFDBFBA375.quest_subtitle: "&cThis will clear your currently selected difficulty settings"
	quest.110C8BBFDBFBA375.title: "&c\"Unspeakable Brute Force and Savagery\""
	quest.11113DE0965217BB.quest_subtitle: "A handy tool for finding the Starlight Portal"
	quest.1117830BC3A66701.quest_desc: [
		"&7The &#66DDCCSpirit Catalyst&7 can consume fuel to accelerate the &#CC99FFSpirit Focusing&7 process of the &#66FF99Spirit Crucible&7, and can also hold &e1&7 augment."
		""
		"&7The &#66DDCCSpirit Catalyst&7 has &e1&7 item slot. A &#FFCC44Redstone Comparator&7 can detect how full that slot is."
		""
		"&7Burn time is half the item's burn time. The item is consumed immediately, but burn time is only consumed while Spirit Focusing is in progress, consuming burn time each tick equal to &#FFDD55Fuel Usage Rate&7 * &#FFDD55Focusing Speed&7."
		""
		"&7The &#66DDCCSpirit Catalyst&7 is &e2&7 blocks tall, can only accelerate one nearby &#66FF99Spirit Crucible&7 at a time, and each &#66FF99Spirit Crucible&7 can be accelerated by at most &e8&7 &#66DDCCSpirit Catalysts&7. The effective range is measured from the bottommost block, within &e4&7 blocks."
		""
		"&7Only provides acceleration and augment effects when active (has burn time). Each active &#66DDCCSpirit Catalyst&7 gives +&e50%&7 &#FFDD55Focusing Speed&7 and +&e5%&7 &#FF6666Instability Risk&7."
		""
		"{image:kubejs:textures/gui/malum/spirit_crucible.png width:200 height:110 align:center}"
	]
	quest.1117830BC3A66701.quest_subtitle: "Heating Up"
	quest.1117830BC3A66701.title: "Crucible Acceleration"
	quest.11789A166C0520B4.quest_subtitle: "Familiar Summoning Ritual"
	quest.11BB8D522CF607E6.quest_desc: ["击杀鸡蛇获取，或从战利品中开得，虽然会降低攻速和耐久度，但是能提供不错的攻击向加成"]
	quest.11BB8D522CF607E6.quest_subtitle: "你干嘛哈哈哎呦"
	quest.11C363982673E669.quest_desc: [
		"&7I tried many materials to make a scribing table, and ultimately found that runewood works the most effectively (not really)."
		""
		"&7Can copy scrolls into a spellbook. Scrolls copied in will consume mana to cast and can be reused."
	]
	quest.11C363982673E669.quest_subtitle: "Scribing Spells"
	quest.11C4380FD58A7FDA.quest_desc: [
		"&7When held, grants extra &#66CCFFarmor value&7 based on the material's armor value."
		""
		"&7Armor is determined by &6Silent Gear's&7 &earmor&7 attribute."
		"&7Armor toughness is determined by &6Silent Gear's&7 &earmor toughness&7 attribute."
		"&7Knockback resistance is determined by &6Silent Gear's&7 &eknockback resistance&7 attribute."
	]
	quest.11C4380FD58A7FDA.quest_subtitle: "Offense and Defense"
	quest.11DCB93F9E3E9564.quest_desc: ["&7Makes creatures spawned by the spawner have no behavior (no AI)."]
	quest.11DCB93F9E3E9564.quest_subtitle: "Mass Lobotomy"
	quest.11E9AE8529E6FBF2.quest_subtitle: "Village Hero"
	quest.11FE874E44E98ADF.quest_desc: [
		"&7Each &#66FF99Spirit&7 harvested while worn grants a &e30&7-second &#CC99FFArcane Echo&7 effect."
		""
		"&7If the &#CC99FFArcane Echo&7 effect is already present, instead extend this effect by &e7.5&7 seconds (up to &e1&7 hour) and increase the current effect level by &e1&7 (up to level &e20&7)."
		""
		"&7The duration granted or extended is multiplied by the &#CC99FFArcane Resonance&7 attribute value."
	]
	quest.11FE874E44E98ADF.quest_subtitle: "Gain a Special Effect When Harvesting Spirits"
	quest.12070A3305878F5D.quest_desc: [
		"&6Fluid Tank&r"
		""
		"&6Placement&r"
		"&7When Fluid Tanks are arranged into a rectangular cuboid with a square base of 1*1*n, 2*2*n, or 3*3*n, adjacent tanks automatically merge into a single unit.&r"
		"&7The maximum height n of a tank structure is 32 blocks. Tanks above this height are treated as separate new tanks.&r"
		""
		"&6Storing Fluids&r"
		"&7Can store various fluids. Each block holds 8 B (8000 mB, i.e. 8 buckets). Input and output require a Mechanical Pump.&r"
		"&7In Creative Mode, holding a fluid container (such as a bucket) and right-clicking the tank injects fluid directly. In Survival Mode, you need a Spout combined with other fluid components for input.&r"
		"&7Hold a Wrench and right-click the tank to open or close its observation window for checking the internal fluid status.&r"
		"&7Fluid Tanks can be detected by Comparators, Item Detectors, and Stock Converters. The Item Detector's filter slot can be marked with bucketed or bottled fluids.&r"
		""
		"&6As a Boiler&r"
		"&7When a Steam Whistle or Steam Engine is installed on the surface of a Fluid Tank, the tank structure transforms into a boiler structure. The observation windows disappear and a pressure gauge appears on each side.&r"
		"&7The boiler provides steam to connected Steam Whistles or Steam Engines.&r"
		""
		"&8On this manuscript page, the margin shows a sketch of a stacked tank with a few simple gauges attached to the side. Below it, a line of small text is scrawled: Fill it full, see it clear, and when needed, let it roar.&r"
	]
	quest.1247B36652F553E7.quest_desc: [
		"&7&#FFD700Naturally Spawns&7: Spawns naturally in &#FFD700Sanctuary&7 structures at a low probability;"
		""
		"&7&#AA00AAPhantoms&7 will actively attack &#FFAA33Blazes&7. A &#FFAA33Blaze&7 killed by a &#AA00AAPhantom&7 will always transform into a &#66DDCCSoulless One&7;"
		""
		"&7After a &#66DDCCSoulless One&7 is killed, there is a chance a new &#AA00AAPhantom&7 will spawn in its place (Easy &#FF55550%&7, Normal &#FFAA3316.67%&7, Hard &#FF555525%&7);"
		""
		"&7If a &#AA00AAPhantom&7 approaches a [Corpse-Eating] &#AA00AAgargoyle statue&7, it will immediately transform into a &#66DDCCSoulless One&7"
		""
		"&7Immune to &#FF5555fire damage&7"
		""
		"&7Only performs ranged attacks, does not move during attacks (teleportation is passively triggered);"
		""
		"&7Upon spotting a target, it triggers a teleport and floats upward, fixing itself &#FFAA332~3&7 blocks above the ground of its current cell;"
		""
		"&7Teleport distance is limited to a radius of a few blocks around itself. There is also a low chance to trigger teleportation when the target gets too close / after taking damage;"
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"&7&#FFD700Ranged Attack&7:"
		""
		"&7After a short charge-up, fires a &#66DDCCWill-o'-Wisp Orb&7 that flies slowly but tracks the target's movement and is unaffected by gravity;"
		""
		"&7&#66DDCCWill-o'-Wisp Orb&7 damage can be reduced by armor value;"
		""
		"&7&#66DDCCWill-o'-Wisp Orbs&7 fired by a &#66DDCCSoulless One&7 can coexist in large numbers, and even if that &#66DDCCSoulless One&7 is killed, its &#66DDCCWill-o'-Wisp Orbs&7 will still track the player's movement;"
		""
		"&7&#66DDCCWill-o'-Wisp Orbs&7 disappear immediately upon hitting a block. Please make reasonable use of surrounding walls to restrain/avoid their attack damage."
		""
		"&7When a &#66DDCCSoulless One&7 touches water (fluid), is exposed to rainy weather, or is hit by a splash/lingering water bottle:"
		""
		"&7It will immediately transform into a &#FFAA33Blaze&7 and gain 10 seconds of &#AA00AANausea&7, 5 seconds of &#AA00AAWeakness II&7, and 5 seconds of &#AA00AASlowness III&7."
	]
	quest.1247B36652F553E7.quest_subtitle: "Utterly Soulless"
	quest.1247B36652F553E7.title: "Observation: Soulless One"
	quest.124A3DCF1B3DA894.quest_subtitle: "法力之子"
	quest.124EF6C94011C149.quest_desc: [
		"&6Strange Mushroom&r"
		"&7Right-click on a tamed familiar to grant it 1 stack of the '&cRage&r&7' effect (when attacked, there is a chance to consume 1 stack of '&cRage&r&7' to gain the '&cHeart-Stop Technique&r&7' status for several seconds). Each familiar can stack up to 10 layers. Dropped by &eMooshrooms&r&7 and sheared &eSwamp Villagers&r&7.&r"
	]
	quest.12C9785ECF565304.quest_desc: [
		"Can be summoned via the Altar"
		""
		"&7Special drops mainly include: Slime Staff, Shield of Cthulhu."
		""
		"&7The Shield of Cthulhu provides some horizontal mobility, but its practicality in actual combat varies from person to person."
		""
		"&7Has a small chance to drop a random Seven Deadly Sins trinket."
	]
	quest.12C9785ECF565304.quest_subtitle: "Stage 0"
	quest.131FF32C0FF28CA8.quest_desc: [
		"Found in its corresponding structure; crafting the &eHomeward Compass&r points you to the nearest Tomb of the King of the Dead; can also be summoned via the Altar"
		""
		"Defeat it—boiling deathly authority gathered into a scepter, that inert heart a specimen of time's end drawn out of nothingness... Defeat it, and the world's &#66CCFFmagic minerals&7 shall be freed."
		""
		"&7Defeating the &#FF6666King of the Dead&7 unlocks the following ores:  "
		"&7&#67B1E5Gober&7  "
		"&7&#757369Rune Fragments&7"
	]
	quest.131FF32C0FF28CA8.quest_subtitle: "Stage 0 - kill to unlock Stage 1"
	quest.1350642D5141B3BF.quest_desc: [
		"&6Eye of Seeking&r"
		"&7Can be used to locate the structures where &6Bosses&r&7 reside within the Starlight Dimension."
		""
		"&7Before starting: You need to hold one of the following specific items in your off-hand, which will determine the structure the Eye of Seeking will search for afterward."
		""
		"&6Cursed Garden&r&7 (&cMoonvine Colossus&r&7):"
		"&8Vines, Cave Moss, Moonlight Berries&r"
		"&8Red Crystal Roots, Blue Crystal Roots&r"
		"&8Ground Red Crystal Moss, Ground Blue Crystal Moss&r"
		""
		"&6Golem Forge&r&7 (&cStarlight Golem&r&7):"
		"&8Redstone Dust, Golem Steel Ingots, Oxidized Golem Steel Ingots&r"
		""
		"&7The Eye of Seeking works on the same logic as the Eye of Ender."
		"&7After right-clicking to use, it flies a certain distance toward the structure where the &6Boss&r&7 resides, then hovers in the air and turns into a dropped item after a period of time."
		"&7Similarly, the Eye of Seeking also has a chance to &cshatter&r&7 while hovering (directly consumed without being returned)."
	]
	quest.1350642D5141B3BF.quest_subtitle: "Starlight's Guidance"
	quest.13AFD3688361872A.quest_desc: [
		"# &aGame Modifications &r"
		""
		"### &eIce and Fire Tweaks &r"
		"&7- &fPixies no longer steal player items&a, safe to keep around &r"
		""
		"### &#FFBB1AKeep-Inventory-on-Death Tweaks &r"
		"&7- &fIf keep-inventory is not enabled, respawning no longer restores you to perfect condition, and death preserves your hotbar items and equipment&r"
		""
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"### &#FF9F9AItem Tooltip Tweaks&r"
		"&7- &fIf an item's tooltip is too long, use the scroll wheel to scroll up and down &r"
		""
		"### &#FF91EESign Tweaks&r"
		"&7- &fSigns attached to things like chests can be edited by sneaking; clicking normally passes through the sign to the container's items &r"
		""
		"### &#C9FF74Entity Cleanup System &r"
		"&7- Config file path: &9kubejs/server_scripts/entity_clean.js &r  "
		"&7- &fThe modpack includes an &6automatic cleanup system (disabled by default)&f, configurable in this file:  "
		"  &7▪ &fWhat to clean  "
		"  &7▪ &fOn/off state &r  "
		"&7- &fFor manual cleanup, use the command: &b/rf entityclean &r"
	]
	quest.13AFD3688361872A.quest_subtitle: "Gameplay Experience Changes"
	quest.13AFD3688361872A.title: "Some Changes"
	quest.13C22895EB17EE88.quest_desc: [
		"&6Spout&r"
		""
		"&7A device dedicated to performing \"filling\" processing. It can accomplish the following:&r"
		"&7Fill container-type items with fluids (such as buckets, glass bottles); also works for most modded fluids;&r"
		"&7Execute special filling recipes provided by the Create mod (such as wetting grass blocks, making Blaze Cakes, etc.).&r"
		""
		"&6Usage Requirements&r"
		"&7Fluid must be supplied to the Spout through fluid pipes or other fluid components. You cannot fill it manually with a bucket.&r"
		"&7It can process items on the conveyor belt or depot below. When a processable item enters its work range, it plays a filling animation and consumes the corresponding amount of fluid. Each filling process takes 21 game ticks (1.05 seconds).&r"
		"&7When the Spout has no fluid or insufficient fluid, it stops processable items on the conveyor belt until fluid is replenished.&r"
		""
		"&8It has to drink its fill before it can feed those below.&r"
	]
	quest.13C542FCBB189AEA.quest_subtitle: "Nameless Traveler"
	quest.13CCBB1FAF6834F4.quest_desc: [
		"There are two kinds of obelisks, with different functions"
		"&6Runewood Obelisk"
		""
		"&7When placed near a &#CC99FFSpirit Altar&7 (within &e4&7 blocks horizontally and &e3&7 blocks vertically), each &#FFAA33Runewood Obelisk&7 speeds up &#CC99FFSpirit Infusion&7 by &e25%&7. It can accelerate multiple &#CC99FFSpirit Altars&7 simultaneously, and each &#CC99FFSpirit Altar&7 can benefit from at most &e4&7 obelisks."
		""
		"&7This block occupies &e2&7 blocks; only the lower half provides acceleration."
		""
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"&7Spirit Infusion is growing ever more necessary and ever more tedious—even making a batch of Hex Ash takes several minutes."
		""
		"&7The method of acceleration lies within &6Hallowed Gold&r&7. Place up to four obelisks made from it around the altar, and each one speeds up the process by &aone quarter&r&7."
		""
		"A technology that can dramatically accelerate Spirit Infusion, thoroughly implementing the philosophy of \"faster is better\""
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"&6Experience Crystal Obelisk"
		""
		"&7When placed, each &#66DDCCExperience Crystal Obelisk&7 provides &e5&7 enchanting levels (a bookshelf provides &e1&7). Placing just &e3&7 around an Enchanting Table allows for &e30&7-level enchanting."
		"&7This block occupies &e2&7 blocks; only the lower half provides enchanting levels."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"&7Unlike the &#FFAA33Runewood Obelisk&7, the &#66DDCCExperience Crystal Obelisk&7 cannot accelerate &#CC99FFSpirit Infusion&7."
		"&7Although it is not of much use to the infusion process itself, the obelisk's construction can be put to further use."
		""
		"&7Replace the Hallowed Gold with &eExperience Crystal&r&7, and the obelisk harmonizes with the intellect of enchanting, providing a large amount of enchanting power."
		"&7A single such obelisk is equivalent to &bfive bookshelves&r&7."
	]
	quest.13CCBB1FAF6834F4.quest_subtitle: "Obelisk"
	quest.13CCBB1FAF6834F4.title: "Altar Acceleration"
	quest.13CDF0A883DC5AE7.quest_desc: ["In the End, some Eternal Gates will spawn naturally"]
	quest.13CDF0A883DC5AE7.quest_subtitle: "The End seems to have become unstable"
	quest.13CDF0A883DC5AE7.title: "Head to the End"
	quest.13DF171E70CF449D.quest_desc: [
		"&oBy wind, or by water, or even the most primitive manpower—in any case, it began to turn."
		"&r"
		"Connect the gears, let them spin and collide, transmit stress, and play a symphony—so the manuscript says."
		""
		"All my doubts can be resolved by &6pressing [W] to ponder&r. I believe the road ahead is clear."
		""
		"&8Still, any windmill with wool spins without wind. Is this also a machinist's wisdom?&r"
	]
	quest.13DF171E70CF449D.quest_subtitle: "And then the gears began to turn..."
	quest.13DF171E70CF449D.title: "First Turn of the Gears"
	quest.13FB94D18517171F.quest_desc: [
		"&6Basin&r"
		""
		"&7It is the most tolerant container in a machinist's workshop, patiently holding various items and fluids, waiting for them to transform according to established recipes.&r"
		""
		"&6Internal Order&r"
		"&7The Basin has 18 item slots: the first 9 receive ingredients, the last 9 store finished products. Each item can stack up to one group (64).&r"
		"&7It also has 4 fluid slots. Each fluid holds up to &c1000 mB&7, with a total of no more than &c4000 mB&7. At no time does a single fluid exceed the 1000 mB limit.&r"
		"&7Items and fluids coexist peacefully here without interfering with each other. Even lava and water can coexist safely—they do not interact inside the Basin.&r"
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"&6Input and Output Rules&r"
		"&7All six faces can accept or output items, but any automated input can only insert &c1 to 16&7 items at a time. The exception is items entering as dropped entities, which can fill a full stack of 64 at once.&r"
		"&7Mechanical Arms, Brass Funnels, and similar components can also only input 16 at most, and Brass Funnels cannot set a specific quantity.&r"
		"&7Output is much more lenient: Andesite Funnels output 1 at a time, while Brass Funnels and Mechanical Arms can output 1 to 64 according to configuration. Conveyor Belts and Spouts can also serve as input ends, letting items slide into the basin from the edge.&r"
		"&7Fluids must be transferred through Mechanical Pumps or pipes connected to them. Pumping in prioritizes filling input slots; pumping out prioritizes extracting from output slots. If output slots are empty and there is space, it will extract fluid from input slots—pay special attention to this to avoid confusing recipes.&r"
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"&6Filtering and Guiding&r"
		"&7The Basin has a filter slot on its side. Placing a single item, a &eFilter&7, or an &eAttribute Filter&7 specifies that it only produces the marked output (fluids can be marked with bottled samples).&r"
		"&7When the side is unobstructed and there is an open container diagonally below, the Basin automatically generates an &eoutput faucet/opening&7 and attempts to send products out. This faucet has a hidden output slot—as long as there is an item in it, the Basin stops working. This is a common cause of production lines mysteriously jamming.&r"
		"&7The faucet holds only one recipe's output at a time. If a recipe produces multiple items, the first enters the faucet slot and the rest go into the Basin's output slots. Use a &eWrench&7 to adjust the faucet's position or turn it off. As long as the block diagonally below does not update, the faucet will not reappear.&r"
		"&7Blocks recognized as automatic output containers include: Basins, Depots, Conveyor Belts, Funnels, Crushing Wheels, and most other Create components—but vanilla Hoppers are not included.&r"
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"&6Recipe Processing Order&r"
		"&7When working with devices such as the &eMechanical Press&7 or &eMechanical Mixer&7, the Basin processes recipes in the following order:&r"
		"&7If input slots have processable recipes: it processes pure-item recipes first, then item-and-fluid mixed recipes, and finally pure-fluid recipes.&r"
		"&7If input slots have no recipes: it prioritizes recipes across all item slots, then item-and-fluid mixtures, and finally pure fluids.&r"
		""
		"&7Other details: identical items stack into existing slots as much as possible rather than occupying new slots. If all 9 output slots are full, all processing stops.&r"
		""
		"&8There is a dark stain at the edge of the page, as if someone pressed an oil-covered thumb here.&r"
	]
	quest.13FB94D18517171F.quest_subtitle: "A small square container, yet the core of the entire factory"
	quest.142C80D05D6B1FDC.quest_subtitle: "Clear all difficulty settings you have adjusted"
	quest.1430F9DAB7F87A6E.quest_desc: [
		"&7The base material for crafting all upgrade orbs. Considering the high cost, it's actually not recommended to craft this in the early game."
		""
		"&7Upgrade orbs can be applied to armor/spellbooks using the Arcane Anvil. Note that orbs are difficult to recover once applied, so think twice before applying an orb."
	]
	quest.143A6CDB76F7A3DC.quest_desc: [
		"Naturally spawns in its exclusive underground arena; after victory, Sulfuric Honey can be used to reset it, and it can also be summoned via the Altar"
		""
		"&7Special drops mainly include: Void Thorn, Crystal Fruit, Miracle Fruit, Nova Forbidden Fruit."
		""
		"&7The Nova Forbidden Fruit can be used to unlock the Nova Voice EGO."
		""
		"&7Has a small chance to drop a random Seven Deadly Sins trinket."
	]
	quest.143A6CDB76F7A3DC.quest_subtitle: "Stage 0"
	quest.1444AD82BC8B46CF.quest_desc: [
		"&7When the wearer attacks a creature with health greater than &e98.75%&7, &e2&7 &#88DDFFSoul Breath Voids&7 are produced. Similar to &#66FF99Spirits&7, they fly toward the wearer, and harvesting them triggers the effects of harvesting &#66FF99Spirits&7 (does not generate &#66FF99Spirits&7, only triggers the effects). This effect can trigger at most &e1&7 time every &e5&7 seconds."
		""
		"&7If the target is a player, the number of &#88DDFFSoul Breath Voids&7 produced is &e5&7."
	]
	quest.1444AD82BC8B46CF.quest_subtitle: "Faster Buff Acquisition"
	quest.1448882981E09E31.quest_desc: ["&7敌人越多，伤害加成便愈发恐怖。高额攻击属性加持之下，清场效率随敌群规模攀升，是应对围攻局势的利器"]
	quest.1448882981E09E31.quest_subtitle: "天体力量"
	quest.147DBFF8D9EC5476.quest_desc: ["&7You can pre-load &#FFD700arrows&7 before firing."]
	quest.147DBFF8D9EC5476.quest_subtitle: "Illager's Favorite"
	quest.14D4101B90CF5417.quest_subtitle: "Time to take a break, huh?"
	quest.14D4101B90CF5417.title: "Play for One Hour"
	quest.14F646FF9C81DCA0.quest_desc: [
		"&6Poison Spider Fang&r"
		"&7Used to craft &cToxic Reagent&r&7 and to heal &cPlague Doctor&r&7 familiars. Dropped by &cCave Spiders&r&7.&r"
	]
	quest.14F646FF9C81DCA0.quest_subtitle: "Deadly Poison"
	quest.15161B10C01BAD98.quest_subtitle: "Tier 5 Grading Catalyst"
	quest.153B8C23F5FF23C5.quest_desc: ["Increases the wireless access point's transmission distance to infinite blocks, and enables cross-dimensional transmission"]
	quest.153B8C23F5FF23C5.quest_subtitle: "Dimensional Transmission"
	quest.15420045F7ABF5AD.quest_desc: [
		"Through &bInfusion&r upgrading, the Nether Bookshelf gains even more powerful magic, providing higher &aTier&r and &4Quantization&r."
		"&l(Recommended Bookshelf)&r"
	]
	quest.15420045F7ABF5AD.quest_subtitle: "Better Quantization and Tier"
	quest.15420045F7ABF5AD.title: "Disordered Magic Enhancement"
	quest.159E4C31CF4AB181.quest_desc: [
		"&6Oath of the Undiscerned Maw&r"
		""
		"&7The essence devoured comes from malice, and thus craves corrosion.&r"
		"&7-Abuse slowly decays all &chealing received&r"
		""
		"&7An etching carved into the malice soul-return.&r"
		"&7-&6Malice Critical&r&7 will &8devour&r&7 the &8life essence&r&7 of affected creatures"
		"&7-&8Devoured&r&7 essence &aheals&r&7 you according to the damage dealt&r"
		"{image:kubejs:textures/gui/malum/oath_of_the_undiscerned_maw.png width:160 height:200 align:center}"
	]
	quest.159E4C31CF4AB181.quest_subtitle: "Devouring All Things"
	quest.159E4C31CF4AB181.title: "Oath of the Undiscerned Maw"
	quest.15DC053FF5BA0E9B.quest_subtitle: "Has both armor and a small amount of spell attributes—very popular"
	quest.15DDBCE29F4CEB4B.quest_subtitle: "A crafting material, mainly used to craft some advanced machines and smart components."
	quest.15DDE00E526D43A1.quest_subtitle: "举头望明月"
	quest.1618DB9594EF15C3.quest_subtitle: "How lonely it is to be invincible"
	quest.161C42E6B708C7DA.quest_subtitle: "后面再更新这里的...苦露西"
	quest.1633AD29D81FB414.quest_desc: [
		"&aTier&7 is just a tiny, tiny, tiny bit higher than vanilla bookshelves... Blocks of different Tier levels placed near the Enchanting Table stack from low to high. For example, 15 normal bookshelves can stack 30 Tier; placing ten amethysts then adds +10 Tier to reach 40. This also holds true for other bookshelves."
		""
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"&7In the mines, a geode radiating magic attracted you"
		"&7You discovered this thriving crystal cluster. It emits a faint yet somewhat powerful magic—at least better than the current bookshelves. You carefully brought it back and placed it beside the Enchanting Table. You found the Enchanting Table's magic had increased somewhat, and its enchantment instability had also decreased slightly. But this small amount is still too little. You wonder if there could be a more powerful version."
	]
	quest.1633AD29D81FB414.quest_subtitle: "Mysterious Crystal"
	quest.1633AD29D81FB414.title: "Nature's Magic Stabilizer"
	quest.1669DD338D104D3F.quest_desc: ["I can't believe my little raggedy pack actually attracted an art teacher! Even helped with rendering code—that's amazing..."]
	quest.1669DD338D104D3F.quest_subtitle: "Art + Some Code"
	quest.1675C48578D2D979.quest_desc: ["&7&#FF6666Wither Skeleton Skulls&7 and &#FF6666Skeleton Skulls&7 have both been given crafting recipes. When you want to fight the &#FF6666Wither&7 but have no skulls, you can just craft them directly instead of chasing &#FF6666Wither Skeletons&7 around chopping endlessly..."]
	quest.1675C48578D2D979.quest_subtitle: "Doo da doo da doo"
	quest.1684A811A37D8C86.quest_desc: ["Some materials being listed under Stage 2 doesn't necessarily mean you can only obtain them after the King of the Dead; it just means their stats fall into the T2 category"]
	quest.1684A811A37D8C86.quest_subtitle: "Before defeating the King of the Dead"
	quest.16FD71D5EBCE3C6A.quest_desc: [
		"&6Train Controls&r"
		""
		"&7This is the \"helm\" of a train structure, allowing the driver—or other creatures—to control the movement of the entire mechanical contraption.&r"
		""
		"&6Installation&r"
		"&7Each train structure must contain at least one set of Train Controls, firmly glued to the structure when assembling the train.&r"
		"&7To let a creature drive in your place, place a &eSeat&7 or &eBlaze Burner&7 directly in front of the Train Controls.&r"
		"&7If you want the train to travel in both directions, install one set of Train Controls at each end of the structure.&r"
		""
		"&6Controls&r"
		"&7After assembly, two control levers appear on the Train Controls. Right-click to enter control mode.&r"
		"&7At this point, use the movement keys (WASD) to control the train. The speed bar in the interface shows the current speed in real time. The speed bar has 18 segments divided into five stages.&r"
		"&7The train automatically slows down when turning.&r"
		"&7Coal can be stored on the train to increase travel speed; fuel is consumed over time.&r"
		"&7Scroll the mouse wheel to adjust the speed limit, which is visually shown by the position of a brass slider.&r"
		"&7The arrow above the speed bar indicates the train's forward direction relative to your view.&r"
		"&7If the train has a whistle installed, press the sprint key (default Ctrl) to sound it.&r"
		""
		"&8The corner of this page is folded up. On it, a simple sketch of Train Controls is drawn in charcoal, with a scrawled note beside it: Hold tight, watch the road, remember to bring coal.&r"
	]
	quest.17695E30CD9EB522.quest_subtitle: "Surely no one would die 100+ times just for this quest's reward, right?"
	quest.176BAFF834F6F888.quest_desc: ["&7The resulting impact is: the Nether ceiling is raised to &#FFAA33192 blocks&7, and the bottom of the lava sea extends downward by &#FFAA3332 blocks&7."]
	quest.176BAFF834F6F888.quest_subtitle: "A vanilla-style Nether expansion mod"
	quest.176BAFF834F6F888.title: "Jaden's Nether Expansion"
	quest.178BC08D4F2D3809.quest_desc: ["&7“陷入思考”是强而有力的控制手段，虽材料负面效果不少，但作为提升魔法伤害的路径而言，性价比依然可观。控制与增伤兼得"]
	quest.178BC08D4F2D3809.quest_subtitle: "1+1=？"
	quest.17B9D8741CF45918.quest_desc: [
		"&7While researching enchanting, I discovered some strange bookshelves."
		""
		"&7Stone Bookshelves and Melon Bookshelves can be used to suppress untimely &5Arcana&7 and &cQuantization&7, creating conditions for &eInfusion&7."
		""
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"&7The Stone Bookshelf was an item born simultaneously in that accident. Unlike the unremarkable bookshelf made from deepslate, this bookshelf made from more common stone displays a repulsion toward enchantment. Perhaps because andesite is too deeply entangled with machinery, this bookshelf instead reduces both &aTier&7 and &5Arcana&7 attributes. The certainty of technology here denies the mystery of magic—even though magic does exist in this world."
		""
		"&7The Melon Bookshelf was a laughable accident. While harvesting melons, I temporarily piled them on top of a bookshelf. When I was about to move the melons to the warehouse, I found the bookshelf's enchanting power had been suppressed. So I continued researching, and finally, on a whim, I gold-plated the melons and made them into a bookshelf. Perhaps it's related to eating melons in hot weather—this bookshelf reduces &aTier&7 while also suppressing the effects of &cQuantization&7. Whether this absurd reason is truly the cause, or whether the demonic power was partly bribed by melons, I cannot say."
	]
	quest.17B9D8741CF45918.quest_subtitle: "Ability Suppression"
	quest.17B9D8741CF45918.title: "The Strangest Bookshelf"
	quest.17C284A1B07922A4.quest_subtitle: "Lord of Ender"
	quest.17CD8FFD1387207D.quest_desc: [
		"&7Besides finding naturally spawning bosses, you can also use Spirit Calamity's Spirit Altar to summon bosses yourself. For specific summoning recipes, check JEI."
		""
		"&7Search directly for the boss name. If there is a spawn egg named \"&eSpawn: ****&7\" and it is labeled \"&eImmediately summons the associated creature when in the world&7\", that means it can be summoned manually. Click this spawn egg to view the summoning recipe."
		""
		"&cPlease note that, as the label says, this ritual is a summoning ritual and will immediately spawn the boss upon completion, so please summon in an open area."
		""
		"{image:kubejs:textures/gui/spawn.png width:150 height:130 align:center}"
	]
	quest.17CD8FFD1387207D.quest_subtitle: "At your age, at your stage, how can you sleep?"
	quest.17CD8FFD1387207D.title: "Repeated Killing"
	quest.17DE5C30E0CA8765.quest_desc: [
		"# &bPerformance Optimization Recommendations &r"
		""
		"### &e Video Settings Suggestions &r"
		"&b▸ &6Render Distance: &r&l8&r  "
		"&b▸ &6Max Shadow Distance: &r&l6&r  "
		"&b▸ &6Simulation Distance: &r&l6&r  "
		"&b▸ &6VSync: &r&cOff&r  "
		"&b▸ &6Max Framerate: &r&aUnlimited&r  "
		"&b▸ &6Entity Render Distance: &r&975%&r  "
		""
		"&7Keep other settings at default~  "
		""
		"### &3Notes &r"
		"&7- Fine-tune values based on your device's performance  "
		"&7- Lower render distance if you experience stuttering  "
	]
	quest.17DE5C30E0CA8765.quest_subtitle: "Huh? The optimization isn't as good as expected?"
	quest.182289427E06D427.quest_desc: ["&7A light, compact weapon with slightly lower damage and attack range, but very high &#FFAA33attack speed&7. On hit, it &#66CCFFreduces the target's invincibility frame time&7."]
	quest.182289427E06D427.quest_subtitle: "Small is also cute"
	quest.182321BDA643635C.quest_desc: ["如今存储网络的访问效率已难以满足我的需求，我需要寻求更快的数据读写方案。"]
	quest.182321BDA643635C.quest_subtitle: "更快，更好，更强！"
	quest.188CFA97BB5A32C2.quest_desc: ["&7A base trinket used only to increase &FF8844armor value&7 by a small amount. A necessary prerequisite for crafting its higher-tier material variants."]
	quest.188CFA97BB5A32C2.quest_subtitle: "Trinket Base"
	quest.18AC27B34367E1DD.quest_desc: ["&7Performs area mining in a &#FFAA333×3×1&7 area."]
	quest.18AC27B34367E1DD.quest_subtitle: "Tunnel Digger"
	quest.18B62DD6017843BC.quest_desc: ["{\"text\":\"\",\"extra\":[{\"text\":\"I know you might get a headache seeing this mod's \",\"color\":\"gray\"},{\"text\":\"eyes\",\"color\":\"red\"},{\"text\":\", but now they can all be \",\"color\":\"gray\"},{\"text\":\"crafted\",\"color\":\"green\"},{\"text\":\".\",\"color\":\"gray\"}]}"]
	quest.18B62DD6017843BC.quest_subtitle: "Craftable"
	quest.18C5ACA6F816EDCB.quest_desc: [
		"&6Miniature Shield&r"
		"&7Right-click on a tamed familiar to give it a low chance to &ablock&r&7 attacks. Each familiar can only use 1. Obtained through the &eShrinker&r&7.&r"
	]
	quest.18D4FAD08F8837FD.quest_desc: [
		"&6Pandora's Box&r"
		"&7Allows up to 10 familiars to be &asummoned/dismissed&r&7 at the same time (obtained by crafting).&r"
	]
	quest.18D4FAD08F8837FD.quest_subtitle: "You opened Pandora's Box..."
	quest.190BDB7675C3DDE6.quest_desc: [
		"&7Provides &#55D5D5Soul Ward capacity&7 based on &#66CCFFmagic armor&7."
		"&7Provides &#55D5D5Soul Ward recovery rate&7 based on &#66CCFFcharge value&7."
		"&7Provides &#55D5D5Soul Ward integrity&7 based on &#66CCFFmagic armor&7 and &#66CCFFcharge value&7."
		"&7Can obtain &#55D5D5pact cap&7 based on materials."
		"&7Can obtain &cknockback resistance&7 based on materials."
	]
	quest.190BDB7675C3DDE6.quest_subtitle: "A Good Partner for Soul Armor"
	quest.190BDB7675C3DDE6.title: "Soul Hunter Leggings Template"
	quest.192F6B22F5E521FF.quest_desc: [
		"&7At least there's a place to sleep now..."
		""
		"&7The modpack has changed &#66CCFFPhantom&7 spawning. Players who don't sleep for a long time will no longer spawn &#66CCFFPhantoms&7. Instead, &#FFD700sleeping continuously will spawn Phantoms&7, serving as a &#FF6666punishment&7 for skipping the night."
		"&7&mThen if I just keep sleeping, they'll never spawn&r"
		""
		"&7This change may make naturally spawning &#66CCFFPhantoms&7 rare. If you need &#66CCFFPhantom&7 drops, look for structures containing &#66CCFFPhantom&7 spawners."
	]
	quest.192F6B22F5E521FF.quest_subtitle: "Actually, you can also use the sky as your blanket and the ground as your bed"
	quest.192F6B22F5E521FF.title: "Establish a Base"
	quest.193E18AC43275A46.quest_desc: [
		"&7Food. Restores &#FFAA339&7 hunger points and &#FFAA3314.5&7 saturation after eating;"
		""
		"&7Also grants 3 seconds of &#AA00AAWeakness I&7;"
		""
		"&7Can be used to \"tame\" the &#AA00AAStomp Beast&7."
	]
	quest.193E18AC43275A46.quest_subtitle: "Tastes like bone, nice and crunchy!"
	quest.194FFC9454CBCBA2.quest_desc: [
		"{\"text\":\"\",\"extra\":[{\"text\":\"Basic Attributes\",\"color\":\"gold\"}]}"
		"{\"text\":\"\",\"extra\":[{\"text\":\"Pigment\",\"color\":\"aqua\"},{\"text\":\" is an item used to color equipment parts.\",\"color\":\"gray\"}]}"
		""
		"{\"text\":\"\",\"extra\":[{\"text\":\"Color Mixing Logic\",\"color\":\"gold\"}]}"
		"{\"text\":\"\",\"extra\":[{\"text\":\"When mixing items of multiple colors, the final pigment color is the \",\"color\":\"gray\"},{\"text\":\"mixed color\",\"color\":\"light_purple\"},{\"text\":\" of the input colors (following pigment mixing principles, similar to color mixing in art).\",\"color\":\"gray\"}]}"
		""
		"{\"text\":\"\",\"extra\":[{\"text\":\"Coloring Equipment\",\"color\":\"gold\"}]}"
		"{\"text\":\"\",\"extra\":[{\"text\":\"Silent Gear can be colored in the following three ways:\",\"color\":\"gray\"}]}"
		"{\"text\":\"\",\"extra\":[{\"text\":\"Craft Silent Gear together with pigment or dye\",\"color\":\"gray\"},{\"text\":\"→\",\"color\":\"yellow\"},{\"text\":\"Only colors the equipment's main part\",\"color\":\"green\"}]}"
		"{\"text\":\"\",\"extra\":[{\"text\":\"Craft Silent Gear together with an Equipment Adjustment Part + pigment/dye\",\"color\":\"gray\"},{\"text\":\"→\",\"color\":\"yellow\"},{\"text\":\"Colors the part specified by the Equipment Adjustment Part\",\"color\":\"aqua\"}]}"
		"{\"text\":\"\",\"extra\":[{\"text\":\"Craft the part item together with pigment/dye\",\"color\":\"gray\"},{\"text\":\"→\",\"color\":\"yellow\"},{\"text\":\"The part is colored, and equipment crafted with that part afterward inherits the color\",\"color\":\"green\"}]}"
	]
	quest.194FFC9454CBCBA2.quest_subtitle: "Color Philosopher"
	quest.1954C7719D379871.quest_desc: [
		"&6Warding Device&r"
		""
		"&7Drawing on the multi-phase stacking nature of Soulstained Steel, the Warding Device has a chance to completely absorb durability loss taken by the &eCatalyst Charm&r&7, while slightly stabilizing the &aFocusing Process&r&7. However, it does slow down focusing speed.&r"
	]
	quest.1954C7719D379871.quest_subtitle: "Facing the Storm"
	quest.1A4259700BD803E8.quest_desc: [
		"&6Andesite Funnel&r"
		""
		"&6Funnels and Dropped Items&r"
		"&7When attached to a container, the Andesite Funnel defaults to output mode, pushing items out from the front as dropped entities. Switched to input mode, it rapidly absorbs all dropped items in its cell with no speed limit. Right-click with a Wrench to switch modes.&r"
		"&7In input mode, hold an item and right-click the front of the funnel to deposit the item directly into its connected container.&r"
		"&7As with common designs, a redstone signal can lock the Andesite Funnel, stopping its work.&r"
		""
		"&7The Andesite Funnel can be installed above or below a container. When outputting upward, items are ejected with some inertia. If not collected in time, dropped items pile up above the funnel. Using this trait, you can achieve &avertical upward item transport&r.&r"
		""
		"&6About Vertical Orientation&r"
		"&7When the funnel opening faces straight up or down, it cannot be used directly as a vertical transport pipe. For pure vertical conveyance, use Chutes or vanilla Hoppers.&r"
		""
		"&6Funnel and Work Block Interface&r"
		"&7When the Andesite Funnel is attached to the side of a block and a specific work block exists directly below it, it exchanges items directly with that block. Using a Wrench to switch modes at this point changes its appearance to an '&eAndesite Funnel Belt&r'.&r"
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"&7Blocks it can interface with directly include: &eDepot&r, &eEjector&r, &eConveyor Belt&r, &eSpout&r, &eMechanical Saw&r (only when facing up), &eTrain Station&r.&r"
		""
		"&7If you place an Andesite Funnel on a Conveyor Belt with its opening aligned with the belt's direction of travel, it enters tunnel mode. In this mode, item input or output is entirely determined by the belt's transport direction.&r"
		"&7Tunnel-mode funnels default to a retracted form. Use a Wrench to switch them to an extended form. Extended funnels cover part of the belt below and can be used for decoration; their collision box also changes accordingly.&r"
		""
		"&8A note in the manuscript margin: It's flexible, but don't expect it to break the basic rules.&r"
	]
	quest.1A58667FA2440598.quest_desc: [
		"&7Preface: This modpack's key quest descriptions are in the &#FFD700side quests&7, not the &#FF85CBmain questline&7. The main questline only serves to &#FF85CBdrive progression&7!!!!!"
		""
		"&7Preface: This modpack's key quest descriptions are in the &#FFD700side quests&7, not the &#FF85CBmain questline&7. The main questline only serves to &#FF85CBdrive progression&7!!!!!"
		""
		"&7Preface: This modpack's key quest descriptions are in the &#FFD700side quests&7, not the &#FF85CBmain questline&7. The main questline only serves to &#FF85CBdrive progression&7!!!!!"
	]
	quest.1A58667FA2440598.quest_subtitle: "Pack Your Bag"
	quest.1A58667FA2440598.title: "Wilderness Pioneering"
	quest.1A8CEE0746A74FC4.quest_desc: [
		"Found in the Cursed Garden structure in the Starlight Dimension; can also be summoned via the Altar"
		""
		"&7Special drops mainly include: Crescent Moon Pendant, Soul Dew, Moonvine series weapons, Nova Voice."
		""
		"&7Attaching the Crescent Moon Pendant to a chestpiece provides considerable bonuses."
		""
		"&7Has a small chance to drop a random Seven Deadly Sins trinket."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"&7Passive abilities"
		""
		"&7Damage reduction: while not on fire, all attack damage taken by the Lunar Monstrosity is &cforcibly reduced to 1 point&7;"
		""
		"&7Phase 2"
		""
		"&7When its health drops to ≤ 50%, the Lunar Monstrosity plays a phase-transition animation: the eye at the center of the flower turns into a mouth full of fangs and roars loudly;"
		""
		"&7During the phase-transition animation, the Lunar Monstrosity is not immune to attack damage and will not use any moves; after entering Phase 2, it unlocks new moves, while its original moves can still be used during Phase 2."
	]
	quest.1A8CEE0746A74FC4.quest_subtitle: "Stage 1"
	quest.1AA4DC70AD282F2B.quest_desc: [
		"&6Impurity Stabilizer&r"
		""
		"&7&8Malicious Spirits&r&7 actively approach the weak and vulnerable, craving slaughter. The Impurity Stabilizer exploits this trait, providing a large &apercentage tuning bonus&r&7 to the crucible's weakest attribute, excluding Fuel Usage Rate and Instability Risk. However, this does have side effects, adding a slight burden to the standard &eTuning Process&r&7.&r"
	]
	quest.1AA4DC70AD282F2B.quest_subtitle: "Strength from Weakness"
	quest.1AA82BAE61749007.quest_desc: [
		"&6Rune of Slaughter&r"
		""
		"&7The Rune of Slaughter urges the mind to pursue destruction, and increases the wearer's &eScythe Proficiency&r&7 against wounded targets. The rune seems to take effect on targets at or below half health, increasing scythe damage dealt to them by roughly two fifths.&r"
	]
	quest.1AA82BAE61749007.quest_subtitle: "A Pulse That Spurs Destruction"
	quest.1AB5165BCAD5820E.quest_desc: [
		"&6Rune of Blazing Intensity&r"
		""
		"&7The Rune of Blazing Intensity urges the mind to share its radiance with surrounding things, without considering the consequences; it doubles the &efire damage&r&7 dealt by the wearer.&r"
	]
	quest.1AB5165BCAD5820E.quest_subtitle: "A Pulse That Spurs Burning"
	quest.1ACA39ABEB90A9F5.quest_desc: [
		"&7Right-click to throw a &#66CCFFboomerang&7 at enemies. Good thing it won't hit yourself."
		"&7Damage is dynamically determined by &6Silent Gear's&7 &eattack power&7 attribute."
		"&7Flight speed is dynamically determined by &6Silent Gear's&7 &eattack speed&7 attribute. &cHigher attack speed means faster speed&7."
		"&7Each throw or hit consumes &c1&7 durability."
	]
	quest.1ACA39ABEB90A9F5.quest_subtitle: "Watch Your Eyes!"
	quest.1AF5C4332908323D.quest_desc: ["&7词缀与属性俱为顶级，提供扎实的面板数值与可观增伤。击败骷髅王后方可入手，是构筑中极具分量的核心组件，可与戈伯锭形成强力连携"]
	quest.1AF5C4332908323D.quest_subtitle: "愿您的旅途充满诅咒与祝福"
	quest.1B66EC1641E0B30A.quest_desc: ["{\"text\":\"\",\"extra\":[{\"text\":\"I know you might get a headache seeing this mod's \",\"color\":\"gray\"},{\"text\":\"eyes\",\"color\":\"red\"},{\"text\":\", but now they can all be \",\"color\":\"gray\"},{\"text\":\"crafted\",\"color\":\"green\"},{\"text\":\".\",\"color\":\"gray\"}]}"]
	quest.1B66EC1641E0B30A.quest_subtitle: "Craftable"
	quest.1B819E833413B729.title: "Eerie Ghoul"
	quest.1BD8D56B55550058.quest_desc: [
		"&6Pact of the Reaper"
		"&7Breaking the bond means falling into &cperil&r&7.&r&cWeapons not permitted by the Oath deal one tenth damage&r&cWeapons not permitted by the Oath rapidly break when used"
		"&7The soul signs a pact with the scythe; chains of arcane energy bind the two tightly together.&r&aScythe attacks have a chance to trigger Chain Slash"
		""
		"{image:kubejs:textures/gui/malum/pact_of_the_reaper.png width:160 height:200 align:center}"
	]
	quest.1BD8D56B55550058.quest_subtitle: "Mastering the Scythe Blade"
	quest.1BD8D56B55550058.title: "Pact of the Reaper"
	quest.1BF4B358E8923423.quest_desc: [
		"&#66DDFFSanity &7is a &#FFAA00basic stat&7 for players in the game"
		""
		"&#66DDFFSanity &7is displayed via the UI in the top-left corner of the screen"
		""
		"The upper and lower limits of &#66DDFFSanity &7are &#FFAA00-45 &7to &#FFAA00+45"
		""
		"&7Normally, a unit's initial &#66DDFFSanity &7is &f0"
		""
		"&#66DDFFSanity &7changes under different conditions. Generally, &#66DD88favorable states &7raise a unit's &#66DDFFSanity&7, while &#FF6644unfavorable states &7lower it"
		""
		"&7When a unit with a sanity bar has &#66DDFFSanity &7at &#FF4444-45&7, it will &#FF7733&lwith high probability &7enter &#FF6644Panic State&7, and &#44DDFFwith low probability &7enter &#CC77FFErosion State&7 (see later quests for Erosion)"
	]
	quest.1BF4B358E8923423.quest_subtitle: "&zBasic Understanding"
	quest.1BF4B358E8923423.title: "Sanity"
	quest.1BF526B37EC8A965.quest_desc: ["&7以降低攻速为代价，换取较大幅度的伤害加成"]
	quest.1BF526B37EC8A965.quest_subtitle: "代价换力量"
	quest.1C22E01E9591DC36.quest_subtitle: "N E V E R   E M P T Y - H A N D E D"
	quest.1C22E01E9591DC36.title: "Catch Ten Fish"
	quest.1CBEB689E8C2B677.quest_desc: [
		"&6Research: Void Slate"
		"&7After passing through the &dWeeping Well&r&7, the &bSoulstone&r&7 became a substance I call \"&8Void Slate&r&7.\" Though its physical properties resemble Soulstone, it seems to lack a soul... yet the way it interacts with arcane energy is no different from Soulstone."
		"&7"
		"&7Perhaps this is the state of Soulstone before acquiring &dsoul energy&r&7? I cannot determine its mode of interaction with souls, nor can I transfer this property the way I do when making &6Soulstained Steel&r&7. My only theory is that a state of complete absence of arcane energy—not even a trace—somehow possesses its own unique arcane energy. What could this energy be?"
		"&7"
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"&6Re-Examination: Void Slate"
		"&7The complete absence of arcane energy also has its effect. The essence of Void Slate should now be clearer than ever—Soulstone; Soulstone attuned to the &8Void&r&7, rather than to arcane energy."
		"&7"
		"&7It may still be a predecessor of Soulstone, but the two may be related in other ways... Its externally observable physical properties match Soulstone. The differing properties are entirely due to what the stone interacts with."
	]
	quest.1CBEB689E8C2B677.quest_subtitle: "A Blank Slate, Perhaps the Predecessor"
	quest.1CD6A8BB98046D3C.quest_desc: [
		"&7Little things that provide bonuses in various aspects for aircraft. You can use them to shore up a plane's weaknesses depending on its model, or to strengthen a particular advantage."
		""
		"&7It's worth noting that the Enhanced Propeller's air resistance reduction seems to help quite a bit with speeding up aircraft."
	]
	quest.1CDBC70DB8D56271.quest_desc: [
		"&7The early game focuses mainly on Overworld exploration. The player's primary goal is to advance the development of &#66C7CFSilent Gear&7, forging high-quality armor, weapons, and trinkets. If you have trouble choosing materials, you can check the &6Material Recommendations&7 chapter for suggestions. The secondary goal is to advance the development of &3Spirit Calamity&7 and &3Apotheosis&7. The former provides a large number of unique materials, while the latter provides convenient enchanting and mob spawning functions."
		" "
		"&7After completing early-game development, you can begin exploring other dimensions and seeking out various bosses to fight."
	]
	quest.1CDBC70DB8D56271.quest_subtitle: "Combat, fun"
	quest.1CDBC70DB8D56271.title: "If You Want War, Then War It Is"
	quest.1CE41ACD131E060B.quest_desc: [
		"&6Starfire&r"
		"&7Can upgrade &eHotspring Stone equipment&r&7 into the stronger &6Starfire equipment&r&7. The upgrade process requires consuming a &bSmithing Template (Starfire Upgrade)&r."
		""
		"&7Starfire can also provide &dtexture colors&r for armor trim smithing templates at a smithing table."
		""
		"&7Holding and right-clicking can &athrow&r&7 the Starfire in hand. A thrown Starfire explodes upon hitting a creature or block, while applying a &c10-second Starfire I&r&7 effect to all creatures within a &b3-block&r&7 radius of the impact point."
		"&7A thrown Starfire hitting a creature &cdoes not deal attack damage&r."
		""
		"&7Throwing Starfire at &8sand&r&7 or &8Twilight Sand&r&7 converts the struck sand or Twilight Sand into &eRaw Glass&r."
		"&7The &eGlass&r&7 processed from Raw Glass is a material used to craft another kind of &6tier-two equipment&r&7."
		""
		"&7Hold Starfire and right-click a &8Torreya Campfire&r&7 to convert its burning flame to a brighter red."
		"&7The upgraded Torreya Campfire continuously applies a &c4-second Starfire I&r&7 effect to non-friendly targets within a &b10-block&r&7 radius."
		"&7After upgrading, the Torreya Campfire's previously inherent &ahealth regeneration effect&r&7 is still retained."
		"&7Even if the Torreya Campfire is extinguished, the above enhanced ability will continue to &atake effect&r after it is relit."
	]
	quest.1CE41ACD131E060B.quest_subtitle: "Flame of the Blazing Crystal"
	quest.1D08BC5C6C98F4D7.quest_desc: ["&7You'd better not have done that on purpose"]
	quest.1D08BC5C6C98F4D7.quest_subtitle: "A legendary hero who triggered 5 raids?!?"
	quest.1D0A4CF257B8F53C.quest_subtitle: "魔法特化"
	quest.1D30682DE64D68A1.quest_desc: ["&7A &#FF8844redstone device&7 used to regulate &#CC99FFMalum&7."]
	quest.1D30682DE64D68A1.quest_subtitle: "Device Conditions"
	quest.1D3C94736A0C19AA.quest_desc: ["管理你存储网络中所有已配置的自动合成方案，随时进行物品的存取与调度。"]
	quest.1D3C94736A0C19AA.quest_subtitle: "流水作业"
	quest.1D7C2FBD7B33CA7A.quest_desc: [
		"Can be summoned via the Altar"
		""
		"&7Special drops mainly include: Bee Spawn Egg, Bee Backpack, Honey Goggles, Vaporwave Ingot."
		""
		"&7Has a small chance to drop a random Seven Deadly Sins trinket."
	]
	quest.1D7C2FBD7B33CA7A.quest_subtitle: "Stage 1"
	quest.1DBA0BF33C43D227.quest_desc: ["Kill the Ender Dragon to obtain high-tier spell materials"]
	quest.1DBA0BF33C43D227.quest_subtitle: "You're a dragon, that's fine too"
	quest.1DC249D36D54E164.quest_desc: [
		"&7Passive Abilities"
		""
		"&7Damage Limit:  "
		"&7In the broken-defense state, the total damage the Starlight Golem takes cannot exceed &#FFAA332/3&7 of its own max health."
		""
		"&7Invincibility (Phase One only): When not in the broken-defense state, the Starlight Golem &#FF6666is immune to all damage&7."
		""
		"&7Energy (Phase One only):  "
		"&7The Starlight Golem can hold at most &#FFAA33100 points&7 of energy;  "
		"&7Each move consumes a certain amount of energy, and even if the Starlight Golem's remaining energy is insufficient to supply a move's cost, it can still use that move (except when remaining energy is 0);  "
		"&7Energy consumption will not be reduced below zero. When it reaches 0, the Starlight Golem immediately enters the charging state;  "
		"&7Each time the Starlight Golem is hit by a thrown Negative Temperature Test Tube, its held energy is &#FF6666-3&7."
		""
		"&7Energy Block Charging (Charging State)  "
		"&7The Starlight Golem is always initially in the charging state;  "
		"&7Afterward, it only enters the charging state again every &#FFAA3390 seconds&7;  "
		"&7During charging, the Starlight Golem cannot attack, and the four surrounding energy blocks continuously charge the Starlight Golem;  "
		"&7During charging, the Starlight Golem recovers &#66FF660.4 health&7 per second;  "
		"&7After charging completes, the Starlight Golem regains &#FFAA33100 points&7 of energy;  "
		"&7Players must (right-click / fire arrows or other projectiles to) &#FF6666extinguish&7 all energy blocks charging the Starlight Golem, otherwise the Starlight Golem remains invincible;  "
		"&7After all are extinguished: the Starlight Golem enters the broken-defense state."
		""
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"&7Broken-Defense State  "
		"&7Runs in sync with the charging state. After successfully entering the broken-defense state, the Starlight Golem &#FF6666no longer is immune&7 to damage taken, until the current charging state ends;  "
		"&7After taking at most &#FFAA337 hits&7, the Starlight Golem forcibly removes the charging and broken-defense states and resumes attacking;  "
		"&7The broken-defense state lasts at most &#FFAA3360 seconds&7;  "
		"&7If the Starlight Golem enters Phase Two, its current charging state and broken-defense state are also forcibly removed."
		""
		"&7Phase Two  "
		"&7When the Starlight Golem's remaining health ≤&#FFAA3320%&7:  "
		"&7The Starlight Golem loses its invincibility passive and permanently never switches between the charging state and broken-defense state;  "
		"&7From this point on, players can freely attack the Starlight Golem with normal means and deal damage;  "
		"&7In this phase, the Starlight Golem's body continuously trembles and emits sparks, occasionally producing the same red-flash effect as when taking damage (but the red flash here is only a visual effect; the Starlight Golem does not actually have a self-damage passive)."
	]
	quest.1DC249D36D54E164.quest_subtitle: "Exquisite Creation"
	quest.1DDF2D0C0D0D8DDA.quest_desc: ["&7A flying fortress that can fly slowly through the air and strafe downward with onboard weapons. Due to its huge size, slow speed, and unimpressive onboard weapons, it's only introduced here and not recommended for actual use."]
	quest.1DEBD3A3C7F6C452.quest_subtitle: "Increases the extra strength of effects triggered when collecting Spirits"
	quest.1DFDD58AC91C2543.quest_desc: [
		"&7Prioritizes consuming &#FFD700shells&7 in the bag. Usable bullet types: &#FFD700Shells&7, &#FF6666Volatile Shells&7, &#55D5D5Spirit Shells&7. Blank cartridges are not used."
		""
		"&7If there are no bullets in the bag, consumes &#66DDCCdurability&7 based on charge level."
		""
		"&7Projectile damage effect determined by the equipment's &branged damage&7 attribute"
		"&7Firing speed effect determined by the equipment's &6projectile speed&7 attribute"
		"&7Spread range effect determined by the equipment's &aprojectile accuracy&7 attribute"
		"&7Projectile count effect determined by the equipment's &dcharge value&7 attribute"
		""
		"&7Sneak-right-click to reload. Pump count is stackable, up to &c4&7."
		"&7When pump count exceeds &c3&7, it overloads and explodes:"
		"&7• Deals damage to yourself"
		"&7• Consumes &c5&7 durability"
		"&7• Produces a &c4-block&7 explosion"
	]
	quest.1DFDD58AC91C2543.quest_subtitle: "I Gave You a Chance and You Blew It"
	quest.1E1304B2BD351410.quest_desc: ["&7A classic combination, ever fresh. Tanks combined with an Experience Pump can store experience, so even death won't cause you to lose XP. The amount of experience a tank can store varies with the backpack's stack count. Install enough stack upgrades and you can store enormous amounts of experience for a rainy day."]
	quest.1E1304B2BD351410.quest_subtitle: "Liquid Experience"
	quest.1E2790853AD3FE5E.quest_desc: ["&7You can specify a destruction mode to destroy unwanted junk items in your backpack. It's very useful whether for daily killing and mining or for collection and processing at mob farms, but be careful not to destroy things you need."]
	quest.1E2790853AD3FE5E.quest_subtitle: "It's called Void but it's actually a trash can"
	quest.1E5FC0856DAA4E01.quest_subtitle: "Slayer of a Hundred"
	quest.1E5FC0856DAA4E01.title: "Kill Champion Creatures x100"
	quest.1EA661BBFE32AD97.quest_desc: ["&7A weapon with a faster &#FFAA33attack speed&7 than a sword, slightly lower damage, but &#66CCFFwider attack range&7."]
	quest.1EA661BBFE32AD97.quest_subtitle: "Sword of Agility"
	quest.1EB3E26B49C19C5C.quest_desc: [
		"&7Provides &#55D5D5Malice Ward capacity&7 based on &#66CCFFmagic armor&7."
		"&7Provides &#55D5D5Malice Ward recovery rate&7 based on &#66CCFFcharge value&7."
		"&7Provides &#55D5D5Malice Ward recovery bonus&7 based on &#66CCFFmagic armor&7."
		"&7Provides &#FFAA3325%&7 &#66CCFFMalice Conversion&7."
		"&7Can obtain &#55D5D5pact cap&7 based on materials."
	]
	quest.1EB3E26B49C19C5C.quest_subtitle: "Number Shield Enjoyer"
	quest.1EB3E26B49C19C5C.title: "Malice Fortress Leggings Template"
	quest.1EBAE1ABF6C57762.quest_desc: [
		"&7Indeed, permanent Oaths are also a &8heavy burden&r&7. Oaths are powerful, but their &cnegative effects&r&7 follow closely."
		"&7Oaths can be reclaimed at a &6Brazier&r&7, allowing you to choose what price to pay."
		""
		"&7To reclaim an Oath, first prepare the materials used in its declaration at the Brazier, and light it with &5Paradox Flame&r&7 instead."
		"&7This operation &crevokes&r&7 rather than declares the Oath. Other procedures are the same as declaration; reclaiming the Oath of a simple soul also requires weakening it before lighting."
	]
	quest.1EBAE1ABF6C57762.quest_subtitle: "The Price Is Too High"
	quest.1EBAE1ABF6C57762.title: "Reclaiming Oaths"
	quest.1EBDC6E060A25C43.quest_desc: [
		"&6Memory Fragment&r"
		"&7Remnants of a familiar's forgotten past. They will guide you to the place the familiar considers its &bhome&r&7.&r"
	]
	quest.1EC459CAACF854F3.quest_desc: [
		"&c&lNote:"
		"&eStats may become outdated due to lack of maintenance, but &aCodfish will do their best to keep this page updated!"
		""
		"&6&lTips:"
		"&7- &fThe modpack has adjusted and made &eJEI &f(actually &eEMI&f) compatible. You can search for the &dtraits&f a material has in &bEMI &f to find all items with that trait."
		""
		"For example:"
		"%+trait name"
		"&eSearches all items with this trait&r"
		"{\"text\":\"\",\"extra\":[\"And &+part name\"]} "
		"&eSearches all materials usable for this part&r"
		""
		"&7- &fPress &e&lU &f(default key) on a material to view its &eJEI &fpage."
		""
		"&7- &fPress &e&lShift + Ctrl &f on a material weapon to directly view the &dtrait properties&f on the weapon."
	]
	quest.1EC459CAACF854F3.quest_subtitle: "View the attributes and values of all recommended materials here"
	quest.1EC459CAACF854F3.title: "Material Recommendations"
	quest.1EE0B5A8018CD9BB.title: "Soul-Returning Edge Scythe Template"
	quest.1F0087CBFB4E0275.quest_subtitle: "天下武功，唯快不破"
	quest.1F0DFA4EF202BD42.quest_desc: [
		"&7Obtained through manual crafting.  "
		"&7The existence of the &#FFD700Netherite Plating&7 allows players to mass-craft &#66DDCCNetherite-Studded Blocks&7 and their variants as \"fakes\" for building and decoration.  "
		"&7When dropped as an item, it &#FF6666will not be destroyed by fire/lava&7."
	]
	quest.1F0DFA4EF202BD42.quest_subtitle: "Gilded? No, Netherite-Plated is the new trend!"
	quest.1F1102772124A040.quest_desc: ["&7Has a trait that provides extra damage based on &#FFAA33experience level&7. Although its attributes are slightly inferior, your traits make up for that part."]
	quest.1F1102772124A040.quest_subtitle: "Never too much!"
	quest.1F113AE0032F16AA.quest_desc: ["&7Auto-pickup activated. Sometimes it can save dropped items—after all, it really does suck them up fast. You can also try to attract dropped items that might be nearby but you can't find."]
	quest.1F113AE0032F16AA.quest_subtitle: "Sorry, forgot to turn off auto-pickup"
	quest.1F38C534465F33BC.quest_desc: [
		"&6Fluid Pipe&r"
		""
		"&6Purpose / How to Use&r"
		""
		"&6Transferring Fluids&r"
		"&7A &eMechanical Pump&r&7 is required to provide pressure (power) to transfer fluids. By default, a Mechanical Pump can only transfer fluid over &c16 blocks&r&7. Beyond that, another Mechanical Pump is needed to extend the distance.&r"
		"&7The pipe itself has no fluid transfer speed limit; transfer speed depends on the extraction rate.&r"
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"&7If a pipe opening is exposed, it consumes 1000 mB of fluid to generate a corresponding fluid block in the direction of the opening. (Fluids without a block form only show a leaking effect and consume at 1 mB/t.) It can also reverse-extract fluid blocks adjacent to the pipe opening.&r"
		"&7When extracting from infinite water, the pipe only appears not to consume the water source; the extracted water blocks actually alternate between source and flowing states. When a single water block is extracted faster than 200 mB/t (equivalent to using two Mechanical Pumps at 200 RPM), the water source cannot replenish fast enough (open the observation window with a Wrench to see the flow stuttering), and the actual extraction speed stops increasing with pump RPM.&r"
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"&7Additionally, when using multiple pipes to extract infinite water, ensure each extracted water block is adjacent to at least two water sources not being extracted by other pipes. Otherwise, multiple source blocks may be removed at once, breaking the infinite water or causing extraction speed fluctuations.&r"
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"&7When water contains kelp, the pipe cannot extract that water block. Breaking the kelp directly does not restore it; a block update within the pipe system is required (such as changing block state, adjusting pump speed, or re-placing the fluid at the pipe opening). Other waterlogged blocks can be extracted normally.&r"
		"&7Fluid Pipes can extract water and lava from a &eCauldron&r&7.&r"
		"&7Fluid Pipes can extract &ehoney&r&7 from a honey-filled &eBee Nest&r&7 or &eBeehive&r&7. Doing so unlocks the advancement [Automated Apiary].&r"
		"&7The pipe itself has no buffer. If a pipe already carrying fluid is cut off mid-way (pipe broken or Fluid Valve closed), the fluid in the cut-off pipe disappears because the flow process is reset. Suddenly switching the source fluid type also causes this effect.&r"
		""
		"&6Effects on Entities&r"
		"&7When the fluid leaked from a pipe opening is a potion, it applies that potion effect to creatures in front of the opening; milk removes potion effects from creatures.&r"
		"&7Water particles leaked from Fluid Pipes extinguish fire on entities and blocks; lava particles leaked from Fluid Pipes ignite entities.&r"
		"&7No matter how much fluid is sprayed on an entity, the game always gives the entity the full effect. This means players can use 1 mB of potion to give an entity the full potion effect.&r"
		""
		"&6Opening the Observation Window&r"
		"&7Right-click with a Wrench to open a pipe's observation window to see the fluid passing through. A pipe with an open window cannot bend. Right-click again with a Wrench to close it.&r"
		""
		"&6Encasing&r"
		"&7Right-click with a &eCopper Casing&r&7 to encase it. The Copper Casing is not consumed in the process.&r"
		"&7An encased pipe's opening direction and number of openings are locked and will no longer automatically connect to newly placed pipes nearby.&r"
		""
		"&6Fluid Interaction Reactions Inside Pipes&r"
		"&7When two fluids meet inside a pipe, the pipe is destroyed and a block is generated depending on the fluid types: (reaction table omitted)&r"
	]
	quest.1F71B459B51B8E4B.quest_desc: [
		"&6Complex Component&r"
		""
		"&7The Complex Component draws power from its fractal-like, chaotic, complex nature, just as its name suggests. When installed, reliance on fuel increases and focusing speed decreases, but the &eCrucible&r&7 has a chance to produce double output in a single &6Focusing Cycle&r&7.&r"
	]
	quest.1F71B459B51B8E4B.quest_subtitle: "Abundance and Wealth"
	quest.1F9846B94E48DEDF.quest_desc: ["&7Using the light of End Rods, I strengthened the End Bookshelf that symbolizes the end. It can now provide more enchantment values. However, the magic of End Rods is not intense enough to reach the pinnacle of enchanting power"]
	quest.1F9846B94E48DEDF.quest_subtitle: "Enhanced End Bookshelf"
	quest.1F9846B94E48DEDF.title: "Ender Power Reborn"
	quest.1FABC71D3623013A.quest_desc: [
		"&7&#66CCFFSilent Gear&7 — a mod that lets players customize trinkets, armor, weapons, tools, and more."
		""
		"&7This modpack has applied various &#FFD700QOL changes&7 and mechanic overhauls to it. You should be able to get a gameplay experience different from other modpacks!"
		""
		"&7Even if you've never played it before, it's fine—just follow this side quest step by step."
	]
	quest.1FABC71D3623013A.quest_subtitle: "Feels Great!"
	quest.1FB3D1FAE9A88C39.quest_desc: [
		"&6Machinist's Notes&r"
		"&7During my travels I happened to pick up a notebook, seemingly the legacy of some machinist.&r"
		"&7According to the manuscript, mastering these skills would let me become a machinist. That means I could build my own production lines, produce endless resources, unlock more crafting methods, and extract resources from ores that a furnace cannot refine.&r"
		""
		"&7However, this is not a required path on the journey. Becoming a machinist does almost nothing for my combat strength. The original owner of this manuscript couldn't even build a malfunctioning robot to help fight. The benefits to be gained are more of a bonus.&r"
		""
		"&7If interested, perhaps give it a try. The starting point of everything seems to be this cheap material called &6Andesite Alloy&r&7.&r"
	]
	quest.1FB3D1FAE9A88C39.quest_subtitle: "Not knowing how to use it won't matter, probably"
	quest.1FB3D1FAE9A88C39.title: "Prologue of Gears"
	quest.1FB95C69AF3C83E3.quest_desc: [
		"&6Archmage Settlements&r"
		"&7The Archmages traveled to the &6End&r&7 dimension to study the secrets of the endless void, and thus needed a temporary residence. So they decided to build temporary homes throughout the End to conduct research and exploration there.&r"
	]
	quest.1FB95C69AF3C83E3.title: "&6Archmage Settlement&r"
	quest.1FBA0FE6A13F8E70.quest_desc: ["Choose your starting class reward"]
	quest.1FBA0FE6A13F8E70.quest_subtitle: "You will receive a starter gift pack"
	quest.1FBA0FE6A13F8E70.title: "&a\"Honey That Conceals Suffering at the Start\""
	quest.1FC7A319D738A388.quest_desc: ["&7Functions the same as a vanilla &#66CCFFsword&7. You can place a vanilla &#66CCFFsword&7 in a crafting table to convert it into a &#66DDCCSilent Gear Sword&7."]
	quest.1FC7A319D738A388.quest_subtitle: "Classic Weapon"
	quest.1FD98B36E1B61A56.quest_desc: ["As an advanced version of the bookshelf, the Nether Bookshelf provides a higher enchantment cap than normal bookshelves. The magic from the Nether grants the bookshelf additional &4&lQuantization&r&r."]
	quest.1FD98B36E1B61A56.quest_subtitle: "The Arrival of Quantization"
	quest.1FD98B36E1B61A56.title: "Nether Enchanting Power — Embrace Chaos"
	quest.20026163291DE7A2.quest_desc: ["&7This bookshelf currently looks no different from an ordinary wooden bookshelf. The cracks on it make you feel it is even older and more mediocre than ordinary bookshelves. But you can sense that mysterious power is stirring within it, like a heart, like sculk, waiting to be awakened."]
	quest.20026163291DE7A2.quest_subtitle: "Sculk Power Slumbers Deep"
	quest.20026163291DE7A2.title: "An Accidental Attempt?"
	quest.20736EF41F1FED8E.quest_desc: ["&7Echo Shards can effectively increase the various drops produced by creatures, triggering an additional drop roll when a creature dies. This attribute has a maximum of three levels."]
	quest.20736EF41F1FED8E.quest_subtitle: "Increased Drops\\nIncreased Drops"
	quest.2075CDEF8E217AEA.quest_subtitle: "Who are you?"
	quest.2075CDEF8E217AEA.title: "First Champion Creature Kill"
	quest.20848CB8F54AD783.quest_desc: [
		"&7提供简单的攻击向属性加成，缺点是卫城可能很远很难跑……"
		""
		"&7可以使用风暴之眼定位卫城，卫城的一部分怪以及boss受阶段锁限制，但水母莉亚仍然可以攻击，并正常掉落泪石。"
		""
		"推荐部位：武器的顶端升级"
	]
	quest.20848CB8F54AD783.quest_subtitle: "你和数值怪一桌"
	quest.20AB2C2F60CDFE1C.quest_subtitle: "Just as the title says"
	quest.20B149C81F944E27.quest_desc: [
		"&7Hold a glass bottle and right-click a &#66FF66Lesser Wisp&7 to bottle it;  "
		""
		"&7Hold a Wisp Bottle and right-click a block to release the &#66FF66Lesser Wisp&7 and get the glass bottle back;  "
		""
		"&7Besides being used to transport &#66FF66Lesser Wisps&7, this item can also be used as a crafting material."
	]
	quest.20B149C81F944E27.quest_subtitle: "Oi, old man, I parked my wisp downstairs"
	quest.20C6879D332BCC1C.quest_subtitle: "法力之子"
	quest.20DE0F4E18ED1452.quest_subtitle: "Dark Authority"
	quest.20E0FE36906F6A98.quest_desc: [
		"&7Reduces the target's &#FF6666max health&7 based on damage dealt (does not deal damage when health is above 50%, only reduces the cap)."
		"&7Right-click to detonate the reduced max health, dealing damage equal to &#FFAA3320%&7 of the total reduction."
		"&7Cooldown is dynamically determined by &6Silent Gear's&7 &eattack speed&7 attribute."
	]
	quest.20E0FE36906F6A98.quest_subtitle: "You Forgot to Defrost Me"
	quest.20EF8A85CD3EFF3A.quest_desc: [
		"&7The &#66FF99Spirit Crucible&7 can consume &#FFAA33Catalyst Charm&7 durability and &#66FF99Spirits&7 to perform &#CC99FFSpirit Focusing&7 and generate resources."
		""
		"&7The &#66FF99Spirit Crucible&7 is &e2&7 blocks tall and has &e1&7 item slot, &e4&7 spirit slots, &e4&7 augment slots, and &e1&7 core augment slot. Multiple augments of the same type stack their effects. A &#FFCC44Redstone Comparator&7 can detect how full the item slots and spirit slots are."
		""
		"&7Can receive acceleration and augment effects from the &#66DDCCSpirit Catalyst&7. It must be within &e4&7 blocks of the &#66FF99Spirit Crucible&7 (&e3&7 blocks in 1.20.1), and at most &e8&7 can take effect."
		""
		"&7Holding the &#66DDCCTuning Fork&7 or a &#FF8844Create Wrench&7 displays all attributes, and also allows you to select one attribute to tune."
		""
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"&b&lFocusing Speed"
		"&7The speed of Spirit Focusing. Base is &e100%&7. Progress increases each tick by &#FFDD55Focusing Speed&7 until one Spirit Focusing completes after the recipe's required time."
		""
		"&b&lFuel Usage Rate"
		"&7The rate at which the &#66DDCCSpirit Catalyst&7 consumes fuel. Base is &e100%&7. While Spirit Focusing is in progress, it consumes burn time each tick equal to &#FFDD55Fuel Usage Rate&7 * &#FFDD55Focusing Speed&7."
		""
		"&b&lInstability Risk"
		"&7The probability of an item consuming double durability. Base is &e20%&7. When this value exceeds &e100%&7, it consumes round(double durability * &#FF6666Instability Risk&7)."
		""
		"&b&lDamage Absorption Chance"
		"&7The probability that an item consumes no durability at all."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"&b&lRepair Chance"
		"&7After focusing completes and durability is consumed, the probability of repairing the item's durability. For every &e100%&7, it repairs &e1&7 time for certain; the remainder has a corresponding chance to repair &e1&7 more time. Each repair restores &e1%&7 of max durability."
		""
		"&b&lChain Focusing Chance"
		"&7The probability that, when Spirit Focusing completes, the next focusing is completed instantly. After triggering, the time required to complete the next focusing is &#FFDD55Focusing Speed&7 * &e10&7 (about &e10&7 game ticks). All attribute multipliers +&e20%&7, and the Chain Focusing multiplier is -&e20%&7. Stackable. On trigger failure, attribute changes reset to &e0&7."
		""
		"&b&lFortune Chance"
		"&7The probability of increasing the number of output items. For every &e100%&7, output increases by &e1&7 for certain; the remainder has a corresponding chance to increase output by &e1&7 more."
		""
		"&b&lTuning Burden"
		"&7The debuff multiplier of the Tuning Fork. Base is &e100%&7. The tuned attribute value is: current value * (&e1&7 + Tuning Fork debuff multiplier * &#FF6666Tuning Burden&7)."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"&b&lTuning Strength"
		"&7The buff multiplier of the Tuning Fork. Base is &e100%&7. The tuned attribute value is: current value * (&e1&7 + Tuning Fork buff multiplier * &#66FF66Tuning Strength&7)."
		""
		"&b&lWeakest Attribute Tuning"
		"&7The buff can be tuned to the lowest-valued one among tunable attributes, calculated after tuning."
		""
		"&b&lMisfortune Reversal"
		"&7When the &#66FF66Misfortune Reversal&7 value is greater than &e0&7 and Chain Focusing has not triggered, accumulate the durability lost by items and reduce the number of buffs by &e1&7. When repairing via the Repair Chance attribute, additionally restore &e1%&7 * &#66FF66Misfortune Reversal&7 max durability, gain &e20%&7 + accumulated lost durability * &e5%&7 to all attributes, and reset accumulated lost durability to &e0&7. Buff count is &e3&7."
		""
		"&b&lCaustic Harmony"
		"&7Increases &#66FF66Tuning Strength&7 by &#FF6666Instability Risk&7 * &#66FF66Caustic Harmony&7 * &e2&7. Example: when Instability Risk is &e50%&7 and Caustic Harmony is &e100%&7, Tuning Strength +&e100%&7."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"&b&lResonant Tuning"
		"&7Calculated after tuning and Weakest Attribute Tuning. Reduces &#FF6666Instability Risk&7 at the cost of reducing &#FFDD55Focusing Speed&7, with some loss in the process. When &#FFDD55Focusing Speed&7 ≥ &e2&7 * &#FF6666Instability Risk&7 and &#FF6666Instability Risk&7 ≤ &e1&7, it can always reduce Instability Risk to &e0&7."
		""
		"&7The calculation process is as follows:"
		""
		"&7Target value = min(&#FF6666Instability Risk&7 * &#66FF66Resonant Tuning&7, &#FFDD55Focusing Speed&7) * &e2&7;"
		"&7Conversion value = clamp(&#FFDD55Focusing Speed&7/target value, &e0&7, &e1&7);"
		"&7When conversion value > &e0&7:"
		"&#FFDD55Focusing Speed&7 -= clamp(target value/&#FFDD55Focusing Speed&7, &e0&7, &e1&7) * &e0.8&7;"
		"&#FF6666Instability Risk&7 -= conversion value."
	]
	quest.20EF8A85CD3EFF3A.quest_subtitle: "Mysterious Duplication"
	quest.20EF8A85CD3EFF3A.title: "Spirit Focusing"
	quest.2105AA28B15D5C1C.title: "Tool Handle Parts"
	quest.21294371EDEA78C6.quest_desc: [
		"&7权限卡是通过右键单击与玩家绑定的项目"
		""
		"右击在与玩家绑定的同时会打开配置界面，潜行右击重置权限配置"
	]
	quest.21294371EDEA78C6.quest_subtitle: "让我访问！"
	quest.2139D29C06E64C48.quest_desc: [
		"&7After defeating it, you can craft the &#66CCFFMeat Grinder Blueprint&7. Right-click to deal an attack to entities in front that &#FF6666ignores invincibility frames&7."
		""
		"&7Of course, you can also use it as an &#66DDCCaxe&7, except it can't be used for skinning."
	]
	quest.2139D29C06E64C48.quest_subtitle: "Kill kill kill"
	quest.214D64602702D242.quest_desc: [
		"&6Suspicious Device&r"
		""
		"&7Arcane and Malefic are indeed opposites, and they can indeed be used to craft opposition augments. However, in the torrent-like surge from arcane to the end of malefic, what is produced is only chaos, and the result is... an explosion that corrodes all things, and the Blight it brings. This entry is meant only as a warning, not a recommendation.&r"
	]
	quest.214D64602702D242.quest_subtitle: "A Cautionary Tale"
	quest.2150AC43C2C52806.quest_desc: ["较为便宜的造价"]
	quest.2150AC43C2C52806.quest_subtitle: "苦苦卡卡"
	quest.215AB6260ED8DAAD.quest_desc: ["&7Take a gamble?&r"]
	quest.215AB6260ED8DAAD.quest_subtitle: "Random Level + Random Enchantment"
	quest.215AB6260ED8DAAD.title: "Random Enchanted Book Vendor"
	quest.2190DB8F13415C43.quest_desc: [
		"&6Flame-Spurring Launcher"
		"&7&cThe Fire of Evolution&r&7 is extremely intense; it destroys everything in its path for its own evolution and spread. Thus destructive weapons based on it must exist—and in fact, they do."
		"&7"
		"&7I used a pair of &6Lantern Tongs&r&7 to create this \"&6Flame-Spurring Launcher&r&7.\" It recalibrates &bAura Embers&r&7 to \"unlock\" them, transforming their gentle flames into explosive fire, and restrains them before they are ready to launch."
		"&7"
		"&7I also added a layer of safety measures, because... I don't want to rebuild the laboratory again. These flames are extremely explosive. Of course, basic blast protection like obsidian can stop them."
	]
	quest.2190DB8F13415C43.quest_subtitle: "Evolution Surpasses All"
	quest.219B219DA2F8C114.quest_desc: [
		"&6Lush Shallows&r"
		"&7is one of the Starlight ocean biomes."
		""
		"&7Lush Shallows have vegetation coverage completely different from the Starlit Sea."
		"&7Its iconic &#32CD32Sea Bell Stem Thickets&r&7 and unique &#9ACD32yellow-green ambient color&r&7 give the biome an overall unique and tranquil atmosphere."
		""
		"&7Non-aquatic creatures can only spawn underground, dozens of blocks deep from the Lush Shallows."
	]
	quest.219B219DA2F8C114.quest_subtitle: "Prosperous Forest"
	quest.219B219DA2F8C114.title: "Lush Shallows"
	quest.219F39116C48B242.quest_desc: [
		"&7若是想对流体进行存储，而不是连桶一起存储，则需要使用流体存储"
		""
		"在终端中，将桶右键可把液体倾倒至终端内部，手持空桶右键可装桶"
	]
	quest.219F39116C48B242.quest_subtitle: "流体存储"
	quest.21A80A164028813C.quest_desc: ["{\"text\":\"\",\"extra\":[{\"text\":\"I know you might get a headache seeing this mod's \",\"color\":\"gray\"},{\"text\":\"eyes\",\"color\":\"red\"},{\"text\":\", but now they can all be \",\"color\":\"gray\"},{\"text\":\"crafted\",\"color\":\"green\"},{\"text\":\".\",\"color\":\"gray\"}]}"]
	quest.21A80A164028813C.quest_subtitle: "Craftable"
	quest.21DFA7D5BF06FF3A.quest_desc: [
		"&6Mirror of Truth&r"
		"&7Used to reveal disguised &dIllusionist&r&7 familiars. Can be obtained through &6rituals&r&7.&r"
	]
	quest.21FE19A7D8EFA94C.quest_desc: [
		"&7Sneak-right-click to dash forward. On hitting a target, deals damage and stuns the target."
		"&7Charge speed = &c1.5 + attack speed × 0.3&7."
		"&7Charge damage = &cattack power × 0.15&7."
		"&7Jump height = &c0.6 + armor toughness × 0.05&7."
		"&7Cooldown = &c40 × (4 ÷ attack speed)&7, max &c100 ticks (5 seconds)&7."
	]
	quest.21FE19A7D8EFA94C.quest_subtitle: "The Shield Hero"
	quest.221645B2BE16D7E1.quest_desc: [
		"&6Pact of the Prospector&r"
		""
		"&7Greed Burns the Body&r"
		"&7-While afflicted by the '&cGreed&r&7' status, being hit causes you to be consumed by &cflames&r"
		""
		"&7A boon originating from flame.&r"
		"&7-Collecting &eprecious minerals&r&7 grants the '&6Greed&r&7' status"
		"&7-The '&6Greed&r&7' status gradually increases &aLuck chance&r"
		"&7-When gaining the '&6Greed&r&7' status, additionally restores one heart of &alost health&r"
		""
		"{image:kubejs:textures/gui/malum/pact_of_combustion.png width:160 height:200 align:center}"
	]
	quest.221645B2BE16D7E1.quest_subtitle: "Treasures of the Earth"
	quest.221645B2BE16D7E1.title: "Pact of the Prospector"
	quest.2218345B2D47B183.title: "Bitter Comet Fear"
	quest.2227DDA9A63E5685.quest_desc: [
		"Um.... do we really need a tutorial on how to summon the Wither?"
		""
		"&7Special drops mainly include: Nether Star, Demon Heart. Defeating the Wither while flying with Elytra drops the Soaring Insignia."
		""
		"&7Using the Demon Heart grants +1 maximum accessory slot; limited to one use per player."
		""
		"&7Has a small chance to drop a random Seven Deadly Sins trinket."
	]
	quest.2227DDA9A63E5685.quest_subtitle: "Stage 0"
	quest.223819B7B37AEFB2.quest_desc: [
		"Back when I barely knew Java modding, Codfish just stated a requirement and they made a mod for it (though it was later optimized)"
		""
		"But I still won't forget it!"
	]
	quest.223819B7B37AEFB2.quest_subtitle: "Contributor"
	quest.223819B7B37AEFB2.title: "The P"
	quest.2239EBD39F850AC6.quest_desc: [
		"&7Since traditional spears are limited by attack range, why not just fire projectiles instead."
		""
		"&7When the &#FFD700Ancient Spear&7 is fully charged, left-click produces a slightly homing &#66CCFFprojectile&7 to attack enemies."
		"&7Projectile damage = &cplayer melee damage × 0.75&7 (benefits from Strength potions and other buffs)."
		"&7Each shot consumes &c1&7 durability."
	]
	quest.2239EBD39F850AC6.quest_subtitle: "Wisdom of the Ancients"
	quest.2248B07BE012F5B4.quest_desc: ["&7The original airship model. Steady in flight with a smaller size. Its downside is probably being on the slower side, making it unremarkable for exploration."]
	quest.2254C590DE6A8100.quest_desc: [
		"&6Pact of the Berserker"
		"&7Harm yourself, and harm others.&r&cWrath subsides over time&r&cDamage taken doubled"
		"&7Endless wrath, eternal fury; pain brings wrath, and wrath is power.&r&aDamage taken becomes Wrath&r&aWhen dealing damage, continuously fires &cMalefic Arcane&r&a barrages at enemies using Wrath"
		""
		"{image:kubejs:textures/gui/malum/pact_of_the_berserker.png width:160 height:200 align:center}"
	]
	quest.2254C590DE6A8100.quest_subtitle: "An Eye for an Eye"
	quest.2254C590DE6A8100.title: "Pact of the Berserker"
	quest.226A2B7E35FB2F05.quest_desc: ["通过战利品获得，冰河时代减益可以有效伤害低速敌人"]
	quest.226A2B7E35FB2F05.quest_subtitle: "提供法强加成"
	quest.22DBDBE68B6E1B4D.quest_desc: [
		"&6Weapon Enchanting&r"
		"&7Spell scrolls can be applied to weapons, allowing the player to cast that spell while holding the weapon. Note: This will override this mod's spells or other mods' weapon right-click abilities.&r"
		""
		"&6Robe Enchanting&r"
		"&7Players can also infuse spells into certain robes added by the mod (such as the &cPlague Doctor's Coat&r&7, &cBlood Cultist Robe&r&7, etc.) in a similar way. While wearing a robe infused with a spell, the player can cast the infused spell. However, the &eWandering Mage Robe&r&7 and &eSpooky Pumpkin Robe&r&7 cannot be used for this.&r"
		""
		"&7When a weapon/armor already has an infused spellbook, using a &bStone of Repentance&7 can remove the infused spell."
	]
	quest.22E5438A416558FF.quest_desc: ["Right-click to clear an ongoing invasion"]
	quest.22E5438A416558FF.quest_subtitle: "Tired of annoying invasions?"
	quest.2327AC873A01051D.title: "Plate Parts"
	quest.2331CCFEF5A9EEE5.quest_desc: [
		"&6Pact of the Lone Druid&r"
		""
		"&7Unbound means unarmored.&r"
		"&7-After taking damage, armor weighs you down and grows &cthorns&r&7 that harm your soul&r"
		""
		"&7Whole means unbound.&r"
		"&7-Each empty armor slot grants five points of &earmor value&r&7 and two points of &earmor toughness&r"
		"&7-Each empty armor slot increases &ahealing received&r&7 by one quarter&r"
		""
		"{image:kubejs:textures/gui/malum/pact_of_the_lone_druid.png width:160 height:200 align:center}"
	]
	quest.2331CCFEF5A9EEE5.quest_subtitle: "Shunning the External"
	quest.2331CCFEF5A9EEE5.title: "Pact of the Lone Druid"
	quest.233B0326CCA639C7.quest_desc: [
		"&6Rune of Doubled Duration&r"
		""
		"&7The Rune of Doubled Duration suppresses the form's process of breaking down substances, thereby extending the duration of &apositive effects&r&7 on the form.&r"
	]
	quest.233B0326CCA639C7.quest_subtitle: "That Which Stills Evolution"
	quest.2358AB144E490565.quest_subtitle: "Familiar Summoning Ritual"
	quest.2376D883261AE9AC.quest_desc: ["焰魔出品，可以有效降低敌人的护甲值"]
	quest.2376D883261AE9AC.quest_subtitle: "腾炎力量"
	quest.2377B4B5C5413B34.quest_desc: ["{\"text\":\"\",\"extra\":[{\"text\":\"I know you might get a headache seeing this mod's \",\"color\":\"gray\"},{\"text\":\"eyes\",\"color\":\"red\"},{\"text\":\", but now they can all be \",\"color\":\"gray\"},{\"text\":\"crafted\",\"color\":\"green\"},{\"text\":\".\",\"color\":\"gray\"}]}"]
	quest.2377B4B5C5413B34.quest_subtitle: "Craftable"
	quest.23B6D00570354BE3.quest_desc: [
		"&6Boiler&r"
		""
		"&7An advanced power structure that generates stress by heating water to produce steam. It produces large amounts of stress and is a core power source widely used in the mid-to-late game.&r  "
		"&7Stress output: &c2048~294912 su&7  "
		"&7Speed range: &c16~64 RPM&7  "
		""
		"&6Construction&r  "
		"&7Place a &eSteam Engine&7 or &eSteam Whistle&7 on a &eFluid Tank&7 structure of any size, and the tank transforms into a boiler.&r  "
		""
		"&6Operating Conditions&r  "
		"&7The boiler needs a continuous water supply and a heat source at its bottom to operate.&r  "
		"&7Its efficiency is affected by three attributes: **Size**, **Water**, and **Heat**, each with 18 levels. Wear &eEngineer's Goggles&7 to inspect the boiler and view specific attributes.&r  "
		""
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"&7Attribute        Calculation&r  "
		"&7📏 Size      Depends on boiler volume (m³). Size level = total volume / 4&r  "
		"&7💧 Water     Depends on water supply rate. One Mechanical Pump provides 1 mB/tick per 2 RPM. Water level = supply rate (mB/tick) / 10, or Water level = Mechanical Pump RPM / 20&r  "
		"&7🔥 Heat      Depends on the total heat provided by all heat sources at the bottom. See below.&r  "
		"&7The boiler does not store water; it calculates the water level only from the intake rate. Water disappears once it enters. If the tank held fluid before transforming into a boiler, it is emptied upon transformation.&r  "
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"&6Heat Source Types&r  "
		"&7Heat sources that can heat the boiler include:&r  "
		"&7Heat Source Type        Source                                Heat Provided&r  "
		"&7Passive Heat Source     Blaze Burner (extinguished/empty), Campfire, Fire, Magma Block, Lava, Stove (Farmer's Delight), etc.        0&r  "
		"&7Tier 1 Heat Source      Blaze Burner (normal burning)               1&r  "
		"&7Tier 2 Heat Source      Blaze Burner (super burning)               2&r  "
		"&7Passive heat sources only put the boiler into a &cpassive state&7, in which the boiler fixedly produces &c2048 su&7 stress. Adding more passive heat sources does not improve efficiency. When a higher-tier heat source is present, passive heat sources do not take effect.&r  "
		"&7The boiler is only heated by heat sources directly below its bottom.&r  "
		""
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"&6Power Output&r  "
		"&7The boiler's final level is determined by the **lowest value** among its Size, Water, and Heat attributes.&r  "
		"&7A &eSteam Engine&7 must be installed on the boiler, with a &eShaft&7 placed in the second block directly in front of the engine. Stress is output through the shaft.&r  "
		""
		"&6Stress Calculation&r  "
		"&7Except in the passive state, the boiler produces &cboiler level × 16384 su&7 stress, distributed evenly to each Steam Engine.&r  "
		"&7A single Steam Engine outputs at most &c16384 su&7 stress. If total stress exceeds this, install multiple Steam Engines to avoid waste.&r  "
		"&7Installing a number equal to the boiler level fully outputs all stress; exceeding that number does not improve efficiency.&r  "
		""
		"&6Speed Output&r  "
		"&7The Steam Engine's output speed is determined by the boiler's operating state and the ratio of engine count to level, ranging from &c16 RPM ~ 64 RPM&7.&r  "
		""
		"&8This page's paper seems slightly curled from steam exposure&r"
	]
	quest.23C66ED4DAFAC1F8.quest_subtitle: "Basic Part"
	quest.24024A47877C3B54.quest_desc: ["Right-click to reset the invasion counter to 0 and enter a long period of safety"]
	quest.24024A47877C3B54.quest_subtitle: "Tired of annoying invasions?"
	quest.244305D501AB31AA.quest_desc: [
		"&7Determined by &6Silent Gear&7 attributes:"
		"&7• Armor &7→ &cArmor value&7, also provides &cbonus health (armor ÷ 2)"
		"&7• Armor Toughness &7→ &cArmor toughness"
		"&7• Knockback Resistance &7→ &cKnockback resistance"
	]
	quest.244305D501AB31AA.quest_subtitle: "Compared to normal armor, its armor value and other attributes are higher, at the cost of losing spell attributes"
	quest.2443B7C22B13BC1F.quest_desc: [
		"&7Inspired by the Hallowed Gold Obelisk, you made the Experience Crystal you considered useless into an obelisk as well. The magic of experience did not affect the Soul Infusion ritual. Instead, it showed enhancement of another magical power—enchanting."
		""
		"&7Although it can provide a large amount of &aTier&7, it is affected by its original world. Its &aTier&7 cap is no different from ordinary bookshelves."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"&7And you may later regret why I wasted such a precious thing ("
	]
	quest.2443B7C22B13BC1F.quest_subtitle: "Ordinary-High Bookshelf (?"
	quest.2443B7C22B13BC1F.title: "Powerful Yet Weak"
	quest.24525BF493E3277C.quest_desc: ["可以向它传入物品，也可以由它抽出物品，是输入终端和输出方法的上位替代"]
	quest.24525BF493E3277C.quest_subtitle: "向RS网络输入或输出物品或流体"
	quest.2453187E1E29FF73.quest_desc: ["&7Using the light of Prismarine Shards, I amplified and distorted the power of the Ocean Bookshelf. Now it not only provides &5Arcana&7, but also some &4Quantization&7 attribute. After all, uncertainty is also part of mystery."]
	quest.2453187E1E29FF73.quest_subtitle: "A More Balanced Ocean Bookshelf"
	quest.2453187E1E29FF73.title: "Mysterious Extension"
	quest.24535EE9B76923B6.quest_subtitle: "Trait parts; you can apply whichever traits you want. No recommendations."
	quest.24535EE9B76923B6.title: "Binding Parts"
	quest.2482C01B41948195.quest_desc: ["&7A cheap and versatile material. Excellent performance whether for &#CC99FFweapons&7 or &#66CCFFarmor&7. An excellent &#FFD700transition material&7. Its low cost lets you mass-produce it, fill repair kits to repair on the go, and with a bit of enchanting it can handle most early-game enemies."]
	quest.2482C01B41948195.quest_subtitle: "King of Transitions"
	quest.24A6B77DD8DEA131.quest_desc: [
		"&7As a one-time consumable, scrolls have enormous material costs, making their cost-efficiency quite poor."
		""
		"&7Players can hold a scroll to cast, without consuming mana, but the cost is directly &4consuming the scroll&r."
		"&7Using the &6Spell Scribing Table&7 allows you to write scrolls into a spellbook, and spells in the spellbook can be reused by consuming mana."
	]
	quest.24C387A38C376961.quest_subtitle: "You didn't farm deaths to get this quest's reward, right? You didn't, right?"
	quest.24F8461D0711F786.quest_desc: [
		"&6Rune of Anomalous Stamina&r"
		""
		"&7The Rune of Anomalous Stamina grants the wearer hysterical speed. They will always be able to move swiftly, and can even sprint when &chunger&r&7 is too low to sprint.&r"
	]
	quest.24F8461D0711F786.quest_subtitle: "Fleeing the Pursued"
	quest.252D5B1C2C327A08.quest_subtitle: "假如我是神射手"
	quest.257E95B5ED03904D.quest_desc: ["&7An upgraded hoe. You can also use it as an &#66DDCCaxe&7 and &#66DDCCshovel&7, and it can chain-mine grass on the ground in a small area. But functionally, it cannot fully replace the &#66DDCCaxe&7 and &#66DDCCshovel&7—after all, it's a hoe."]
	quest.257E95B5ED03904D.quest_subtitle: "Better Than a Hoe"
	quest.25C80C95F10CF3DB.quest_desc: [
		"&7The &#FFD700Smelting Controller&7 supports automated input, so we can achieve automated output."
		"{image:kubejs:textures/gui/alloy_forgery/alloy_forgery4.png width:120 height:100 align:center}"
		"&7As shown, the left side requires &#FFD700fuel&7 input, the right side requires &#66DDCCmaterial&7 input, and the bottom is the output."
		"&7You can use &#66CCFFRS&7 patterns to achieve fully controllable automation."
		""
		"&7See the next page for the tutorial."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"&7First, you need a &#FFD700Pattern Terminal&7 in your storage network and some &#66DDCCBlank Patterns&7."
		"{image:kubejs:textures/gui/alloy_forgery/auto_alloy_forgery1.png width:200 height:90 align:center click_action:none:}"
		"&7Select the furnace icon button, place the pattern into the indicated slot, then put the &#66DDCCinput&7 you need on the left and the output on the right."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		""
		"&7Then place the &#66DDCCAuto-Crafting Chamber&7 as shown and connect it to the terminal using cables, or use any other item output method you prefer."
		"{image:kubejs:textures/gui/alloy_forgery/auto_alloy_forgery2.png width:170 height:100 align:center click_action:none:}"
		""
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"&7After processing, place the pattern into the &#66DDCCAuto-Crafting Chamber&7."
		"{image:kubejs:textures/gui/alloy_forgery/auto_alloy_forgery3.png width:200 height:80 align:center fit:true click_action:none:}"
		"&7Then you can see the processed content in the terminal. &#FFD700Shift+Left-click&7 to select for automation."
	]
	quest.25C80C95F10CF3DB.quest_subtitle: "More knowledge! And more!"
	quest.25C80C95F10CF3DB.title: "Automation!"
	quest.25CE20F4B934CF78.quest_desc: [
		"Can be summoned via the Altar"
		""
		"&7Special drops mainly include: Slime Staff, Swamp Vines, Slime Saddle, Nether Slimeball, Gober Slimeball."
		""
		"&7The Slime Saddle provides some mobility with good jumping performance. Hold the Slime Saddle and right-click to summon a slime mount; press Shift to dismount."
		""
		"&7Has a small chance to drop a random Seven Deadly Sins trinket."
	]
	quest.25CE20F4B934CF78.quest_subtitle: "Stage 0"
	quest.26199250ABE1AA3E.quest_desc: [
		"&7Used to accelerate crop growth within a &#FFAA333×3×3&7 area.  "
		"&7Since it's &#FFAA333×3×3&7, centered on the crop in the block the player clicks, all crops within range will have a &#66FF66bone meal effect&7 applied once."
	]
	quest.26199250ABE1AA3E.quest_subtitle: "The alarm bell rings on"
	quest.2650317F3653A86F.quest_desc: ["&7获取难度极高，攻击可对敌人施加冰冻累积，叠满后直接冻结目标"]
	quest.2650317F3653A86F.quest_subtitle: "奴役巨龙实在可耻"
	quest.266954CE47E5BBAA.quest_desc: [
		"&7Right-click to throw a &#FFD700thunder spear&7. On hitting the ground, generates a small-area &#66CCFFthunder pool&7."
		"&7Projectile damage = &cmelee damage&7."
		"&7Area damage = &cmelee damage × 0.5&7."
		"&7Cooldown = &c100 × (4 ÷ attack speed)&7, max &c600 ticks (&c30 seconds&7)."
		"&7Each normal attack consumes &c1&7 durability."
	]
	quest.266954CE47E5BBAA.quest_subtitle: "I Won't Tell You Anything AHHHHH"
	quest.26F574E2557F8ADF.quest_desc: ["Another big shot! Provided some modding in the pack's early days, though the code was later abandoned... but they still helped Codfish!"]
	quest.26F574E2557F8ADF.quest_subtitle: "Some Code + Contributor"
	quest.26FC3272EF9F44E8.quest_desc: [
		"&6Crystallized Berries&r"
		"&7Obtained by &bSniffers&r&7 digging them up. Can be fed to your familiar to obtain &eMemory Fragments&r&7.&r"
	]
	quest.270113919FB0BE75.quest_desc: ["The best percentage bonus in Stage One"]
	quest.270113919FB0BE75.quest_subtitle: "Feels tingly when you hold it"
	quest.27220D017F7E0659.quest_desc: ["&7Each &#66FF99Spirit&7 harvested while worn grants a random (&e1.0&7~&e4.0&7) * &#CC99FFArcane Resonance&7 experience (rounded)."]
	quest.27220D017F7E0659.quest_subtitle: "Gain a Special Effect When Harvesting Spirits"
	quest.2723E285F0AD8412.quest_desc: [
		"&7Determined by &6Silent Gear&7 attributes:"
		"&7• Armor &7→ &cArmor value&7, also provides &cbonus health (armor ÷ 2)"
		"&7• Armor Toughness &7→ &cArmor toughness"
		"&7• Knockback Resistance &7→ &cKnockback resistance"
	]
	quest.2723E285F0AD8412.quest_subtitle: "Compared to normal armor, its armor value and other attributes are higher, at the cost of losing spell attributes"
	quest.2723F0F916E98181.quest_desc: [
		"&7Each &#66FF99Spirit&7 harvested while worn:"
		""
		"&7Extends all positive effects by &e3&7 seconds, up to &e150&7 seconds;"
		"&7Shortens all negative effects by &e6&7 seconds."
		""
		"&7The extended or shortened duration is multiplied by the &#CC99FFArcane Resonance&7 attribute value and rounded to game ticks."
	]
	quest.2723F0F916E98181.quest_subtitle: "Gain a Special Effect When Harvesting Spirits"
	quest.278B31B68AFBBC11.quest_desc: ["&7Relying on &#66CCFFSilent Gear's&7 alloy mechanics, multiple materials can be fused into one via the &#FFD700Alloy Machine&7. During fusion, the first material serves as the base for modification, and traits are overwritten by higher-tier traits of the same type. This means you can pair the stats of high-tier materials with the &#66FF66useful traits&7 of low-tier materials to freely customize your ideal material."]
	quest.278B31B68AFBBC11.quest_subtitle: "Stacking Effects"
	quest.27B6C00949F92CCF.quest_desc: [
		"&7I seem to have discovered something strange: a form of magic hitherto unrecorded. If one forgoes the chance to learn magic, one cannot call oneself a mage."
		""
		"&7The energy manipulated by this mysterious school seems rooted in the &6soul&r&7. More precisely, it is the energy of the soul—the will and pulse that constitutes each of us."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"&7So far, what I have described is only the basics. But I discovered a method to separate the soul's pulse and condense it into matter; I call these substances \"&6Spirit Crystals&r&7.\" This is the cornerstone of my research."
		""
		"&7The nature of the condensed soul affects the crystal's properties. Every soul is unique, and the crystals formed are of various kinds. I believe these crystals are the breakthrough of my research."
	]
	quest.27B6C00949F92CCF.quest_subtitle: "Soul Magic"
	quest.27E185702EBFAB90.quest_subtitle: "Tier 3 Grading Catalyst"
	quest.27E19E564DC0F89F.quest_subtitle: "Familiar Summoning Ritual"
	quest.27E1C7E671DF7C03.quest_desc: [
		"&7Can point to the nearest unopened &#FFD700Lootr loot container&7 within &#FFAA3364 blocks&7 of you. Right-click to highlight the found container."
		""
		"&7No more worrying about missing treasures tucked away in some corner of a structure."
		"（Only searches when in the hotbar/held, and requires no UI to be currently open）"
	]
	quest.27E1C7E671DF7C03.quest_subtitle: "Treasure Gourmet"
	quest.2808547613BD84C8.title: "Vine Remains"
	quest.28235FFD2D0DE1DD.quest_desc: [
		"&#CC99FFSpirit Calamity&7 studies the harvesting and application of &#55D5D5souls&7. Harvesting &#55D5D5souls&7 for the first time requires a &#FFD700scythe weapon&7, but most materials made from &#55D5D5spirits&7 also have the ability to harvest &#55D5D5souls&7. Just add a small amount of material to &#66CCFFweapons, armor&7, or even trinkets, and you can break free from the &#FFD700scythe&7. Attacking enemies with &#66CCFFspells&7 can achieve the same effect."
		""
		"&7Rumor has it that villagers once studied &#55D5D5souls&7 too, but a major &#FF6666accident&7 made them abolish all related research. Was it village-nature distortion or moral decay..."
		""
		"[ { \"text\": \"Click to jump to Spirit Calamity side quests\", \"underlined\": true, \"clickEvent\": { \"action\": \"change_page\", \"value\": \"27B6C00949F92CCF\" }  ,\"color\":\"blue\"}]"
		""
		"Please be sure to check the side quests. The main questline only serves to guide the progression and contains nothing else!"
	]
	quest.28235FFD2D0DE1DD.quest_subtitle: "Soul Magic"
	quest.28235FFD2D0DE1DD.title: "The Bizarre"
	quest.283E7DF6FCE579BC.quest_subtitle: "词条发射器"
	quest.284BD033E472B251.quest_desc: [
		"Misery Heap is a block that does not spawn naturally;"
		""
		"Players need to use Bone Meal and right-click a Misery Melon that has already been placed on Soul Sand:"
		""
		"Afterward, several random Soul Sand blocks within a few blocks of the Misery Melon will transform into Misery Heaps;"
	]
	quest.284BD033E472B251.quest_subtitle: "Bitter"
	quest.284F3685C1A776D4.quest_desc: [
		"&7需要进入星光维度寻找冰封魔法森林获取，可以作为握柄材料，对低攻速武器加成不错。"
		""
		"推荐部位：握柄"
	]
	quest.284F3685C1A776D4.quest_subtitle: "上等皮毛"
	quest.287148E99E399EB1.quest_desc: ["Makes the spawner ignore light level when spawning."]
	quest.287148E99E399EB1.quest_subtitle: "Eternal Night Falls (at the Spawner)"
	quest.287148E99E399EB1.title: "Soul Lantern"
	quest.288F52920CC79FEC.quest_desc: [
		"The pack was originally made just for a get-together with friends. Later the ideas grew more ambitious, and then... Reverie Foundry was born"
		""
		"P.S. Carrot-chan is cute"
	]
	quest.288F52920CC79FEC.quest_subtitle: "Planning + Contributor"
	quest.28A651F6B7D52DF2.quest_desc: [
		"&6Pact of the Warlock"
		"&7Feel &canger&r&7, and evoke &canger&r&7.&r&cEnemies can detect you from twice as far"
		"&7A pact specialized in fusing &canger&r&7 into &cpain&r&7.&r&aThe first strike against an enemy carries a &cMalefic Arcane&r&a barrage"
		""
		"{image:kubejs:textures/gui/malum/pact_of_the_warlock.png width:160 height:200 align:center}"
	]
	quest.28A651F6B7D52DF2.quest_subtitle: "Endless Battle"
	quest.28A651F6B7D52DF2.title: "Pact of the Warlock"
	quest.28F42F3025DEB18C.quest_desc: [
		"&6Crystal Moth&r&7"
		"&7Flying neutral creature. Fights back only when attacked itself;&r"
		""
		"&7Group aggro: After it is attacked, all &#A351DACrystal Moths&r&7 around it will lock that attacker as a hatred target;&r"
		""
		"&7Before each attack, the Crystal Moth needs a certain amount of time to charge up:&r"
		""
		"&7It will try to stay away from the target to keep distance, flying around the target in left and right directions;&r"
		""
		"&7Afterward, it continuously fires &#F159BBsound waves&r&7 that track the target and ignore shield blocking. Each round of sound wave attacks can hit the same target at most 10 times (all can instantly deal damage to the target);&r"
		""
		"&7Although it looks similar to the Warden's sonic boom attack, the Crystal Moth's sound wave is physical damage (reducible by armor value) rather than magic damage.&r"
		""
		"&7Players can hold any meat and right-click to feed the Crystal Moth, with a chance to tame it;&r"
		""
		"&7A tamed Crystal Moth has only one behavior mode: following the player (it cannot sit and stay);&r"
		""
		"&7A tamed Crystal Moth will actively attack monsters attacked by the player / that attack the player;&r"
		""
		"&7Hold &eMoonmoth Paste&r&7 and right-click a tamed Crystal Moth:&r"
		""
		"&7The Crystal Moth will consume it, with a lower chance to produce 1 &#F8CD4BTremor Gel&r&7.&r"
	]
	quest.28F42F3025DEB18C.title: "Crystal Moth"
	quest.28FBA3F985201394.quest_desc: [
		"&7Determined by &6Silent Gear&7 attributes:"
		"&7• Armor &7→ &cArmor value&7, also provides &cbonus health (armor ÷ 2)"
		"&7• Armor Toughness &7→ &cArmor toughness"
		"&7• Knockback Resistance &7→ &cKnockback resistance"
	]
	quest.28FBA3F985201394.quest_subtitle: "Compared to normal armor, its armor value and other attributes are higher, at the cost of losing spell attributes"
	quest.2911813B45667FF4.quest_desc: ["Using the symbol of the dragon's domineering power, I made this bookshelf. Perhaps due to a return to simplicity, this bookshelf only provides an enormous amount of &aTier&r, and most importantly, can raise the &aTier&r cap to the maximum value."]
	quest.2911813B45667FF4.quest_subtitle: "The Road to the Pinnacle of Tier"
	quest.2911813B45667FF4.title: "Roar of the Dragon"
	quest.291925E282FCB75C.quest_desc: [
		"&7Basic trinket, no special mechanics."
		"&7Attributes are determined by &6Silent Gear&7 material traits."
	]
	quest.291925E282FCB75C.quest_subtitle: "Probably a Ring"
	quest.292EE3446E29D4BA.quest_desc: [
		"&6Pact of Contentedness"
		"&7Fullness requires health.&r&cArmor value and armor toughness halved when approaching starvation"
		"&7Whole means full.&r&aArmor value and armor toughness increased by one fifth when near fully sated"
		""
		"{image:kubejs:textures/gui/malum/pact_of_contentedness.png width:160 height:200 align:center click_action:none:}"
	]
	quest.292EE3446E29D4BA.quest_subtitle: "Seeking Satisfaction"
	quest.292EE3446E29D4BA.title: "Pact of Contentedness"
	quest.293A85724AE2C0E6.quest_desc: [
		"&eQuantum Stability:&r&7 Changes the minimum value of the final enchantment level affected by Quantization fluctuations, effectively correcting Quantization's negative effects while retaining its positive effects."
		""
		"&eGeode-Sealed Stabilizing Bookshelf&7 can provide Quantum Stability."
	]
	quest.29833D624EE0F60A.quest_subtitle: "&cDisables natural sanity recovery (does not disable trait effects)"
	quest.29833D624EE0F60A.title: "&c\"Crazy Juice Seeps from the Corners of Your Eyes\""
	quest.2A0C75F0BB1001BC.quest_desc: [
		"&6Precision Mechanism&r"
		""
		"&7An advanced internal component that requires multiple fine processes to manufacture. Commonly used in the assembly of complex machines such as the &eMechanical Arm&7.&r"
	]
	quest.2A3657E05759C933.quest_desc: ["&7Extremely excellent attributes across the board for the early game, but only has a &#FFAA335%&7 chance to be mined from &#66CCFFDiamond Ore&7."]
	quest.2A3657E05759C933.quest_subtitle: "Fortune's Favored"
	quest.2A56714310939AFB.quest_desc: ["&7直接提升玩家幸运值，从而影响战利品品质与掉落物质量。前期优先堆叠幸运，是回报率极高的发育策略，长远来看受益无穷。"]
	quest.2A56714310939AFB.quest_subtitle: "幸运儿"
	quest.2A8629B66F128293.quest_desc: ["&7Enough said, it sounds good, I love hearing it."]
	quest.2A8629B66F128293.quest_subtitle: "Comes with its own entrance sound effect"
	quest.2AE9864AC40241A7.quest_desc: ["提供百分比护甲值加成，缺点是会降低受治疗的倍率和附魔属性"]
	quest.2AE9864AC40241A7.quest_subtitle: "极端思维"
	quest.2AF2FF75BEEDF6FF.quest_desc: [
		"&7Increases the number of creatures the spawner spawns at once. Use with caution—don't bite off more than you can chew."
		""
		"&7Must be modified together with Ghast Tears, otherwise spawning efficiency will be affected because the spawn count cap has not been raised."
	]
	quest.2AF2FF75BEEDF6FF.quest_subtitle: "Buying from me costs at least 2000 bucks"
	quest.2B4635BB16624A15.quest_desc: [
		"&7The Spirit Altar can perform &#CC99FFSpirit Infusion crafting&7."
		"{image:kubejs:textures/gui/malum_kjs1.png width:150 height:100 align:center fit:true}"
		"&7The Spirit Altar has &e1&7 item slot, &e8&7 spirit slots, and &e8&7 extra slots. A &#FFCC44Redstone Comparator&7 can detect how full the slots are."
		""
		"&b&lSpirit Infusion:"
		"&7The recipe's main item must be placed in the &eitem slot (center of the altar)&7"
		"&#66FF99Spirits&7 must be placed in the &espirit slots (center of the altar)&7"
		"&aOther items must be placed in the &eextra slots (item pedestals, etc.)&7—specifically on nearby &#66DDCCItem Pedestals&7, &#66DDCCItem Stands&7, or the &#CC99FFRune Workbench"
		"&7(range is within &e4&7 blocks horizontally and &e3&7 blocks vertically of the Spirit Altar)."
		""
		"&7Extra slots can only interact with non-directional item transport, and after each crafting, all items in the extra slots are &ccleared&7."
		""
		"&7The &#66FF99Spirit&7 types in the spirit slots must exactly match the recipe; no extra &#66FF99Spirit&7 types are allowed."
		""
		"&7Each nearby &#FFAA33Runewood Obelisk&7 speeds up Spirit Infusion by &e25%&7, with at most &e4&7 taking effect."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"&7You can view &#CC99FFSpirit Infusion&7 recipes in &#66DDCCEMI&7."
		"{image:kubejs:textures/gui/malum/recipe.png width:125 height:160 align:center}"
		"&7The left &#FF6666red box&7 marks the required &#66FF99Spirit&7 type"
		"&7The right &#66CCFFblue box&7 marks the required &eother items&r"
		"&7The middle &#FFAA33orange box&7 marks the required &6main item&r"
		""
		"&7Place them according to the logic described on the previous page to begin &#CC99FFSpirit Infusion&7."
	]
	quest.2B4635BB16624A15.quest_subtitle: "Miraculous Creations"
	quest.2B4635BB16624A15.title: "Spirit Infusion"
	quest.2B8DFC4AE68FE112.quest_desc: [
		"&7I should now know what happens when a living being enters the well—at least, the consequences of a sapient living being entering it."
		"&7"
		"&7I was too careless during my experiments, then tripped over a reagent flask on the floor... and fell directly into the pitch-black substance in the well. The fact that I can still write this clearly means I &asurvived&r&7... though I probably won't repeat that test."
		"&7"
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"&7I was spat out by what is now confirmed to be a liquid, just like the items I threw in. I later tested with monsters and calves; they &cdid not&r&7 bounce back, but simply vanished into the well, and I had no reason to waste more resources on further testing. Besides, my attention is now entirely on what returned with me."
		"&7"
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"&7It was as if I had shattered a soul; and my soul was the only one present at the time. The thought is somewhat frightening, but all data on my bodily functions remain within acceptable range. What returned with me was also a &8black&r&7 &dSpirit Crystal&r&7, which I collected. Is this an omen of a ninth arcane energy? If so, what form of pulse does it represent? Further research is needed."
	]
	quest.2B8DFC4AE68FE112.quest_subtitle: "A Mistake, or a Blessing?"
	quest.2B8DFC4AE68FE112.title: "The Pitch-Black Crystal"
	quest.2BA0CB58302C7BD4.quest_desc: [
		"&6Pact of Tidal Affinity"
		"&7The ocean's chains tightly bind your heart.&r&cCannot receive healing when out of water"
		"&7Imprison yourself within the ocean, and remember the singing call of the tides.&r&aWhile underwater, increases movement speed, attack speed, mining speed, and damage resistance&r&aConduit Power enhances the above effects and also lets you regenerate health normally"
		"{image:kubejs:textures/gui/malum/pact_of_tidal_affinity.png width:160 height:200 align:center}"
	]
	quest.2BA0CB58302C7BD4.quest_subtitle: "One with the Sea"
	quest.2BA0CB58302C7BD4.title: "Pact of Tidal Affinity"
	quest.2C2C118EAFE0B1B7.quest_desc: [
		"&6Soul-Seeking Ember Bell&r"
		"&7Obtained by crafting. Used to summon the Boss &6Telos Echo · The Primordial Fire-Bearer&r&7.&r"
		"&7Hold and right-click to use. Upon use, it emits a sound, produces special particles, and attempts to summon the Fire-Bearer.&r"
		"&7If a &cEmber Soul Rune&r&7 is nearby, the Soul-Seeking Ember Bell will be consumed and the Fire-Bearer will be summoned; if there is no Ember Soul Rune nearby, it will not be consumed and will display '&cNo response received&r&7'.&r"
		"&7After each use, as long as it is not consumed, there is a 3-second cooldown.&r"
		""
		"&8\"A resonance bell forged to recall the 'fire seed' stolen since the world's first ignition, one that resonates only with the lament of Ember Soul Runes.\""
	]
	quest.2C2C118EAFE0B1B7.quest_subtitle: "Ding Ding Ding"
	quest.2C34F57D3538E222.quest_desc: [
		"This bookshelf is made by performing a &bInfusion&r operation on the Dormant Deep Dark Bookshelf. It provides a not-insignificant amount of enchantment values and a Tier cap of 70."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"&7What did I do?"
		"&7I seem to have thrown that crack-covered bookshelf into the Enchanting Table. Then, under the entanglement of Sculk and Deep Dark, It began to grow, to fuse. Eventually, the cracks of this bookshelf were filled by It. It became a new existence."
		"&7I felt Its more powerful force, and also felt that this bookshelf bore no ill intent. Perhaps because It is my creation. Or perhaps It needs me to do something. In any case, I now possess a more powerful bookshelf."
	]
	quest.2C34F57D3538E222.quest_subtitle: "Embrace the Sculk"
	quest.2C34F57D3538E222.title: "Sculk Energy Awakened"
	quest.2C5A0FE2059F81B1.quest_desc: ["&7A tool made for familiars. Shrunken versions of certain items/armor can be called trinkets that familiars can equip, while shrunken food can be fed to familiars to restore health. Please note that all food effects and buffs/debuffs will not take effect, so choose foods with high satiation."]
	quest.2C7083B1D7EFB4EE.quest_desc: ["Unlocked after the Fire-Bearer"]
	quest.2C7083B1D7EFB4EE.quest_subtitle: "Basic Part"
	quest.2C9F35CB08351DC4.quest_subtitle: "简单的获取，简单的提升"
	quest.2CA02120B210EB2D.quest_desc: [
		"&6Blaze Burner&r"
		""
		"&6Obtaining&r"
		"&7Obtained by right-clicking a &cBlaze&r&7 or &cBlaze Spawner&r&7 with an empty Blaze Burner.&r"
		""
		"&6Purpose / How to Use&r"
		""
		"&6Burning States&r"
		"&7The Blaze Burner needs fuel to operate. Players can right-click it while holding fuel to feed it.&r"
		"&7Feeding it normal fuel puts it into normal burning state, with burn time determined by that fuel's burn time in a vanilla &eFurnace&r&7. After normal burning ends, it enters the &cextinguished&r&7 state.&r"
		"&7Feeding it a &6Blaze Cake&r&7 puts it into super burning state. The blaze inside turns blue. One Blaze Cake sustains super burning for &c160 seconds&r&7. After super burning ends, it enters 250 seconds of normal burning, then extinguishes.&r"
		"&7Using a &6Creative Blaze Cake&r&7 on it toggles between burning modes and permanently maintains the current state.&r"
		"&7Throwing an &eEgg&r&7 at it puts it into normal burning state for 4 seconds and plays a chewing sound.&r"
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"&7The Blaze Burner's default maximum burn time is &c500 seconds&r&7.&r"
		"&7However, when a single item's burn time exceeds the 500-second cap while the Blaze Burner is &cextinguished&r&7, that item's burn cap is applied instead of the 500-second maximum. For example: a Coal Block provides 800 seconds of burn time.&r"
		"&7If the Blaze Burner is already burning, feeding it normal fuel again will not exceed the 500-second cap. For example: if the burner already has 200 seconds of burn time, feeding a Coal Block results in 500 seconds, not 800.&r"
		""
		"&7Blazes can be fed by a &eDeployer&r&7 or &eMechanical Arm&r&7. Both components automatically recognize the Blaze Burner's state and stop feeding when fuel is sufficient.&r"
		"&7When using a Mechanical Arm to feed it, if the Blaze Burner is super burning and the arm's input has sufficient Blaze Cakes, it will not enter normal burning. The arm detects the Blaze Burner's state and feeds before super burning ends. Feel free to feed.&r"
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"&6Heating Basins&r"
		"&7The Blaze Burner can supply heat to a Basin to complete '&cMixing&r&7', '&cCompacting&r&7', or '&cAutomated Brewing&r&7' recipes that require higher heat.&r"
		"&7Some Basin recipes require normal heating or super heating. Place the Blaze Burner below the Basin and provide fuel to reach the corresponding burning state. The burning state does not affect the execution of recipes requiring a lower heat level.&r"
		""
		"&6Heating Boilers&r"
		"&7The Blaze Burner can be used to heat a boiler.&r"
		"&7Normal burning and super burning states provide &c1 point&r&7 and &c2 points&r&7 of heat respectively. See Boiler for details.&r"
		""
		"&6As a Fan Heating Medium&r"
		"&7The Blaze Burner changes the airflow (wind) state of an Encased Fan.&r"
		"&7When the fan's airflow (wind) passes through a Blaze Burner, it becomes &aBulk Smoking/Bulk Blasting&r&7 airflow (wind) depending on the burning state.&r"
		"&7When the Blaze Burner is &cextinguished&r&7, the airflow (wind) operates in Bulk Smoking mode.&r"
		"&7When the Blaze Burner is in normal burning or super burning, the airflow (wind) operates in Bulk Blasting mode.&r"
		""
		"&6Redstone Comparator&r"
		"&7The Blaze Burner can be detected by a Redstone Comparator and produce a redstone signal.&r"
		"&7When the burner is &cextinguished&r&7, the redstone signal is 0.&r"
		"&7When the burner is in normal burning state, it produces at most 2 redstone signal strength. When burn time is less than 5 seconds, signal strength is 1; when burn time is greater, signal strength is 2.&r"
		"&7When the burner is in super burning state, the redstone signal is 3.&r"
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"&6Driving Trains&r"
		"&7The Blaze Burner can drive trains.&r"
		"&7To let a Blaze Burner drive a train, the player must secure the Blaze Burner in front of the Train Controls on the train structure when assembling the train. After assembly, right-click the Blaze Burner with a Train Schedule that has a set route. A hat then appears on the blaze's head, and it drives the train automatically according to the schedule's program.&r"
		""
		"&6As a Warehouse Keeper&r"
		"&7The Blaze Burner can serve as a Warehouse Keeper.&r"
		"&7When placed adjacent to a Stock Ticker, the Blaze Burner acts as the Warehouse Keeper and can be right-clicked to interact.&r"
	]
	quest.2CDE34C4A866D6AE.quest_subtitle: "Tier 1 Grading Catalyst"
	quest.2CE15B505BACCDC3.quest_desc: ["When a big shot suddenly appeared while I was writing the pack to help with items, I was absolutely delighted!"]
	quest.2CE15B505BACCDC3.quest_subtitle: "Code + Contributor"
	quest.2D0DFDD4C050FFA3.quest_desc: [
		"This bookshelf utilizes the Ancient City power entangled by Sculk, providing a brand-new ability—obtaining treasure enchantments directly at the Enchanting Table."
		"However, opportunity and risk coexist. Those curse enchantments will also appear as treasure enchantments at the Enchanting Table. But I recall there is a device that can prevent curses from attaching."
	]
	quest.2D0DFDD4C050FFA3.quest_subtitle: "The Ancient City Reappears"
	quest.2D0DFDD4C050FFA3.title: "A Gift from the Deep Dark"
	quest.2D343AAA8E8523D1.quest_desc: [
		"&7Each &#66FF99Spirit&7 harvested while worn grants a &e30&7-second &#66BB66Tumorous Growth&7 effect."
		""
		"&7If the &#66BB66Tumorous Growth&7 effect is already present, instead extend this effect by &e7.5&7 seconds (up to &e1&7 hour) and increase the current effect level by &e1&7 (up to level &e20&7)."
		""
		"&7The duration granted or extended is multiplied by the &#CC99FFArcane Resonance&7 attribute value."
	]
	quest.2D343AAA8E8523D1.quest_subtitle: "Gain a Special Effect When Harvesting Spirits"
	quest.2D740B904DAEAB78.quest_desc: [
		"&6Familiar Bed&r"
		"&7The familiar bed is a block that familiars can use to &asleep&r&7 and &arestore health&r&7. Familiars will search for nearby beds when they need healing.&r"
	]
	quest.2D740B904DAEAB78.quest_subtitle: "A Warm Home"
	quest.2D7AB1B4FC01C3F8.quest_desc: [
		"&6Empathy Driver&r"
		""
		"&7Malefic and Hallowed are opposing forces—so why not combine the two? With the Empathy Driver installed in the &eCrucible&r&7, &8Malicious Spirits&r&7 will remember the damage taken by the &eCatalyst Charm&r&7. Then, after the &eMending Diffuser&r&7 performs repairs, the &bHallowed Spirit&r&7 will 'forgive' that damage, further repairing the Catalyst Charm and granting all attributes a boost for the next three &6Focusing Cycles&r&7.&r"
	]
	quest.2D7AB1B4FC01C3F8.quest_subtitle: "Accepting Hatred"
	quest.2DCF4B22632FEAA6.quest_desc: ["&7获取难度不低，但词条强度足以让人心甘情愿。自带超绝破甲效果，削减防御的同时额外造成大量魔法伤害，物理与法术双重压制，让高抗性敌人在你面前形同虚设"]
	quest.2DCF4B22632FEAA6.quest_subtitle: "奴役巨龙实在可耻"
	quest.2DE8D48077862833.quest_desc: [
		"{\"text\":\"\",\"extra\":[{\"text\":\"Obtained by crafting, used to summon the \",\"color\":\"gray\"},{\"text\":\"Boss\",\"color\":\"red\"},{\"text\":\"\",\"color\":\"gray\"},{\"text\":\"Telos Echo · The Primordial Fire-Bearer\",\"color\":\"gold\"}]}"
		"{\"text\":\"\",\"extra\":[{\"text\":\"Hold and \",\"color\":\"gray\"},{\"text\":\"right-click\",\"color\":\"yellow\"},{\"text\":\" to use. Upon use, it emits a sound, produces special particles, and attempts to summon the Fire-Bearer.\",\"color\":\"gray\"}]}"
		""
		"{\"text\":\"\",\"extra\":[{\"text\":\"If a \",\"color\":\"gray\"},{\"text\":\"Ember Soul Rune\",\"color\":\"gold\"},{\"text\":\" is nearby, the \",\"color\":\"gray\"},{\"text\":\"Soul-Seeking Ember Bell\",\"color\":\"red\"},{\"text\":\" will be consumed and the Fire-Bearer will be summoned; if there is no Ember Soul Rune nearby, it will not be consumed.\",\"color\":\"gray\"}]}"
	]
	quest.2DE8D48077862833.quest_subtitle: "\"You should trust me and devote your life to me\""
	quest.2E49C6ACDB5A84E2.quest_desc: [
		"&6Gloomstone Golem&r&7"
		"&7Place a &#F5F5DCCarved Moonmoth Cactus Fruit&r&7 on top of a &#C0C0C0Gloomstone Bricks&r&7 block to &esummon&r&7 a Gloomstone Golem.&r"
		""
		"&7Functions similar to the &#808080Tuff Golem&r&7 once mentioned in an MC mob vote;&r"
		""
		"&7Hold any item and right-click the Gloomstone Golem, and it will &ehold the item up for display&r&7;&r"
		""
		"&7While displaying an item, the Gloomstone Golem &cdoes not move&r&7, but still turns its body toward other directions;&r"
		""
		"&7Some items with &#FF8C00special held models&r&7 also have corresponding rendering in the Gloomstone Golem's hands;&r"
		""
		"&7&#FF4500Kill&r&7 / &#FFD700right-click while holding an item&r&7 the Gloomstone Golem to retrieve the item.&r"
	]
	quest.2E49C6ACDB5A84E2.quest_subtitle: "Item Display Stone Frame"
	quest.2E49C6ACDB5A84E2.title: "Gloomstone Golem"
	quest.2E830C01A529257D.quest_subtitle: "Acropolis"
	quest.2E97A995E360F29D.quest_desc: [
		"&7The &#66DDCCBlueprint Book&7 is a tool for conveniently storing blueprints, letting you put them inside to save space. Blueprints stored inside can also be used as if they weren't stored, crafting the corresponding &#66CCFFSilent Gear&7 tools at a crafting table."
		"{image:kubejs:textures/gui/silentgear/blueprint_book.png width:160 height:140 align:center fit:true}"
		"&7After opening the Blueprint Book, use &#FFD700Ctrl+Left-click&7 to select the desired blueprint, and the Blueprint Book will switch to that type."
		"{image:kubejs:textures/gui/silentgear/blueprint_book2.png width:200 height:120 align:center}"
		"&7Of course, besides blueprints, &#66DDCCGem Tools&7 can also be placed inside."
	]
	quest.2E97A995E360F29D.quest_subtitle: "Blueprint Warehouse"
	quest.2EC1ACF371E42F03.quest_desc: [
		"&7Massive in scale, generating outward from the inner region of the &#8B4513Soul Sand Valley&7, spanning and crossing most of the &#8B4513Soul Sand Valley&7 and even multiple Nether biomes as a challenge structure;"
		""
		"&7Its main internal substructures are multiple &#FFD700\"Towers\"&7 and one &#FFD700\"Central Church\"&7. Large numbers of &#AA00AAFeigning Death Remains&7 spawn on the surface passages connecting various areas;"
		""
		"&7Players can pass through &#66CCFFSoul Glass&7 to enter and exit some substructures;"
		""
		"&7&#FFD700Towers&7:"
		""
		"&7Divided into multiple floors. Except for the bottom floor which holds a small amount of supplies, each floor spawns a &#FFD700Cunning Candle&7 for players to light and challenge;"
		""
		"&7The higher the floor, the harder the challenge brought by the &#FFD700Cunning Candle&7;"
		""
		"&7&#FFD700Central Church&7:"
		""
		"&7In front of the &#66DDCCEctoplasm Fountain&7 generated on the upper level, an &#AA00AASculk Grinding Body&7 always spawns. This fountain is also the entrance to the lower level;"
		""
		"&7&#FFD700Underground Passage&7:"
		""
		"&7Go around to the back of the &#FFD700Central Church's&7 fountain, and you can see an inconspicuous lower-level entrance. The lower level is a very long, narrow passage area (comparable to the &#FF5555Nether Fortress&7);"
		""
		"&7Here you can find the &#66DDCC\"Lower Fountain\"&7, as well as &#AA00AACrimson Fungus&7 and a large number of &#FFD700Brazier Chests&7;"
		""
		"&7Consume &#FFD700Cunning Candle Flames&7 to open &#FFD700Brazier Chests&7, which contain large amounts of valuable loot;"
		""
		"&7If you have enough patience, remember that opened &#FFD700Brazier Chests&7 can close again after &#FFAA331 hour&7 and refresh their loot."
	]
	quest.2EC1ACF371E42F03.quest_subtitle: "Pilgrim"
	quest.2EC1ACF371E42F03.title: "Find Structure: Sanctuary"
	quest.2EC244BC65F18268.quest_desc: [
		"&7Runewood logs sometimes generate as &#FFAA33Resin-Rich Runewood&7, a material with unique &#88DDFFmagical properties&7. After stripping it with an &#FFCC44axe&7, right-clicking it with a &#66DDCCGlass Bottle&7 collects &#66FF99Rune Resin&7."
		""
		"&7Processing it yields &#66FF99Rune Resin Balls&7, which can replace &#66DDCCSlimeballs&7 to some extent."
	]
	quest.2EC244BC65F18268.quest_subtitle: "Palatable Material"
	quest.2F38AC908EC156D9.quest_desc: [
		"&6Oath of Unmaker's Disdain&r"
		""
		"&7The Oath coexists with Malice Ward, and its power is also weakened by it.&r"
		"&7-Reduces &cMalice Ward&r&7 capacity&r"
		""
		"&7An etching carved into the malice soul-return.&r"
		"&7-&6Malice Critical&r&7 triggers &econtinuous slashes&r on the target"
		"&7-&6Malice Conversion&r&7 increases the number of accompanying &eslashes&r&7 and their power&r"
		"{image:kubejs:textures/gui/malum/oath_of_unmakers_disdain.png width:160 height:200 align:center}"
	]
	quest.2F38AC908EC156D9.quest_subtitle: "Above All Things"
	quest.2F38AC908EC156D9.title: "Oath of Unmaker's Disdain"
	quest.2F6AEED848143A46.quest_desc: [
		"&7After defeating it, you can craft the following blueprints:"
		""
		"&#66CCFFThunder Anchor&7, &7right-click to throw a giant &#FFD700anchor&7 at enemies; sneaking and right-clicking summons a &#66CCFFtide&7 around you."
		""
		"&#66CCFFLong Lance&7, right-click to throw a &#FFD700thunder spear&7, which generates a small-area &#66CCFFthunder pool&7 upon hitting the ground."
	]
	quest.2F6AEED848143A46.quest_subtitle: "Kill kill kill"
	quest.2F959196FB453034.quest_desc: [
		"These bookshelves are the highest-tier versions of the Sculk Bookshelf. While providing large amounts of &aTier&r, &4Quantization&r, and &5Arcana&r, they also provide extra &3Enchantment Clues"
		"&r. Personally, I recommend making several and welding them permanently next to your regular enchanting Enchanting Table."
	]
	quest.2F959196FB453034.quest_subtitle: "Listen to the Bookshelf's Heartbeat"
	quest.2F959196FB453034.title: "Warden's Enhancement — Pinnacle of Sculk Energy"
	quest.2FE49A9C24350211.quest_desc: [
		"&7Functions the same as a vanilla &#66CCFFtrident&7. &#FFAA33Charge speed&7, &#FFAA33throw damage&7, and &#FFAA33throw speed&7 can be customized through materials."
		""
		"No enchantment needed to summon lightning on hit"
	]
	quest.2FE49A9C24350211.quest_subtitle: "Big Fork"
	quest.2FE5426155A22ADD.quest_desc: [
		"&7Eating rotten food while worn (Rotten Flesh, &#66BB66Decayed Essence&7, &#FFAA33Gluttony Condensate&7):"
		""
		"&7Grants a &e30&7-second &#FF8844Gluttony II&7 effect, or raises an existing &#FF8844Gluttony&7 effect by &e2&7 levels (up to level &eX&7)."
		""
		"&7After eating &#FFAA33Gluttony Condensate&7, the &#FF8844Gluttony&7 effect's level +&e1&7 and duration +&e40&7 seconds."
	]
	quest.2FE5426155A22ADD.quest_subtitle: "Endless Hunger"
	quest.30039833D92481A3.quest_desc: ["Yes, you can have Creative Items 2.0"]
	quest.30039833D92481A3.quest_subtitle: "Endless Storage 2.0"
	quest.302E888C7909A950.quest_desc: [
		"&7The &#FFD700Cunning Candle&7 is a block in Sanctuaries (structures) used to trigger challenges;"
		""
		"&7Use a &#FFD700Flint and Steel&7 to right-click and activate the &#FFD700Cunning Candle&7:  "
		"&7Starts the challenge, and players continuously gain the &#FF6666Betrayed&7 effect during the challenge;  "
		""
		"&7While under the &#FF6666Betrayed&7 effect:  "
		"&7Blocks you place are replaced with special &#66CCFFCloud Smoke Blocks&7 (does not consume blocks from your hotbar);  "
		"&7Only players can step on &#66CCFFCloud Smoke Blocks&7 to move/be blocked. Other creatures can pass straight through &#66CCFFCloud Smoke Blocks&7, ignoring them and moving normally;  "
		"&7&#66CCFFCloud Smoke Blocks&7 automatically break after being generated for a period of time."
		""
		"&7The &#FFD700Cunning Candle&7 summons monsters around itself in waves (every &#FFAA3332 seconds/wave&7);  "
		"&7Players must protect the &#FFD700Cunning Candle&7 from being destroyed by these monsters and kill all summoned monsters to succeed in the challenge;"
		""
		"&7These monsters also have only one method to destroy the &#FFD700Cunning Candle&7:  "
		"&7Approach the &#FFD700Cunning Candle's&7 collision box and continuously deal source-less damage to it (the monster's original behavior and stats are completely independent of, and do not interfere with, its candle-destroying behavior);  "
		"&7The higher the floor the &#FFD700Cunning Candle&7 generates on, the higher its \"tier.\""
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"&7If the player succeeds in the challenge:  "
		"&7The &#FFD700Cunning Candle&7 produces a corresponding amount of &#FFD700Cunning Candle Flames&7 based on its tier;  "
		"&7For each additional player present: the &#FFD700Cunning Candle's&7 output is doubled (meaning each player ultimately receives an identical amount of &#FFD700Cunning Candle Flames&7);  "
		"&7Afterward, the &#FFD700Cunning Candle&7 enters a &#FFAA3330-minute&7 cooldown. Players must wait for the cooldown to end before activating the &#FFD700Cunning Candle&7 again."
		""
		"&7If the player fails the challenge:  "
		"&7The &#FFD700Cunning Candle&7 breaks. Players need to hold &#FFD700Honeycomb&7 and right-click the broken &#FFD700Cunning Candle&7 to repair it before they can challenge again."
		""
		"&7Based on how high up the structure the player climbs, &#FFD700Cunning Candles&7 are also divided into different &#FFAA33difficulty tiers&7;  "
		"&7You can tell its difficulty tier by the &#FFD700Cunning Candle's&7 base block (&#66DDCCBone Block&7→&#FFAA33Copper Block&7→&#66CCFFIron Block&7→&#FFD700Gold Block&7);  "
		"&7Different difficulties &#FF6666do not change the monsters' base stats&7; they only increase their spawn count to a certain extent and weaken the candle's damage resistance;"
		""
		"&7If multiple players participate in the &#FFD700Cunning Candle&7 challenge at the same time:  "
		"&7For each additional player, the &#FFD700Cunning Candle&7 spawns &#FFAA33+2&7 monsters per wave."
	]
	quest.302E888C7909A950.quest_subtitle: "The cunning enemy dares to disguise as my teammate"
	quest.302E888C7909A950.title: "Observation: Cunning Candle"
	quest.302F073922CA3873.quest_desc: ["You're a good person, I'll follow you"]
	quest.302F073922CA3873.quest_subtitle: "Without their help, Reverie Foundry wouldn't exist!"
	quest.305EC81E54A58CA7.quest_desc: ["提供弹射物速度加成与攻击力加成，做箭矢或许会很好用"]
	quest.305EC81E54A58CA7.quest_subtitle: "biubiu"
	quest.307FD783B49CA47C.title: "Discover the Cursed Pyramid"
	quest.309D32324902DF18.quest_subtitle: "Food value > 8"
	quest.309D32324902DF18.title: "Main Course Recovery x10"
	quest.30C9167F3BD42C27.quest_desc: [
		"&7Provides &#55D5D5Soul Ward capacity&7 based on &#66CCFFmagic armor&7."
		"&7Provides &#55D5D5Soul Ward recovery rate&7 based on &#66CCFFcharge value&7."
		"&7Provides &#55D5D5Soul Ward integrity&7 based on &#66CCFFmagic armor&7 and &#66CCFFcharge value&7."
		"&7Can obtain &#55D5D5pact cap&7 based on materials."
		"&7Can obtain &cknockback resistance&7 based on materials."
	]
	quest.30C9167F3BD42C27.quest_subtitle: "A Good Partner for Soul Armor"
	quest.30C9167F3BD42C27.title: "Soul Hunter Chestplate Template"
	quest.30E1A8BF53339ACD.quest_desc: ["&7A base trinket used only to increase &FF8844armor value&7 by a small amount. A necessary prerequisite for crafting its higher-tier material variants."]
	quest.30E1A8BF53339ACD.quest_subtitle: "Trinket Base"
	quest.31259F6B81819141.quest_desc: ["&7Functions the same as a vanilla &#FFD700mace&7, increasing damage based on &#FFAA33fall height&7."]
	quest.31259F6B81819141.quest_subtitle: "A Blow to the Head"
	quest.313E8F6035C2E842.quest_desc: [
		"&7The Runewood Tree is a strange fusion of magic and nature, and quite common. It is very &#FFCC44beautiful&7, but I value its &#66FF99practicality&7 more. Runewood is infused with &#88DDFFmagic&7, and thus can serve as a base material for &#CC99FFarcane arts&7."
		""
		"&7This tree mainly appears in wide &#66DD88plains&7, and also in &#66DD88forests&7. Its most distinctive feature is its &#FFCC44leaves&7, which are a bright &#FFAA33orange-yellow&7; &#66CCDDvariants&7 also include &#88DDFFcyan-blue&7 and others."
		""
		"{image:kubejs:textures/gui/malum/tree.png width:100 height:100 align:center}"
		""
		"{image:kubejs:textures/gui/malum/tree2.png width:100 height:100 align:center}"
	]
	quest.313E8F6035C2E842.quest_subtitle: "Magical Material"
	quest.314084A1E2474F20.quest_desc: [
		"&6Alchemy Cauldron&r"
		""
		"&7The Alchemy Cauldron has a light level of 3.&r"
		""
		"&6Main Functions&r"
		"&7Boil &bbottled materials&r&7 in liquid form&r"
		"&7Craft &bspecific materials&r&7"
		"&7Brew &evanilla potions&r&7"
		"&7Convert &espell scrolls&r&7 back into ink&r"
		"&7Improve &eink quality&r&7"
		"&7Refine mod-exclusive &6potions&r&7"
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"&7Note: It does not have most of the vanilla cauldron's features (such as interaction with pointed dripstone, filling with rain, washing dyed leather armor, etc.).&r"
		""
		"&6Interaction System&r"
		""
		"&6Storage Space&r"
		"&7The Alchemy Cauldron contains three storage spaces:&r"
		"&7&eWater Level&r&7: Four water levels, corresponding to different liquid heights in the cauldron&r"
		"&7&eMaterial Slots&r&7: Four material slots, can hold various materials&r"
		"&7&ePotion Slots&r&7: Four potion slots, used to store liquid products&r"
		""
		"&6Capacity Description&r"
		"&7Each water level stores one bottle of water (250mB), full water level can store one bucket of water (1B)&r"
		"&7Each potion slot can store one bottle of &eink&r&7, &epotion&r&7, &6potion&r&7, or other special liquids&r"
		"&7Each material slot can store one material, and materials will float or sink in the cauldron&r"
		""
		"&6Basic Operations&r"
		""
		"&6Placing Items&r"
		"&7Use a water bucket to raise the water level to level four. Use water bottles to raise it by one level each&r"
		"&7Using potions, reagents, or special liquids will occupy one potion slot&r"
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"&7Placeable materials include:&r"
		"&7Vanilla &ebrewing materials&r&7"
		"&7&eInk upgrade&r&7 materials (copper ingots, iron ingots, gold ingots, amethyst shards, etc.)&r"
		"&7Mod &6potion&r&7 materials (dragon's breath, ender pearls, amethyst clusters, Stone of Repentance, etc.)&r"
		""
		"&6Collecting Items&r"
		"&7Empty hand right-click: Take out one item from a material slot&r"
		"&7Empty bottle right-click: Prioritize collecting from potion slots; when potion slots are empty, collect water bottles&r"
		"&7Automation support: Can be input through hoppers, observers detect state changes, dispensers automatically collect products&r"
	]
	quest.31B0A26B1374A322.quest_desc: [
		"&6Spark Bird&r"
		"&7A small bird usually only encountered in Starlight Forest (excluding its variant Starlight Thicket), skilled at flying, very friendly and cute."
		"&7Has two appearance variants, &#FF6B6Bred&r&7 and &#1E90FFblue&r&7. The &#FF6B6Bred variant&r&7 is far more common than the blue variant."
		""
		"&7You can find the accompanying &eSpark Bird Nests&r on nearby Moonlight Trees."
		"&7Spark Birds usually actively &aclaim&r&7 one nearby Spark Bird Nest or &eSpark Bird House&r&7 for resting and breeding."
		"&7If they take a long time to claim one, place &8seeds&r&7 in the nest/house, or try to use the nest/house they initially claimed."
		"&7Each Spark Bird Nest / Spark Bird House can hold at most &b2&r&7 adult Spark Birds and several baby Spark Birds or Spark Bird Eggs at once."
		""
		"&7Players need to hold &8seeds&r&7 and actively right-click to &afeed&r&7 two Spark Birds."
		"&7After the breeding animation completes, one of the Spark Birds will fly to its claimed Spark Bird Nest / Spark Bird House and lay an &eegg&r."
		"&7If Spark Birds have not successfully claimed a Spark Bird Nest / Spark Bird House, they may &cbe unable to breed successfully&r."
		""
		"&7Eggs need a certain amount of time before hatching into baby Spark Birds."
		"&7At this point, you can choose to hold Shift + right-click the nest/house with an empty hand to take out the Spark Bird Egg inside."
		"&7A taken Spark Bird Egg can also be placed back by holding Shift + right-clicking with the egg in hand."
		"&7Note! If the nest/house is &cbroken by mining&r&7, the egg inside will be &cspoiled&r as a result."
		""
		"{@pagebreak}"
		""
		"&7Baby Spark Birds have no flight ability and will not leave the nest/house until they mature."
		"&7Baby Spark Birds that have not left the nest/house &ccannot be interacted with via items&r&7 (e.g. feeding seeds to speed up growth)."
		"&7If needed, you can break the nest/house, in which case the baby birds will automatically leave the nest/house and allow player interaction."
		""
		"&7Of course, when breaking the nest/house with an axe enchanted with &bSilk Touch&r&7, all adult Spark Birds, baby Spark Birds, Spark Bird Eggs, and seeds placed by the player inside will be &astored&r&7 in this nest/house."
		"&7After the player places this nest/house again, they will also be restored intact within the nest/house."
		""
		"&7Players can place any kind of &8seeds&r&7 in a Spark Bird Nest / Spark Bird House (up to &b5&r at once)."
		"&7When there are still seeds in the nest/house claimed by a Spark Bird, that Spark Bird will &aconsume&r&7 them and fly toward you when leaving the nest/house, then spit out &b1~2 kinds&r&7 of random items for you."
		""
		"&7The items a Spark Bird can gift to the player are drawn from the following loot table."
		"&7Among them, &eStarfire (item)&r&7 is the Spark Bird's &6exclusive output&r."
		"&7This is a &6very important resource&r&7 and the core material for crafting some &6tier-two equipment&r&7."
	]
	quest.31B0A26B1374A322.quest_subtitle: "Round and Plump"
	quest.31B0A26B1374A322.title: "Spark Bird"
	quest.31B78363809DB5AF.quest_desc: [
		"&7Functions the same as other &#CC99FFIron's Spells staves&7. Holding it in the left hand also grants the effect bonus, with the bonus intensity determined by materials."
		""
		"&7Determined by &6Silent Gear&7 attributes:"
		"&7• Spell Power &7→ &#CC99FFSpell Power&7"
		"&7• Spell Resistance &7→ &#CC99FFSpell Resistance&7"
		"&7• Mana Regeneration &7→ &#66FFCCMana Regeneration&7"
		"&7• Max Mana &7→ &#CC99FFMax Mana&7"
	]
	quest.31B78363809DB5AF.quest_subtitle: "Arcane Amplification"
	quest.321BA6F89B9F2F5E.quest_desc: ["&7A relatively rare but powerful &#66CCFFgem material&7 found in mines. It doesn't reduce attack speed and has extremely high durability. Though production is limited and can't be mass-produced, a single piece performs well enough to handle most early-game enemies."]
	quest.321BA6F89B9F2F5E.quest_subtitle: "Heart of Bedrock"
	quest.32590328D9FB113D.quest_desc: [
		"{\"text\":\"\",\"extra\":[{\"text\":\"Trinkets can be \",\"color\":\"gray\"},{\"text\":\"merged and upgraded\",\"color\":\"aqua\"},{\"text\":\" like in Terraria. Some simple \",\"color\":\"gray\"},{\"text\":\"mobility trinkets\",\"color\":\"yellow\"},{\"text\":\" can speed up early exploration. A very small number of trinkets are \",\"color\":\"gray\"},{\"text\":\"disabled due to being too powerful\",\"color\":\"red\"},{\"text\":\" (Flying Carpet: why me)\",\"color\":\"gray\"}]}"
		""
		"{\"text\":\"\",\"extra\":[{\"text\":\"Defeating the \",\"color\":\"gray\"},{\"text\":\"Wither\",\"color\":\"red\"},{\"text\":\" has a chance to \",\"color\":\"gold\"},{\"text\":\"drop\",\"color\":\"gray\"},{\"text\":\" the \",\"color\":\"gray\"},{\"text\":\"Demon Heart\",\"color\":\"light_purple\"},{\"text\":\". Using it increases \",\"color\":\"gray\"},{\"text\":\"accessory slots\",\"color\":\"aqua\"},{\"text\":\", but it has a \",\"color\":\"gray\"},{\"text\":\"usage limit\",\"color\":\"red\"}]}"
	]
	quest.3280E06AA7147B28.quest_desc: [
		"&7Basic trinket, no special mechanics."
		"&7Attributes are determined by &6Silent Gear&7 material traits."
	]
	quest.3280E06AA7147B28.quest_subtitle: "Can only be worn on the arm"
	quest.32EC8C6D17383BB2.quest_desc: ["&cQuantization (0%~100%):&r &7Fluctuates your final enchantment level, raising the cap while lowering the floor. The Enchanting Table defaults to 15%"]
	quest.332CE7AF2598E3F1.quest_desc: [
		"Summon it via the Altar using the Shadow Orb; once the ritual succeeds, the final BOSS will be summoned at the Altar immediately, just like other summoning rituals"
		""
		"It is extremely powerful—proceed with caution"
	]
	quest.332CE7AF2598E3F1.quest_subtitle: "&4Audience"
	quest.3368D9266C268467.quest_subtitle: "Familiar Summoning Ritual"
	quest.337B0F8208EA7383.quest_desc: [
		"&6Placing Ink&r"
		"&7The quality of the ink determines the quality of the scroll.&r"
		""
		"&6Placing Paper&r"
		"&7Writing a scroll consumes one sheet of paper.&r"
		""
		"&6Placing School Materials&r"
		"&7&eSchool materials&r&7 determine the spell school.&r"
		"&7After placing &eschool materials&r&7, the spells that can be written will be displayed. Some spells may display a question mark icon; try using higher-tier ink to write them.&r"
		"&7The written scroll is located here. Note that only taking it out with a left-click will consume the raw materials.&r"
		""
		"List of materials required for different schools is as follows:"
		"&7Abyss: Crystallized Coral / Crystallized Coral Shard"
		"&6Blaze: Blaze Rod / Charred Bone"
		"&aHarmonic Spirit: Note Block"
		"&3Frost: Ice / Frozen Bone"
		"&bLightning: Lightning Bottle"
		"&eHoly: Holy Pearl"
		"&5Ender: Ender Pearl"
		"&4Crimson: Crimson Essence Bottle"
		"&aEvocation: Emerald"
		"&2Nature: Poisonous Potato"
		"&1Hex: Echo Shard"
		"&dIllusion: Infused Starstone"
	]
	quest.337B2D306A06DD6D.quest_desc: [
		"{\"text\":\"\",\"extra\":[{\"text\":\"Holding and \",\"color\":\"gray\"},{\"text\":\"right-clicking\",\"color\":\"yellow\"},{\"text\":\" will cause a \",\"color\":\"gray\"},{\"text\":\"Desert Eye\",\"color\":\"gold\"},{\"text\":\" copy to fly from the player's hand toward the nearest \",\"color\":\"gray\"},{\"text\":\"Cursed Pyramid\",\"color\":\"gold\"},{\"text\":\", while the Desert Eye in the player's hand enters a \",\"color\":\"gray\"},{\"text\":\"3s\",\"color\":\"yellow\"},{\"text\":\" cooldown.\",\"color\":\"gray\"}]}"
		""
		"{\"text\":\"\",\"extra\":[{\"text\":\"The flight function only works in the \",\"color\":\"gray\"},{\"text\":\"Overworld\",\"color\":\"green\"},{\"text\":\". It will not work in the \",\"color\":\"gray\"},{\"text\":\"Nether, the End\",\"color\":\"red\"},{\"text\":\", or worlds without a Cursed Pyramid.\",\"color\":\"gray\"}]}"
	]
	quest.337C34C06A879409.quest_desc: [
		"This upgraded Deep Dark Bookshelf channels its power into Quantization, providing large amounts of &4Quantization&r without providing &5Arcana&r."
		"(Important Bookshelf)"
	]
	quest.337C34C06A879409.quest_subtitle: "Chaotic Power Surges"
	quest.337C34C06A879409.title: "Sculk Growth — Soul Bargain"
	quest.339C3EB0CB099097.quest_desc: [
		"&7So far, every &6Charm&r&7 I have made has been put to practical use. Side effects naturally followed, and I had to spend much time choosing suitable charms. However, these charms can certainly have certain effects isolated from them."
		"&7"
		"&7&6Rune Crafting&r&7 begins here, with the specific tools being the &dBrooch&r&7 and the &eRune&r&7. The brooch exists only as a base core; its wearing position is close to the heart, symbolizing the inherent painful price within rune power."
		"&7"
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"&7Rune Crafting starts with inscribing &eRunes&r&7, an operation that must be done at the &bRune Workbench&r&7, so one should be crafted first. The simplest entry-level brooch is the &dRune Brooch&r&7, which can be used to wear the runes I create."
	]
	quest.339C3EB0CB099097.quest_subtitle: "The Needle of Insight"
	quest.339C3EB0CB099097.title: "Rune Crafting"
	quest.33CD4086B68C7B42.quest_desc: [
		"&7When a &#AA00AAPhantom&7 approaches a &#AA00AACorpse-Eating Gargoyle Statue&7, it transforms into a &#66DDCCSoulless One&7"
		""
		"&7You can also eat &#AA00AASoul-Bound Meat&7 near a &#FFAA33Blaze&7 to transform it into a &#66DDCCSoulless One&7"
	]
	quest.33CD4086B68C7B42.quest_subtitle: "Cold Bones"
	quest.340694D4FDC5A098.quest_desc: ["&7Can be reliably produced with a Level 10 Enchanting Table. This material significantly strengthens the base attributes of &#66CCFFOsmium Ingots&7 and brings a considerable &#FFD700experience bonus&7. Well-rounded performance with excellent value—an indispensable practical choice."]
	quest.340694D4FDC5A098.quest_subtitle: "Enchantment Amplifier"
	quest.346013B6D966C7F2.quest_desc: ["A hundred flowers bloom!"]
	quest.346013B6D966C7F2.quest_subtitle: "Usually unlocked only after defeating the Skeleton King"
	quest.3462310EEE3AC2DF.quest_desc: ["会试图把容器中的物品输入"]
	quest.3462310EEE3AC2DF.quest_subtitle: "向RS网络输入物品或流体"
	quest.34AFC6414A805C2D.quest_desc: [
		"&7Recovery method: eat a &#FFD700Golden Apple&7, &#FFD700Enchanted Golden Apple&7, &#FFD700GoodApple&7, or enter the command &#66CCFF/reveriefoundry soulfading reset <player>&7."
		""
		"&7Fragile Soul was reworked in 1.2. If you are transferring a save from a 1.1-series version, please use the &#66CCFF/rf deathsystem&7 series of commands to disable the old Fragile Soul, then use the old commands to recover before death refreshes the state."
	]
	quest.34AFC6414A805C2D.quest_subtitle: "&cYou lose max health every time you die"
	quest.34AFC6414A805C2D.title: "&c\"Death Is the Process of Discarding Yourself\""
	quest.34D446AE0315168C.quest_desc: [
		"&7Right-click to deal an attack to entities in front that &#FF6666ignores invincibility frames&7."
		"&7Damage = &cmelee damage ÷ 5&7."
		""
		"&7Of course, you can also use it as an &#66DDCCaxe&7, except it can't be used for skinning."
	]
	quest.34D446AE0315168C.quest_subtitle: "Zzzap"
	quest.34D5717A03B609A1.quest_desc: [
		"&6Rune of Spell Mastery&r"
		""
		"&7The Rune of Spell Mastery reflects mimicked arcane energy, allowing me to charge &estaves&r&7 at double speed.&r"
	]
	quest.34D5717A03B609A1.quest_subtitle: "Creating Things of Destruction"
	quest.34F5839A32156AF0.title: "Discover the Acropolis"
	quest.350A83A36269F87B.quest_desc: ["&7Finally, I produced an experimental substrate called \"&6Alchemical Mineral Dust&r&7.\" Its texture is close to solid animal fat under normal conditions, but applying just a little force reveals its powerful &aplasticity&r&7. This must be a useful &6material&r&7."]
	quest.350A83A36269F87B.quest_subtitle: "Clay Number Two"
	quest.3530C0A36931A1D6.quest_subtitle: "Blast Miner"
	quest.3531099CA2E8832A.quest_desc: [
		"&6Rune of the Bountiful Catch&r"
		""
		"&7The Rune of the Bountiful Catch functions similarly to the ritual of the same name, granting the wearer a half-strength &bBountiful Catch&r&7 effect, providing a bonus equivalent to an extra level of the &eLure&r&7 enchantment.&r"
	]
	quest.3531099CA2E8832A.quest_subtitle: "Blessed Pulse"
	quest.35560F1953AD1C76.quest_subtitle: "Familiar Summoning Ritual"
	quest.357A96DA2D1987CE.quest_subtitle: "永恒力量"
	quest.35957B7E0ACF4060.quest_desc: [
		"&6Super Glue&r"
		""
		"&6Purpose&r"
		"&7This viscous medium can glue multiple blocks into a single unit, allowing dynamic structure components to recognize and assemble them into a unified &edynamic structure&7.&r"
		""
		"&6Gluing Blocks&r"
		"&7Right-click one block to set the start point, then right-click a second block. All blocks within the rectangular space formed by the two points are glued, and a \"Super Glue\" entity is generated as a marker.&r"
		"&7There must be actual blocks connecting the two selected blocks, otherwise the highlight box turns yellow and the gluing cannot be completed.&r"
		"&7When holding Super Glue and aiming at a block, press Ctrl to highlight in blue all glued blocks associated with that block.&r"
		"&7If Super Glue is placed in the off-hand, blocks placed by the main hand automatically glue to the right-clicked block.&r"
		"&7When using a Schematicannon to print a schematic containing Super Glue, place Super Glue with sufficient durability in the chest in advance; the cannon will complete the gluing automatically.&r"
		""
		"&6Removing Glue&r"
		"&7Hold Super Glue and left-click a block within any glued rectangle to delete that glue frame and remove all associated gluing.&r"
		""
		"&8A small dried glue stain clings to the manuscript's edge, with a scrawled note beside it: Easy to stick together, not hard to pull apart either—just remember not to glue your own hands.&r"
	]
	quest.35957B7E0ACF4060.quest_subtitle: "Time to start gluing"
	quest.359B24E94B66AFA3.quest_desc: ["Spawns automatically upon entering the End. To respawn the Ender Dragon, place 4 End Crystals around the portal. The Ender Dragon has not been buffed, so you can more or less steamroll it—and farm Replica Gel from it"]
	quest.359B24E94B66AFA3.quest_subtitle: "Stage 3"
	quest.35AEBBC251933E78.quest_desc: [
		"Naturally spawns in the Bitter Cold Prison structure; defeat the Aptrgangr to obtain the Strange Key and open the sealed Door of Seal at the bottom, then right-click the Cursed Tombstone to activate the fight. Can be located using the Cursed Eye, and can also be summoned via the Altar."
		""
		"&7After defeating it, you can craft the following blueprints:"
		""
		"&#66CCFFAnnihilator&7, has higher &#FFAA33critical damage&7 than other weapons. When dual-wielding, hold right-click to perform a &#FFD700Slam&7, dealing damage to nearby entities."
		""
		"&#66CCFFWar Halberd&7, right-click to &#FFD700Charge&7, producing &#CC99FFspear thrusts&7 along the charge path at enemies; sneaking and right-clicking produces &#CC99FFspear thrusts&7 at nearby enemies."
		""
		"&#66CCFFCursed Bow&7, fires homing &#66CCFFghost arrows&7 at enemies."
	]
	quest.35AEBBC251933E78.quest_subtitle: "Stage 2"
	quest.35B14862D3D903B2.quest_desc: ["&7The most outstanding stat-wise among common Stage One ores. Requires a &#66CCFFDiamond Pickaxe&7 or better to mine. Its advantage is being usable immediately upon mining, with no tedious processing required."]
	quest.35B14862D3D903B2.quest_subtitle: "Excellent Basic Material"
	quest.35C26E629284AC1A.quest_desc: [
		"&7需要到处找疣猪兽……优秀的握柄材料，加成均衡还有个壁垒做赠品，但是获取不是很轻松。"
		""
		"&7上位浸血疣猪皮属性与其完全一致，只多了猩红法术强度加成，不再单独列出。"
		""
		"推荐部位：握柄，插板"
	]
	quest.35C26E629284AC1A.quest_subtitle: "为什么猪皮加法强……"
	quest.35FDA2B4446874E0.quest_desc: ["Increases the player's reach distance. The value of the Gibbon should go without saying"]
	quest.35FDA2B4446874E0.quest_subtitle: "Short is also cute!"
	quest.35FFD854DFF94776.quest_desc: [
		"&7To overcome the limitation of wireless terminals losing connection when too far away..."
		""
		"Setting up wireless access points to expand signal coverage and building a base-station-like architecture may be a more viable solution."
	]
	quest.35FFD854DFF94776.quest_subtitle: "WiFi"
	quest.360AE4AB3B482FAC.quest_desc: [
		"&nCrime and Reputation System&r"
		""
		"&eTrading with villagers slightly increases reputation, up to a maximum of 25."
		""
		"&6Core Mechanics"
		"&b1. &3Crime Levels&r"
		"Criminal acts are divided into three levels, affecting the player's relationship with villagers:"
		""
		"&aLight Crime&r: Slightly lowers reputation."
		""
		"&eMedium Crime&r: Significantly lowers reputation; &cIron Golems or Guards&r will attack the player."
		""
		"&cHeavy Crime&r: Reputation drops to the minimum; &4Iron Golems will immediately attack the player&r."
		""
		"&b2. &3Trigger Conditions&r"
		"Players must perform the act within a &9protected structure&r (by default, villages only)."
		"A villager or guard must &6witness&r the criminal act (detection distance is affected by the player's invisibility, sneaking, and light level)."
		"&4Villagers have limited \"intelligence.\" Even if the player is the one who placed the block, breaking it is still considered theft."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		""
		"&6Criminal Act List"
		"&b1. &3Breaking Blocks&r"
		"&aLight Crime&r: Breaking crops, hay bales, lanterns, campfires, etc."
		"&eMedium Crime&r: Breaking chests, barrels, workstation blocks (such as cartography tables), beds."
		"&cHeavy Crime&r: Breaking bells."
		"&b2. &3Interacting with Blocks&r"
		"&eMedium Crime&r: Opening chests or barrels (considered attempted theft)."
		"&b3. &3Killing Creatures&r"
		"&eMedium Crime&r: Killing passive animals (pigs, cows, chickens, etc.) or villagers' pets (cats, horses, etc.)."
		"&b4. &3Bed-Related&r"
		"&aLight Crime&r: Shooing a villager off a bed."
		"&eMedium Crime&r: Occupying a bed already claimed by a villager."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		""
		"&6Witnessing and Detection&r"
		"&bWitness Range&r"
		"Detection distance is affected by the following factors:"
		""
		"&7Sneaking&r reduces the chance of being discovered."
		"&5Low light or invisibility potions&r can hide criminal acts."
		"&bWitness Reactions&r"
		"&cIron Golems and Guards&r will attack players who commit &eMedium Crimes&r or &cHeavy Crimes&r (if witnessed)."
		"&aLight Crimes&r only lower reputation and do not trigger attacks."
		"&bOf course, you can also slaughter where other villagers can't see"
	]
	quest.360AE4AB3B482FAC.quest_subtitle: "Reputation"
	quest.3611F55056F7105F.quest_desc: [
		"&7&#66FF66Gluttony&7  "
		"&7When eating any food:  "
		"&7If health is not full: each point of hunger the food provides &#66FF66restores 2 health&7  "
		"&7If health is full: gain a &#66FF66random positive buff&7 lasting &#FFAA3330 seconds&7  "
		"&7Other players within &#FFAA335 blocks&7 also &#FFD700restore an equal amount of hunger and saturation&7"
	]
	quest.3611F55056F7105F.quest_subtitle: "Gluttony Erosion"
	quest.3611F55056F7105F.title: "Gluttony Erosion"
	quest.3616639AFFC791CE.title: "Sword Weapons"
	quest.363CDDFE0664CBE2.quest_desc: [
		"&7Obtained by throwing &#66FF66Beetroot Seeds&7 into the &#CC99FFVoid Well&7.  "
		"&8&mDamn, which beet came up with this recipe&r&r"
		""
		"Or found in the Devil's Misfortune structure in the Nether"
		""
		"&7Can only be planted by right-clicking into a &#FFD700Skeleton Skull&7."
		"  "
		"&7After planting, destroying it returns the &#FFD700Skeleton Skull&7 and &#FF8E9EBrainheart Cabbage Seeds&r;  "
		""
		"&7The Brainheart Cabbage crop grows over time. When fully mature, players can &#66CCFFright-click directly to harvest&7;  "
		"&7Harvesting always drops &#FFAA335&7 Brainheart Cabbages, with a very low chance to drop &#FFAA331&7 Brainheart Cabbage Seed."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"&7Bone Meal can also &#66FF66accelerate&7 the Brainheart Cabbage crop;"
		""
		"&7However, if the player continues to use Bone Meal on the Brainheart Cabbage crop when it is mature and has enough space above:  "
		"&7It will cause the Brainheart Cabbage crop to grow into a &#66DDCCBrain Tree&7 on the spot;"
		""
		"&7The Brainheart Cabbage crop &#FF6666cannot grow naturally&7 into a Brain Tree;"
		""
		"&7After the Brain Tree has grown, the player must also &#FFD700right-click the Brainheart Cabbage crop with an empty hand&7 once (pulling out its stem), and only then will the Brainheart Cabbage crop return to its previous growth mode (otherwise it stops growing)."
	]
	quest.363CDDFE0664CBE2.quest_subtitle: "Ahhh!!! Brain... brain is trembling trembling trembling!!!"
	quest.364547BCDEFB8DDE.quest_desc: [
		"&6Portable Storage Interface&r"
		""
		"&7When a structure begins to rotate or slide, those golden interfaces fixed on a &edynamic structure&r&7 seem to awaken. As long as it detects another similar \"face\" looking at it within the correct distance, it pours out all items from its container in the direction of that invisible agreement.&r"
		""
		"&6Getting It to Work&r"
		"&7This requires some careful arrangement: the two interfaces must &cface each other&r&7 and be &cexactly 1 to 2 blocks&r&7 apart. Also, at least one of them must belong to a &edynamic structure&r&7—motion is what gives this exchange meaning.&r"
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"&7Don't be troubled by occasional slight misalignment during docking; the transmission contract remains valid.&r"
		""
		"&6Finer Control&r"
		"&7Combined with an &eItem Detector&r&7 or &eStock Converter&r&7, you can know the contents of a dynamic container. A simple redstone signal can &alock&r&7 the block-form interface, making it ignore passing companions—though from the outside, you can't see any change.&r"
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"&7Finally, remember the rule of elegance: &cexcessive movement speed or rotation speed&r&7 makes this handshake rushed and prone to failure. If the receiving side is stationary, be sure to equip it with a &eHopper&r&7 or &eChute&r&7; it needs a \"hand\" to catch that flowing gift.&r"
		""
		"&8Here in the manuscript is a rough sketch of two docked interfaces, with a note beside it: They hate bumps, but love to dance.&r"
	]
	quest.364547BCDEFB8DDE.quest_subtitle: "An interface for exchanging items, allowing containers on dynamic structures to interact with the outside world."
	quest.3656700FBAEA1A3A.quest_desc: [
		"&7If you throw any item upward, the dropped item will &#66CCFFslowly pass&7 through Insight Glass, which can achieve an &#FFD700item filtering&7 function to a certain extent. Creatures &#FF6666cannot pass through&7 Insight Glass."
		""
		"How to use:"
		""
		"&7&#66FF66Whitelist Mode&7:"
		"&7First, place any one type of item into the Insight Glass;"
		"&7Afterward, except for that type of item, no item can &#FF6666pass through&7 this block."
		""
		"&7&#FF6666Blacklist Mode&7:"
		"&7Insight Glass turns red after receiving a &#FFD700redstone signal&7, entering &#FF6666Blacklist Mode&7;"
		"&7In Blacklist Mode, except for (the item placed inside) that type of item, any item &#66CCFFcan pass through&7 this block."
		""
		"&7You can attach a &#FFD700Hopper&7 + any container (such as a chest) below this block;"
		"&7In &#66FF66Whitelist Mode&7: this logistics line can &#66CCFFfocus solely on collecting&7 the one item type you specify;"
		"&7In &#FF6666Blacklist Mode&7: this logistics line can &#FF6666filter out&7 the one item type you specify and collect other items."
		""
		"&7Besides that, simply putting items into Insight Glass also gives a bit of a &#FFD700displaying collectibles&7 feel, useful for decorating your building's interior."
	]
	quest.3656700FBAEA1A3A.quest_subtitle: "I will forever time you..."
	quest.366BD92ABD4B70A0.quest_desc: ["&7Obtained through &#66CCFFfishing&7. You can stack &#FFD700Luck&7 to increase the catch chance. Has Stage 2 stats."]
	quest.366BD92ABD4B70A0.quest_subtitle: "I am the Sea King!"
	quest.36713AC6F99D301E.quest_desc: [
		"&7Sometimes, matter can also be infused with the &6energy of souls&r&7, even though the matter itself has no soul."
		""
		"&7This is precisely the foundation of &6Spirit Magic&r&7—attaching souls to soulless things. &6Soulstone&r&7 is a mineral whose arcane nature surpasses its physical nature; once refined, it has many uses in the magic I study. It radiates &dmagical energy&r&7 intensely."
	]
	quest.36713AC6F99D301E.quest_subtitle: "Anomalous Phase"
	quest.369E5D74EA1CA624.quest_desc: ["&7Big enough to hold everything... or is it. It has a huge cargo space and can move your whole household along, but it falls far short of the Sophisticated Backpack panel—so it probably doesn't qualify for the job."]
	quest.36DB408ECAE73BC5.quest_desc: [
		"&7Right-click to fire a &#CC99FFspell charge volley&7. Dealing &#FFAA33burning damage&7 restores spell charges."
		"&7Left-click attacks can set enemies &#FFAA33on fire&7."
		""
		"&7Determined by &6Silent Gear&7 attributes:"
		"&7• Magic Damage &7→ &bSpell Damage&7 and &dCharge Capacity&7"
		"&7• Attack Speed &7→ &6Charge Speed&7"
	]
	quest.36DB408ECAE73BC5.quest_subtitle: "A More Advanced Staff"
	quest.36DC8D2564CAC70C.quest_desc: [
		"&7Deeprock Aurum is a strange and very useful metal. Its physical appearance is identical to &6gold&r&7, but its properties are &cvastly different&r&7."
		""
		"&7This ore can be found in the underground &8deepslate layer&r&7, buried within veins full of &6gold ore&r&7."
	]
	quest.36DC8D2564CAC70C.quest_subtitle: "Fused with Arcane"
	quest.37AB4AF2D44BDEB1.quest_desc: [
		"&5I discovered a... structure&r&7. Its implications are deeper than almost anything I have found before; its very existence is proof that someone has already stepped into arcane research."
		""
		"&7I call this well the \"&5Weeping Well&r&7,\" because it continuously emits an &5aura of sorrow&r&7, and within it is a small pool of... &5substance&r&7."
		""
		"&7I cannot quite determine what that substance is. Though it does not look like a liquid, physically speaking it is certainly not a solid either."
		""
		"&7The Arcane Compendium in my backpack even emitted an &6unusual radiance&7, as if it had gained a will of its own, wanting to be thrown into the well."
	]
	quest.37AB4AF2D44BDEB1.quest_subtitle: "&zAn Urge to Jump In"
	quest.37B8C9432DCC6DAD.quest_desc: ["&7By common sense, a place resembling the Nether must contain combustible substances, and &cBlaze Quartz&r&7 is one such substance. It is similar to &8coal&r&7, and can even be used to craft &etorches&r&7. Though relatively &7mundane&r&7, its uses are not few."]
	quest.37B8C9432DCC6DAD.quest_subtitle: "Nether Coal"
	quest.37E8E57C588A9106.quest_subtitle: "Quickly add doors"
	quest.37EDF1917F18D163.quest_desc: ["稀少而强力的全能型材料，全方位提升装备性能，缺点是获取不易"]
	quest.37EDF1917F18D163.quest_subtitle: "全面增幅"
	quest.3801B9633700F23D.quest_desc: [
		"&6Pact of Wyrd Reconstruction&r"
		""
		"&7The burning star makes you decay.&r"
		"&7-&cWyrd Reconstruction&r&7 has an extremely long cooldown&r"
		"&7-While on cooldown, &cArcane Resonance&r&7 is halved&r"
		"&7-Harvesting Spirits consumes &chunger&r"
		""
		"&7The unrestrained might brought by Death itself.&r"
		"&7-&6Wyrd Reconstruction&r&7 can prevent death&r"
		"&7-&6Wyrd Reconstruction&r&7 grants brief &ainvincibility&r&7 and rapidly triggers &bSpirit harvesting&r&7 effects"
		"{image:kubejs:textures/gui/malum/pact_of_wyrd_reconstruction.png width:160 height:200 align:center}"
	]
	quest.3801B9633700F23D.quest_subtitle: "Deceiving Fate"
	quest.3801B9633700F23D.title: "Pact of Wyrd Reconstruction"
	quest.38092862F38315D2.quest_subtitle: "A handy tool for finding the nearest Ancient City"
	quest.3834AAC7BBB3BDAF.quest_desc: [
		"&6Rune of Vitality&r"
		""
		"&7The Rune of Vitality urges the form to heal itself, increasing &aall healing received&r&7 by the wearer by roughly one fifth.&r"
	]
	quest.3834AAC7BBB3BDAF.quest_subtitle: "A Pulse That Spurs Mending"
	quest.3847F6BA291E6556.quest_desc: [
		"Through &bInfusion&r upgrading, the Ocean Bookshelf gains even more powerful magic, providing higher &aTier&r and &5Arcana&r."
		"&l(Recommended Bookshelf)&r"
	]
	quest.3847F6BA291E6556.quest_subtitle: "Better Arcana and Tier"
	quest.3847F6BA291E6556.title: "Mysterious Magic Enhancement"
	quest.388B4D246EC83BC4.quest_desc: [
		"&6Pact of the Lifeweaver"
		"&7All living things deserve &acare&r&7.&r&cThe healing aura makes no distinction between friend and foe"
		"&7Rarely seen is such &agenerosity&r&7: you share your skin and will with others.&r&aNormal health regeneration&r&aHealing is shared with nearby creatures"
		"{image:kubejs:textures/gui/malum/pact_of_the_lifeweaver.png width=160 height=200 align=center}"
	]
	quest.388B4D246EC83BC4.quest_subtitle: "Bestowing Upon All"
	quest.388B4D246EC83BC4.title: "Pact of the Lifeweaver"
	quest.3890E1D60D9F389F.quest_desc: [
		"&6Rune of Defense&r"
		""
		"&7The Rune of Defense urges the form to hold fast, increasing the wearer's &aarmor value&r&7 by roughly one fifth.&r"
	]
	quest.3890E1D60D9F389F.quest_subtitle: "A Pulse That Spurs Endurance"
	quest.38AC7ED986231005.quest_desc: ["&7前期即能提供不俗的伤害加成与经验获取效率，是开荒阶段性价比极高的选择。"]
	quest.38AC7ED986231005.quest_subtitle: "我有fomo台"
	quest.38C6EDEB38BC8B99.quest_subtitle: "Enable the setting for Eternal Gates to spawn naturally in the End"
	quest.39138773ED14B1BA.quest_desc: [
		"Directly solved the biggest problem Codfish had since starting the pack"
		""
		"Also, why are there so many bugs"
	]
	quest.39138773ED14B1BA.quest_subtitle: "Balance Design + Contributor"
	quest.396C3E0A51A61D92.quest_desc: ["&7Right-click to perform a &#FFD700slam&7 on the ground, dealing area damage. When the holder is below &#FF6666half health&7, adds &#FFAA33fire damage&7."]
	quest.396C3E0A51A61D92.quest_subtitle: "Bang!"
	quest.3983E32C1CEC4DAA.quest_desc: ["如果你玩镰刀，灵魂露珠提供的镰刀加成可以有效提升前期的伤害"]
	quest.3983E32C1CEC4DAA.quest_subtitle: "廉价好用"
	quest.39980DF0631D9B6C.quest_desc: [
		"&6Pact of the Profane Ascetic&r"
		""
		"&7Your loyalty to corruption ravages your form.&r"
		"&7-&cSaturation and hunger&r&7 cannot restore health&r"
		"&7-The Oath permits eating only &8corrupted food&r&7; eating food it forbids deals &cdamage&r"
		""
		"&7Corruption becomes your best friend.&r"
		"&7-&6Gluttony&r&7 becomes &6Trial of Faith&r"
		"&7-&6Trial of Faith&r&7 increases &ahealing received&r&7 and produces &blocusts&r&7 when healing"
		"&7-&6Trial of Faith&r&7 lasts significantly longer&r"
		"&7-Eating &8corrupted food&r&7 restores health&r"
		"{image:kubejs:textures/gui/malum/pact_of_the_profane_ascetic.png width:160 height:200 align:center}"
	]
	quest.39980DF0631D9B6C.quest_subtitle: "Seeking Beauty in Dregs"
	quest.39980DF0631D9B6C.title: "Pact of the Profane Ascetic"
	quest.39AB32E04D04B64F.quest_desc: [
		"Can be summoned via the Altar"
		""
		"&7Special drops mainly include: Shadow Scales, Worm Scarf, Foul Flesh."
		""
		"&7Has a small chance to drop a random Seven Deadly Sins trinket."
	]
	quest.39AB32E04D04B64F.quest_subtitle: "Stage 1"
	quest.39EB3B61CB5E3E73.quest_desc: [
		"&7A set of spell robes."
		""
		"&7Can obtain &#CC99FFSpell Power&7, &#CC99FFSpell Resistance&7, and &#66FFCCMana Regeneration&7 based on materials."
		"&7Can obtain &#55D5D5pact cap&7, &#55D5D5healing multiplier&7, and &cknockback resistance&7 based on materials."
	]
	quest.39EB3B61CB5E3E73.quest_subtitle: "Less defensive than other armor, but specialized against spell-related attributes"
	quest.39F72CD10646574F.quest_desc: ["&7Finding specific entries among hundreds of enchantments is like searching for a needle in a haystack. Type-limited enchanted books can significantly improve this—such books only have affinity for a specific category of enchantments, making them an excellent way to obtain target enchantments."]
	quest.39F72CD10646574F.quest_subtitle: "Practical Enchanting"
	quest.3A08D5D6D65FF6F2.quest_desc: [
		"&7The tomb contains multiple branches and a large number of &#66CCFFundead&7 spawners. A small number of rooms contain &#FF6666traps&7, so check carefully before opening chests."
		""
		"&7The &#FF6666King of the Dead&7 sleeps on the throne in the central hall of the tomb. The hall also contains spawners and continuously spawns &#66CCFFZombies&7. Prepare before the fight. Right-click the sleeping &#FF6666King of the Dead&7 to awaken him."
		""
		"&mWait, why don't I just ambush him.&r"
	]
	quest.3A08D5D6D65FF6F2.quest_subtitle: "Pry it open (∠・ω< )⌒★"
	quest.3A08D5D6D65FF6F2.title: "Underground Tomb"
	quest.3A1009BCADB2C895.quest_desc: [
		"&7The &#66DDCCSalvager&7 is a great helper for recycling materials. It gives you different output content based on the input."
		""
		"&7&#FFD700Input some vanilla equipment:  "
		"&7Produces the &#66FF66raw materials&7 used to craft them."
		"{image:kubejs:textures/gui/silentgear/salvager2.png width:180 height:100 align:center}"
		"&7&#FFD700Input Silent Gear:  "
		"&7&#66FF66Salvages&7 &#66CCFFSilent Gear&7."
		"{image:kubejs:textures/gui/silentgear/salvager.png width:180 height:100 align=center}"
		"See the next page for more"
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"&7&#FFD700Input Silent Gear parts:  "
		"&7Produces the &#66FF66raw materials&7 used to craft the part. However, note that &#FF6666tool handles cannot be salvaged&7."
		"{image:kubejs:textures/gui/silentgear/salvager3.png width:180 height=100 align=center}"
		"See the next page for more"
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"&7&#FFD700Input Silent Gear alloys:  "
		"&7If the input quantity equals the alloy's mix count (for example, I have a three-in-one alloy of iron, copper, and gold, and I input &#FFAA333&7 of this alloy into the Salvager), then the alloy's materials are &#66FF66fully returned&7!  "
		"&7The Salvager will output: &#66CCFFIron&7 x1, &#66CCFFCopper&7 x1, &#66CCFFGold&7 x1."
		"{image:kubejs:textures/gui/silentgear/salvager6.png width=180 height=100 align=center}"
		"&7If the input quantity is less than the alloy's mix count (for example, I have a three-in-one alloy of iron, copper, and gold, and I input &#FFAA331&7 of this alloy into the Salvager), then the alloy's materials are &#FFD700randomly returned&7!  "
		"&7The Salvager will output: one random raw material among &#66CCFFIron&7, &#66CCFFCopper&7, and &#66CCFFGold&7."
		"{image:kubejs:textures/gui/silentgear/salvager7.png width=180 height=100 align=center}"
		"See the next page for more"
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"&7&#FFD700Input Silent Gear materials:  "
		"&7Produces &#FFAA331~5 tier&7 Grading Catalysts based on material rarity.  "
		"&7You can view each material's &#FFD700probability&7 in EMI."
		"{image:kubejs:textures/gui/silentgear/salvager5.png width=140 height=160 align=center}"
	]
	quest.3A1009BCADB2C895.quest_subtitle: "Salvage! Salvage! Salvage Everything!"
	quest.3A3892760CA0F960.quest_desc: ["让任意武器皆可触发精魂收割效果，无需拘泥于镰刀流派。若你追求精魂体系却不愿被武器类型束缚，这款材料便是为你量身打造的不二之选"]
	quest.3A3892760CA0F960.quest_subtitle: "灵魂触媒"
	quest.3A5D807E30DF3E8C.quest_desc: [
		"&7Whatever profession you pursue or goal you strive for, &creds tone&r&7 is an indispensable aid."
		"&7Building &cpiston doors&r&7 is not the exclusive domain of engineers. Now I too have contributed to the advancement of redstone&7."
		""
		"&7By inscribing the pulse of &eElemental Spirits&r&7 into a &6copper substrate&r&7 treated with &bSpirit Fire&r&7, four kinds of interesting &creds tone devices&r&7 can be crafted."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"&6Signal Wave Transient"
		"&7The &#66DDCCSignal Wave Transient&7 maintains output strength equal to input strength, and after input strength decreases, extends the previous output strength for a period of time."
		""
		"&7The &#66DDCCSignal Wave Transient&7 can be placed horizontally; when placed, the ◉ side is the input and the other side is the output."
		""
		"&7When &#66FF66input strength&7 > &#FF8844output strength&7, creates a scheduled tick with a &e1&7 redstone tick delay."
		"&7When &#66FF66input strength&7 < &#FF8844output strength&7, creates a scheduled tick according to its frequency."
		""
		"&7When that scheduled tick takes effect, changes the &#FF8844output strength&7 to the current &#66FF66input strength&7."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"&6Signal Wave Interrupter"
		"&7The &#66DDCCSignal Wave Interrupter&7 is similar to an adjustable-delay repeater and maintains output strength equal to input strength."
		""
		"&7The &#66DDCCSignal Wave Interrupter&7 can be placed horizontally; when placed, the ◉ side is the input and the other side is the output."
		"Total delay is frequency + (&e1&7 redstone tick). After &e1&7 redstone tick, if the input strength still equals the pending strength, the output will not update."
		""
		"&7When &#66FF66input strength&7 ≠ &#FF8844output strength&7:"
		"&7&#FF8844output strength&7 = &#88DDFFpending strength&7: creates a scheduled tick with a &e1&7 redstone tick delay; when that scheduled tick takes effect, changes the &#88DDFFpending strength&7 to the current &#66FF66input strength&7;"
		""
		"&7Otherwise: creates a scheduled tick according to its frequency; when that scheduled tick takes effect, changes the &#FF8844output strength&7 to the &#88DDFFpending strength&7."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"&6Signal Wave Sustainer"
		"&7The &#66DDCCSignal Wave Sustainer&7 slowly increases or decreases output strength toward input strength."
		""
		"&7The &#66DDCCSignal Wave Sustainer&7 can be placed horizontally; when placed, the ◉ side is the input and the other side is the output."
		"When input strength ≠ output strength, creates a scheduled tick according to its frequency; when that scheduled tick takes effect, changes the output:"
		""
		"&#66FF66input&7 > &#FF8844output&7: output strength +&e1&7;"
		"&#66FF66input&7 < &#FF8844output&7: output strength -&e1&7."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"&6Signal Wave Generator"
		"&7The &#66DDCCSignal Wave Generator&7 is similar to a redstone clock, sending pulses at intervals, inverting input strength during the pulse, and otherwise keeping output strength equal to input strength."
		""
		"&7The &#66DDCCSignal Wave Generator&7 can be placed horizontally; when placed, the ◉ side is the input and the other side is the output."
		"When placed, creates a scheduled tick with a &e1&7-second delay."
		""
		"&7The period is frequency + (&e5&7 game ticks):"
		""
		"&7Normally, creates a scheduled tick according to its frequency;"
		"&7When inverted, creates a scheduled tick with a &e5&7 game tick delay."
		""
		"&7When that scheduled tick takes effect, changes output strength: normally &#FF8844output strength&7 = &#66FF66input strength&7; when inverted, &#FF8844output strength&7 = &e15&7 - &#66FF66input strength&7."
	]
	quest.3A5D807E30DF3E8C.quest_subtitle: "Signal Modulation"
	quest.3A5D807E30DF3E8C.title: "Signal Wave Crafting"
	quest.3A5DD56949CF4827.quest_desc: [
		""
		"{image:kubejs:textures/gui/key_reload.png width:150 height:40 align:center}"
		""
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"Of course, due to some mod reasons, please manually set the <key combination> key group to the B key"
	]
	quest.3A5DD56949CF4827.quest_subtitle: "The modpack's default keys are already configured. You just need to find Key Bindings and click (Reset All Keys)."
	quest.3AEB318A46096D60.quest_desc: [
		"&7This structure is extremely small, formed by piles of various &#AA00AAvariant Netherrack&7 from this mod and other &#FF5555red blocks&7. Very messy;"
		""
		"&7Inside, it spawns a small amount of mature &#66DDCCBrainheart Cabbage crops&7, &#DDDDDDSuspicious Gravel&7, and &#FFD700Nether Gold Ore&7;"
		""
		"&7This structure is the only way to obtain &#66DDCCBrainheart Cabbage Seeds&7 in normal progression."
	]
	quest.3AEB318A46096D60.quest_subtitle: "Why it's called this, I don't know either"
	quest.3AEB318A46096D60.title: "Find Structure: Devil's Misfortune"
	quest.3B0E439056FB5B0B.quest_desc: [
		"&7Backpacks can be fitted with multiple &#66DDCCupgrades&7. The number of upgrade slots is directly related to the backpack's &#66CCFFtier&7. The &#66CCFFDiamond Backpack&7 has &#FFAA33five&7 upgrade slots, while the &#CC99FFNetherite Backpack&7 has &#FFAA33seven&7. So increasing your backpack tier is the only way to install more upgrades."
		""
		"Common upgrades are listed on the right"
	]
	quest.3B0E439056FB5B0B.quest_subtitle: "Upgrade your backpack!"
	quest.3B3B3605F4F0AC43.quest_desc: ["Not attractive enough after all..."]
	quest.3B3B3605F4F0AC43.quest_subtitle: "Some Item Textures Provided"
	quest.3B7226A9387FD816.quest_desc: [
		"&7Passive Abilities"
		""
		"&7Damage Reduction: When not ignited by fire, all attack damage the Moonvine Colossus takes is &cforcibly reduced to 1 point&7;"
		""
		"&7Phase Two"
		""
		"&7The Moonvine Colossus enters a phase-transition animation when its health ≤ 50%. The eye at the stamen position becomes a mouth full of sharp teeth and roars loudly;"
		""
		"&7During the phase-transition animation, the Moonvine Colossus is not immune to attack damage and does not release attack moves; after entering Phase Two, the Moonvine Colossus unlocks new attack moves, while its original attack moves can still be used during Phase Two."
	]
	quest.3B7226A9387FD816.quest_subtitle: "Cursed Flower"
	quest.3B98D98415628260.quest_desc: ["This chapter only exists because enough people asked about it. The stuff inside isn't important (and there might not be much of it either)."]
	quest.3B98D98415628260.quest_subtitle: "This chapter is full of things Codfish made on a &mwhim&r"
	quest.3B98D98415628260.title: "Whimsical Ideas"
	quest.3BB2417F411ABDDE.quest_desc: [
		"{\"text\":\"\",\"extra\":[{\"text\":\"Important crafting material\",\"color\":\"gold\"}]}"
		""
		"{\"text\":\"\",\"extra\":[{\"text\":\"If you want to craft some \",\"color\":\"gray\"},{\"text\":\"Boss summoning items\",\"color\":\"red\"},{\"text\":\", or some \",\"color\":\"gray\"},{\"text\":\"novel materials\",\"color\":\"aqua\"},{\"text\":\", then you will absolutely need it.\",\"color\":\"gray\"}]}"
		""
		"&7It is also a crafting material for various eyeballs. This means that after defeating the King of the Dead, the End softlock is already gone, and before that, players are not advised to enter the End."
	]
	quest.3BB2417F411ABDDE.quest_subtitle: "First Glimpse of the Path"
	quest.3BBDB096C8442119.quest_desc: [
		"&7Hold right-click to charge, dealing &#FFAA33massive damage&7 to entities within a certain range in front."
		""
		"&7Releases after fully charging for &c60 ticks (3 seconds)&7."
		"&7Summons &c10&7 flame pillars in front, continuously dealing damage."
		"&7Flame pillar damage = &cattack power ÷ 4&7, with an additional 2% max health damage."
		"&7Flame pillar radius = &c1 + attack power × 0.05&7, max &c2&7."
		""
		"&7Cooldown is dynamically determined by &6Silent Gear's&7 &eattack speed&7 attribute. Higher attack speed means shorter cooldown, max &c200 ticks (10 seconds)&7."
	]
	quest.3BBDB096C8442119.quest_subtitle: "I Am Fire!"
	quest.3C4F9B874C336EB6.quest_desc: [
		"# &cBUG Report Channels &r"
		""
		"### &eHow to Report &r"
		"&6➤ &fOfficial group chat"
		"&6➤ &fSubmit an Issue on GitHub"
		""
		"&6If Codfish sees it, it'll be handled ASAP!!!"
		""
		"### &9Official Links &r"
		"&6▪ &bGitHub Issues: "
		"&fhttps://github.com/DrowningFish233/Reverie-Foundry/issues"
		"&6▪ &bMC Encyclopedia Page: "
		"&fhttps://www.mcmod.cn/modpack/907.html"
		""
		"### &3Notes &r"
		"&7- When reporting, please try to provide:"
		"  &8• &fDetailed reproduction steps"
		"  &8• &fRelevant screenshots/logs"
		"  &8• &fModpack version info "
	]
	quest.3C4F9B874C336EB6.quest_subtitle: "Oh no!"
	quest.3C8D7934954DA215.quest_subtitle: "并不能透视"
	quest.3CCFC8763640AC83.quest_desc: [
		"&6Mechanical Arm&r"
		""
		"&6Moving Items&r"
		"&7The Mechanical Arm is the most flexible logistics method in the Create mod, able to move items between any two points within its work range.&r"
		"&7The Mechanical Arm is powered by gears. The faster the rotation speed, the faster it works. Its work range is roughly a sphere with a radius of &c5&r&7 (three-dimensional space).&r"
		"&7A Mechanical Arm can move at most one stack of items at a time.&r"
		""
		"&6Placement&r"
		"&7Using a Mechanical Arm requires setting input and output targets. The arm picks up items at the input end and places them at the output end, as follows:&r"
		"&7Hold the Mechanical Arm and right-click the position to set. One right-click sets it as an input (blue); two right-clicks set it as an output (yellow). Multiple inputs or outputs can be set. After setting, place the Mechanical Arm. Targets outside its work range are automatically removed. Left-click during setting to cancel.&r"
		"&7Note that the Mechanical Arm can only target '&eopen storage spaces&r&7', such as Conveyor Belts, Depots, Chutes, etc. Vanilla Hoppers and Chests cannot be set as targets.&r"
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"&7All usable work targets include (red marks can only be output ends):&r"
		"&7Conveyor Belts, Chutes (Smart Chutes), Depots, Ejectors, Basins, Mechanical Crafters, Millstones, Deployers, powered Mechanical Saws, Jukeboxes, Train Stations, Packagers, Repackagers, Blaze Burners (empty Blaze Burners), Crushing Wheel Controllers, Composters, Respawn Anchors, Create Funnels in input mode, Campfires (Soul Campfires).&r"
		"&7Placing the Mechanical Arm against the bottom face of a block makes it inverted.&r"
		""
		"&6Distribution Methods&r"
		"&7If the Mechanical Arm has multiple output ends, you can set how it distributes between them. Long-press right-click the panel on the side of the arm's base to configure.&r"
	]
	quest.3CDB29B0059175A8.quest_desc: [
		"&6Familiar Soul&r"
		"&7The core material for manifesting a familiar into the world. This item is obtained by capturing a &8Lost Soul&r&7 on the &6Origin Island&r&7 using an empty bottle. Bottled souls can be released back into the wild.&r"
	]
	quest.3CDB29B0059175A8.quest_subtitle: "Lost Souls"
	quest.3D277D76C151604A.quest_desc: ["&7自带永恒词条，彻底免除耐久忧虑。基础属性极为扎实，省心与强力兼得，是长久征战中的可靠基石。"]
	quest.3D277D76C151604A.quest_subtitle: "亘古之持"
	quest.3D485A80778437EF.quest_desc: [
		"&aTier (0~100):&r&7 Determines the maximum enchantment level the Enchanting Table can enchant. Maximum enchantment level = Tier level."
		""
		"&7The vanilla Tier cap is 30, so the Tier cap vanilla bookshelves can reach is also 30. If you want higher-level enchantments, you need the power of Apotheosis bookshelves..."
		""
		"&7The higher the Tier, the better the enchantment results naturally, and it can far exceed the vanilla enchantment level limit."
	]
	quest.3D58537D375B1FB6.quest_desc: ["Physical attributes obtained from materials reduced by 75%"]
	quest.3D58537D375B1FB6.quest_subtitle: "Magic Scythe! Stable! Stable!"
	quest.3D58537D375B1FB6.title: "Arcane Scythe Template"
	quest.3D65B82D6967E302.quest_desc: [
		"&7Compared to storage blocks, &#66DDCCStorage Disks&7 are a more space-efficient design. A &#66DDCCDisk Drive&7 only takes up one block of space and can hold eight &#66DDCCStorage Disks&7."
		""
		"&7&#66DDCCDisks&7 require &#66DDCCStorage Components&7 and &#66DDCCDisk Housings&7 to craft. &#66DDCCStorage Components&7 start from &#FFAA331k&7 and are crafted upward from there. Making a &#FFAA3364k&7 storage component requires making &#FFAA3327&7 1k components, &#FFAA3336&7 basic processors, &#FFAA3312&7 advanced processors, and &#FFAA334&7 elite processors, consuming a large amount of &#66CCFFquartz&7."
		""
		"&7Since the &#FF6666Nether&7 is not suitable for early-game entry, if you want to craft large-capacity disks as soon as possible, it's more recommended to enchant &#FFD700Fortune&7 and head deep into the Overworld to find natural &#66CCFFquartz geodes&7. With &#FFD700Fortune III&7, one geode can meet the needs of a &#FFAA3364k&7 disk. You can also consider relying on &#66CCFFLapis Lazuli&7 parts stacked with large amounts of &#FFD700Luck&7 to loot ruins. Some ruin chests can produce &#66CCFFquartz&7, and with high &#FFD700Luck&7, almost one chest can yield a stack of &#66CCFFquartz&7."
		""
		"&7Hold a &#66DDCCDisk&7 and shift-right-click to extract the &#66DDCCStorage Component&7 from the disk. The same applies to &#66DDCCStorage Blocks&7."
	]
	quest.3D65B82D6967E302.quest_subtitle: "Plug and Play"
	quest.3D65B82D6967E302.title: "Disk Storage"
	quest.3D71CE179BBC6433.quest_desc: [
		"&6Tower Squid Air Sac&r&7"
		"&7Material dropped after killing a &#1E90FFTower Squid&r&7 (creature);&r"
		""
		"&7Cannot be used as a substitute for &8vanilla Ink Sacs&r&7 in other crafting recipes.&r"
	]
	quest.3DFF41190EEED602.quest_desc: ["Yes, you can have Creative Items"]
	quest.3DFF41190EEED602.quest_subtitle: "Endless Storage"
	quest.3E76BD1AEDBFF421.quest_desc: ["&7对远程伤害有较好提升，负面属性在武器制作中几乎可以忽略不计。纯粹而高效的远程增幅组件"]
	quest.3E76BD1AEDBFF421.quest_subtitle: "天体力量"
	quest.3E8F381CC8783800.quest_desc: ["提供可观的攻击伤害加成和护甲值加成，一件可能强不到哪去，但是覆层怎么都能打上去好几件的"]
	quest.3E8F381CC8783800.quest_subtitle: "现在知道坚守者为什么那么肉了"
	quest.3ED42E95C5C052BC.quest_desc: [
		"&7A sub-biome of the &#66CCFFSoul Sand Valley&7;"
		""
		"&7On top of the existing &#55D5D5Soul Sand&7, &#55D5D5Soul Soil&7, &#55D5D5Pale Soul Slate&7 and other base blocks, this biome condenses large numbers of giant ice spikes made of &#66CCFFBlack Ice&7, &#66CCFFBlack Thin Ice&7, and &#66CCFFBlack Icicles&7;"
		""
		"&7Around these giant ice spikes, &#66DDCCSoul Permafrost&7, &#66DDCCSoul Tendrils&7, and other monsters that can spawn in the &#66CCFFSoul Sand Valley&7 will also generate;"
		""
		"&7Black snowflake particles continuously fill this biome, and the color tone of the constituent blocks themselves makes &#FF6666visibility extremely low&7 here."
		""
		"&7&#66CCFFBlack Thin Ice&7 only generates above lava, making lava lakes or lava sea shores look like frozen lakes;"
		""
		"&7&#66DDCCSoul Permafrost&7 tends to generate in concentrated clusters only in certain surface areas, with coverage far lower than &#55D5D5Soul Sand&7/&#55D5D5Soul Soil&7 but still common."
	]
	quest.3ED42E95C5C052BC.quest_subtitle: "Baby, eat some ice!"
	quest.3ED42E95C5C052BC.title: "Black Glacier"
	quest.3F1E59D47DB55A82.quest_desc: ["{\"text\":\"\",\"extra\":[{\"text\":\"I know you might get a headache seeing this mod's \",\"color\":\"gray\"},{\"text\":\"eyes\",\"color\":\"red\"},{\"text\":\", but now they can all be \",\"color\":\"gray\"},{\"text\":\"crafted\",\"color\":\"green\"},{\"text\":\".\",\"color\":\"gray\"}]}"]
	quest.3F1E59D47DB55A82.quest_subtitle: "Craftable"
	quest.3F36E58182CFD1EA.quest_desc: [
		"&7Right-click to cast &#66CCFFIon Slash&7."
		""
		"&7Increases &#66CCFFThunder Spell Power&7 based on &#FFAA3310%&7 of &#CC99FFmagic damage&7, cap = attack power × &#FFAA331.5&7."
		""
		"&7Every &#FFAA3310 points&7 of attack damage increases spell level by &#FFAA331&7 and mana cost by &#FFAA3315&7."
		"&7Cooldown = &#FFAA33200 ÷ attack speed&7 ticks (&#FFAA3320 ÷ attack speed&7 seconds)."
	]
	quest.3F36E58182CFD1EA.quest_subtitle: "Zzzap"
	quest.3F3E9DDBDE86C19C.quest_desc: [
		"&#55D5D5Sanity &7changes based on &#66CCFFplayer traits&7, &#CC99FFweapon traits&7, taking damage, &#55D5D5player states&7, and more. You can also use certain items to &#66FF66adjust &#55D5D5Sanity"
		""
		"&7Without holding &#888888Miscellaneous traits&7"
		""
		"&#FF6666Conditions that lower Sanity:"
		"&7When your condition worsens, &#55D5D5Sanity &7begins to drain:"
		""
		"&7Health below &#FFAA33&l30%&7: &#55D5D5Sanity &7continuously drops"
		"&7Health below &#FF6633&l15%&7: &#55D5D5Sanity &7drains twice as fast"
		""
		"&7Taking heavy damage directly reduces &#55D5D5Sanity:"
		""
		"&7Single hit exceeds &#FFAA3350%&7 of max health: &#FF6666lose 10 Sanity"
		"&7Single hit exceeds &#FFAA3330%&7 of max health: &#FF6666lose 5 Sanity"
		""
		"&#66FF66Conditions that raise Sanity:"
		"&7When well-fed (&#FFDD44hunger &7≥ &#66FF6616&7) and healthy (above &#66FF8875%&7), &#55D5D5Sanity &7slowly recovers"
		""
		"&#66CCFFTrait Effects"
		"&7Your &#66CCFFplayer traits&7 and &#CC99FFweapon traits&7 change the rate at which &#55D5D5Sanity &7drains or recovers. The specific effect depends on the type of trait you hold"
		""
		"&#CC99FFItem Adjustments"
		"&7Some items can directly &#66FF66restore or lower &#55D5D5Sanity&7, or temporarily change the rate at which &#55D5D5Sanity &7changes"
	]
	quest.3F3E9DDBDE86C19C.quest_subtitle: "&zAdvanced Understanding"
	quest.3F3E9DDBDE86C19C.title: "Sanity's Effects and Changes"
	quest.3F4F2D1D8EC995BA.quest_desc: [
		"&7A Redstone Comparator lets the spawner be controlled by redstone."
		"&7With this modification installed, the spawner will only start working when it receives a redstone signal. This provides a more direct control method for automated mob farms."
	]
	quest.3F4F2D1D8EC995BA.quest_subtitle: "Redstone Spawner"
	quest.3F65163CBB21A321.quest_desc: [
		"&7The &#FF6666King of the Dead&7 is a main questline boss. Defeating him unlocks Stage One."
		""
		"&7Before challenging the &#FF6666King of the Dead&7, you can also try defeating other &#FFAA33Stage 0 BOSSES&7 to obtain materials and further strengthen your equipment. Specific boss stages can be viewed in the &#66CCFFBOSS List&7."
		""
		"&7Although the &#FF6666King of the Dead&7 mostly uses spell attacks, since &#FFD700Iron's Spells is iron physics&7, you don't need to specifically prepare magic resistance; regular armor is enough."
	]
	quest.3F65163CBB21A321.quest_subtitle: "Sprint, go"
	quest.3F65163CBB21A321.title: "Prepare for Battle"
	quest.3F95B455EACD5B91.quest_desc: ["为玩家工具提供全方位加成"]
	quest.3F95B455EACD5B91.quest_subtitle: "全面提升"
	quest.3FA1E5E68F50BA85.quest_desc: [
		"&7这种器械可以实时监控存储网络里的某种物品，要选择你想监控的物品，请空手潜行右键打开面板调整"
		""
		"空手左键物品图标可以直接取出物品，右键存入物品"
	]
	quest.3FA1E5E68F50BA85.quest_subtitle: "实时监控"
	quest.3FB8B9BB50F88F62.quest_subtitle: "A handy tool for finding a Nether Fortress"
	quest.3FC49807F1694CE5.quest_desc: ["&7自带永恒词条，持有后彻底告别耐久焦虑。数值极其扎实，一劳永逸之余，战力亦毫不妥协，是追求省心与强度兼备的理想之选。"]
	quest.3FC49807F1694CE5.quest_subtitle: "永恒力量"
	quest.3FD324391F9D0115.quest_desc: ["This summoning ritual can only be performed in the Golem Forge"]
	quest.3FD324391F9D0115.quest_subtitle: "Starlight Golem"
	quest.3FD324391F9D0115.title: "Summoning Ritual"
	quest.3FD3535AE922834F.quest_desc: [
		"&7The number of BOSSes you defeat raises your (personal) Rank."
		""
		"Eating a \"&bGood Apple&r\" or killing the final BOSS lowers your Rank by 1."
		""
		"&bRank affects:"
		"&7The rarity of Silent Gear items obtained from Gear Bags."
		""
		"&7The spawn rate of Champion mobs and the chance of higher-tier Champions appearing."
	]
	quest.3FD3535AE922834F.quest_subtitle: "&zYou believe you're ready to face the challenge, and most importantly, you feel Lady Luck smiling upon you. Time to embark on an adventure of your own!"
	quest.3FFA3C2B5E1FC24A.quest_desc: [
		"&6Cursed Garden&r"
		"&7is a large surface structure guarded by the &cMoonvine Colossus&r&7."
		""
		"&7The entire Cursed Garden is a &8large maze&r built from various high walls."
		"&7Each of the four outer walls generates a &8narrow passage&r&7, while the central endpoint is a very flat and &aspacious area&r."
		""
		"&7All &6loot chests&r&7 are distributed within the maze passages. Both the maze passages and the endpoint generate large numbers of &#8FBC8FVine Remains&r&7 as guards."
		"&7You can use the &eEye of Seeking&r&7 to locate this structure."
		""
		"&4The Moonvine Colossus has high damage reduction when not ignited"
	]
	quest.3FFA3C2B5E1FC24A.quest_subtitle: "A garden that was once lush and verdant is now eroded by a curse."
	quest.3FFA3C2B5E1FC24A.title: "Cursed Garden"
	quest.401A3487AEA60E00.quest_subtitle: "A handy tool for finding the Ancient Battlefield"
	quest.4073FA79B270F976.quest_desc: [
		"&7优秀的生存类材料，本体直接制作护甲强度较低，但可以作为合金材料。"
		""
		"&7灵魂触媒词条可以提供大量灵魂护盾相关的增益，同时还能增加镰刀熟练度。"
		""
		"&7灵魂护盾是一种独立的减伤机制，无加成情况下对魔法伤害减免极高，对物理伤害减免一般。镰刀熟练度可以直接增加镰刀武器的攻击倍率。"
		""
		"&7击碎灵魂词条可以让非镰刀击杀也能产出精魂，即便不使用镰刀武器也可以在日常收集精魂用于灵灾。"
		""
		"&7此外魂染钢衬板可以作为插板材料，但不能提供灵魂护盾，效果转变为增加誓令数量上限。"
		""
		"推荐部位：盔甲任意位置"
	]
	quest.4073FA79B270F976.quest_subtitle: "叠甲，过"
	quest.40AAE3AB0A6C05DF.quest_desc: [
		"The pack was originally made just for a get-together with friends. Later the ideas grew more ambitious, and then... Reverie Foundry was born"
		""
		"P.S. The great steward!"
	]
	quest.40AAE3AB0A6C05DF.quest_subtitle: "Some Writing + Some Planning + Contributor"
	quest.40ACEE794ED65B95.quest_desc: [
		"&7&#FFD700What is an alloy?&7  "
		"&7An alloy is a new material formed by placing multiple materials into an &#66DDCCAlloy Machine&7. An alloy's attributes are determined by all its sub-materials together, with the &#FFAA33first placed material&7 having the greatest influence on the final attributes."
		""
		"&7&#FFD700Alloy Attribute Calculation Mechanism&7  "
		"&7Alloy attributes use a &#FFAA33weighted average&7 biased toward the first material (alloy attributes ≈ weighted average of all sub-material attributes, with the 1st material weighted the most)."
		""
		"&7Relying on &#66CCFFSilent Gear's&7 alloy mechanics, multiple materials can be fused into one via the &#FFD700Alloy Machine&7. During fusion, the first material serves as the base for modification, and traits are overwritten by higher-tier traits of the same type. This means you can pair the stats of high-tier materials with the &#66FF66useful traits&7 of low-tier materials to freely customize your ideal material."
		""
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"&7Next, let me explain the &#FFD700Alloy Machine interface&7, which also applies to any working block of the same alloy machine nature."
		"{image:kubejs:textures/gui/silentgear/crude_mixer.png width=200 height=100 align=center click_action:none:}"
		"&7The left &#FF6666red box&7 contains the &#66CCFFinput slots&7, used to place [Silent Gear materials];  "
		"&7The right &#FFD700orange box&7 contains the &#66CCFFoutput slot&7, used to output the produced alloy;  "
		"&7The bottom &#66FF66green box&7 contains the &#FFD700on/off&7 button for the Alloy Machine. Click to toggle."
	]
	quest.40ACEE794ED65B95.quest_subtitle: "Alloy!"
	quest.40C75417213642DC.quest_desc: [
		"Found in the Golem Forge structure in the Starlight Dimension; can also be summoned via the Altar"
		""
		"&7Special drops mainly include: Oxidized Alloy Smelter, Oxidized Golem Steel Ingots, Shard of the Beyond."
		""
		"&7Has a small chance to drop a random Seven Deadly Sins trinket."
		""
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"&7Passive abilities"
		""
		"&7Damage limit:  "
		"&7While in the Guard Break state, the total damage the Starlight Golem takes cannot exceed &#FFAA332/3&7 of its maximum health."
		""
		"&7Invincibility (Phase 1 only): while not in the Guard Break state, the Starlight Golem &#FF6666is immune to all damage&7."
		""
		"&7Energy (Phase 1 only):  "
		"&7The Starlight Golem can hold up to &#FFAA33100&7 energy;  "
		"&7Each move consumes a certain amount of energy, and even if the remaining energy is insufficient for a move's cost, the Starlight Golem can still use that move (unless remaining energy is 0);  "
		"&7Energy consumption never goes negative—when it reaches 0, the Starlight Golem immediately enters the Charging state;  "
		"&7Each time the Starlight Golem is hit by a thrown Subzero Test Tube, its energy &#FF6666decreases by 3&7."
		""
		"&7Energy block charging (Charging state)  "
		"&7The Starlight Golem always starts in the Charging state;  "
		"&7Afterward, it only enters the Charging state again once every &#FFAA3390 seconds&7;  "
		"&7While charging, the Starlight Golem cannot attack, and the four energy blocks around it continuously charge it;  "
		"&7While charging, the Starlight Golem recovers &#66FF660.4&7 health per second;  "
		"&7Once charging completes, the Starlight Golem regains &#FFAA33100&7 energy;  "
		"&7The player must &#FF6666extinguish&7 all energy blocks charging the Starlight Golem (by right-clicking / shooting arrows or other projectiles at them), otherwise it remains invincible;  "
		"&7Once all are extinguished: the Starlight Golem enters the Guard Break state."
		""
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"&7Guard Break state  "
		"&7It runs concurrently with the Charging state; after successfully entering the Guard Break state, the Starlight Golem &#FF6666is no longer immune&7 to damage it takes until the current Charging state ends;  "
		"&7After taking at most &#FFAA337&7 hits, the Starlight Golem forcibly exits both the Charging and Guard Break states and resumes attacking;  "
		"&7The Guard Break state lasts at most &#FFAA3360 seconds&7;  "
		"&7If the Starlight Golem enters Phase 2, any ongoing Charging and Guard Break states are also forcibly ended."
		""
		"&7Phase 2  "
		"&7When the Starlight Golem's remaining health ≤&#FFAA3320%&7:  "
		"&7It loses its invincibility passive and permanently stops switching between the Charging and Guard Break states;  "
		"&7From this point on, the player can freely attack the Starlight Golem with normal means and deal damage;  "
		"&7In this phase, the Starlight Golem's body trembles continuously with sparks flying, occasionally producing the same red-flash effect as when it takes damage (but the red flash here is purely visual—the Starlight Golem has no passive that drains its own health)."
	]
	quest.40C75417213642DC.quest_subtitle: "Stage 1"
	quest.41555B67D70627EB.quest_subtitle: "Who can kill me!"
	quest.417E7341644D16C8.quest_desc: [
		"&6Pact of Rune Exploitation"
		"&7Your soul has its carrying limit.&r&cEach equipped rune reduces healing received, armor value, armor toughness, and magic resistance by one twentieth"
		"&7A part of your soul has become a rune socket.&r&aGrants two rune slots"
		""
		"{image:kubejs:textures/gui/malum/pact_of_rune_exploitation.png width:160 height:200 align:center}"
	]
	quest.417E7341644D16C8.quest_subtitle: "Abiding by the Ancient Pact"
	quest.417E7341644D16C8.title: "Pact of Rune Exploitation"
	quest.41968B5035595DD8.quest_desc: [
		"&7In Apotheosis, Silk Touch is enhanced. Mining a spawner with a pickaxe-type mining tool enchanted with Silk Touch consumes 150 durability and drops the spawner. This setting lets players collect spawners and place them in suitable locations for use."
		""
		"&7Additionally, Apotheosis allows players to adjust various spawner attributes through various materials, so a single spawner can reach a greater potential."
		""
		"Please note that the &eCapture&r enchantment is disabled. You need the &eArcane Ender Leash&r to change the creature inside the spawner. This means that empty spawners obtained before defeating the &cPrimordial Fire-Bearer&r are meaningless. It is more appropriate to modify spawners on-site and use a monolith to travel back and forth."
		""
		"&7Hold Ctrl to view detailed spawner information"
	]
	quest.41968B5035595DD8.quest_subtitle: "Massive Silk Touch Buff"
	quest.41968B5035595DD8.title: "How to Obtain Spawners"
	quest.41A6E2C475A1E6F5.quest_desc: ["&7The pro version of the biplane. Larger than the original biplane, but gains the ability to land on water, so with a wide water surface the risk of crashing during takeoff and landing is lower. After all, wild lakes are plentiful, but wild runways basically don't exist."]
	quest.41E17B4557322ADD.quest_desc: ["&7Increases damage based on the player's current &#FFAA33movement speed&7."]
	quest.41E17B4557322ADD.quest_subtitle: "Long, Pointy, Stick"
	quest.4213B825EDC1B32D.quest_desc: [
		"&6Rune Brooch&r"
		""
		"&7The Rune Brooch is the simplest and most unadorned brooch. It symbolizes power at an added cost, or bloodied hands gripping thorn-covered enlightenment. When worn, it removes one slot in my hands reserved for &cring&r&7 power and grants me the &aability&r&7 to inscribe one rune on each palm.&r"
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"&6Glass Brooch&r"
		""
		"&7The Rune Brooch works well, but the symbolic vessel of power is not limited to the hands. Through the Glass Brooch, I can channel it into my blood, trading away a portion of &cvitality&r&7 for the &aability&r&7 to inscribe two runes on my chest.&r"
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"&6Exquisite Brooch&r"
		""
		"&7A brooch symbolizes sacrifice. But in the eyes of others, this sacrifice can be somewhat abstract and vague, even absurd or comical. The form of a necklace is not much different from a belt; if the concepts of fashion and propriety are stripped away, I can wear a belt's &apower&r&7 around my neck.&r"
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"&6Gluttony Brooch&r"
		""
		"&7Sacrifice is not limited to the physical level; spiritual sacrifice is also sacrifice. The Gluttony Brooch strips away &csatiation&r&7, so that even after eating my fill I still constantly want to eat. In exchange, my shrunken abdomen gains room for one more &abelt&r&7.&r"
	]
	quest.4213B825EDC1B32D.quest_subtitle: "Obtaining rune slots at a cost—one of the sources of rune slots"
	quest.4276FE7E4037AC05.quest_desc: [
		"&7A relatively common structure in the Nether."
		"&7In the center of the battlefield is a trial spawner that spawns Ancient Knights. There is also a considerable amount of scattered armor in the surrounding environment. Mining it has a chance to drop &6Netherite Scraps&7 and spawn Ancient Knights."
		""
		"&7When you can defeat Ancient Knights, this is a relatively convenient place to obtain Netherite, and the &6Ash Essence&7 it produces is also an important material."
	]
	quest.4276FE7E4037AC05.quest_subtitle: "Combat, fun"
	quest.4276FE7E4037AC05.title: "Ancient Battlefield"
	quest.429669316E4CF3A9.quest_subtitle: "Has both armor and a small amount of spell attributes—very popular"
	quest.42A270AF2F03EE3B.quest_desc: [
		"{\"text\":\"\",\"extra\":[{\"text\":\"Holding and \",\"color\":\"gray\"},{\"text\":\"right-clicking\",\"color\":\"yellow\"},{\"text\":\" will cause a \",\"color\":\"gray\"},{\"text\":\"Mechanical Eye\",\"color\":\"aqua\"},{\"text\":\" copy to fly from the player's hand toward the nearest \",\"color\":\"gray\"},{\"text\":\"Ancient Factory\",\"color\":\"gold\"},{\"text\":\", while the Mechanical Eye in the player's hand enters a \",\"color\":\"gray\"},{\"text\":\"3s\",\"color\":\"yellow\"},{\"text\":\" cooldown.\",\"color\":\"gray\"}]}"
		""
		"{\"text\":\"\",\"extra\":[{\"text\":\"The flight function only works in the \",\"color\":\"gray\"},{\"text\":\"Overworld\",\"color\":\"green\"},{\"text\":\". It will not work in the \",\"color\":\"gray\"},{\"text\":\"Nether, the End\",\"color\":\"red\"},{\"text\":\", or worlds without an Ancient Factory.\",\"color\":\"gray\"}]}"
	]
	quest.42F6170490C96218.quest_subtitle: "No Rival Left"
	quest.42F6170490C96218.title: "Kill Champion Creatures x1000"
	quest.42FEDD895565B7A9.quest_desc: [
		"&7Provides &#55D5D5Malice Ward capacity&7 based on &#66CCFFmagic armor&7."
		"&7Provides &#55D5D5Malice Ward recovery rate&7 based on &#66CCFFcharge value&7."
		"&7Provides &#55D5D5Malice Ward recovery bonus&7 based on &#66CCFFmagic armor&7."
		"&7Provides &#FFAA3325%&7 &#66CCFFMalice Conversion&7."
		"&7Can obtain &#55D5D5pact cap&7 based on materials."
	]
	quest.42FEDD895565B7A9.quest_subtitle: "Number Shield Enjoyer"
	quest.42FEDD895565B7A9.title: "Malice Fortress Boots Template"
	quest.4342761A11C8B0C0.quest_desc: [
		"&7Has higher &#FFAA33critical damage&7 than other weapons."
		""
		"&7When dual-wielding, hold right-click to perform a &#FFD700slam&7, dealing damage to nearby entities."
		"&7Slam damage = &cmelee damage × 2.0&7."
		"&7Slam radius = &c4 + attack power × 0.2&7."
		"&7Slam cooldown = &c100 × (4 ÷ attack speed)&7, max &c600 ticks (&c30 seconds&7)."
	]
	quest.4342761A11C8B0C0.quest_subtitle: "Critical!"
	quest.43B69EBAF5DCC756.quest_desc: ["&7A tool that works as a &#66DDCCpickaxe&7, an &#66DDCCaxe&7, and a &#66DDCCshovel&7."]
	quest.43B69EBAF5DCC756.quest_subtitle: "All-Purpose Tool"
	quest.43DA0D2247FEE7E0.quest_desc: ["作为前期法力值恢复手段的词条很不错，即使是为了提供攻击力加成也是值得一穿的"]
	quest.43DA0D2247FEE7E0.quest_subtitle: "锟斤拷烫烫烫"
	quest.43DDDB9D9BA35A28.quest_desc: [
		"&7The &#FF8844Soulbound Brazier&7 is used to declare or reclaim Oaths."
		""
		"&7After placing the materials required for declaration into the &#FF8844Soulbound Brazier&7 in any order, light the brazier with &#FFAA33Spirit Fire&7 to begin the ritual."
		""
		"&7The ritual lasts &e30&7 seconds and does not limit the number of participants. Each second, it adds all creatures within &e4&7 blocks that have the &#CC6666Weakness&7 effect to the Oath. Players can right-click the brazier directly to join the Oath without needing the &#CC6666Weakness&7 effect."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"&7When joining an Oath, the creature takes damage equal to &e25%&7 of its own max health, with damage type &#CC6666malum:karmic&7. This damage can be reduced by armor value and Protection enchantments, and ignores post-hit damage immunity."
		"&7After the ritual completes, all creatures that joined the Oath gain the Oath effect. Each creature can hold at most two Oaths simultaneously. Oaths are soul-bound and persist even after death and respawn."
		""
		"&7If already holding &etwo Oaths&r&7, no new Oath is gained and the creature takes damage equal to &e50%&7 of its own max health, with damage type &#CC6666malum:karmic&7."
		"&7To reclaim an Oath, light with &#6666CCParadox Flame&7 instead of &#FFAA33Spirit Fire&7; all other procedures are identical to declaring an Oath. If reclaiming an Oath you do not hold, you take damage equal to &e50%&7 of your own max health."
		""
		"&7Players can view declared Oaths in the trinket slot; they cannot be removed."
		""
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"&6As shown in the figure:"
		"&r{image:kubejs:textures/gui/malum/malum.png width:115 height:140 align:center}"
		"&7Items in the &#66CCFFblue box&7 area are the required &#66FF99Spirits&7;"
		"&7Items in the &#FF6666red box&7 area are the required items;"
		"&7Items in the &#FFAA33orange box&7 area are the required main items."
		""
		"&7After placing them into the brazier, insert &r&zSpirit Fire&r&7 and right-click the brazier to perform the Oath declaration ritual"
		"&eDuring the Oath ritual, creatures in a weakened state will also be included in the declaration ritual&r"
	]
	quest.43DDDB9D9BA35A28.quest_subtitle: "Power at a Price"
	quest.43DDDB9D9BA35A28.title: "Oaths, and Other Pacts"
	quest.441A5EBCA3952517.quest_subtitle: "Standalone keep-inventory-on-death system"
	quest.441A5EBCA3952517.title: "Keep Inventory on Death"
	quest.4432A2327732E7FF.quest_desc: [
		"&7Blight, &cthat which can destroy and damage&r&7. The creations of the Directionless Ritual have many strange properties; I want to try classifying them."
		"&7"
		"&7One simple explanation is that it is just another form of energy infecting the world, but this explanation is clearly incorrect. Blight is harmless—at least, harmless in itself. It is just a kind of... &7matter."
		"&7"
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"&6Blight Research: Matter"
		"&7&bThe Directionless Ritual&r&7, as its name suggests, is a random process. It transmutes matter, but the transmuted products are unpredictable. So the powder it randomly produces is just unrelated fragments of matter piled together, and it smells quite bad. Not recommended for eating or planting, but otherwise there is nothing harmful about it."
		"&7"
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"&6Blight Research: Vegetation"
		"&7While testing the interaction between &8Blight&r&7 and bone meal, I observed that two plants appear frequently—&aBlight Roots&r&7 and &aBlight Bead Clusters&r&7. They are both rather useless, but they seem to be able to grow on Blight without needing water or light. Interesting."
		"&7"
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"&6Blight Research: Spread"
		"&7Blight does not spread on its own—after all, it is just randomly produced matter. But it has a kind of &dSpirit Memory&r&7, a reproducible pattern. If given &earcane energy&r&7 or effective fertilizer, Blight will randomly reproduce this pattern in the surrounding area."
		"&7"
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"&6Blight Research: Resonance"
		"&7This reproduction is precisely why it is extremely important for the &bRite of Unbinding&r&7. The &bRite of Unbinding&r&7 remembers the brutality of its creation process and &dresonates&r&7 with the memory within Blight, thereby injecting its energy into things above the Blight."
	]
	quest.443DAEA62297C415.quest_desc: [
		"&6Origin Island&r"
		"&7A long-forgotten isolated island in the vast ocean, holding the &6secret&r&7 of the familiars' origin. The only inhabitants of the island are tiny '&8Lost Souls&r&7'—early forms of familiars that failed to evolve into complete familiars. These souls can be captured with empty bottles for use in new rituals. The ritual must be performed on the &ePedestal&r&7 at the center of the island.&r"
		""
		"&7To locate this island, you first need a &bSniffer&r&7. They can sometimes dig up &eCrystallized Berries&r&7. Additionally, you can buy berries from &dFlower Ender Men&r&7. Feeding Crystallized Berries to a tamed familiar will awaken their vague memories of birth and the past, condensing into &eMemory Fragments&r&7. Memory Fragments are used in the same way as Eyes of Ender, guiding you to the location of the Origin Island.&r"
	]
	quest.443DAEA62297C415.quest_subtitle: "Discover the Origin Island"
	quest.443DAEA62297C415.title: "Land of Origin"
	quest.4440AB0D70D690ED.quest_subtitle: "Some FTB Quest Help + Contributor"
	quest.44568D0ED1546BF5.quest_desc: ["优秀的属性，高额又没啥影响的负面(bushi)"]
	quest.44568D0ED1546BF5.quest_subtitle: "蛊人的智慧"
	quest.446683FEB932319C.quest_desc: [
		"&6Rune of Warped Uncertainty&r"
		""
		"&7The Rune of Warped Uncertainty does not enhance the mind's abilities, but instead randomly distorts its behavior, causing the wearer's attack damage to fluctuate randomly—sometimes striking exactly at an enemy's weak point, in which case attack damage is &adoubled&r&7.&r"
	]
	quest.446683FEB932319C.quest_subtitle: "A Pulse That Spurs Corruption"
	quest.447E0F674624A5FA.quest_desc: [
		"&6Rose Quartz&r"
		"&7A pale red crystal formed by fusing redstone and nether quartz.&r"
		"&7When holding Rose Quartz in the main hand and Sand Paper in the off-hand, you can begin polishing. Polishing immediately consumes the Rose Quartz; if the animation is interrupted midway, the item is returned. After polishing is complete, you obtain &ePolished Rose Quartz&7.&r"
	]
	quest.44BFA62BE707B244.quest_desc: ["&7This adjustment affects the initial health of spawned creatures. Lower initial health benefits automated devices or manual harvesting by players, reducing kill time and preventing jams. Each of this item changes this value by 5%. The minimum value is 20%"]
	quest.44BFA62BE707B244.quest_subtitle: "Born with an Extremely Weak Constitution"
	quest.44FF46EF1BE66093.quest_desc: [
		"&6Yeti&r&7"
		"&7Passive creature, only spawns in the &#87CEEBStarlight Permafrost Forest&r&7;&r"
		""
		"&7Sometimes changes its movement to rolling along the ground;&r"
		""
		"&7Hold shears and right-click the Yeti to shear it (similar to shearing a sheep):&r"
		""
		"&7Immediately drops 1~3 &#F5F5DCWhite Yeti Fur&r&7, and this Yeti also becomes a skin-exposed hairless texture (restores after 2~3 minutes; cannot be sheared again before restoring).&r"
	]
	quest.44FF46EF1BE66093.title: "Yeti"
	quest.4520B52CE47AF428.quest_desc: [
		"&7Only performs melee attacks;"
		"&7Despite its creepy appearance, the &#AA00AARemains&7 are completely passive toward players;"
		""
		"&7It will actively help you attack most &#FF5555hostile / &#FFAA33neutral&7 monsters (but will not follow the player);"
		""
		"&7In every room where a &#FFD700Cunning Candle&7 spawns (regardless of tier), three &#AA00AA\"feigning death\"&7 &#AA00AARemains&7 spawn alongside it;"
		""
		"&7Players can revive them when needed to face the challenge brought by the &#FFD700Cunning Candle&7 together (the &#FFD700Cunning Candle&7 does not give the &#FF6666Betrayed&7 effect to creatures other than players);"
		""
		"&7Additionally, players need to watch out for friendly fire from their own attacks on the &#AA00AARemains&7."
		""
		"&7&#FFD700Feigning Death State&7"
		"&7&#AA00AARemains&7 spawned by any means are in the &#FFD700\"feigning death\"&7 state;"
		""
		"&7In the &#FFD700\"feigning death\"&7 state, &#AA00AARemains&7 are immune to all attack damage and cannot move/attack;"
		""
		"&7Use a &#FFD700Flint and Steel&7 to right-click / any attack with a flaming projectile hits the &#FFD700\"feigning death\"&7 &#AA00AARemains&7 to revive them;"
		""
		"&7After a revived &#AA00AARemains&7 runs out of health, it returns to the &#FFD700\"feigning death\"&7 state;"
		""
		"&7&#AA00AARemains&7 in the &#FFD700\"feigning death\"&7 state cannot be killed by most damage types;"
		""
		"&7Players in Creative Mode can left-click &#FFD700\"feigning death\"&7 &#AA00AARemains&7 to remove them."
	]
	quest.4520B52CE47AF428.quest_subtitle: "H.P. Minecraft-style"
	quest.4520B52CE47AF428.title: "Observation: Remains"
	quest.45220A64CA75EEB5.title: "感受魔力"
	quest.455B8465AECDA168.quest_desc: [
		"{\"text\":\"\",\"extra\":[{\"text\":\"Holding and \",\"color\":\"gray\"},{\"text\":\"right-clicking\",\"color\":\"yellow\"},{\"text\":\" will cause a \",\"color\":\"gray\"},{\"text\":\"Blaze Eye\",\"color\":\"gold\"},{\"text\":\" copy to fly from the player's hand toward the nearest \",\"color\":\"gray\"},{\"text\":\"Blaze Arena\",\"color\":\"red\"},{\"text\":\", while the Blaze Eye in the player's hand enters a \",\"color\":\"gray\"},{\"text\":\"3s\",\"color\":\"yellow\"},{\"text\":\" cooldown.\",\"color\":\"gray\"}]}"
		""
		"{\"text\":\"\",\"extra\":[{\"text\":\"The flight function only works in the \",\"color\":\"gray\"},{\"text\":\"Nether\",\"color\":\"red\"},{\"text\":\". It will not work in the \",\"color\":\"gray\"},{\"text\":\"Overworld, the End\",\"color\":\"green\"},{\"text\":\", or worlds without a Blaze Arena.\",\"color\":\"gray\"}]}"
	]
	quest.455B8465AECDA168.quest_subtitle: "Blaze Arena"
	quest.45983509EA6BD841.quest_desc: ["ATM材料的上位升级，&7自带永恒词条，持有后彻底告别耐久焦虑。数值极其扎实！一劳永逸之余，战力亦毫不妥协，是追求省心与强度兼备的理想之选。"]
	quest.45983509EA6BD841.quest_subtitle: "永恒力量"
	quest.45A1C2B4E1B4D9BC.quest_desc: [
		"&6Pact of the Profane Glutton&r"
		""
		"&7Corruption will eventually devour you.&r"
		"&7-Each level of &cRavenous Craving&r&7 adds to &cdamage taken&r"
		"&7-&cPoison&r&7 damage taken is doubled&r"
		"&7-&cHunger&r&7 damage inflicts &cpoison&r"
		""
		"&7Corruption becomes your strongest weapon.&r"
		"&7-&6Gluttony&r&7 becomes &6Ravenous Craving&r"
		"&7-&6Ravenous Craving&r&7 increases &eScythe Proficiency&r&7 and produces &blocusts&r&7 when the scythe deals damage"
		"&7-&6Ravenous Craving&r&7 builds up faster and has a higher cap&r"
		""
		"{image:kubejs:textures/gui/malum/pact_of_the_profane_glutton.png width:160 height:200 align:center}"
	]
	quest.45A1C2B4E1B4D9BC.quest_subtitle: "Ceaseless Feeding"
	quest.45A1C2B4E1B4D9BC.title: "Pact of the Profane Glutton"
	quest.45A31DEFA09A002A.quest_desc: [
		"&6Starlight Permafrost Forest&r"
		"&7is one of the surface biomes of the Starlight Dimension."
		""
		"&7The Starlight Permafrost Forest's surface undulation is &ahigher&r&7 (similar to the Overworld's mountain biomes). Year-round snow cover gives the vegetation here a &fsilvery-white&r color distinct from other biomes."
		"&7The main tree species of the Starlight Permafrost Forest is the &8Northern Tree&r&7 (corresponding to the Overworld's spruce)."
		""
		"&7The underground (Y > 0) of the Starlight Permafrost Forest is mainly composed of &bEverice&r&7 rather than Gloomstone. Its underground is also the only way for players to find &ePermafrost Stone&r&7."
		"&7You can also find some unique plants in this biome: &8Pine Cone Flowers, Umbrella Moon Grass, Glowing Umbrella Moon Grass, etc&r."
	]
	quest.45A31DEFA09A002A.quest_subtitle: "Bone-Chilling Forest"
	quest.45A31DEFA09A002A.title: "Starlight Permafrost Forest"
	quest.45DD7B7012AF1E60.quest_desc: ["The Nether seems to have undergone some kind of change"]
	quest.45DD7B7012AF1E60.quest_subtitle: "Enslaving creatures is truly shameful"
	quest.45DD7B7012AF1E60.title: "Nether Expansion"
	quest.45ED7996360032EC.quest_desc: ["&7加成极为全面，覆盖输出、生存等多个维度，是不可多得的全能材料。即便不进行合金，单独使用也已是超级强大的存在。"]
	quest.45ED7996360032EC.quest_subtitle: "龙，可是帝王之征啊"
	quest.463ED67306260BA3.quest_desc: [
		"&7This bookshelf differs from other bookshelves in that it can provide a unique attribute—&eQuantum Stability&7."
		"&eQuantum Stability&7 provides a way to eliminate Quantization's negative effects. When it is present, the minimum enchantment level effect of &4Quantization&7 is eliminated, leaving only the ability to provide extra enchantment levels. And -15% &4Quantization&7 can help the Enchanting Table suppress &4Quantization&r and &5Arcana&7, facilitating later &aInfusion&7 operations."
		""
		"&7The Amethyst Cluster required for crafting can be obtained through an &bInfusion&r operation on Amethyst Blocks. (Recommended Bookshelf)"
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"Influenced by the idea of magic strengthening magic, I attempted a &9Infusion&r operation on amethyst."
		"Amethyst Shards are too weak, and Amethyst Clusters are already occupied by ancient power. Only Amethyst Blocks can carry this power and become Amethyst Cluster. Unfortunately, Amethyst Cluster is too fragile, and all the power within it is channeled into growing Amethyst Clusters. So I encased it in a bookshelf made from calcite. The geode-like setting fully draws out the power of the Amethyst Cluster, allowing it to display a more powerful suppression of &4Quantization&r—&eQuantum Stability&r. This attribute is different from simply reducing &4Quantization&r; this ability only removes Quantization's negative effects while fully retaining its benefits. So can I weld this bookshelf and the Enchanting Table together ("
	]
	quest.463ED67306260BA3.quest_subtitle: "Nature's Power Awakens"
	quest.463ED67306260BA3.title: "Stable Magic Amplification"
	quest.46A501D36D26360F.quest_subtitle: "Basic Part"
	quest.46B041A7876340F6.quest_desc: [
		"&7&#FFD700Harmony Mechanic&7"
		"&7Harmony is the &#FFAA33core multiplier&7 of alloy strength. The higher the harmony, the stronger the equipment attributes."
		""
		"&7&#FFD700Base Harmony&7"
		"&7Base Harmony is determined by the alloy's &#FFD700number of material types&7. Some traits can further raise the base value. Material rarity, category, and other factors &#FF6666do not&7 affect Harmony."
		""
		"&7&#FFD700Modifier Coefficient&7"
		"&7Base Harmony must be multiplied by a modifier coefficient to become the &#FFAA33final effective Harmony&7. The modifier coefficient is determined by the following three rules:"
		""
		"&7&#FF6666Quantity Penalty&7: When the total number of materials in the alloy exceeds &#FFAA333&7, each additional material reduces the modifier coefficient by &#FF6666-5%&7."
		"&7&#FF6666Type Penalty&7: When the number of different materials in the alloy exceeds &#FFAA334 types&7, each additional different material reduces the modifier coefficient by &#FF6666-10%&7."
		"&7&#66FF66Duplicate Bonus&7: When the same material reaches &#FFAA332&7 or more, each additional identical material increases the modifier coefficient by &#66FF66+10%&7."
		""
		"&7&#FFD700Final Calculation&7"
		"&7Modifier coefficient = 100% - Quantity Penalty - Type Penalty + Duplicate Bonus"
		"&7&#FFAA33Final Harmony&7 = Base Harmony × Modifier Coefficient"
	]
	quest.46B041A7876340F6.quest_subtitle: "Harmony and Friendship"
	quest.46B041A7876340F6.title: "Cognition: Harmony"
	quest.46B09EB249B0D6E0.title: "Lone Star Skeleton"
	quest.46C1263DC7062475.quest_desc: [
		"&6Warp Engine&r"
		""
		"&7The Warp Engine violates natural law, and its practical application requires extreme caution. The Warp Engine repels causality and occasionally, after a &6Focusing Cycle&r&7 ends normally, instantly completes that cycle shortly before the next one begins.&r"
		""
		"&7Additionally, chain activation of the Warp Engine grants stackable &abuffs&r&7 to all other attributes. But it is probably also obvious that this operation significantly increases &cfuel consumption&r&7. Finally, it also slightly increases the tuning burden of the standard &eTuning Process&r&7.&r"
	]
	quest.46C1263DC7062475.quest_subtitle: "Detached from Linear Time"
	quest.4761041D4596C446.quest_desc: ["{\"text\":\"\",\"extra\":[{\"text\":\"I know you might get a headache seeing this mod's \",\"color\":\"gray\"},{\"text\":\"eyes\",\"color\":\"red\"},{\"text\":\", but now they can all be \",\"color\":\"gray\"},{\"text\":\"crafted\",\"color\":\"green\"},{\"text\":\".\",\"color\":\"gray\"}]}"]
	quest.4761041D4596C446.quest_subtitle: "Craftable"
	quest.47AE747B665C5151.quest_desc: ["与精制经验晶不同的是，可以打到顶端升级上"]
	quest.47AE747B665C5151.quest_subtitle: "等级越高我越强"
	quest.47CF8DC4847AD311.quest_desc: [
		"Naturally spawns in the Cursed Pyramid structure; use a Brush on Suspicious Sand inside the pyramid to obtain the Desert Necklace and activate it; can be located using the Desert Eye, and can also be summoned via the Altar."
		""
		"&7After defeating it, you can craft the following blueprints:"
		""
		"&#66CCFFAncient Spear&7, when the weapon is fully charged, left-click to produce a slightly homing &#66CCFFprojectile&7 that attacks enemies. The projectile's attack power depends on the player's damage (benefits from Strength, etc.)."
		""
		"&#66CCFFTracking Bow,&7 fires homing &#66CCFFghost sandstorms&7 at enemies."
	]
	quest.47CF8DC4847AD311.quest_subtitle: "Stage 2"
	quest.47F4C8B4C8082915.quest_desc: ["&7The &#66DDCCEquipment Adjustment Kit&7 lets you remove individual parts from equipment rather than all tools. Craft it with the tool you want to disassemble to remove the corresponding part. Before that, you need to adjust the &#66DDCCEquipment Adjustment Kit&7 to the corresponding type."]
	quest.47F4C8B4C8082915.quest_subtitle: "This one, don't need it anymore"
	quest.4846CE562BCEFAD5.quest_desc: ["Increases the wireless access point's transmission distance to infinite blocks"]
	quest.4846CE562BCEFAD5.quest_subtitle: "Signal Base Station"
	quest.48A06F2501866438.quest_desc: [
		"&7This bookshelf is an extreme enhancement of the Nether Bookshelf. Using the chaos and blaze power contained in Blaze Powder and Fire Charges, this bookshelf has ascended, becoming a more powerful existence. It can provide an even stronger &aTier&7 cap and &4Quantization&7 than the Nether Bookshelf."
		"&7But this power is too violent, so much so that it wants to devour everything it knows, dragging the world into that eternal chaos. This bookshelf will even prevent you from learning the results previewed from the Enchanting Table. In short, use it with caution."
	]
	quest.48A06F2501866438.quest_subtitle: "Hell Descends"
	quest.48A06F2501866438.title: "Chaos Approaches"
	quest.48BAAB5B16A162FF.quest_desc: ["&7To put items into the &#66DDCCCollector Pouch&7, drag the item above the &#66DDCCCollector Pouch&7 and right-click to insert it; or place the &#66DDCCCollector Pouch&7 above the item and right-click. To take items out, right-click the &#66DDCCCollector Pouch&7 or hold right-click and drag within the inventory. When the &#66DDCCCollector Pouch&7 is selected in the hotbar, pressing the use key throws out all items inside; when dragging within the inventory, items inserted later are released first."]
	quest.48BAAB5B16A162FF.quest_subtitle: "Can automatically store Spirits"
	quest.48BEC55ECB0AC9A3.quest_desc: [
		"&6Portable Fluid Interface&r"
		""
		"&7A connection component dedicated to extracting or inputting fluids between dynamic structures.&r"
		""
		"&6Transferring Fluids&r"
		"&7When a Portable Fluid Interface faces another interface on a dynamic structure head-on and is 1 to 2 blocks apart, the two automatically dock and begin transferring fluid.&r"
		"&7Requires a Mechanical Pump. Transfer direction and speed are determined by the pump's rotation direction and speed.&r"
		"&7If the target interface is on a moving dynamic structure, that structure is temporarily halted until the current transfer completes.&r"
		"&7Slight misalignment may occur during docking but does not affect actual transfer.&r"
		"&7When the dynamic structure's movement speed or rotation speed is too high, the interface's interaction success rate drops significantly.&r"
		""
		"&6Redstone Locking&r"
		"&7The Portable Fluid Interface can be locked by a redstone signal. Once locked, the interface no longer halts dynamic structures and does not transfer fluids.&r"
		""
		"&8They hate bumps, but love to dance together&r"
	]
	quest.48F1FA137148C82F.title: "Discover the Ancient Factory"
	quest.4939B8B2FE7A3B5D.quest_desc: ["A black special arena generates on Nether lava lakes; mine the ancient chiseled blackstone in the central pillar to trigger the fight. It can also be summoned via the Altar"]
	quest.4939B8B2FE7A3B5D.quest_subtitle: "Stage 1"
	quest.496E4A2F2E407B7E.quest_desc: ["&7Before you have enough arrows, the &#FFD700slingshot&7 is indeed a bit more useful."]
	quest.496E4A2F2E407B7E.quest_subtitle: "A Simple Ranged Attack Method"
	quest.49840E89ACF73DAF.quest_desc: ["&7Functions the same as a vanilla &#66CCFFshovel&7. You can place a vanilla &#66CCFFshovel&7 in a crafting table to convert it into a &#66DDCCSilent Gear Shovel&7."]
	quest.49840E89ACF73DAF.quest_subtitle: "Little Spoon"
	quest.4996E5CD9E56D25E.quest_subtitle: "Food value > 8"
	quest.4996E5CD9E56D25E.title: "Main Course Recovery x32"
	quest.49D6FBB86F5D925D.quest_desc: ["啊啊啊啊啊啊啊啊啊啊啊啊啊啊啊啊啊啊啊啊啊啊啊啊啊啊啊啊啊啊啊啊啊啊啊啊啊啊啊啊啊啊啊啊啊啊啊啊啊啊啊啊啊啊啊啊啊啊啊啊啊啊啊啊啊啊啊啊啊啊啊啊啊啊啊啊啊啊啊啊啊啊啊啊啊啊啊啊啊啊啊啊啊啊啊啊啊啊啊啊啊啊啊啊啊啊啊啊啊啊啊啊啊啊啊啊啊啊啊啊啊啊啊啊啊啊啊啊啊啊啊啊啊啊啊啊啊啊啊啊啊啊啊啊啊啊啊啊啊啊啊啊啊啊啊啊"]
	quest.4A1A9E32ABF05FD0.quest_subtitle: "摆放标记的物品或流体。正常工作时前方不能有任何方块（除了流体）"
	quest.4A4168EA1BC0644E.quest_desc: ["灼热魔力可以提高法力值恢复速度，同时材料有着不俗的铁魔法相关属性"]
	quest.4A4168EA1BC0644E.quest_subtitle: "魔力翻涌"
	quest.4A7080BE52CC6335.quest_desc: ["&7Functions the same as a vanilla &#66CCFFhoe&7. You can place a vanilla &#66CCFFhoe&7 in a crafting table to convert it into a &#66DDCCSilent Gear Hoe&7."]
	quest.4A7080BE52CC6335.quest_subtitle: "Garden Tool"
	quest.4AB1523AE2CA75D7.quest_desc: [
		"&7A &#FFD700crossbow&7 that automatically selects arrows from the backpack for auto-loading."
		""
		"&7Ranged damage is dynamically determined by &6Silent Gear's&7 &eranged damage&7 attribute."
	]
	quest.4AB1523AE2CA75D7.quest_subtitle: "Transfer to a Human"
	quest.4AC2F5D5FF711C0F.quest_desc: [
		"&6Resonant Tuner&r"
		""
		"&7&eClear Sky&r&7 and &6Earth&r&7 normally do not react with each other, and this non-reaction also has its uses. The Resonant Tuner softens the interaction of different forces within the &eCrucible&r&7, greatly reducing—or even completely removing—&cInstability Risk&r&7 at the cost of slowing processing speed.&r"
	]
	quest.4AC2F5D5FF711C0F.quest_subtitle: "Dissonance Softened"
	quest.4ACF299AC1220CE6.quest_subtitle: "Grand Hall"
	quest.4ACF299AC1220CE6.title: "Discover the Castle"
	quest.4AEAA66A5B802779.quest_desc: [
		"&e\"Fast is good!\""
		"&7The biplane's base speed is far higher than other models. With an engine and propeller upgrade installed, it can even compete with chunk loading speed—but it also carries a huge crash risk, and crashes cause &cexplosions&7, meaning a downed plane may be burned up by the explosion's flames. Always leave a proper runway and travel with caution."
	]
	quest.4AF740882E852DBF.quest_desc: [
		"&6Familiar House&r"
		"&7The Familiar House is a block that can store up to 10 familiars. Familiars stored inside are &ainvincible&r&7, but usually will not attack other creatures (with some exceptions). The Familiar House has two modes:&r"
		""
		"&7&bStorage Mode&r&7: Allows players to freely &amove&r&7 familiars between their own and those inside the house.&r"
		"&7&bRoaming Mode&r&7: Allows stored familiars to &arove&r&7 around within a configurable distance. In this mode, you can also enable or disable the familiars' abilities while roaming. The Familiar House block can only be broken by its &cowner&r&7, and only when it is in Storage Mode and has no familiars inside.&r"
		""
		"&6Important Note&r&7: Within a 16-block radius, only one Familiar House block can be used.&r"
	]
	quest.4AF740882E852DBF.quest_subtitle: "Big Mansion"
	quest.4AFE778B9A79DA33.quest_subtitle: "Swift as the Wind"
	quest.4B2894FD0E46313C.quest_subtitle: "Fabric Fusion"
	quest.4B307CE1A9A7465A.quest_desc: ["The Silent Gear author never imagined someone would wear Silent Gear with Curse of Binding. If you did, this item might help you."]
	quest.4B307CE1A9A7465A.quest_subtitle: "Dedicated to Baka"
	quest.4B3F9F49C0FF6B3B.quest_desc: [
		"&7Although the crafting process has been improved, Arcane Essence Ink—especially higher-tier grades—still holds unquestionable value."
		""
		"&8Its worth is forever engraved upon the cost of its creation."
		""
		"&7Ink is used to craft magic scrolls on the &6Scroll Scribing Table&7. The higher the ink tier, the higher the &6tier&7 of the scroll produced, and the stronger its corresponding effect. Legendary ink is the highest-tier ink, but the scrolls produced may not necessarily be max-tier scrolls. You can use the &6Arcane Anvil&7 to place the scroll in the first slot and ink in the second slot to upgrade the scroll."
		""
		"&7Lower-tier ink can be crafted into higher-tier ink. Pouring four bottles of the same-tier ink into an &6Alchemy Cauldron&7 and adding the specified materials can condense them into one bottle of ink at tier +1, but the efficiency is quite low. Using &6Create's&7 mixing function can condense four bottles of the same-tier ink into three bottles of tier +1 ink."
	]
	quest.4B3F9F49C0FF6B3B.quest_subtitle: "Exquisite"
	quest.4B3F9F49C0FF6B3B.title: "Arcane Ink"
	quest.4BA0280CD5AC4EB5.quest_desc: ["&7Same function as a vanilla &#66CCFFshears&7... why would you bother making this?"]
	quest.4BA0280CD5AC4EB5.quest_subtitle: "A More Noble Pair of Shears...?"
	quest.4BCF7827E9797977.quest_desc: [
		"&7Emits light at level &e14&7, has a block entity, can be waterlogged, and is not destroyed by water flow."
		""
		"&7Can serve as a heat source for the &#FFAA33Farmer's Delight&7 mod."
		""
		"&7Similar to &#FF8844leather armor&7, &#FFAA33Spirit Fire&7 can be dyed with &#66DDCCdye&7 at a crafting table. You can put more than one &#66DDCCdye&7 in the crafting table with &#FFAA33Spirit Fire&7, and you can also dye it multiple times."
		""
		"&7&#FFAA33Spirit Fire&7 has one color, and &#CC66FFIridescent Spirit Fire&7 has two colors. Crafting &#CC66FFIridescent Spirit Fire&7 inherits the first color of &#FFAA33Spirit Fire&7; dyeing can only change the last color of &#CC66FFIridescent Spirit Fire&7. The default colors are &#FFAA33#EFC016&7 and &#6666FF#464FA5&7 respectively."
		""
		"&7Crafting &#FFAA33Spirit Fire Torches&7 and &#FFAA33Spirit Fire Braziers&7 inherits the color."
		""
		"&bCan be used as a ritual material consumed for Oaths&r"
	]
	quest.4C4558B339BA59A5.quest_desc: [
		"&7Each attack draws one of the following effects to trigger:"
		""
		"&7Deals an extra &#FFAA3330%&7 damage to the target and all enemies within &#FFAA331.5 blocks&7 of it"
		"&7Applies a &#CC66FFrandom negative effect&7 to the target"
		"&7Deals true damage equal to &#FFAA3310%&7 of the target's max health"
		"&7Restores health equal to &#66FF665%&7 of the attacker's max health"
		"&7Applies a &#66FF66random positive effect&7 to the attacker"
		"&7Reduces the target's max health by &#FFAA3325%&7"
		"&7Deals an extra &#FFAA3310%&7 base damage"
		"&7Deals &#FFAA333×&7 base damage"
		""
		"&7Can apply &#66CCFFScythe Proficiency&7"
		"&7Counts as a &#FFD700Pickaxe-Axe&7"
		"&7Has the saw's &#66DDCCone-click tree felling&7 function"
		"&7When mining, destroys all blocks within &#FFAA333×3×3&7 of the target (not triggered while sneaking)"
		"&7Can obtain from materials:"
		"&7&#66CCFFArmor&7, &#66CCFFArmor Toughness&7, &#66CCFFKnockback Resistance&7"
		"&7&#CC99FFSpell Power&7, &#CC99FFSpell Resistance&7, &#CC99FFMana Regeneration&7, &#CC99FFMax Mana&7"
		"&7&#55D5D5pact cap&7, &#55D5D5healing multiplier&7"
	]
	quest.4C4558B339BA59A5.quest_subtitle: "One Thing Is One Thing"
	quest.4C4D49730F599ADA.quest_desc: [
		"&6Crystal Desert&r"
		"&7is one of the surface biomes of the Starlight Dimension."
		""
		"&7The Crystal Desert is overall paved with &8Twilight Sand&r&7, with a small amount of &8Dead Moonlight Trees&r generating on the surface."
		"&7The Crystal Desert's surface and dozens of layers underground generate crystal cluster features made of &cRed Starshine Crystals&r&7 and &bBlue Starshine Crystals&r&7. This is also an important way for players to obtain &cthe two crystal cluster shards&r&7."
		""
		"&7Compared to other surface biomes, the Crystal Desert has &alower&r&7 feature coverage, letting players more easily locate &eHot Springs&r&7."
		"&7You can also find some unique plants in this biome: &8Moonmoth Cactus, Dead Moonlight Shrubs, Purple Desert Grass, Desert Purple Flower, Starfly Tree, Twilight Surge Grass, Fly Fruit, etc&r."
	]
	quest.4C4D49730F599ADA.quest_subtitle: "Twinkle Twinkle Little Star"
	quest.4C4D49730F599ADA.title: "Crystal Desert"
	quest.4C7B1F3BC1ACBD92.quest_desc: ["&7Can change fuel consumption and engine output power. The latter directly affects flight speed. By comparison, fuel isn't exactly a precious resource."]
	quest.4C9D927032A98883.quest_desc: ["又是这个攮的过粉的BOSS"]
	quest.4C9D927032A98883.quest_subtitle: "哇袄"
	quest.4CC2D82F6A669265.quest_desc: [
		"&6Blaze Diode&r"
		""
		"&7The Blaze Diode borrows the mighty power of souls burning like fire, reducing the &cfuel demand&r&7 of the &ecatalysts&r&7 around the &eCrucible&r&7 while slightly accelerating the &aFocusing Process&r&7.&r"
	]
	quest.4CC2D82F6A669265.quest_subtitle: "The Mightiest Power"
	quest.4D00769819B3C7B5.quest_desc: [
		"&7昂贵而强大的材料，秘银需要在-63到-38之间挖掘寻找，生成量相当少，在用幽冥锤开路的情况下会轻松一些，挖掘掉落受时运影响。雷电瓶需要使用玻璃瓶右键闪电苦力怕获得，也可以在铁魔法的特殊结构中开启隐藏箱子获取。"
		""
		"&7其强大之处在于奥术谐振4词条，玩家每拥有10点魔力可提供1%增伤，上限词条等级*20，也就是说雷霆织物握柄在魔力值充足的前提下可以提供80%的恐怖增伤。"
		""
		"&e如果不同装备上同时存在多个奥术谐振词条，增加法力值的效果可以叠加，但增伤无法叠加，以最高等级计算。"
	]
	quest.4D00769819B3C7B5.quest_subtitle: "带电就是不一样"
	quest.4D2714BB06E019FF.quest_desc: [
		"&7After carefully pondering the properties I observed in the &dSpirit Crystal&r&7, I cannot help but think that structure itself also matters. To test this conclusion, I created a &8Memory Matter&r&7 imitation, used to mimic &cMalefic Arcane Energy&r&7; condensed soul memory was the closest substance I could think of. It can reach a precision of several hundred-thousandths of a block."
		"&7"
		"&7I didn't expect it to explode right before my eyes."
		"&7"
		"&7But explosions are useful too, provided they can be controlled. So I made another sample, but this time I designed a structure for the pseudo-crystal to channel its power—a mount made of &6Soulwood&r&7 and &6Soulstained Steel&r&7, to transmit energy outward. When focusing a spell into the staff, it is like a miniature version of the ritual, though the effects produced are somewhat different."
		"&7"
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"&7A staff in melee combat... barely adequate. I would probably choose a scythe as my first pick, but a staff's effectiveness is decent too. They usually emphasize magic damage and place less importance on physical damage, which is sometimes useful. Their true specialty shows when I &ause&r&7 them."
		"&7"
		"&7The Memory-Spirit Spellstaff condenses liquid Malefic Arcane Energy into spheres and fires them, reminiscent of a witch's hex. Activating it takes some time, and it apparently cannot fire multiple times in quick succession, but each shot deals large damage to the target. The staff draws on my soul to charge, and because of this, the ammunition count of all staves I carry is calculated collectively."
		"&7"
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"&7This method of producing mimicked arcane energy ran into obstacles with other energies—perhaps due to the materials. The resonance between Memory Matter and Malefic Arcane may simply stem from the death required to create Experience Crystals."
		"&7"
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"&6Capacity"
		"&7As far as I know, the energy contained in a Spirit Crystal is limited... but this only holds true for the strange non-physical matter of arcane energy. The &6Capacity&r&7 enchantment lets a staff accumulate more energy in the same physical space, enough to store roughly one extra spell charge per level. A staff with this enchantment cannot receive the Rapid Continuation enchantment."
		"&7"
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"&6Rapid Continuation"
		"&7A staff can channel magic that has a physical form. Clearly, magic can flow out as well as in, and consciously directing its flow is not impossible either. When using a staff with the &6Rapid Continuation&r&7 enchantment in melee, there is a certain chance to replenish the staff's energy pool, restoring roughly the energy equivalent to one spell charge. A staff with this enchantment cannot receive the Capacity enchantment."
	]
	quest.4D2714BB06E019FF.quest_subtitle: "May Mages Fear My Might"
	quest.4D2714BB06E019FF.title: "Spirit Staff"
	quest.4D2D9898C6477E3B.quest_desc: [
		"&7For all aircraft: press R to dismount. Some models may require pressing twice to prevent accidental dismounts. Since R conflicts with shader pack reloading, remapping the key is recommended."
		""
		"&7After boarding, press the inventory key to open the aircraft page, where you can install aircraft upgrade components. If the aircraft needs fuel, add it on this page too."
		""
		"&7For biplane types: hold &eSpace&7 to start the engine. During startup the plane begins to roll, so prepare a takeoff runway. Once the engine starts, tap &eS&7 to pitch the nose up and take off. After takeoff, press &eD&7 to lower the nose, and hold &eShift&7 to shut down the engine and glide down."
		""
		"&cBiplanes fly fast but have high takeoff/landing risk, and crashes cause explosions. Please be careful (the damage is really high)."
		""
		"&7For helicopter / rotorcraft types: Space to ascend, Shift to descend."
		""
		"&7For human-powered aircraft: hold W to provide power. Once power is maxed it stays fixed, and W then becomes normal forward control. Flight continuously consumes hunger."
	]
	quest.4D2D9898C6477E3B.quest_subtitle: "At least you know how to press the gas and the brakes..."
	quest.4D448B1BA52C6548.quest_desc: ["{\"text\":\"\",\"extra\":[{\"text\":\"I know you might get a headache seeing this mod's \",\"color\":\"gray\"},{\"text\":\"eyes\",\"color\":\"red\"},{\"text\":\", but now they can all be \",\"color\":\"gray\"},{\"text\":\"crafted\",\"color\":\"green\"},{\"text\":\".\",\"color\":\"gray\"}]}"]
	quest.4D448B1BA52C6548.quest_subtitle: "Craftable"
	quest.4D4B372937B102F6.quest_desc: [
		"&7生物持有 &#FFAA33星火&7 效果时，其身上会不断冒出亮橙色火焰粒子。"
		""
		"&7溅射伤害机制：  "
		"&7当持有 &#FFAA33星火&7 效果的生物（下文简称持有者）承受一次伤害时，其所在位置会炸开一团粒子；  "
		"&7同时对（除持有者外）持有者周围半径 &#FFAA333格&7 内所有生物，造成一次溅射伤害，溅射伤害的数值等同于持有者承受的那次伤害数值的 &#FFAA331/3&7；  "
		"&7承受的伤害来源 &#FF6666不能&7 来自星火（效果）本身，否则不会触发溅射伤害；  "
		"&7溅射伤害属于 &#FFD700物理伤害&7，可以无视生物免疫火焰伤害的被动，也可以被生物的盔甲值减免；  "
		"&7溅射伤害 &#FF6666不会&7 对命中的生物造成击退。"
		""
		"&7传染机制：  "
		"&7当持有者死亡时，持有者周围半径 &#FFAA333格&7 内所有生物都会获得 &#FFAA33星火&7 效果；  "
		"&7传染的星火效果的等级不变，但持续时间仅有持有者死亡时星火效果剩余持续时间的 &#FFAA331/2&7（不会低于 &#FFAA331秒&7）；  "
		"&7更高等级的星火效果 &#FF6666不会&7 影响上述一切功能与数值。"
	]
	quest.4D4B372937B102F6.quest_subtitle: "星火燎原！"
	quest.4D79C56FF94C03AE.quest_desc: ["想玩攻速特效流？"]
	quest.4D79C56FF94C03AE.quest_subtitle: "那我问你...你的脑袋怎么尖尖的"
	quest.4DBB3CA0C3949A66.quest_desc: [
		"&6Thunder Warlock Familiar&r"
		"&7Combat: Specializes in &elightning magic&r&7, can attack multiple targets simultaneously.&r"
		"&7Abilities:&r"
		"&7&aLord of Charging&r&7: Can charge the owner for a period of time, increasing their speed and strength.&r"
		"&7&aCharging Creeper&r&7: Whenever a creeper is spotted, it will follow and charge it.&r"
		"&7Spawning: Can be found roaming in &bmountains&r&7, looking for good spots to attract lightning.&r"
		""
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"&6Archmage Familiar&r"
		"&7Combat: Specializes in &ebasic magic&r&7 of different schools.&r"
		"&7Abilities:&r"
		"&7&aTransmutation&r&7: Can convert &espell scrolls&r&7 on the pedestal into other random scrolls of the same rarity, with a small chance to obtain a higher-rarity scroll.&r"
		"&7&cEnder Man's Nightmare&r&7: Endermen fear it and will flee upon seeing it.&r"
		"&7&aShulker Protection&r&7: Can counter Shulker missiles.&r"
		"&7Spawning: Can be studied in temporary laboratories located in the &6End&r&7.&r"
		""
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"&6Necromancer Familiar&r"
		"&7Combat: Specializes in &cblood magic&r&7, including necromantic abilities to summon the undead.&r"
		"&7Abilities:&r"
		"&cUndead Frenzy&r&7: Can cause nearby undead entities to go berserk, attacking nearby entities chaotically.&r"
		"&cWitherization&r&7: Can convert nearby skeletons into Wither Skeletons.&r"
		"&7Spawning: Can be found studying death in graveyards throughout the &8Soul Sand Valley&r&7.&r"
		""
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"&6Evoker Familiar&r"
		"&7Combat: Specializes in &8void magic&r&7 and unknown arts, able to summon creatures born of shadow.&r"
		"&7Abilities:&r"
		"&aTrue Sight&r&7: Can grant the owner &anight vision&r&7 and make them immune to blindness and darkness effects.&r"
		"&aDark Ritual&r&7: Can deactivate &cSculk Shrieker&r&7, allowing the owner to avoid detection by the Warden.&r"
		"&7Spawning: Can be found studying dark arts in laboratories located in &cAncient Cities&r&7.&r"
		""
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"&6Hunter Familiar&r"
		"&7Combat: Specializes in attacking enemies with &ebows&r&7, combined with swift movement.&r"
		"&7Abilities:&r"
		"&aWatcher&r&7: Can protect the owner from attacks by enemies targeting them, even if the owner is unaware.&r"
		"&aScent Loot&r&7: The owner can hold any item and right-click it, causing it to search for entities around that can drop that item and mark them for the owner.&r"
		"&7Spawning: Can live in camps in various &bforest&r&7 biomes.&r"
		""
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"&6Druid Familiar&r"
		"&7Combat: Specializes in using &bnature magic&r&7 to control enemies.&r"
		"&7Abilities:&r"
		"&aOvergrowth&r&7: Can use bone meal on nearby crops.&r"
		"&aNature's Blessing&r&7: Can breed nearby animals.&r"
		"&7Spawning: Can be found protecting forests around the world.&r"
		""
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"&6Illusionist Familiar&r"
		"&7Combat: Specializes in &dillusion magic&r&7, controlling enemies by confusing them.&r"
		"&7Abilities:&r"
		"&aMagic Trick&r&7: When the owner's health is low, the Illusionist will perform a magic trick, hiding the owner from enemies.&r"
		"&aDecoy&r&7: When its health is low, it will disappear and leave behind an explosive copy, taunting nearby enemies to attack it.&r"
		"&aPickpocket&r&7: When no one is watching and there are gold nuggets or emeralds on the ground, this little trickster will claim them for itself.&r"
		"&7Spawning: Illusionists spawn naturally disguised as other Overworld familiars. Use the &eMirror of Truth&r&7 to reveal them.&r"
		""
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"&6Plague Doctor Familiar&r"
		"&7Combat: Specializes in &cpoison magic&r&7, causing enemies to die slowly through poisoning.&r"
		"&7Abilities:&r"
		"&cToxic Blood&r&7: Its owner and itself deal extra damage to poisoned entities. When the Plague Doctor familiar is attacked, it will throw a bottle of poison as a counterattack.&r"
		"&7Obtaining: To obtain it, you need to craft a bottle of &cToxic Reagent&r&7 and give it to a tamed Druid familiar.&r"
		""
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"&6Blaze Familiar&r"
		"&7Combat: Specializes in &efire magic&r&7, burning enemies to death.&r"
		"&7Abilities:&r"
		"&cMolten Heart&r&7: When attacked, causes the attacker to catch fire for a period of time.&r"
		"&aHeat Resistance&r&7: Grants its owner and itself fire immunity.&r"
		"&7Spawning: Can be found roaming in hot places in the &cNether&r&7.&r"
		""
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"&6Cleric Familiar&r"
		"&7Combat: Specializes in &aholy magic&r&7. Its main role is support, but it can also cast powerful holy spells to purify enemies.&r"
		"&7Abilities:&r"
		"&aRedemption&r&7: It will attack undead in its line of sight, but if it sees a zombie villager, it will use holy power to heal and redeem it.&r"
		"&7Obtaining: To obtain the Cleric familiar, you need to cast a &apurification spell&r&7 near an untamed Necromancer familiar.&r"
		""
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"&6Bard Familiar&r"
		"&7Combat: Specializes in &dmelodic magic&r&7, attacking enemies with powerful melodies and helping friends with supportive melodies.&r"
		"&7Abilities:&r"
		"&aMusical Nature&r&7: It plays melodies, making adventures more wonderful.&r"
		"&7Obtaining: To obtain it, you need to cast a &emelodic spell&r&7 near an untamed familiar, causing it to become interested in music.&r"
		""
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"&6Frost Familiar&r"
		"&7Combat: Specializes in &bfrost magic&r&7, with a good balance between attack, defense, and mobility, and decent control abilities.&r"
		"&7Abilities:&r"
		"&aFrost Footprints&r&7: It and its owner can freeze water surfaces underfoot to walk on them.&r"
		"&aFrost Heart&r&7: It and its owner become immune to freezing effects, including freezing from powder snow.&r"
		"&7Spawning: Can be found roaming in &bsnowy biomes&r&7.&r"
		""
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"&6Dragoon Familiar&r"
		"&7Combat: Specializes in &6ender magic&r&7, focusing on melee combat.&r"
		"&7Abilities:&r"
		"&eDragon's Breath&r&7: It can collect dragon's breath using glass bottles.&r"
		"&aDragon Heart&r&7: Its dragon heart allows it to naturally regenerate health.&r"
		"&aGuardian&r&7: When an allied familiar is attacked within melee range, it will swap positions with it and lock onto the attacker.&r"
		"&7Spawning: Spawns on the &6Outer End Islands&r&7.&r"
	]
	quest.4DBB3CA0C3949A66.quest_subtitle: "So Cute"
	quest.4DC5D99569CC3F68.quest_desc: [
		"This upgraded Deep Dark Bookshelf channels its power into &5Arcana&r, providing large amounts of &5Arcana&r without providing &4Quantization&r."
		"(Important Bookshelf)"
	]
	quest.4DC5D99569CC3F68.quest_subtitle: "Mysterious Power Reappears"
	quest.4DC5D99569CC3F68.title: "Sculk Growth — Beholding the Deep Dark Again"
	quest.4E154F6CBE09CA32.quest_desc: [
		"&6Thirsty Fang&r&7"
		"&7Material dropped after killing a &#8B0000Thirsty Walker&r&7;&r"
		""
		"&7Can be used to craft the &#FF4500Thirsty Dagger&r&7 and various decorative blocks.&r"
		""
		"&7Besides kill drops, the Thirsty Fang also has a special drop method:&r"
		""
		"&7If the Thirsty Walker's &#DC143Cbite attack&r&7 is blocked by a &#1E90FFshield&r&7 (including other equipment with the same mechanic), this Thirsty Walker has a &#FFA07A16.67%&r&7 chance to drop 0~2 &#8B0000Thirsty Fangs&r&7;&r"
		""
		"&7\"&#FFD700Losing a tooth&r&7\" does not affect the Thirsty Walker's subsequent behavior or attack damage.&r"
	]
	quest.4E25633D226B8C90.quest_desc: ["极其优秀的属性加成，怪不得打龙这么费劲"]
	quest.4E25633D226B8C90.quest_subtitle: "你是龙，也好"
	quest.4E302A6F9E6AAC09.quest_desc: ["&7To put items into the &#66DDCCCollector Pouch&7, drag the item above the &#66DDCCCollector Pouch&7 and right-click to insert it; or place the &#66DDCCCollector Pouch&7 above the item and right-click. To take items out, right-click the &#66DDCCCollector Pouch&7 or hold right-click and drag within the inventory. When the &#66DDCCCollector Pouch&7 is selected in the hotbar, pressing the use key throws out all items inside; when dragging within the inventory, items inserted later are released first."]
	quest.4E302A6F9E6AAC09.quest_subtitle: "Can automatically store items placed in the Collector Pouch"
	quest.4E7B1EFF01114F88.quest_desc: [
		"&6Steam Engine&r"
		""
		"&7The Steam Engine is an advanced power source that works with a &eBoiler&r&7 to produce power.&r"
		"&7Stress production: &c0 ~ 16384 su&r"
		"&7RPM production: &c16 ~ 64 RPM&r"
		""
		"&6Obtaining&r"
		"&7Crafted at a Crafting Table.&r"
		""
		"&6Purpose&r"
		""
		"&6Placement&r"
		"&7The Steam Engine must be installed on any face of a &eFluid Tank&r&7, after which the Fluid Tank becomes a &6Boiler&r&7. For the Steam Engine to produce power, a &eShaft&r&7 must be placed in front of it. Right-click the Steam Engine with the Shaft item to place it.&r"
		""
		"&6Outputting Stress from the Boiler&r"
		"&7The Steam Engine outputs stress from the boiler. See &6Boiler&r&7 for the boiler's stress generation mechanics.&r"
		"&7The boiler's stress is distributed evenly among each Steam Engine on the boiler. A single Steam Engine outputs at most &c16384 su&r&7 stress, so when stress exceeds 16384 su, more Steam Engines are needed to output all stress, otherwise the excess is wasted. Installing a number of Steam Engines equal to the boiler level fully outputs the boiler's stress.&r"
		"&7When there are already enough Steam Engines to output all stress, adding more does not improve efficiency.&r"
	]
	quest.4E826A5530F49919.quest_desc: [
		"Naturally spawns in the Acropolis structure; right-click the anchor in the arena at the top of the structure to activate it; can be located using the Storm Eye, and can also be summoned via the Altar."
		""
		"&7After defeating it, you can craft the following blueprints:"
		""
		"&#66CCFFThunder Anchor&7, &7right-click to throw a giant &#FFD700anchor&7 at enemies; sneaking and right-clicking summons a &#66CCFFtide&7 around you."
		""
		"&#66CCFFLong Lance&7, right-click to throw a &#FFD700thunder spear&7, which generates a small-area &#66CCFFthunder pool&7 upon hitting the ground."
	]
	quest.4E826A5530F49919.quest_subtitle: "Stage 2"
	quest.4EB3AF395EE2F05E.quest_desc: ["提升玩家的触及距离，长臂猿的含金量应该不必多说"]
	quest.4EB3AF395EE2F05E.quest_subtitle: "一寸长一寸强"
	quest.4EF6614B03841586.quest_desc: [
		"&6Dusk-Eye Fish&r&7"
		"&7One of the common aquatic creatures of the Abyss. It cannot survive out of water (loses movement ability and gradually loses health until death after a period of time);&r"
		""
		"&7Unlike the &#ADD8E6Light Puffer&r&7 and &#87CEEBLight-Horned Piranha&r&7, this creature cannot be placed in a water bucket;&r"
		""
		"&7Fights back only when attacked itself (melee only; attacks can be blocked by a shield);&r"
		""
		"&7Group aggro: After it is attacked, all Dusk-Eye Fish around it will lock that attacker as a hatred target;&r"
		""
		"&7Dusk-Eye Fish will give up the chase after the hatred target leaves the water area it is in.&r"
	]
	quest.4EF6614B03841586.title: "Dusk-Eye Fish"
	quest.501A9D4E77A9D0EA.quest_desc: ["&7Can clear grass on the ground, leaves on trees, and other clutter over a wide area. Right-click for &#66FF66area harvesting with automatic replanting&7. Crops obtained this way have their yield increased by &#FFAA331.5×&7 (rounded up)."]
	quest.501A9D4E77A9D0EA.quest_subtitle: "Farmer's Best Friend"
	quest.501AB9740C6C4447.quest_desc: [
		"&6Rune of Fortitude&r"
		""
		"&7The Rune of Fortitude does not provide healing like similar runes, but instead forces the form to heal beyond its limits, granting a small amount of &abonus health&r&7.&r"
	]
	quest.501AB9740C6C4447.quest_subtitle: "Healing the Whole"
	quest.502FAEFE4F6CF6B2.title: "Playtime 8h"
	quest.5057DE8E48849E95.quest_desc: [
		"&6Brass&r"
		""
		"&7Molten copper and zinc meet in the furnace; once cooled, this warm golden metal is the result. It is somewhat soft, yet enough to shape the first forms of machinery.&r"
		""
		"&6Purpose&r"
		"&7Holding it and using it on a placed &estripped log&r&7 coats it in metallic luster, turning it into a sturdy &eBrass Casing&r&7—an indispensable starting point for many complex contraptions.&r"
		"&7At the &eStonecutter&r&7, it can be shaped into matching &eScaffolding&r&7 and structural components, paving the way for taller builds.&r"
		"&7On the &eCrafting Table&r&7, its forms grow more refined: becoming the nimble joints of &eBrass Hand Parts&r&7, shaping into &eBrass Funnels&r&7 to guide the flow of materials, or extending into &eBrass Tunnels&r&7 to let energy and matter pass quietly through.&r"
		""
		"&8A line of small text in the manuscript margin: It's friendly enough that a beginner can start working with a file and hammer. Of course, don't expect to make a sword from it.&r"
	]
	quest.5057DE8E48849E95.quest_subtitle: "An important metal material, commonly used to craft advanced components"
	quest.5077E77C727BD6FD.quest_desc: ["会试图输出特定物品到容器中"]
	quest.5077E77C727BD6FD.quest_subtitle: "向RS网络输入物品或流体"
	quest.50CA5A1721E6B28E.quest_desc: ["作为顶端升级可以提供不俗的幸运值加成，前期开荒甚至后期开奖的不二之选"]
	quest.50CA5A1721E6B28E.quest_subtitle: "我真幸运"
	quest.50CB5FD8D93B2DF3.quest_subtitle: "Basic Part"
	quest.50E57652755EC341.quest_desc: [
		"{\"text\":\"\",\"extra\":[{\"text\":\"The enchanting table seems to have changed too. I can sense it's more... \",\"color\":\"gray\"},{\"text\":\"unstable\",\"color\":\"red\"},{\"text\":\" than the original version.\",\"color\":\"gray\"}]}"
		""
		"{\"text\":\"\",\"extra\":[{\"text\":\"Added the \",\"color\":\"gray\"},{\"text\":\"Apotheosis enchanting system\",\"color\":\"gold\"},{\"text\":\". Enchantment levels can exceed vanilla limits. The vast majority of enchantments have their \",\"color\":\"gray\"},{\"text\":\"level cap increased by +4\",\"color\":\"green\"},{\"text\":\". A few enchantments may have special adjustments. \",\"color\":\"gray\"},{\"text\":\"Meanwhile, the Apotheosis module provides excellent enchantment manipulation methods, allowing quick enchanting, disenchanting, and even transferring enchantments.\",\"color\":\"gray\"}]}"
		""
		"{\"text\":\"\",\"extra\":[{\"text\":\"If you are unfamiliar with \",\"color\":\"gray\"},{\"text\":\"Apotheosis\",\"color\":\"light_purple\"},{\"text\":\", you can check the specific content in the corresponding chapter.\",\"color\":\"gray\"}]}"
		""
		"{\"text\":\"\",\"extra\":[{\"text\":\"\",\"extra\":[{\"text\":\"[Click to jump]\",\"underlined\":true,\"color\":\"aqua\",\"clickEvent\":{\"action\":\"change_page\",\"value\":\"681DDFCA829035FB\"}}]}]}"
		""
		"Please be sure to check the side quests. The main questline only serves to guide the progression and contains nothing else!"
	]
	quest.50E57652755EC341.quest_subtitle: "I have a fumo table"
	quest.5125C8D0790C81BB.quest_desc: [
		"&6Rune of the Roaring Wind&r"
		""
		"&7The Rune of the Roaring Wind functions similarly to the ritual of the same name, granting the wearer a half-strength &bRoaring Wind&r&7 effect, increasing &amovement speed&r&7 and &aattack speed&r&7.&r"
	]
	quest.5125C8D0790C81BB.quest_subtitle: "Swift Pulse"
	quest.5177469D5E64C1E3.quest_desc: [
		"&6Sand Paper Polishing&r"
		""
		"&6Polishing Methods&r"
		"&7\"Sand Paper Polishing\" can be performed in the following ways:&r"
		"&7Hold Sand Paper and the item to be processed in separate hands, then right-click;&r"
		"&7Hold Sand Paper and right-click a dropped item;&r"
		"&7Have a Deployer hold Sand Paper to polish, with the same effect as manual polishing.&r"
		"&7Each polish consumes 1 durability from the Sand Paper.&r"
		""
		"&6Polishing Copper Blocks&r"
		"&7Can surface-treat vanilla Copper Blocks:&r"
		"&7If the copper block is waxed, it removes the wax;&r"
		"&7If the copper block is oxidized, it lowers the oxidation level by one.&r"
		"&7The handling mechanics are exactly the same as a vanilla axe.&r"
		""
		"&6Polishing Building Blocks&r"
		"&7Can convert some vanilla building blocks (such as stone bricks, andesite, etc.) into their corresponding \"polished\" variants.&r"
		""
		"&6Enchanting&r"
		"&7Sand Paper can be enchanted at an Enchanting Table or Anvil. Available enchantments include Unbreaking, Mending, and Curse of Vanishing.&r"
		"&8A tiny scrawl at the page edge: Would anyone really enchant this?&r"
	]
	quest.51BCF840DB0DBE44.quest_desc: ["&7This is the familiar old friend from your vanilla enchanting days, unremarkable and only providing 2 points of &l&aTier&7. But it can still lead you into the hall of enchanting."]
	quest.51BCF840DB0DBE44.quest_subtitle: "Everything Starts Here"
	quest.51BCF840DB0DBE44.title: "Magic's Oldest Friend"
	quest.51BE2E9C9209091D.quest_desc: [
		"&6Rune of the Flowing Grasp&r"
		""
		"&7The Rune of the Flowing Grasp functions similarly to the ritual of the same name, granting the wearer a half-strength &bFlowing Grasp&r&7 effect, slightly extending &ablock interaction distance&r&7 and &aitem pickup distance&r&7.&r"
	]
	quest.51BE2E9C9209091D.quest_subtitle: "Extended Pulse"
	quest.523AD23A30544888.quest_desc: ["&7词缀与属性俱为顶级，提供扎实的面板数值与可观增伤。击败死者之王后方可入手，是构筑中极具分量的组件。"]
	quest.523AD23A30544888.quest_subtitle: "愿您的旅途充满诅咒与祝福"
	quest.524A12A30F00E96E.quest_desc: ["&7血肉合金锭的上位法术升级材料，专注提升猩红法术体系相关属性，同时狂宴可叠加的最大数值进一步提升。"]
	quest.524A12A30F00E96E.quest_subtitle: "啃食欲望"
	quest.527B5583A09AF510.quest_desc: ["The Wither Skeleton Skull has a deeper connection to the Nether, thus producing a more powerful Quantization force"]
	quest.527B5583A09AF510.quest_subtitle: "Stronger Quantization Growth"
	quest.527B5583A09AF510.title: "Sacrificed Skull"
	quest.52FB65193EF182F4.quest_desc: [
		"&7&#FF6666Wrath&7  "
		"&7When attacked: applies a &#FFAA3310-second&7 &#FF6666\"Wrath Damage\"&7 mark to the attacker and makes them &#FFD700glow&7.  "
		""
		"&7When attacking:  "
		"&7When attacking a target with the &#FF6666\"Wrath Damage\"&7 mark, damage increases by &#66FF6610%&7 (increases by &#66FF6620%&7 when wearing the &#66CCFFSigil of Wrath&7), and the mark is consumed.  "
		"&7Each attack grants 1 stack of &#FFD700\"Empowered Sigil\"&7, up to &#FFAA335 stacks&7, lasting &#66FF6615 seconds&7, with each stack providing an effect.  "
		""
		"&7If you don't attack any target for &#FFAA335 seconds&7, you take &#FF666610% of max health as true damage&7. If you still haven't attacked after this triggers, you take the same damage again every &#FFAA334 seconds&7."
	]
	quest.52FB65193EF182F4.quest_subtitle: "Wrath Erosion"
	quest.52FB65193EF182F4.title: "Wrath Erosion"
	quest.530E224CB690AC4D.quest_desc: [
		"&6Abyss&r"
		"&7is an ocean biome of the Starlight Dimension, relatively rare."
		""
		"&7The Abyss's terrain feature is a typical long, narrow trench, with overall &cnarrow&r&7 space"
		"&7and an &aextremely large&r height difference from the seabed surface."
		"&7The deepest part of the Abyss biome is often &aextremely close&r&7 to the Starlight Dimension's bedrock layer (which also makes it nearly impossible for non-aquatic creatures to spawn in the Abyss biome)."
		""
		"&7The interior of the Abyss generates many unique &#1E90FFaquatic creatures&r&7 and &#FF4500Abyssal Magma Blocks&r&7 that can produce bubble columns."
		"&7The Abyss's unique plants are &#FF0000Red Moss&r&7 and &#32CD32Viscid Moss&r&7. Some coral reefs also generate near the upper layer of the Abyss."
		"&7Viscid Moss Balls can be converted into &#8FBC8Fslimeballs&r&7 in a crafting grid."
		""
		"&7Players within the Abyss biome have their vision &cextremely restricted&r&7. It is recommended that players prepare &#00FF00Night Vision Potions&r&7 and &#00CED1Water Breathing Potions&r of sufficient duration before exploring."
	]
	quest.530E224CB690AC4D.quest_subtitle: "If you gaze into the abyss..."
	quest.530E224CB690AC4D.title: "Abyss"
	quest.532E3C393BCE6BA6.quest_desc: ["&7Ghast Tears can increase the spawn count cap of the spawner. Normally, a spawner stops spawning after N creatures have spawned nearby. Ghast Tears can raise the value of N."]
	quest.532E3C393BCE6BA6.quest_subtitle: "Rush Hour Subway"
	quest.533E6E13F1C9E939.quest_desc: [
		"&6Conveyor Belt&r"
		""
		"&7It is the flowing road in a machinist's hands, responsible for carrying items between two points, or transmitting those invisible rotational forces.&r"
		""
		"&6Laying This Road&r"
		"&7You need at least two Shafts facing the same direction as start and end points. Hold the Conveyor Belt and right-click the first shaft. Red particle trails then appear where your crosshair points—that is it asking for the endpoint. Only when the particles turn green does it mean the other shaft has accepted the connection; right-click again and the road is laid. If the particles remain crimson, the placement is wrong; if the particles simply dissipate, the distance exceeds its limit.&r"
		"&7It can extend horizontally, vertically, and even at a precise 45-degree diagonal, but the total length (including the shafts at both ends) cannot exceed &c20 blocks&7 (&c15 blocks&7 if diagonal).&r"
		""
		"&6Trimming and Modifying&r"
		"&7Hold a new Conveyor Belt and right-click the end of an existing belt (this does not consume the item in your hand) to extend it one block forward, and the shaft at the end moves accordingly. To retract it, tap the end with a Wrench.&r"
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"&7Using a Wrench mid-way cuts the belt—this usually consumes two shafts (unless you're in Creative Mode). For two separated belt segments with legal total length and matching direction, hold a Conveyor Belt and click the endpoint of one segment to connect them; this returns one Conveyor Belt and two Shafts.&r"
		"&7You can also hold a Shaft and right-click an empty spot in the middle of a belt to insert a new support point; right-click with a Wrench to remove it.&r"
		""
		"&7It doesn't have to be dull metallic gray. Using dye, you can color it any shade you want. To wash off the decoration, a bucket of water or a bottle of water is enough.&r"
		""
		"&8In the blank space of the manuscript, a winding conveyor belt is drawn, with text beside it: The road is laid, now, let things move.&r"
	]
	quest.536380EE035D7850.quest_subtitle: "拿着任意末地创世的眼睛右键门框上已有的眼睛可以卸下"
	quest.5372150CD0958B7B.quest_desc: [
		"&6Crushing Wheel&r"
		""
		"&6Item Processing&r"
		"&7Designed specifically to execute '&cCrushing&r&7' recipes. Items without a corresponding recipe are destroyed directly."
		"&7Most '&cCrushing&r&7' recipes are the same as '&eMilling&r&7' recipes, so functionally it can replace most &eMillstones&7."
		"&7Must be used in pairs, and the two wheels' rotation directions must work together to function.&r"
		""
		"&6Creature Processing&r"
		"&7Active Crushing Wheels deal &cdamage&7 to creatures entering their work range (except players on Peaceful difficulty), and drop the crushed products at the output end."
		"&7This damage ignores armor, Protection enchantments, and Resistance effects, but can be offset by Absorption."
		"&7For horizontally placed Crushing Wheels, placing a block above prevents being sucked in; for vertically placed ones, placing a Chute above the gap prevents suction without affecting normal operation.&r"
		""
		"{@pagebreak}"
		""
		"&6Placement and Operation Mechanics&r"
		"&7When a pair of Crushing Wheels is correctly placed and the one block between them is unobstructed, an invisible block is automatically generated: the &eCrushing Wheel Controller&7."
		"&7This block has collision volume, cannot be moved by pistons or dynamic structures, and can be regarded as an open container that absorbs and processes items and also supports logistics input and output."
		"&7It controls the behavior of the entire Crushing Wheel assembly. When the Crushing Wheels are separated, this block disappears with them."
		""
		"&7A pair of properly working Crushing Wheels must satisfy:"
		"&7The two are only &c1 block&7 apart with nothing in between;"
		"&7Their wheel faces must be &cparallel&7.&r"
		""
		"&8There are several deep scratches here in the manuscript, as if ground by wheel teeth. The fact that you can see this manuscript is thanks to the owner installing a proper shutoff device...&r"
	]
	quest.5372150CD0958B7B.quest_subtitle: "A work component capable of crushing items."
	quest.5378D02C832E3260.quest_subtitle: "Food value >= 14"
	quest.5378D02C832E3260.title: "Feast Recovery"
	quest.5394037EDC7769D9.quest_desc: [
		"&6Pact of the Continuing Shot"
		"&7You cannot pretend to hit every shot.&r&cA missed arrow removes all draw speed bonuses and instead reduces this attribute"
		"&7Precision is the key.&r&aDealing ranged damage speeds up the draw speed of most ranged weapons"
		"{image:kubejs:textures/gui/malum/pact_of_the_continuing_shot.png width:160 height:200 align:center}"
	]
	quest.5394037EDC7769D9.quest_subtitle: "Become the Arrowhead"
	quest.5394037EDC7769D9.title: "Pact of the Continuing Shot"
	quest.53A39052B8DFFE3E.quest_desc: ["{\"text\":\"\",\"extra\":[{\"text\":\"I know you might get a headache seeing this mod's \",\"color\":\"gray\"},{\"text\":\"eyes\",\"color\":\"red\"},{\"text\":\", but now they can all be \",\"color\":\"gray\"},{\"text\":\"crafted\",\"color\":\"green\"},{\"text\":\".\",\"color\":\"gray\"}]}"]
	quest.53A39052B8DFFE3E.quest_subtitle: "Craftable"
	quest.53C821423589F530.quest_desc: [
		"Can be summoned via the Altar"
		""
		"Please do not summon it during the day—the Skeleton King goes berserk in daylight, gaining extremely high defense and a massive damage boost that can one-shot players."
		""
		"Defeating it unlocks:"
		"&#FF3D5CNether Gober Ore"
		"&r&#7EE344Chlorophyte Ore&r&7"
		"&#770808Dreadstone&r&7"
		"&#DD660ASun Core&r"
		"Zenith Ore"
		""
		"&7Special drops mainly include: Bone Glove, Orichalcum Ingots."
	]
	quest.53C821423589F530.quest_subtitle: "Stage 1 - kill to unlock Stage 2"
	quest.54207C49530C50BC.quest_desc: [
		"&6World Difficulty&r"
		"&7You may or may not have noticed, but world difficulty changes aren't just a simple name change&r"
		"&7It affects mob spawn health, damage, and more&r"
		""
		"&7&6Classic Mode&r&7: Default values&r"
		""
		"&7&6Expert Mode&r&7:&r"
		"&7Health, Attack, Armor x&c1.2&r"
		""
		"&7&6Master Mode&r&7:&r"
		"&7Health, Attack, Armor, Armor Toughness, Tracking Range x&c1.5&r"
		"{image:kubejs:textures/gui/difficuity_kjs.png width:180 height:50 align:center fit:true}"
		"&dSo... dear... if you can't win, don't play on high difficulty...&r"
	]
	quest.54207C49530C50BC.quest_subtitle: "Must-Read Notice Nobody Reads.png"
	quest.54DAB6324FA151F2.quest_desc: [
		"&7The book spat out by the well seems to have changed. Even though it is the book in which I recorded my research process, countless shadows have grown from it."
		""
		"&7I need to concentrate to make out the shapes of the shadows. They are also paper-like beings, yet tangible and intangible at once, like... Spirits."
		""
		"&7These shadows connect my research notes, like annotations, like guidance; what is written on them is familiar yet strange."
		""
		"&z&mI have seen the truth"
	]
	quest.54DAB6324FA151F2.quest_subtitle: "Falling into Darkness"
	quest.54DCDB42738F0557.quest_desc: [
		"&6Authority of the Inverted Heart&r"
		""
		"&7Your soul is the world's soul. Your heart is the world's heart. Open your heart, for all to peer into, and for all to control.&r"
		"&7-&cMagic damage&r&7 taken is quadrupled&r"
		""
		"&7Authority—the treaty between your form and the world itself.&r"
		"&7-Your soul is open to the world; if other souls see your soul, the two establish a &elink&r"
		"&7-Damage you take and deal is &bshared&r with them"
		"{image:kubejs:textures/gui/malum/authority_of_the_inverted_heart.png width:160 height:200 align:center}"
	]
	quest.54DCDB42738F0557.quest_subtitle: "Forging Many Hearts into One"
	quest.54DCDB42738F0557.title: "Authority of the Inverted Heart"
	quest.54F1765FA7F3571B.quest_desc: [
		"&7Basic trinket, no special mechanics."
		"&7Attributes are determined by &6Silent Gear&7 material traits."
	]
	quest.54F1765FA7F3571B.quest_subtitle: "Rare Treasure"
	quest.550AF87A12E6F954.quest_subtitle: "Tier 2 Grading Catalyst"
	quest.551FB78D5B444E41.quest_desc: [
		"&7The &#88DDFFMending Pylon&7 is used for Spirit repair, capable of repairing shattered &#FFAA33Catalyst Charms&7 and some items."
		""
		"&7The &#88DDFFMending Pylon&7 is &e3&7 blocks tall and has &e1&7 item slot and &e4&7 spirit slots. A &#FFCC44Redstone Comparator&7 can detect how full the slots are."
		"&7Place the repair materials and &#66FF99Spirits&7 on the Mending Pylon, and place the item to be repaired nearby (measured from the lowest block, within &e6&7 blocks horizontally and &e4&7 blocks vertically) on a &#66DDCCItem Pedestal&7, &#66DDCCItem Stand&7, or &#CC99FFRune Workbench&7 to repair it."
		""
		"&aThe interval for detecting repair recipes&7 is &e2&7 seconds. Repair takes &e32&7 seconds, and after a successful repair there is a &e60&7-second cooldown."
		"&7When repair begins, the target position is recorded; if the target is lost when the phase ends, it re-enters the recipe detection phase."
		""
		"Go to the next page to view the diagram"
		"{@pagebreak}"
		""
		"&7As shown, this is a &#88DDFFrepair&7 recipe:"
		"{image:kubejs:textures/gui/malum/repair_pylon2.png width:110 height:150 align:center}"
		"&7Items in the &#FF6666red area&7 must be placed within the &#88DDFFMending Pylon&7 structure;"
		"&7Items in the &#FFAA33orange area&7 must be placed on nearby &#66DDCCItem Stands&7, &#66DDCCItem Pedestals&7, etc.;"
		"&7Items in the &#66CCFFblue area&7 are the output items."
		""
		"&cWhen repairing items, ensure the items and Spirit quantities placed in the pylon match exactly!"
		""
		"&rGo to the next page for a practical example"
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"A simple example of repairing a Tyrfing weapon"
		"{image:kubejs:textures/gui/malum/repair_pylon.png width:150 height:150 align:center}"
	]
	quest.551FB78D5B444E41.quest_subtitle: "Mysterious Repair"
	quest.551FB78D5B444E41.title: "Arcane Restoration"
	quest.5538FE04FFC149D5.quest_desc: [
		"As an advanced version of the bookshelf, the Ocean Bookshelf provides a higher enchantment cap than normal bookshelves. The magic from the deep sea grants the bookshelf additional &5&lArcana&r&r."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"&oPS: You can check the pufferfish's JEI page&r"
	]
	quest.5538FE04FFC149D5.quest_subtitle: "Arcana's Blessing"
	quest.5538FE04FFC149D5.title: "Deep Sea Enchanting Power — Peering into Mystery"
	quest.553B4B865F0C526B.quest_desc: ["Want to remove a curse from your weapon? The properties of Prismarine Webs can adhere to and strip away curses—though no one knows how it works"]
	quest.553B4B865F0C526B.quest_subtitle: "Curse Removal"
	quest.5543C9B27A71B835.quest_desc: [
		"&7Fire is the cornerstone, and &#FFAA33metal&7 is the pillar. With &#66CCFFiron&7, I can forge &#CC99FFweapons and equipment&7 myself. I can piece materials together and strap them on for protection, but that's clearly a waste of materials—only a stopgap measure. What I truly need is a &#FFD700roaring blast furnace&7."
		""
		"&7While searching for &#66CCFFiron&7, I found some familiar crystals. These are exactly the raw materials needed for &#66DDCCHardened Steel&7. I think I'll be able to forge my own &#CC99FFequipment&7 soon."
	]
	quest.5543C9B27A71B835.quest_subtitle: "Smelting Preparations"
	quest.5543C9B27A71B835.title: "Metal Smelting"
	quest.55566ED56D9E8281.quest_desc: ["This summoning ritual can only be performed in the Cursed Garden"]
	quest.55566ED56D9E8281.quest_subtitle: "Moonvine Colossus"
	quest.55566ED56D9E8281.title: "Summoning Ritual"
	quest.555729244B7C2153.quest_desc: [
		"&6Magic Essence&r"
		"&7A consumable used to increase &bspell power&r&7 and &bspell resistance&r&7. Each type has 3 tiers and a usage cap. Obtained through the following methods:&r"
		"&7Power: Dropped by &emagic creatures&r&7, upgraded through &6rituals&r&7.&r"
		"&7Resistance: Obtained through the &eShrinker&r&7, upgraded through &6rituals&r&7.&r"
	]
	quest.555729244B7C2153.title: "&6Magic Essence: Power&r"
	quest.558E23816B266EF8.title: "Glow Leech"
	quest.55A1FBEF21D0FE68.quest_desc: [
		"Summon it by using the Abyssal Offering on the Abyssal Altar in the Sunken City structure; can be located using the Abyssal Eye, and can also be summoned via the Altar"
		""
		"&7After defeating it, you can craft the &#66CCFFTidal Claw Blueprint&7. Left-click fires an abyssal tentacle that tracks enemies; right-click fires a chain that pulls you forward."
		""
		"&7This BOSS is invincible out of water—pay attention to the summoning environment when using the Altar."
	]
	quest.55A1FBEF21D0FE68.quest_subtitle: "Stage 2"
	quest.55A79D65F67123C4.quest_desc: [
		"&6Rune of the Sky Tether&r"
		""
		"&7The Rune of the Sky Tether functions similarly to the ritual of the same name, granting the wearer a half-strength &bSky Tether&r&7 effect, increasing &ajump height&r&7, slightly reducing the effect of &agravity&r&7 on them, and very slightly reducing &cfall damage&r&7.&r"
	]
	quest.55A79D65F67123C4.quest_subtitle: "Rising Pulse"
	quest.55BA0F294A5D2F55.quest_desc: ["&7A flower infused with magic. When a caster selects a spell but has no mana left, it replenishes the energy needed.&r"]
	quest.55BA0F294A5D2F55.quest_subtitle: "Auto Recovery"
	quest.55FBD2DCCC7E79D2.quest_desc: ["永恒星光维度特产，获取较为繁琐，但其强大的词条能大幅度提升你的强度"]
	quest.55FBD2DCCC7E79D2.quest_subtitle: "永！恒！星！光！"
	quest.56820AFBA7B5FE0A.title: "Tip Upgrade Parts"
	quest.568D517E18953F2F.quest_desc: [
		"&6Crimson Essence&r"
		""
		"&7When there is water in the Alchemy Cauldron, it deals &cdamage&r&7 to creatures inside it. If there are empty potion slots, it will attempt to generate &cblood&r&7. Right-click with a glass bottle to collect and obtain &cCrimson Essence&r&7.&r"
		""
		"&8Immerse sin that still pulses into this boiling cauldron of judgment. Wait for the crimson to struggle and precipitate out from the gap between life and the liquid surface, and you may hold a bottle to catch it—that is the condensed negation formed from wrath, an extracted and stripped 'proof of life' that still carries warmth.&r"
	]
	quest.56AFCEF4D1507B1B.quest_desc: [
		"&7Fires homing &#66CCFFghost arrows&7 at enemies."
		""
		"&7Ranged damage is determined by &6Silent Gear's&7 &eranged damage&7 attribute."
		"&7Damage is also affected by &eattack speed&7: &clower attack speed means lower damage&7, minimum &c0.1&7."
	]
	quest.56AFCEF4D1507B1B.quest_subtitle: "Hacks!"
	quest.56B3E6FD85D52F60.quest_desc: [
		"{\"text\":\"\",\"extra\":[{\"text\":\"Wandering this world, I often encounter those who hold \",\"color\":\"gray\"},{\"text\":\"tomes\",\"color\":\"gold\"},{\"text\":\" and \",\"color\":\"gray\"},{\"text\":\"strange short staves\",\"color\":\"light_purple\"},{\"text\":\". The \",\"color\":\"gray\"},{\"text\":\"spells\",\"color\":\"aqua\"},{\"text\":\" they cast make my \",\"color\":\"gray\"},{\"text\":\"head split with pain\",\"color\":\"red\"},{\"text\":\".\",\"color\":\"gray\"}]}"
		"{\"text\":\"\",\"extra\":[{\"text\":\"Since I can't beat them, I might as well walk this path myself.\",\"color\":\"gray\"}]}"
		""
		"{\"text\":\"Click to jump to Iron's Spells side quests\",\"clickEvent\":{\"action\":\"change_page\",\"value\":\"60C42244ED37BA5F\"},\"underlined\":true,\"color\":\"yellow\"}"
		""
		"Please be sure to check the side quests. The main questline only serves to guide the progression and contains nothing else!"
	]
	quest.56B3E6FD85D52F60.quest_subtitle: "Endless Mysteries"
	quest.56B3E6FD85D52F60.title: "First Encounter with Magic"
	quest.56B761C2894F3C2E.quest_desc: [
		"&7A simple application of &#FFD700Hallowed Gold&7 is the &#FFAA33Spirit Jar&7."
		""
		"&7The &#FFAA33Spirit Jar&7 is used for &ainfinite storage&7 of a single type of &#66FF99Spirit&7. Its operation logic is similar to the &#66DDCCDrawer&7:"
		""
		"&7Left-click: Deposit &e1 stack&7 of &#66FF99Spirits&7"
		"&7Sneak + left-click: Withdraw &e1 stack&7 of &#66FF99Spirits&7"
		""
		"&7Right-click: Deposit &e1 stack&7 of &#66FF99Spirits&7"
		"&7Double right-click: Deposit all Spirits of the same type"
		""
		"&7Does not support automatic input and output, but you can use a &#FFCC44Deployer&7 or similar for automated access."
		""
		"&7The capacity of these jars is &anearly infinite&7, but they can only store &ca single type of Spirit&7."
	]
	quest.56B761C2894F3C2E.quest_subtitle: "&7Simple and practical &#66FF99Spirit&7 storage technology"
	quest.56B761C2894F3C2E.title: "Spirit Storage"
	quest.56CB359C8D5426A3.quest_desc: [
		"&7Please note this is for setting difficulty. &cN1&7 is not the initial difficulty. To remove difficulty settings, use the &6Clear Difficulty Settings&r below."
		""
		"&7. Base game difficulty (world difficulty)"
		""
		"&6Classic&7: stat multiplier &a1.0&7x"
		"&6Expert&7: stat multiplier &a1.2&7x"
		"&6Master&7: stat multiplier &a1.5&7x + extra &b10&7 blocks of tracking range"
		""
		"&6N1&7: Health/Armor &a2&7x, Toughness &a2&7x, Attack &a1.2&7x"
		"&6N2&7: Health/Armor &a3&7x, Toughness &a2&7x, Attack &a1.4&7x"
		"&6N3&7: Health/Armor &a4&7x, Toughness &a3&7x, Attack &a1.6&7x"
		"&6N4&7: Health/Armor &a5&7x, Toughness &a3&7x, Attack &a1.8&7x"
		"&6N5&7: Health/Armor &a6&7x, Toughness &a4&7x, Attack &a2&7x"
		"&6N6&7: Health/Armor &a8&7x, Toughness &a4&7x, Attack &a3&7x"
		"&6N7&7: Health/Armor &a10&7x, Toughness &a5&7x, Attack &a3&7x"
		"&6N8&7: Health/Armor &a12&7x, Toughness &a6&7x, Attack &a3.5&7x"
		"&6N9&7: Health/Armor &a14&7x, Toughness &a7&7x, Attack &a4&7x"
		"&6N10&7: Health/Armor &a16&7x, Toughness &a8&7x, Attack &a4.5&7x"
		"&6N11&7: Health/Armor &a18&7x, Toughness &a9&7x, Attack &a5&7x"
		"&6N12&7: Health/Armor &a20&7x, Toughness &a10&7x, Attack &a6&7x"
		""
		"&7Final stats = &6game difficulty multiplier &7× &6player stage multiplier&7"
		""
		"&cThis rule only applies to monsters&7"
		""
		"&7Difficulty is checked within &b129 blocks&7 centered on the player"
		""
		"&7The player with the &6highest stage difficulty&7 is used as the baseline"
		""
		"I know the current balance may be a bit broken, and it'll be gradually optimized in future updates—just bear with this for now ("
	]
	quest.56CB359C8D5426A3.quest_subtitle: "Abandon all hope, ye who enter here"
	quest.57045442B4763EC9.quest_subtitle: "Swimming Champion"
	quest.5704D090CFE3D913.quest_desc: ["&7Each &#66FF99Spirit&7 harvested while worn shortens &#88DDFFSoul Ward&7 recovery time by &e2&7 * &#88DDFFSoul Ward Recovery Rate&7 * &#CC99FFArcane Resonance&7. Also restores &e10&7 * &#CC99FFArcane Resonance&7 mana."]
	quest.5704D090CFE3D913.quest_subtitle: "Gain a Special Effect When Harvesting Spirits"
	quest.57084B014CE6C718.quest_desc: ["凋零标弹可以提供伤害加成，以及提供冲锋能力"]
	quest.57084B014CE6C718.quest_subtitle: "哈！看来不是浪费我子弹的家伙啊"
	quest.571979CF7DC3291C.quest_desc: [
		"&7&#FFD700Pride&7  "
		"&7Per-second effect: gain 1 stack of &#FFD700\"Divinity\"&7, each stack providing &#66FF667.5% crit chance&7 (increased to &#66FF6615%&7 when wearing the &#FFD700Crown of Pride&7), up to &#FFAA336&7 stacks (increased to &#FFAA3310&7 stacks when wearing the Crown of Pride)  "
		""
		"&7When attacking:  "
		"&7Whether a crit occurs is determined by the number of &#FFD700\"Divinity\"&7 stacks  "
		""
		"&7On crit:  "
		"&7Deals &#66FF66110% damage&7 (increased to &#66FF66120%&7 when wearing the Crown of Pride)  "
		"&7Resets &#FFD700\"Divinity\"&7 stacks  "
		"&7Gain 1 stack of &#FFD700\"Godhood\"&7, up to &#FFAA336&7 stacks (increased to &#FFAA3310&7 stacks when wearing the Crown of Pride), each stack providing &#66FF665% crit damage&7"
	]
	quest.571979CF7DC3291C.quest_subtitle: "Pride Erosion"
	quest.571979CF7DC3291C.title: "Pride Erosion"
	quest.5731A86EC589BF22.quest_desc: [
		"&7Tired of placing &bblocks&r&7 one by one?&r"
		"&7Don't worry! The &bBuilding Wand&r&7 can place multiple blocks at once!!!&r"
		""
		"&7Whether you're a design-savvy &bbuilder&r&7 or just have simple building needs, it's well worth using!&r"
	]
	quest.5731A86EC589BF22.quest_subtitle: "Artisan Craftsmanship"
	quest.57925645E9E7F4D8.quest_desc: ["&7获取是它的缺点，也是唯一的缺点。附带词条极为契合清杂场景，在面对大量敌人时效率出众"]
	quest.57925645E9E7F4D8.quest_subtitle: "奴役巨龙实在可耻"
	quest.57D76B1B33C57F9F.quest_desc: ["You've swum this long, so you probably don't lack these anymore, but I'll still give them to you—because I don't know what else to give... have some water specialties"]
	quest.57D76B1B33C57F9F.quest_subtitle: "So let me ask you, why don't I just take a boat"
	quest.581EF1441D0469EA.title: "Staff Weapons"
	quest.587FB780DD173114.quest_desc: [
		"&7Provides &#55D5D5Soul Ward capacity&7 based on &#66CCFFmagic armor&7."
		"&7Provides &#55D5D5Soul Ward recovery rate&7 based on &#66CCFFcharge value&7."
		"&7Provides &#55D5D5Soul Ward integrity&7 based on &#66CCFFmagic armor&7 and &#66CCFFcharge value&7."
		"&7Can obtain &#55D5D5pact cap&7 based on materials."
		"&7Can obtain &cknockback resistance&7 based on materials."
	]
	quest.587FB780DD173114.quest_subtitle: "A Good Partner for Soul Armor"
	quest.587FB780DD173114.title: "Soul Hunter Boots Template"
	quest.5883458218829D00.quest_desc: [
		"&7魂染钢ProMAX版本，造价高昂，效果强力，始源恶意词条提供大量灵魂护盾与镰刀熟练度。"
		""
		"推荐部位：护甲所有部位"
	]
	quest.5883458218829D00.quest_subtitle: "叠最厚的甲"
	quest.589CD98F3C3AA8D3.quest_desc: [
		"&e\"Running fast doesn't guarantee a win—not falling down is what counts as success\"&7"
		"&7Holding to the philosophy of steady, ever steadier, the quadcopter has achieved a record of 0 air disasters. As for the cost... well."
		""
		"&7A model suited for hovering assistance while building. Extremely stable but also extremely slow. Since the aircraft itself is considered silent, it can also hold its own when teasing the Warden in the Ancient City."
	]
	quest.58B30930CE3B8139.quest_desc: ["I don't even know why I made this thing"]
	quest.58B30930CE3B8139.quest_subtitle: "Don't you think its dancing is nice?"
	quest.58BCF9F1BE8BAA5E.quest_desc: [
		"&7When it fell, the power sealed within it seemed to dissipate... I must investigate and see what traces it left behind."
		""
		"\"The King of the Dead has been defeated, and the sealed minerals have reappeared.&r\""
		""
		"&#67B1E5Gober&r&7 generates in the Overworld at depths from -40 to 30"
		""
		"&#757369Rune Fragments&r&7 generate in the Overworld above height 0"
	]
	quest.58BCF9F1BE8BAA5E.quest_subtitle: "Taken down~"
	quest.58C802ED3AA66357.quest_desc: ["{\"text\":\"\",\"extra\":[{\"text\":\"I know you might get a headache seeing this mod's \",\"color\":\"gray\"},{\"text\":\"eyes\",\"color\":\"red\"},{\"text\":\", but now they can all be \",\"color\":\"gray\"},{\"text\":\"crafted\",\"color\":\"green\"},{\"text\":\".\",\"color\":\"gray\"}]}"]
	quest.58C802ED3AA66357.quest_subtitle: "Craftable"
	quest.58CA43B9AA0530E2.quest_desc: [
		"Defeat the Ignited Revenants in the Blaze Arena to obtain Blazing Embers, then use a Blazing Ember on the Blaze Altar to summon it; can be located using the Blaze Eye, and can also be summoned via the Altar"
		""
		"&7After defeating it, you can craft the &#66CCFFIncinerator Blueprint&7. Hold right-click to charge up and deal &#FFAA33massive damage&7 to entities within a certain range in front."
	]
	quest.58CA43B9AA0530E2.quest_subtitle: "Stage 2"
	quest.58DE58D4F8290C1C.quest_desc: [
		"&7This item was obtained by chance during my travels"
		""
		"&7However, with my current shallow understanding, I still cannot comprehend the mysteries hidden within it."
		""
		"Magic scrolls are dropped by killing certain special enemies, with random levels. Generally, the &6Scroll Scribing Table&r is used to craft scrolls according to demand."
		""
		"A small number of special scrolls cannot be crafted and can only be dropped by defeating the corresponding Boss, or released through specified equipment."
	]
	quest.58DE58D4F8290C1C.quest_subtitle: "Novel Power"
	quest.58DE58D4F8290C1C.title: "Magic Scroll"
	quest.58FD71F9C065E1AC.quest_desc: ["&7Take a gamble?&r"]
	quest.58FD71F9C065E1AC.quest_subtitle: "Random Spell + Random Level"
	quest.5910207B1ED4EDEA.quest_subtitle: "Tier 4 Grading Catalyst"
	quest.5914AF3C360016D7.quest_desc: ["Maybe strong, who knows"]
	quest.5914AF3C360016D7.quest_subtitle: "Graduation Template"
	quest.5920027DB9EF2592.quest_desc: ["Range is between Y=168-184, optimal mining height is Y=176"]
	quest.5920027DB9EF2592.quest_subtitle: "Since most of the Nether's bottom area is submerged in lava, Ancient Debris generation has moved to the area near the top bedrock layer"
	quest.593ABE7FAC454B34.quest_desc: [
		"&6Rune of Affliction Cleansing&r"
		""
		"&7The Rune of Affliction Cleansing urges the form to catalyze, transform, and alter matter, in order to accelerate the processing and dissolution of &cnegative effects&r&7, overcoming them at extraordinary speed.&r"
	]
	quest.593ABE7FAC454B34.quest_subtitle: "A Pulse That Spurs Processing"
	quest.598B46F6AEFCA272.quest_subtitle: "Alloy Fusion"
	quest.59CAC75D442ED208.quest_desc: [
		"&7When worn:  "
		"&7+&e50%&7 &#66FF66Scythe Proficiency&7;  "
		""
		"&7Enhances &#FFCC44Scythe&7 enchantments:  "
		""
		"&7&#FFAA33Boomerang&7: Returns immediately upon hitting an entity. Return speed increased to &e2&7x, damage dealt increased to &e1.5&7x.  "
		""
		"&7&#88DDFFSurging&7:  "
		"&7If in a &#66FF66sprinting&7 state, the player's horizontal velocity is -&e0.6&7x the view unit vector;  "
		"&7Attack range reduced to &e2&7 blocks and offset &e2&7 blocks along the view direction, damage dealt increased to &e1.25&7x.  "
		""
		"&7Disables &#FFCC44Scythe&7 sweep attacks."
	]
	quest.59CAC75D442ED208.quest_subtitle: "Scythe Authority"
	quest.59FD6ADB15123223.quest_desc: [
		"&7Blueprints and templates are important components of &#66CCFFSilent Gear&7. All equipment crafting requires a blueprint or template."
		""
		"&7Equipment crafting requires different &#FFAA33main parts&7. The type of Silent Gear equipment is determined by the &#FFAA33main part&7."
		""
		"&7You can view the equipment crafting section in EMI to see how many parts are needed to craft using this blueprint."
		""
		"&7The next page is a diagram"
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"{image:kubejs:textures/gui/silentgear/crafting_silentgear.png width:200 height:200 align:center}"
		"&7In EMI's equipment crafting interface, you will see the following:"
		"&7The &#FF6666red arrow&7 points to the equipment's &#FFAA33main part&7, which determines the equipment type;"
		"&7The &#FFD700yellow arrow&7 points to the &#66DDCCother parts&7 needed to craft the equipment. You must gather both the &#FFAA33main part&7 and the &#66DDCCother parts&7 in the crafting table to craft the complete equipment;"
		"&7That is the output interface pointed to by the &#66FF66green arrow&7."
		""
		"&7You can usually press R on the desired &#66CCFFSilent Gear&7 tool to find this interface."
	]
	quest.59FD6ADB15123223.quest_subtitle: "We Unite!"
	quest.59FD6ADB15123223.title: "Blank Blueprint / Mold Substrate"
	quest.59FF1DA682FCF7E2.quest_desc: ["Since you've enabled edit mode, you should also discover this content"]
	quest.59FF1DA682FCF7E2.quest_subtitle: "Players interested in code or other content can use this tool to quickly create expansion content"
	quest.5A39E6F1E8907C86.quest_desc: [
		"&7Flying passive creature, extremely small;"
		""
		"&7After spawning, it seeks out nearby &#8B4513Soul Sand&7, hides inside it, and transforms it into &#66DDCCSoul-Infused Soul Sand&7;"
		""
		"&7The &#AA00AALesser Wisp&7 will re-emerge after hiding in the &#66DDCCSoul-Infused Soul Sand&7 for an &#FFAA33extremely long time&7, and transforms that &#66DDCCSoul-Infused Soul Sand&7 into &#DDDDDDSuspicious Soul Sand&7;"
		""
		"&7The &#DDDDDDSuspicious Soul Sand&7 transformed this way inherits the corresponding archaeology loot table based on its biome/structure;"
		""
		"&7A &#AA00AALesser Wisp&7 that has been right-clicked with &#FFD700Honeycomb&7 / named with a &#FFD700Name Tag&7 loses its ability to burrow into &#8B4513Soul Sand&7;"
		""
		"&7You can also use a &#66CCFFGlass Bottle&7 to right-click a &#AA00AALesser Wisp&7, transforming it into a &#66CCFFWisp Bottle&7 for easier transport."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"&7The &#AA00AALesser Wisp&7 inherits some passive abilities from the &#AA00AAPhantom&7:"
		""
		"&7Immune to &#FF5555fire damage&7 and the vast majority of projectile damage (projectiles pass straight through its body);"
		""
		"&7The only projectile attack that can hurt it is the &#AA00AASpirit Arrow&7;"
		""
		"&7The &#AA00AALesser Wisp&7 dies instantly upon contact with water (fluid water, splash/lingering water bottles), and continuously loses health when exposed to rainy weather."
		"&7Hold a &#FFD700Brush&7 and long-press right-click on &#66DDCCSoul-Infused Soul Sand&7 containing a &#AA00AALesser Wisp&7 to forcibly expel it from the block"
		"&7&#AA00AALesser Wisps&7 are immune to &#AA00AASoul Buckshot&7."
	]
	quest.5A39E6F1E8907C86.quest_subtitle: "Small is also cute"
	quest.5A39E6F1E8907C86.title: "Observation: Lesser Wisp"
	quest.5A46895D552BC15F.quest_subtitle: "Am I not energetic? I'm perfectly energetic"
	quest.5A59A7F48EA53168.quest_desc: [
		"Create is basically not part of the modpack's main progression; it only serves as an automation and efficiency tool. If you're unfamiliar with or dislike Create, you can ignore this mod."
		""
		"Please be sure to check the side quests. The main questline only serves to guide the progression and contains nothing else!"
		""
		"[ { \"text\": \"Click to go to the Create side quests\", \"underlined\": true, \"color\":\"yellow\",\"clickEvent\": { \"action\": \"change_page\", \"value\": \"1FB3D1FAE9A88C39\" } } ]"
	]
	quest.5A59A7F48EA53168.quest_subtitle: "Create Power"
	quest.5A59A7F48EA53168.title: "Spinning Gears"
	quest.5A8ACB926DFAB615.quest_desc: ["Random starting class reward"]
	quest.5A8ACB926DFAB615.quest_subtitle: "You will receive a starter gift pack"
	quest.5A8ACB926DFAB615.title: "&a\"Honey That Conceals Suffering at the Start?!\""
	quest.5A8B7CD00226572C.quest_desc: [
		"&7When undead mobs are killed by a player, they have a low chance to drop a Soul Star."
		""
		"&7Right-click to throw a Soul Star like an Eye of Ender; following the direction it flies, the player can find the Night Lich Tower, where they need to place four Soul Stars on the altar to summon the Night Lich."
		""
		"&7After victory, Sulfuric Honey can be used to reset the altar and summon it again."
		""
		"&7It can also be summoned via the Altar."
	]
	quest.5A8B7CD00226572C.quest_subtitle: "Stage 1"
	quest.5A9B842FAAFBFD26.quest_desc: ["&7对火焰类伤害拥有极强的抗性，同时攻击燃烧状态的目标时可造成额外伤害"]
	quest.5A9B842FAAFBFD26.quest_subtitle: "没融化真是个奇迹"
	quest.5AD7799D9EF0BFBE.quest_desc: ["&7After defeating it, you can craft the &#66CCFFIncinerator Blueprint&7. Long-press right-click to charge up and deal &#FFAA33massive damage&7 to entities within a certain range in front."]
	quest.5AD7799D9EF0BFBE.quest_subtitle: "Kill kill kill"
	quest.5AEF01E9FF0A0727.quest_desc: [
		"&bAn upgraded version of the lead"
		""
		"&bLeft-click an animal (other targets are invalid) to store it inside. Right-click the ground to release it."
		""
		"&dNo one knows the inner workings of this rope... not even Endermen."
	]
	quest.5AEF01E9FF0A0727.quest_subtitle: "Poké Ball"
	quest.5B0DD1682972CBF0.quest_desc: ["&7拥有较高的远程伤害倍率，同时提供不错的护甲值。攻守兼备，让远程输出角色在保持火力的同时，亦具备一定的生存底气。"]
	quest.5B0DD1682972CBF0.quest_subtitle: "哔哔"
	quest.5B38A4F8CD3C9B98.quest_desc: ["{\"text\":\"\",\"extra\":[{\"text\":\"I know you might get a headache seeing this mod's \",\"color\":\"gray\"},{\"text\":\"eyes\",\"color\":\"red\"},{\"text\":\", but now they can all be \",\"color\":\"gray\"},{\"text\":\"crafted\",\"color\":\"green\"},{\"text\":\".\",\"color\":\"gray\"}]}"]
	quest.5B38A4F8CD3C9B98.quest_subtitle: "Craftable"
	quest.5B941F073DDCD277.quest_subtitle: "Eating twisted-type products raises sanity instead of lowering it"
	quest.5B941F073DDCD277.title: "&a\"Sweet Rain Blossoming from Rot\""
	quest.5BCF3F0899CE62B9.quest_subtitle: "Disable the setting for Eternal Gates to spawn naturally in the End"
	quest.5BDB153064430D05.quest_desc: [
		"&6Research: Aura Embers"
		"&7After passing through the &dWeeping Well&r&7, &eBlaze Powder&r&7 became a substance I call \"&6Aura Embers&r&7.\" Ethereal golden flames that are simultaneously solid and tangible objects. It burns like charcoal, but its flame is unrelated to the burning process."
		"&7"
		"&7Though this dazzlingly bright substance stands out among all materials obtained from the well, it still follows a similar pattern. The well stripped away certain components of the materials thrown in—impurities, material components, something more hidden; any of these are possible. In this case, what was stripped away seems to be everything except the pure flame, and what is produced is the embodiment of change."
		"&7"
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"&6Re-Examination: Aura Embers"
		"&7Contrary to my earlier conception, the well does not strip things away. It &creverses&r&7 them, replacing them with void-like similar substances. Aura Embers is probably the purest example of this: everything not belonging to &cEvolution Essence&r&7 is covered by a layer of void shadow, producing a material &afar&r&7 more perfect than \"suited for a particular purpose.\""
	]
	quest.5BDB153064430D05.quest_subtitle: "Essence of Evolution"
	quest.5C063BC7C8CDF924.quest_desc: [
		"&7Provides &#55D5D5Malice Ward capacity&7 based on &#66CCFFmagic armor&7."
		"&7Provides &#55D5D5Malice Ward recovery rate&7 based on &#66CCFFcharge value&7."
		"&7Provides &#55D5D5Malice Ward recovery bonus&7 based on &#66CCFFmagic armor&7."
		"&7Provides &#FFAA3325%&7 &#66CCFFMalice Conversion&7."
		"&7Can obtain &#55D5D5pact cap&7 based on materials."
	]
	quest.5C063BC7C8CDF924.quest_subtitle: "Number Shield Enjoyer"
	quest.5C063BC7C8CDF924.title: "Malice Fortress Helmet Template"
	quest.5C10F3B6A94BA227.quest_desc: [
		"&7Material required for crafting &#66DDCCSoulstained Steel series&7 tools, weapons, equipment, and trinkets, etc. In most cases, it provides the &#88DDFFSoul Ward&7 effect."
		""
		"&7The &#88DDFFSoul Ward&7 reduces damage taken by the player."
		""
		"&7The &#88DDFFSoul Ward&7 is affected by the following:"
		""
		"&6Soul Ward Capacity&7"
		"&6Soul Ward Firmness&7"
		"&6Soul Ward Recovery Rate&7"
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"&7The &#88DDFFSoul Ward&7 cap is the &#88DDFFSoul Ward Capacity&7."
		""
		"&7&#88DDFFSoul Ward&7 recovery interval = floor(&#FFDD55Base Recovery Time&7 / &#88DDFFSoul Ward Recovery Rate&7)."
		"&7Actual time required to restore &e1&7 point of &#88DDFFSoul Ward&7 = &#88DDFFSoul Ward&7 recovery interval + &e1&7."
		"&7When taking damage greater than &e0&7, the remaining time of this recovery is reset to &#FFDD55Base Recovery Time&7 + &#88DDFFSoul Ward&7 recovery interval."
		"&7If wearing the &#CC6666Belt of Calamity&7 and the damage type is &#CC99FFmagic damage&7, the remaining time of this recovery is reset to &e0&7 (recovers on the next player tick)."
		"&7Each &#66FF99Spirit&7 harvested while wearing the &#FFAA33Ring of Weaving&7 shortens recovery time by &e2&7 * &#88DDFFSoul Ward Recovery Rate&7 * &#CC99FFArcane Resonance&7."
		""
		"&b&lDamage Reduction"
		"&7When taking damage greater than &e0&7, if the &#88DDFFSoul Ward&7 is greater than &e0&7, damage is reduced according to the damage type."
		"&7If the damage type is &#CC99FFmagic damage&7 or the &#CC6666Belt of Boundless Absence&7 is worn, use the &#CC99FFmagic damage multiplier&7; otherwise use the &#FF8844general damage multiplier&7."
		"&7Damage taken = damage amount * damage multiplier."
		"&7&#88DDFFSoul Ward&7 loss = absorbed damage / &#88DDFFSoul Ward Firmness&7; the &#88DDFFSoul Ward&7 will not go below &e0&7."
	]
	quest.5C10F3B6A94BA227.quest_subtitle: "Casting Reality"
	quest.5C65959659507556.quest_desc: [
		"&7This item affects the spawner's minimum spawn time, usually used with a clock. Each of this item affects 10 ticks of time. After modification, the minimum is 20 ticks."
		""
		"&7The maximum spawn time combined with the minimum spawn time forms the spawn interval. The interval duration takes a random number between these two values."
	]
	quest.5C65959659507556.quest_subtitle: "I can't wait"
	quest.5C6B5AC7571785F6.quest_desc: [
		"&6Rotation Speed Controller&r"
		""
		"&6Purpose&r  "
		"&7Before use, place a &eLarge Cogwheel&7 on top. Either the Large Cogwheel above or the shaft at the bottom of the controller can serve as stress input or output.&r"
		""
		"&7Long-press right-click the rotation speed display on the controller's surface to precisely adjust the output end's &aspeed&7 and &arotation direction&7.&r"
		""
		"&7If power is input from the bottom shaft, the controller controls the top Large Cogwheel's speed and direction; if power is input from the top Large Cogwheel, the controller regulates the bottom shaft's output state.&r"
		""
		"&7You can think of it as an automatic transmission—but note: when setting a higher output speed, make sure the power source has sufficient &cstress&7, otherwise the system may overload.&r"
		""
		"&8This page of the manuscript has been torn&r"
	]
	quest.5C6B5AC7571785F6.quest_subtitle: "A transmission component that maintains a constant rotation speed"
	quest.5CCD14497FCA00DE.quest_desc: ["&7Each &#66FF99Spirit&7 harvested while worn restores &e5%&7 * &#CC99FFArcane Resonance&7 health."]
	quest.5CCD14497FCA00DE.quest_subtitle: "Gain a Special Effect When Harvesting Spirits"
	quest.5CF40BE797380E84.quest_desc: [
		"&7Killing creatures with a &#FFCC44Scythe&7 in hand easily harvests the creature's &#88DDFFsoul&7, quickly obtaining &#66FF99Spirits&7. Harvested &#66FF99Spirits&7 automatically fly toward the player."
		""
		"&7Additionally, using &#CC99FFmagic&7 can also obtain the creature's &#88DDFFsoul&7."
		""
		"&7Different creatures have different &#88DDFFsoul natures&7, so the harvested &#66FF99Spirits&7 also differ. Try killing different creatures to obtain more varieties."
	]
	quest.5CF40BE797380E84.quest_subtitle: "Harvest"
	quest.5CF40BE797380E84.title: "Any Scythe"
	quest.5D095029A0B8B414.quest_subtitle: "mcmod.cn"
	quest.5D2677DFFEE1AFA1.quest_desc: [
		"&7When mining, simultaneously destroys blocks of the same type within a &c5×5×5&7 area."
		"&7Mining while sneaking does not trigger area destruction."
	]
	quest.5D2677DFFEE1AFA1.quest_subtitle: "True Area Mining"
	quest.5DA66C973C8C8C39.quest_subtitle: "Usually unlocked only after defeating the King of the Dead"
	quest.5DAD3734F5DAA6B1.quest_desc: ["&7较大幅度提升再生能力与保命能力，在持久战中提供稳定续航与容错保障。"]
	quest.5DAD3734F5DAA6B1.quest_subtitle: "就当是为了我，活下去吧！"
	quest.5DEF70A03509B309.quest_desc: [
		"&7In Apotheosis, your spawner is highly customizable. You can adjust it yourself according to your needs.&7 Adjustment is divided into two aspects: spawn target adjustment and spawner attribute adjustment."
		""
		"&7Spawn target adjustment requires right-clicking the target spawner with an &3Arcane Ender Leash&7 that has captured a creature."
		""
		"&7Spawner attribute adjustment requires right-clicking the spawner with the corresponding adjustment item, consuming the item to adjust the spawner's attributes."
	]
	quest.5DEF70A03509B309.quest_subtitle: "Creature Energy Adjustment"
	quest.5DFF9CA04548FAB9.quest_desc: [
		"&7Unlike the other staff, this staff uses &#55D5D5soul energy&7. Right-click to fire &#CC99FFspell charges&7. Left-click can deal &#CC99FFmagic damage&7."
		""
		"&7Determined by &6Silent Gear&7 attributes:"
		"&7• Magic Damage &7→ &bSpell Damage&7 and &dCharge Capacity"
		"&7• Attack Speed &7→ &6Charge Speed"
	]
	quest.5DFF9CA04548FAB9.quest_subtitle: "The Most Basic Staff"
	quest.5E01EC2AC8CE43F0.quest_desc: [
		"&6Graveyard&r"
		"&7This new structure belongs to the &8Soul Sand Valley&r&7, a place ruled by &cdeath&r&7. &cNecromancers&r&7 are naturally drawn to these places, so you are sure to find them here.&r"
	]
	quest.5E01EC2AC8CE43F0.title: "&6Graveyard&r"
	quest.5E0B8E874FA58643.quest_desc: ["{\"text\":\"\",\"extra\":[{\"text\":\"I know you might get a headache seeing this mod's \",\"color\":\"gray\"},{\"text\":\"eyes\",\"color\":\"red\"},{\"text\":\", but now they can all be \",\"color\":\"gray\"},{\"text\":\"crafted\",\"color\":\"green\"},{\"text\":\".\",\"color\":\"gray\"}]}"]
	quest.5E0B8E874FA58643.quest_subtitle: "Craftable"
	quest.5E1CADCE38118460.quest_desc: ["造价低廉，属性却不遑多让。专为下界探索而生"]
	quest.5E313592ACB65BC2.quest_desc: [
		"&7Gober's peculiar properties allow it to carry the abilities contained in other objects. Crafting it into medals and rings lets it absorb other objects, thereby activating the corresponding effects for extended periods. Check the recipes yourself. Notably, even rings do not need to be worn—simply activating them and placing them in an Ender Chest will make them take effect."
		""
		"&7Note: The Low-Grade Healing Medal's effect is to slowly restore the player's saturation."
	]
	quest.5E313592ACB65BC2.title: "Gober Medals/Rings"
	quest.5E3B1B0AB352F0F3.quest_subtitle: "Familiar Summoning Ritual"
	quest.5E4E12ACE4F534AD.quest_desc: [
		"{\"text\":\"\",\"extra\":[{\"text\":\"Holding and \",\"color\":\"gray\"},{\"text\":\"right-clicking\",\"color\":\"yellow\"},{\"text\":\" will cause an \",\"color\":\"gray\"},{\"text\":\"Abyssal Eye\",\"color\":\"blue\"},{\"text\":\" copy to fly from the player's hand toward the nearest \",\"color\":\"gray\"},{\"text\":\"Sunken City\",\"color\":\"blue\"},{\"text\":\", while the Abyssal Eye in the player's hand enters a \",\"color\":\"gray\"},{\"text\":\"3s\",\"color\":\"yellow\"},{\"text\":\" cooldown.\",\"color\":\"gray\"}]}"
		""
		"{\"text\":\"\",\"extra\":[{\"text\":\"The flight function only works in the \",\"color\":\"gray\"},{\"text\":\"Overworld\",\"color\":\"green\"},{\"text\":\". It will not work in the \",\"color\":\"gray\"},{\"text\":\"Nether, the End\",\"color\":\"red\"},{\"text\":\", or worlds without a Sunken City.\",\"color\":\"gray\"}]}"
	]
	quest.5E4E12ACE4F534AD.quest_subtitle: "Sunken City"
	quest.5E513FFD985CDDF9.quest_desc: [
		"&6Golem Forge&r"
		"&7is a large underground structure guarded by the &cStarlight Golem&r&7."
		""
		"&7The Golem Forge usually generates in the &8Voidstone Layer&r&7 at Y<0, mainly composed of &8Voidstone&r&7, &#C0C0C0Golem Steel&r&7, and &#8B7355Oxidized Golem Steel&r&7 decorative blocks."
		"&7The structure's interior is overall made of large numbers of &8narrow passages&r&7, connecting the various rooms below filled with &#FF4500lava&r&7."
		""
		"&7Some rooms generate &bFrozen Man Spawners&r&7, and such rooms also have a higher chance to generate &6loot barrels&r."
		"&7You can use the &eEye of Seeking&r&7 to locate this structure."
		""
		"&4The Starlight Golem is immune to damage while connected to energy blocks"
	]
	quest.5E513FFD985CDDF9.quest_subtitle: "A bulwark that once sheltered countless living beings now leaves only broken walls and ruins silent in the wind and sand."
	quest.5E513FFD985CDDF9.title: "Golem Forge"
	quest.5E69573B6AA70AFA.quest_desc: [
		"&6Acceleration Lining&r"
		""
		"&7The Acceleration Lining utilizes the highly conductive components of Strange Fabric, greatly increasing the &eCrucible's&7 &aFocusing Speed&r&7 with no negative side effects.&r"
	]
	quest.5E69573B6AA70AFA.quest_subtitle: "Doubling Down"
	quest.5E69992403F40955.quest_subtitle: "Familiar Summoning Ritual"
	quest.5E81AAD675EB0F0F.quest_desc: [
		"Before challenging the final boss, please check whether all stages have been fully unlocked"
		"The final BOSS is extremely difficult compared to N0. Please respond with caution"
	]
	quest.5E81AAD675EB0F0F.quest_subtitle: "Summoning Ritual"
	quest.5E89F969FC7A8AF9.quest_desc: ["在前期，最高贵的就是基础值加成"]
	quest.5E89F969FC7A8AF9.quest_subtitle: "优秀的基础伤害加成"
	quest.5EB5BBBCE2AB1245.quest_subtitle: "A handy tool for finding the Weeping Well"
	quest.5EC974496B2CB2F2.quest_desc: [
		"&7Ammunition for bows / crossbows and similar weapons, or dispensers. Fires with a &#55D5D5soul particle&7 trail;  "
		"&7After firing, it can &#66CCFFignore block obstruction&7 and fly through blocks;  "
		""
		"&7This also means that Spirit Arrows that miss creatures will not land, but pass straight through the ground and &#FF6666fall into the void&7 (not returned);  "
		""
		"&7Spirit Arrows are one of the very few projectile attacks that can hurt &#66FF66Phantoms&7, &#66FF66Lesser Wisps&7, or players wearing &#66CCFFPhantom Husk&7 enchanted equipment;  "
		"&7They can also hit Spirit-Tier Horrors in the &#FFD700burrowed state&7."
	]
	quest.5EC974496B2CB2F2.quest_subtitle: "Headshot!"
	quest.5F1C1AA992472C3D.quest_desc: [
		"&6Rune of Heresy&r"
		""
		"&7The Rune of Heresy dismantles magic, thereby &csilencing&r&7 enemies, similar to the Scepter of Erosion. This effect weakens their &eSpirit Magic&r&7, and the effect itself can stack to completely suppress an opponent's &cmagic abilities&r&7.&r"
	]
	quest.5F1C1AA992472C3D.quest_subtitle: "Destroying the Created"
	quest.5F253340FE9F4FCF.quest_desc: [
		"&7Many new materials have been unlocked. It's time to upgrade your equipment and try more alloy combinations, choosing materials according to your needs."
		""
		"&7Many of the Stage One recommended materials from the Silent Gear chapter are still usable. Under the powerful alloy system, it's necessary to weigh materials' traits and values. When incorporating as many traits as possible, you also need to comprehensively consider attributes like armor value/damage."
	]
	quest.5F253340FE9F4FCF.quest_subtitle: "Brand New"
	quest.5FC4F86EF4128003.quest_desc: [
		"&7When attacking, &#FF6666deals an extra instance of damage&7 equal to the target creature's base &#55D5D5Spirit&7 drop count × &#FFAA332&7."
		"&7If the target is a player, the damage is 4 × max(1, (1 + target armor value / 12) × (1 + (1 - 1 / target armor value)) / 12)"
		"&fBefore the target's armor value exceeds 60 (× 30), this value is 4."
		""
		"&7Example: A Creeper drops 4 &#55D5D5Spirits&7, so the &#FF6666extra damage&7 is 4 × 2 = &#FFAA338 points&7."
	]
	quest.5FC4F86EF4128003.quest_subtitle: "Kill!"
	quest.5FFB29607E15D805.quest_desc: [
		"&6Pact of Defiance"
		"&7Magic has transformed your understanding of death: damage becomes ever more &cpainful&r&7.&r&cMax health reduced by one fifth"
		"&7An unnatural recovery ability is fused into the form: an ever-&agrowing&r&7 &adesire&r&7.&r&aSaturation-based health regeneration is doubled, and tripled when near death&r&aHealing received increased by four tenths"
		""
		"{image:kubejs:textures/gui/malum/pact_of_defiance.png width:160 height:200 align:center}"
	]
	quest.5FFB29607E15D805.quest_subtitle: "Defying Limits"
	quest.5FFB29607E15D805.title: "Pact of Defiance"
	quest.601016E861B6036F.quest_subtitle: "奥法之巅"
	quest.6038063D7681AFB5.quest_subtitle: "Food value >= 14"
	quest.6038063D7681AFB5.title: "Feast Recovery x32"
	quest.606FF1CD4B6D090C.quest_desc: ["You can convert some vanilla equipment directly into Silent Gear at a crafting table, letting you experience Silent Gear right from the start"]
	quest.606FF1CD4B6D090C.quest_subtitle: "Ready to Eat Out of the Bag"
	quest.606FF1CD4B6D090C.title: "Conversion"
	quest.609276A8CA8ACF91.quest_desc: [
		"&7Eating rotten food while worn (Rotten Flesh, &#66BB66Decayed Essence&7, &#FFAA33Gluttony Condensate&7):"
		""
		"&7Eating time halved;"
		"&7Extends the &#FF8844Gluttony&7 effect by &e15&7 seconds, up to &e150&7 seconds (only extends an existing effect);"
		"&7Shortens the Hunger effect by &e7.5&7 seconds;"
		"&7Additionally restores &e1&7 hunger and &e1&7 saturation."
		""
		"&7After eating &#FFAA33Gluttony Condensate&7, each &#66DDCCRing of Craving Gluttony&7 worn increases the &#FF8844Gluttony&7 effect's level by +&e1&7 and duration by +&e10&7 seconds."
	]
	quest.609276A8CA8ACF91.quest_subtitle: "Endless Hunger"
	quest.60BAD1C5ADE6C33A.quest_desc: [
		"&6Research: Malignant Lead"
		"&7After passing through the &dWeeping Well&r&7, &eDeeprock Aurum&r&7 converts into &cMalignant Lead&r&7. Most of the various arcane energies bound to gold transform into &cMalefic Arcane Energy&r&7, and this metal therefore falls from the alchemist's altar, becoming the lowest-grade material."
		"&7"
		"&7The arcane energy within the metal has also roughly halved. Was it stripped away by the well, or transformed into something I have not yet separated and identified? Both explanations could hold. This may be related to the arcane interaction ability displayed by &8Void Slate&r&7..."
		"&7"
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"&6Re-Examination: Malignant Lead"
		"&7I currently have only &cMalignant Lead&r&7 as a way to examine the physical form of &8Umbral Crystals&r&7—it has precisely lost half its arcane mass; what else could have caused that?"
		"&7"
		"&7Separating the microcrystals in &eDeeprock Aurum&r&7 and separating the malefic crystals in &cMalignant Lead&r&7 have both still yielded no results. But until I can obtain more materials, this is the best way to study the structure of &8Umbral Arcane Energy&r&7."
	]
	quest.60BAD1C5ADE6C33A.quest_subtitle: "Turning Wonder into Rot"
	quest.60BBE14FB14FB583.quest_desc: [
		"&7This bookshelf differs from previous ones. You can place books in it yourself like a chiseled bookshelf, but it displays precise and powerful magic isolation. &eWhen enchanting, it completely isolates the enchantments it contains (for enchanted books with multiple enchantments, only the first enchantment is isolated)&7, so the Enchanting Table will no longer obtain that enchantment."
		""
		"&7What is this? I feel maternal love here. Like a doting mother, it strips away everything you don't want to have."
	]
	quest.60BBE14FB14FB583.quest_subtitle: "Like a Baby in Its Mother's Arms"
	quest.60BBE14FB14FB583.title: "Embrace of the Ocean"
	quest.60C42244ED37BA5F.quest_desc: [
		"{\"text\":\"\",\"extra\":[{\"text\":\"Looking through my pack, fortunately there are still a few \",\"color\":\"gray\"},{\"text\":\"ancient scrolls\",\"color\":\"gold\"},{\"text\":\"—it turns out they were in my hands all along, I just never looked closely.\",\"color\":\"gray\"}]}"
		"{\"text\":\"\",\"extra\":[\"\"]}"
		"{\"text\":\"\",\"extra\":[{\"text\":\"The so-called \",\"color\":\"gray\"},{\"text\":\"\\\"magic\\\"\",\"color\":\"aqua\"},{\"text\":\" of this world may be hidden within, quietly awaiting a key.\",\"color\":\"gray\"}]}"
	]
	quest.60C42244ED37BA5F.quest_subtitle: "Magical Creations"
	quest.60CCCAA11DDEA68F.quest_desc: [
		"&7Functions similarly to the Rift Anchor Blade; can be thrown. It actively tracks &#FFAA33all nearby creatures&7, &#66CCFFrapidly dashing and slashing&7 between targets, and applies a &#FF6666Hatred&7 effect that stacks with each hit, up to &#FFAA33Hatred X&7. Higher stacks mean more extra damage."
		""
		"&7When thrown, the Rift Anchor Blade in the inventory temporarily transforms into a &#66CCFFAnchor Blade Spirit&7, restoring after it returns."
		""
		"&7Determined by &6Silent Gear&7 attributes:"
		"&7• Attack Damage &7→ &cPhysical Damage"
		"&7• Magic Damage &7→ &bMagic Damage"
		"&7• Attack Speed &7→ &6Cooldown"
	]
	quest.60CCCAA11DDEA68F.quest_subtitle: "Although expensive, you can definitely make it by now"
	quest.6130B6740A8460CE.quest_desc: [
		"&7Left-click to throw a yo-yo, continuously attacking enemies within range."
		""
		"&7Determined by &6Silent Gear&7 attributes:"
		"&7• Attack Damage &7→ &cDamage"
		"&7• Attack Damage &7→ &aAttack Range"
		"&7• Attack Damage &7→ &dDuration"
	]
	quest.6130B6740A8460CE.quest_subtitle: "Swaying To and Fro"
	quest.613D2E97D95993FF.quest_subtitle: "A Mother's Tenderness"
	quest.613D3C5BA25706B6.quest_subtitle: "Is this... a crafting table?"
	quest.613D3C5BA25706B6.title: "Where It All Begins"
	quest.61CD195A772A6255.quest_desc: [
		"&7When &#6Sanity&7 drops to &e-45&7, you have a chance to enter &#88DDFFErosion State&7."
		""
		"&7If you are wearing a &#FFD700Seven Sins Trinket&7, you will be eroded by the corresponding sin."
		""
		"&7Without a trinket, there is a &e25%&7 chance of being eroded by a random sin, and a &e75%&7 chance of falling into &#FF6666Panic&7."
		""
		"&7Once eroded, the Erosion State cannot be removed through normal natural Sanity recovery. It must be removed by death or by consuming items that restore Sanity"
	]
	quest.61CD195A772A6255.quest_subtitle: "Erosion State"
	quest.62214066B0F19784.quest_desc: ["&7Tired of the annoying slaughterhouse noise? Tired of hearing creatures oink and squeak? This modification makes creatures spawned by the spawner no longer emit sound. Reduces noise pollution."]
	quest.62214066B0F19784.quest_subtitle: "SHUT UP!"
	quest.623ECC7C41919422.quest_desc: [
		"&7Attacks have a chance to become &#FFAA33critical hits&7."
		"&7After killing a target, the next attack is &#FFAA33guaranteed to crit&7."
		"&7Attack power is determined by &6Silent Gear's&7 &cattack damage&7 attribute."
	]
	quest.623ECC7C41919422.quest_subtitle: "Every Slash Blazing, Every Slash Crit"
	quest.629600F80E05353F.quest_desc: [
		"&7当权限管理器被添加至存储网络，默认所有玩家都不能访问。"
		""
		"后备权限卡定义了没有对应权限卡的玩家的权限。"
		""
		"&7配置界面与权限卡相同。"
	]
	quest.629600F80E05353F.quest_subtitle: "&m后备隐藏能...权限...!"
	quest.62B6DB17872E27D4.quest_desc: ["&7基础值优秀，星光亲和度极高，即便只吃词条效果也毫不逊色。入手不亏，泛用性极强。"]
	quest.62B6DB17872E27D4.quest_subtitle: "星语之核"
	quest.630EEC8565D962D6.quest_desc: ["&7拥有优秀的远程属性加成，攻击命中叠加至一定层数后，将消耗少量生命值触发额外伤害。以血换伤"]
	quest.630EEC8565D962D6.quest_subtitle: "将我抹去！也将你抹去！"
	quest.631BFAA4FFA96698.quest_desc: ["可以直接从网络中取出物品进行编辑模板"]
	quest.631BFAA4FFA96698.quest_subtitle: "制作模板"
	quest.6324F101E1CFA4CA.quest_desc: [
		"&6Shimmer River&r"
		"&7is one of the surface biomes of the Starlight Dimension."
		""
		"&7Just like rivers in the Overworld, it is usually a &8transitional biome&r that separates waterways within one biome or across multiple biomes."
		"&7The Shimmer River is narrow and long, but it eventually flows into the vast &#87CEEBStarlit Sea&r."
		""
		"&7The Shimmer River also has a small amount of &#9ACD32Abyssal Fruit Plants&r&7 and lily-pad-like &#20B2AAaquatic vegetation&r."
		"&7Non-aquatic creatures can only spawn underground, dozens of blocks deep from the Shimmer River. Actually, that basically doesn't count as being in the river anymore."
	]
	quest.6324F101E1CFA4CA.quest_subtitle: "Shimmer in the Lake"
	quest.6324F101E1CFA4CA.title: "Shimmer River"
	quest.633471475BE20F2E.quest_desc: [
		"&7Material dropped after killing a &#ADD8E6Light Puffer&r&7 (creature);&r"
		""
		"Can be used to craft ink"
		""
		"&8Who knows how it conjures up two glass bottles?"
	]
	quest.633B88042B030B5E.quest_subtitle: "The long, long night... hardest to endure~"
	quest.63423F9C2A3931E5.quest_desc: ["&7Mining speed may be lower than an axe, but it can &#66DDCCfell an entire tree&7 in one go."]
	quest.63423F9C2A3931E5.quest_subtitle: "One Tree at a Time"
	quest.634CBFD54B22E624.quest_desc: [
		"&6Brass Funnel&r"
		""
		"&6Purpose&r"
		"&7Its basic usage is almost identical to the Andesite Funnel, with the core difference being that the Brass Funnel allows finer control: it supports &eitem filtering&7 and can set the &enumber of items transferred per operation&7.&r"
		"&7In output mode, look at its filter slot and scroll the wheel to adjust the single output amount, up to &c64&7.&r"
		""
		"&6Additional Notes&r"
		"&7The Brass Funnel can output up to a full stack of items at a time.&r"
		"&7When in downward output mode, it only continues outputting when it detects no dropped items within one block below; if items have piled up below, output pauses.&r"
		""
		"&8It's smart enough to know when to stop.&r"
	]
	quest.6386F7A674C56D65.quest_subtitle: "钢棍Plus"
	quest.639AC8246CA81675.quest_desc: ["{\"text\":\"\",\"extra\":[{\"text\":\"I know you might get a headache seeing this mod's \",\"color\":\"gray\"},{\"text\":\"eyes\",\"color\":\"red\"},{\"text\":\", but now they can all be \",\"color\":\"gray\"},{\"text\":\"crafted\",\"color\":\"green\"},{\"text\":\".\",\"color\":\"gray\"}]}"]
	quest.639AC8246CA81675.quest_subtitle: "Craftable"
	quest.63A0E5D82118EC71.quest_desc: ["&7属性极佳的泛用性材料，适配各类装备组合，堪称构筑基石。升变效果可提升绝大多数词缀等级，让已有体系再攀新高，是后期优化的不二之选。"]
	quest.63A0E5D82118EC71.quest_subtitle: "变彩"
	quest.63D0E7814E6F4017.quest_desc: ["和骨头相差无几，但是会每5秒召唤鬼火攻击附近敌人，在前期探索时较为有用，需击杀丧魂人获取"]
	quest.63D0E7814E6F4017.quest_subtitle: "魑魅魍魉"
	quest.6449D872847D4B67.quest_desc: ["I can't believe my little raggedy pack actually attracted an art teacher!"]
	quest.6449D872847D4B67.quest_subtitle: "Art"
	quest.6456C4ED798E5EBD.quest_desc: [
		"&6Crimson Forest&r"
		"&7is one of the surface biomes of the Starlight Dimension."
		""
		"&7Unlike most biomes, the Crimson Forest's main color tone is a low-brightness, low-saturation &#DC143Cred&r&7 rather than purple."
		"&7The main tree species of the Crimson Forest is the &#DC143CCrimson Tree&r."
		""
		"&7&#FFD700Glowing Mushrooms&r&7 (features) are more likely to generate within the Crimson Forest."
		"&7Most plant species generating on the Crimson Forest surface are the same as those in the Starlight Forest, but there are also a few unique plant species."
	]
	quest.6456C4ED798E5EBD.quest_subtitle: "A polluted forest, slowly purifying itself"
	quest.6456C4ED798E5EBD.title: "Crimson Forest"
	quest.647E80D4B00C0C82.quest_desc: ["&7The &#FFAA33Boomerang&7 enchantment creates wind vortexes, but the &#FFAA33Boomerang&7 cooldown is extended."]
	quest.647E80D4B00C0C82.quest_subtitle: "Scythe Authority"
	quest.648E4AF815BE0547.quest_desc: [
		"&7Attack damage dealt by the scythe is boosted by &#66CCFFScythe Proficiency&7."
		""
		"&7When attacking a creature with a scythe or spell, the creature's &#55D5D5soul&7 is exposed for &#FFAA3310 seconds&7, refreshing the duration on repeated triggers."
		""
		"&7During this period, when the creature dies, its &#55D5D5soul&7 is shattered, triggering &#55D5D5Spirit Harvest&7 and &#CC99FFSilent Harvest&7."
	]
	quest.648E4AF815BE0547.quest_subtitle: "Tearing Souls"
	quest.6495C96750D3BA0C.quest_desc: ["&7Some models can mount aircraft weapons, but generally aircraft don't really need combat. Among them, the bomb bay has decent output but high consumption."]
	quest.64AC4146C392E8A6.quest_desc: [
		"&7&#FFD700Envy&7  "
		"&7When attacking:  "
		"&7Applies a &#FFAA3310-second&7 &#FF6666\"Hostility\"&7 mark to the target  "
		"&7Against targets without the &#FF6666\"Hostility\"&7 mark, &#FF6666damage is reduced by 30%&7  "
		""
		"&7When attacking a target with the &#FF6666\"Hostility\"&7 mark:  "
		"&7Steals 1 positive effect from the target (at most once per 0.5 seconds)  "
		"&7Reduces the target's &#FF66665% max health&7  "
		"&7The stealer gains &#66FF66temporary health&7  "
		""
		"&7Passive: When attacked by someone with the &#FFD700Envy&7 effect, if you don't have the &#FF6666\"Hostility\"&7 mark, &#FF6666damage is reduced by 30%&7"
	]
	quest.64AC4146C392E8A6.quest_subtitle: "Envy Erosion"
	quest.64AC4146C392E8A6.title: "Envy Erosion"
	quest.64CF53BF15E89336.quest_subtitle: "Basic Part"
	quest.64E40E59C864874C.quest_desc: [
		"&6Meteor Shower&r"
		"&7is a special weather that can only occur in the &bStarlight Dimension&r&7, with a low occurrence probability."
		""
		"&7During a Meteor Shower:"
		"&7Several meteors with &dpurple trails&r&7 fall in straight lines, striking the ground and dealing &cdamage&r to creatures within one block."
		"&7Resource-containing &emeteorites&r&7 also have a chance to fall in the same way. Upon hitting the ground, they produce an &cexplosion&r&7 (does not destroy terrain) and burst out particles."
		""
		"&7After a meteorite falls, it has a chance to produce only &b8&r &6Raw Celestial Ore&r."
		"&7It also has a chance to generate several resource blocks composed of &eNebula Stone&r&7 and &6Raw Celestial Blocks&r at the impact position."
		"&7After a meteorite falls, it has a chance to spawn a &cBitter Comet Fear&r on the spot."
		""
		"&7Survival-mode players can craft and launch a &bStar-Guiding Rocket&r&7 to actively trigger a Meteor Shower event."
		"&7&8Small Bitter Comet Fears&r&7 begin to spawn naturally in any low-light area of the Starlight Dimension during a Meteor Shower event."
		"&7You can build an &aCelestial Golem&r&7 to intercept meteorites falling toward the ground."
	]
	quest.64E40E59C864874C.quest_subtitle: "Meteor showers sometimes occur here. During a meteor shower, countless meteors streak across the night sky, creating a beautiful spectacle..."
	quest.64E40E59C864874C.title: "Meteor Shower"
	quest.651B146F0F9BEA1D.quest_desc: [
		"&6Mechanical Press&r"
		""
		"&6Pressing&r"
		"&7Recipes that process dropped items or items on a &eConveyor Belt/Depot&r&7 using the Mechanical Press.&r"
		"&7Mainly used to process metal ingots into &eMetal Plates&r&7.&r"
		""
		"&6Packing&r"
		"&7Recipes that process items inside a &eBasin&r&7 using the Mechanical Press.&r"
		"&7Can be used to process various ingredients into finished products.&r"
		""
		"&6Automatic Compacting&r"
		"&7Recipes that process items inside a &eBasin&r&7 using the Mechanical Press.&r"
		"&7Used to execute &c4*4&r&7 or &c9*9&r&7 single-material crafting recipes."
	]
	quest.65477F1881F13EBB.quest_desc: ["通过榨血获取，或通过战利品获得，可以在前期较为快速的提供属性值加成"]
	quest.65477F1881F13EBB.quest_subtitle: "提供法强加成"
	quest.65823964A5871AED.quest_desc: ["&dCompared to the previous generation, this version is much more stable, and can even contain some creatures that would resist... dispose of them as you please.&r"]
	quest.65823964A5871AED.quest_subtitle: "Master Ball"
	quest.65B3DDCC5C5B7361.quest_desc: [
		"&6Deployer&r"
		""
		"&6Purpose&r"
		"&7The Deployer has two work modes: Use and Attack. Players can switch between them with a Wrench.&r"
		""
		"&6Use Mode&r"
		"&7The Deployer defaults to Use/Place mode, simulating a player's right-click behavior.&r"
		"&7In this mode, it can place blocks, operate doors, shear sheep, and essentially perform any action possible via right-click in Survival Mode.&r"
		"&7When given a tool or item, enchantments take effect and durability is consumed; when given food, it can feed creatures.&r"
		""
		"&6Attack/Break Mode&r"
		"&7Simulates a player's left-click behavior, including attacking creatures and breaking blocks. When given a weapon or tool, enchantments take effect but durability is consumed.&r"
		"&7Creatures killed by the Deployer count as killed by the player and drop their exclusive items and experience normally.&r"
		"&7The Deployer's attacks are always fully charged, regardless of its work speed.&r"
		""
		"&6Operation Mechanics&r"
		"&7Once powered, the Deployer's forearm extends and retracts rhythmically, performing one use or attack action at full extension.&r"
		"&7The full work cycle is: extend → use/attack → retract → wait.&r"
		"&7Extension frequency is determined by rotation speed. Its effective work speed range is &c4 RPM&7 to &c256 RPM&7; beyond this range, speed changes no longer affect efficiency.&r"
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"&7The Deployer's target is always the block or entity in the second block in front, unaffected by intervening blocks.&r"
		"&6The Deployer stops working under the following conditions:&r"
		"&7Item overflow;"
		"&7No power;"
		"&7The held item is the item form of the target block;"
		"&7The held item is the bucketed form of the target fluid;"
		"&7Receiving a redstone signal (if an action is in progress when activated, it waits for that cycle to finish before stopping).&r"
		""
		"&6Item Storage&r"
		"&7The Deployer has one stack of internal item storage, and items can be input or output through logistics components.&r"
		"&7Placing an item or filter in its filter slot marks items forbidden from being output.&r"
		"&7When the Deployer performs operations that produce drops, such as shearing, breaking blocks, or killing creatures, the products go directly into its internal storage. If there are already items inside, it enters overflow state.&r"
		""
		"&6Item Overflow&r"
		"&7The Deployer enters overflow state in the following two cases:&r"
		"&7More than one type of item is stored inside;"
		"&7Internal items do not match the item set in the filter slot.&r"
		"&7In overflow state the Deployer stops working. Excess items must be removed via logistics components before it resumes.&r"
		"&7Placing a tool currently in use in the filter slot prevents that tool from being accidentally output.&r"
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"&6Feeding/Breeding&r"
		"&7In Use mode, the Deployer can consume held food to feed creatures or players. Fed creatures enter breeding state, while players restore hunger and saturation and gain the food's status effects.&r"
		""
		"&6Item Processing&r"
		"&7The Deployer must be placed above a Depot or Conveyor Belt to process items on them. See the relevant usage notes for specific applications.&r"
		""
		"&6Dynamic Structures&r"
		"&7A Deployer on a dynamic structure still works while moving, but its held item is not displayed.&r"
		"&7You can right-click a Deployer on a dynamic structure to give it items directly, or right-click with a Wrench to switch its work mode.&r"
		"&7A Deployer on a dynamic structure can automatically draw items from the structure's storage and automatically return overflow items to that storage.&r"
		"&7When a deployed schematic is placed in the filter slot, the Deployer draws blocks from the structure's storage to place according to the schematic. This can be used to build automated construction systems like '&e3D Printers&7'.&r"
		""
		"&8It can do what you do—just more stubborn, and more tireless.&r"
	]
	quest.65B599AA9888FBF2.quest_desc: [
		"&6Starcore Mechanism&r"
		""
		"&7Drawing on harmonic crystals forged deep within the star core, the Starcore Mechanism unconditionally stabilizes the foundational framework of the &eTuning Process&r&7, permanently increasing its strength."
	]
	quest.65B599AA9888FBF2.quest_subtitle: "Starry Blessing"
	quest.660EAD8BBC2734CA.quest_desc: [
		"&7&#66CCFFSloth&7  "
		"&7When taking damage:  "
		"&7Upon taking any damage, deals &#CC99FFmagic damage&7 based on your armor value to all enemies within &#FFAA332 blocks&7 (&#FFAA331-second&7 cooldown)  "
		"&7Also triggers a &#66FF6615% damage reduction&7 effect"
	]
	quest.660EAD8BBC2734CA.quest_subtitle: "Sloth Erosion"
	quest.660EAD8BBC2734CA.title: "Sloth Erosion"
	quest.66417960000F082A.quest_desc: ["{\"text\":\"\",\"extra\":[{\"text\":\"I know you might get a headache seeing this mod's \",\"color\":\"gray\"},{\"text\":\"eyes\",\"color\":\"red\"},{\"text\":\", but now they can all be \",\"color\":\"gray\"},{\"text\":\"crafted\",\"color\":\"green\"},{\"text\":\".\",\"color\":\"gray\"}]}"]
	quest.66417960000F082A.quest_subtitle: "Craftable"
	quest.66481C79877E0ED7.quest_subtitle: "Food value >= 14"
	quest.66481C79877E0ED7.title: "Feast Recovery x10"
	quest.664DF00DAF0D957A.quest_desc: [
		"&6Rune of Flame Solace&r"
		""
		"&7The Rune of Flame Solace toughens the skin when the wearer is on fire, granting a certain amount of &aresistance&r&7 to all types of damage taken. However, it does nothing about the &cflames&r&7 currently burning.&r"
	]
	quest.664DF00DAF0D957A.quest_subtitle: "That Which Feeds the Burning"
	quest.664E9A6E52944333.quest_desc: [
		"&7Hold a &#FFCC44Lantern Tongs&7 in one hand and a &#66FF99Spirit&7 in the other, right-click to consume the &#66FF99Spirit&7 and place the corresponding type of &#66FF99Spirit Cluster Block&7. Can be used for decoration."
		""
		"&7&#888888Umbral Spirits&7 and &#66DDCCClear Spirits&7 cannot be used to place &#66FF99Spirit Cluster Blocks&7."
		""
		"&7These arcane cluster blocks are condensations of pure arcane energy, with a thin layer of protective magic on the outside to prevent leakage. They are nearly useless in magic, but look very beautiful as lamps."
	]
	quest.66934F0F1697D259.quest_desc: [
		"&7Provides &#55D5D5Soul Ward capacity&7 based on &#66CCFFmagic armor&7."
		"&7Provides &#55D5D5Soul Ward recovery rate&7 based on &#66CCFFcharge value&7."
		"&7Provides &#55D5D5Soul Ward integrity&7 based on &#66CCFFmagic armor&7 and &#66CCFFcharge value&7."
		"&7Can obtain &#55D5D5pact cap&7 based on materials."
		"&7Can obtain &cknockback resistance&7 based on materials."
	]
	quest.66934F0F1697D259.quest_subtitle: "A Good Partner for Soul Armor"
	quest.66934F0F1697D259.title: "Soul Hunter Helmet Template"
	quest.66B362ABCF6C2B8D.quest_desc: [
		"&7&#888888Tainted Stone&7 decorative blocks can be used for decoration. Blocks crafted from &#888888Tainted Stone&7 are immune to &#FFD700Totem&7 rituals, and are used at the &#CC99FFRune Workbench&7 to craft &#FFAA33Runes&7."
		""
		"&7Stone resists change, but the energy of the &#88DDFFUnbound Soul&7 is also irresistible."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"&7By forcing it to change with &#FF8844Primal Arcane Energy&7, a stone with practical magical properties can be made. If &#88DDFFHallowed Arcane Energy&7 is used as the catalyst, it forms &#9966CCTainted Stone&7, a stone that can dissolve surrounding magic."
	]
	quest.66B362ABCF6C2B8D.quest_subtitle: "Arcane Saturation"
	quest.66B362ABCF6C2B8D.title: "Spirit Stone"
	quest.66D8D31B50D06630.quest_subtitle: "Village Hero...?"
	quest.66E6753DF809DA3D.quest_desc: ["将样板置入后，即可在终端内选定并开始自动合成。"]
	quest.66E6753DF809DA3D.quest_subtitle: "流水作业"
	quest.66EA89C1E75509EB.quest_desc: [
		"&eOptional, not a mandatory quest, does not affect most game content. Don't enable it unless necessary."
		"Actually, some of it is rewards rather than suffering"
	]
	quest.66EA89C1E75509EB.quest_subtitle: "&6\"&6Once you take this step, there is no turning back\"&r"
	quest.66EA89C1E75509EB.title: "&cAdditional Suffering"
	quest.66F8BBB3BC24A7FF.quest_desc: [
		"&dThis rope wrapped in eerie aura can capture the souls of most creatures..."
		""
		"&eUsed with a spawner, it can change the creature inside the spawner, allowing you to quickly farm the drops you want. But it is expensive to craft..."
	]
	quest.66F8BBB3BC24A7FF.quest_subtitle: "Origin Ball"
	quest.6715B1FCEC798B5A.quest_subtitle: "Basic Part"
	quest.6797FA4F6F35E0ED.title: "Grip Parts"
	quest.67A539CCFEDE8EBC.quest_desc: [
		"Naturally generates in the Ancient Factory structure and requires a Nether Star to activate; can be located using the Mechanical Eye, and can also be summoned via the Altar"
		""
		"&7After defeating it, you can craft the &#66CCFFMeat Grinder Blueprint&7. Right-click to deal an attack to entities in front that &#FF6666ignores invincibility frames&7."
	]
	quest.67A539CCFEDE8EBC.quest_subtitle: "Stage 2"
	quest.67D8839DF18183B2.quest_desc: [
		"&6Light Puffer&r&7"
		"&7One of the common aquatic creatures of the Abyss. It cannot survive out of water (it flops in place and gradually loses health until death after a period of time);&r"
		""
		"&7Hold a water bucket and right-click the Light Puffer: converts it into item form (&#ADD8E6Bucket of Light Puffer&r&7) for storage;&r"
		""
		"&7Fights back only after taking damage itself, and its attack method is rather special;&r"
		""
		"&7After the Light Puffer takes damage, if the attacker is within ≤ 3 blocks of this Light Puffer:&r"
		""
		"&7This Light Puffer, after a 0.5-second slight-inflation wind-up, deals damage to that attacker and applies a 3-second &aPoison I&r&7 effect;&r"
		""
		"&7If a single instance of damage is enough to instantly kill the Light Puffer, the Light Puffer will be unable to attack as a result.&r"
	]
	quest.67D8839DF18183B2.title: "Light Puffer"
	quest.680583B3F5EF1CC2.quest_desc: [
		"&6Caustic Catalyst&r"
		""
		"&7&cHellfire&r&7 and &bBilgewater&r&7 combine violently, and this combination usually drives change and destruction. The Caustic Catalyst increases &aTuning Strength&r&7 as the &eCrucible System's&7 Instability Risk rises—that is, trading an impending violent reaction for great power.&r"
	]
	quest.680583B3F5EF1CC2.quest_subtitle: "Unstable Blaze"
	quest.681DDFCA829035FB.quest_desc: [
		"{\"text\":\"\",\"extra\":[{\"text\":\"Apotheosis\",\"color\":\"gold\"},{\"text\":\" is a large general-purpose adventure mod that provides more adventure and higher caps by modifying \",\"color\":\"gray\"},{\"text\":\"potions, enchantments, spawners, equipment\",\"color\":\"aqua\"},{\"text\":\" and other native MC elements.\",\"color\":\"gray\"}]}"
		""
		"{\"text\":\"\",\"extra\":[{\"text\":\"Here, \",\"color\":\"gray\"},{\"text\":\"Apotheosis\",\"color\":\"gold\"},{\"text\":\" is divided into major sections. In this modpack, the \",\"color\":\"gray\"},{\"text\":\"Apotheosis\",\"color\":\"gold\"},{\"text\":\" \",\"color\":\"gray\"},{\"text\":\"Enchanting Module\",\"color\":\"aqua\"},{\"text\":\" and \",\"color\":\"gray\"},{\"text\":\"Spawner Module\",\"color\":\"aqua\"},{\"text\":\" are used.\",\"color\":\"gray\"}]}"
	]
	quest.681DDFCA829035FB.quest_subtitle: "Crowning You with a False Divinity"
	quest.68780331B0515EB6.quest_desc: [
		"&6Oath of the Overeager Fist&r"
		""
		"&7The impulsiveness within your soul makes you act without thinking.&r"
		"&7-&cSpell charges&r&7 are fired immediately upon completing charge&r"
		""
		"&7An impulse fused into form and soul.&r"
		"&7-&aSpell&r&7 charge time halved&r"
		"{image:kubejs:textures/gui/malum/oath_of_the_overeager_fist.png width:160 height:200 align:center}"
	]
	quest.68780331B0515EB6.quest_subtitle: "Never Hesitate"
	quest.68780331B0515EB6.title: "Oath of the Overeager Fist"
	quest.688BD76E40216736.quest_desc: [
		"This modification makes creatures spawned by the spawner into babies (if a baby form exists for the target), otherwise it has no effect."
		"The most direct use of this upgrade seems to be obtaining Turtle Shells."
	]
	quest.688BD76E40216736.quest_subtitle: "Don't Want to Grow Up"
	quest.688BD76E40216736.title: "Turtle Egg"
	quest.68954EBEC12D958D.quest_desc: [
		"Can be summoned via the Altar; search Spawn: XXX in EMI to view the corresponding recipe"
		"{image:kubejs:textures/gui/spawn.png width:150 height:130 align:center}"
	]
	quest.68954EBEC12D958D.quest_subtitle: "Stage 3"
	quest.68EF2FB94A761FFD.quest_desc: [
		"&aI often hear the term \"intellect,\" referring to what others call experience."
		""
		"&7Its link to the soul is not firm, &6but it is part of the soul, and can be collected and reused for enchanting and repair."
		""
		"&eWhat most people do not know is that it can also condense into a physical form."
		""
		"&7I have heard rumors that they drop from ores, but the &6most reliable source is small ore clusters where souls dissipate&f&7; the experience left behind by souls is inscribed upon the rock."
	]
	quest.68EF2FB94A761FFD.quest_subtitle: "Experience Matter"
	quest.69049202784168C9.quest_desc: [
		"&7Hold right-click to whip your enemies (or maybe not enemies)"
		"&7Determined by &6Silent Gear&7 attributes:"
		"&7• Attack Damage &7→ &cSummon Damage"
		"&7• Attack Speed &7→ &6Attack Speed"
		"&7• Attack Range &7→ &aWhip Range"
	]
	quest.69049202784168C9.quest_subtitle: "Brave Wood"
	quest.6930993364FD1814.quest_desc: [
		"&7A set of spell robes."
		""
		"&7Can obtain &#CC99FFSpell Power&7, &#CC99FFSpell Resistance&7, and &#66FFCCMana Regeneration&7 based on materials."
		"&7Can obtain &#55D5D5pact cap&7, &#55D5D5healing multiplier&7, and &cknockback resistance&7 based on materials."
	]
	quest.6930993364FD1814.quest_subtitle: "Less defensive than other armor, but specialized against spell-related attributes"
	quest.69D3241740CA2990.quest_desc: [
		"&7You may have noticed that some tool handle materials, such as &#66CCFFbone&7, directly display attribute values rather than [Silent Gear Material]."
		"{image:kubejs:textures/gui/silentgear/sg_bone.png width:100 height:100 align=center}"
		"&7The advantage of this material is that it is already a part itself and can be used directly as a tool handle."
		"{image:kubejs:textures/gui/silentgear/sg_bone2.png width=140 height=140 align=center}"
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"&7Another type, &#FFD700[Silent Gear Material]&7, requires secondary processing at a crafting table."
		"{image:kubejs:textures/gui/silentgear/sg_cobalt_rod.png width=100 height=100 align=center}"
		"&7You need to secondary-process the tool handle blueprint with this type of material to turn it into something usable for crafting &#66CCFFSilent Gear&7, like the previous type."
		"{image:kubejs:textures/gui/silentgear/sg_cobalt_rod_2.png width=140 height=140 align=center}"
		"&7The advantage of this material is that it can be fused by the &#FFD700Alloy Machine&7 into an alloy to obtain more traits."
		"&7To know what an alloy is, read on."
	]
	quest.69D3241740CA2990.quest_subtitle: "Spot the Difference"
	quest.6A03DEB0CCE71AF2.quest_desc: [
		"&6Armor Plate&r"
		"&7A consumable used to increase a familiar's &aarmor value&r&7. There are 3 tiers, each with a usage cap"
	]
	quest.6A81CCE7A6F38060.quest_desc: [
		"&7Before officially starting your &#66CCFFSilent Gear&7 journey, you may need to obtain blueprints and templates. Before you have a large amount of blue dye, you need to craft a &#FFD700Stone Anvil&7 to obtain &#66DDCCMold Substrates&7 for making Silent Gear."
		""
		"&7Unfortunately, &#66DDCCMold Substrates&7 are one-time use; fortunately, &#66DDCCMold Substrates&7 are still quite cheap."
		""
		"&7See the next page for how to use the &#FFD700Stone Anvil&7."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"&7The &#FFD700Stone Anvil&7 is a GUI-less functional block. Hold an item and right-click to place a single item on the anvil, then hold the corresponding tool and right-click to process the item.&mIsn't this just a cutting board&r"
		""
		"&7This pack has modified the Stone Anvil's usage logic, so you no longer have to experience the vanilla Stone Anvil's mysterious usage logic. You can now use the Stone Anvil like a cutting board for quick crafting, though the Stone Anvil does not throw products into nearby bamboo baskets like the cutting board does."
		""
		"&7To process items quickly and in bulk, hold the item to be processed in the off-hand and the tool in the main hand, aim at the anvil, and hold right-click."
		""
		"{image:kubejs:textures/gui/silentgear/stone_anvil.png width=160 height=120 align=center fit:true}"
	]
	quest.6A81CCE7A6F38060.quest_subtitle: "Where It All Begins"
	quest.6A8313927B15ECEE.quest_desc: [
		"&6Thirsty Walker&r&7"
		"&7is a creature that looks similar to an &#8A2BE2Enderman&r&7, but it does not have the Enderman's &#ADFF2Fteleportation&r&7 ability or its &#1E90FFwater weakness&r&7;&r"
		""
		"&7The Thirsty Walker is a &8conditionally hostile creature&r&7. It only performs melee attacks, and on hit additionally applies 6 seconds of &#FF8C00Hunger I&r&7;&r"
		""
		"&7It has a special &#FFD700hatred logic&r&7:&r"
		""
		"&7Regardless of whether the player actively attacks it, a Thirsty Walker that has never been attacked will &#00CED1actively follow&r&7 the player and try to perform one melee attack on the player;&r"
		""
		"&7This melee attack has a more special attack animation (hereafter referred to as the &#DC143Cbite attack&r&7);&r"
		""
		"&7If the bite hits / is blocked by a shield: this Thirsty Walker will &#A9A9A9quickly flee&r&7 from the player and stop following the player for a period of time;&r"
		""
		"&7If the bite misses: this Thirsty Walker will keep trying to perform melee attacks until it successfully hits once;&r"
		""
		"&7If that player / another creature &#FF4500attacks&r&7 the Thirsty Walker:&r"
		""
		"&7The Thirsty Walker is &#FF0000enraged&r&7, immediately treats it as a hostile target, and &#DC143Cchases&r&7 the target continuously until one of them dies;&r"
		""
		"&7Afterward, the Thirsty Walker's attack animation changes to &#808080swinging its arms to attack&r&7 (the two attacks differ only in animation; actual values and effects are completely identical);&r"
		""
		"&7All of the above attacks can be blocked by a shield.&r"
	]
	quest.6A8313927B15ECEE.title: "Thirsty Walker"
	quest.6ABFDDD6E155A37F.quest_desc: [
		"&6Shade Snail&r&7"
		"&7One of the passive creatures generating in the Starlight Dimension, with &cextremely slow&r&7 movement speed."
		""
		"&7After taking damage, it &bretracts into its shell&r&7 on the spot:"
		"&7During and after retracting, it cannot move, and &aall types of damage taken are reduced by 85%&r&7."
		"&7If it is not attacked within a few seconds after retracting, it pops its head back out and resumes its previous behavior.&r"
	]
	quest.6ABFDDD6E155A37F.title: "Shade Snail"
	quest.6AC481C1ADA516D4.quest_desc: [
		"&7Creatures struck by a &#FFCC44Scythe&7 have their &#88DDFFsoul&7 briefly exposed. If they die during the &88DDFFsoul exposure&7 period, they drop special items."
		""
		"&7Similarly, creatures struck by &#CC99FFspells&7 also have their &#88DDFFsouls&7 exposed, with the same effect as the &#FFCC44Scythe&7."
		""
		"&7See the next-next page for which creatures drop which materials"
		""
		"{@pagebreak}"
		""
		"&7To summarize:"
		""
		"&7Zombie flesh condenses into &#66BB66Decayed Essence&7"
		""
		"&7Skeleton bone crystallizes into &#888888Chilled Bonestone&7"
		""
		"&7Phantom wings weave into &#66CCFFAstral Fabric&7"
		""
		"&7Breeze essence continues as &#FFDD55Galewind Core&7"
		""
		"&7Enderman magic solidifies into &#CC66FFWarped Energy Flow&7"
		""
		"&7Illager bones corrode into &#AA4AFFShadow Soul"
		""
		"&7The energy of mages and village guards sanctifies into &#DD88FFLight Soul"
	]
	quest.6AC481C1ADA516D4.quest_subtitle: "Leaking Magic"
	quest.6AE4DE3DC4964CB6.quest_subtitle: "Has both armor and a small amount of spell attributes—very popular"
	quest.6AE8CFDBDC8CF939.quest_subtitle: "合成用品"
	quest.6AF03EFFD9FB521F.quest_desc: [
		"&7Natural Spawn: Spawns naturally in the &#66CCFFSoul Sand Valley&7 at an extremely low probability;"
		""
		"&7&#CC99FFPhantoms&7 will actively attack &#CC99FFSkeletons&7. A &#CC99FFSkeleton&7 killed by a &#CC99FFPhantom&7 will always transform into a &#FF6666Vessel&7;  "
		"&7After a &#FF6666Vessel&7 is killed, there is a chance a new &#CC99FFPhantom&7 will spawn in its place (Easy 0%, Normal 50%, Hard 100%)."
		""
		"&7If a &#CC99FFPhantom&7 approaches a [Petrification] gargoyle statue, it will immediately transform into a &#FF6666Vessel&7.  "
		"&7Only performs ranged attacks, with movement AI identical to a &#CC99FFSkeleton&7;  "
		"&7Immune to fire damage and &#55D5D5Soul Sand's&7 slowing effect. Will actively attack &#CC99FFPiglins&7;  "
		"&7When attacking, it first charges up for &#FFAA333 seconds&7, then fires &#FFAA3316~20&7 &#55D5D5Soul Buckshots&7 at the target;  "
		"&7This attack &#FF6666cannot be blocked by shields&7 and can ignore creatures' invincibility frames;  "
		"&7The higher the current world difficulty, the more scattered the &#55D5D5Soul Buckshot&7 flight paths become."
		""
		"&7When a &#FF6666Vessel&7 touches water (fluid), is exposed to rainy weather, or is hit by a splash/lingering water bottle:  "
		"&7It will immediately transform into a &#CC99FFSkeleton&7 and gain &#FFAA3310 seconds&7 of Nausea, &#FFAA335 seconds&7 of Weakness II, and &#FFAA335 seconds&7 of Slowness III;  "
		"&7The &#CC99FFSkeleton&7 transformed this way loses all armor and off-hand items it had equipped before (before being possessed and transformed into a &#FF6666Vessel&7);  "
		"&7Regardless of what weapon it previously held in its main hand, after transformation it is forcibly replaced with a &#66CCFFBow&7."
	]
	quest.6AF03EFFD9FB521F.quest_subtitle: "I! WILL! NOT! BE! FORGOTTEN!"
	quest.6AF6ADCEE5546549.quest_desc: [
		"&7The &#FFD700Totem Base&7 serves as the base block of a totem. Right-click to activate or deactivate the Spirit ritual. Once activated, a &#FFCC44Redstone Comparator&7 can detect the number of totem poles in the structure."
		"&7The material of the &#FFD700Totem Base&7 and totem poles (&#FFAA33Runewood&7/&#888888Soulwood&7) must match. Totems built from &#888888Soulwood&7 perform a corrupted version of the ritual."
		""
		"&7Totem poles are obtained by right-clicking &#FFAA33Runewood Logs&7 or &#888888Soulwood Logs&7 with &#66FF99Spirits&7 consumed to inscribe them. The sigil type matches the &#66FF99Spirit&7."
		"&7The sigil directions of multiple totem poles must be consistent. Sigil direction is only related to the orientation when inscribed, not to the log's direction."
		"&7Right-clicking a totem pole with an axe removes the sigil and restores the log, without returning the &#66FF99Spirit&7."
		"&7When the totem is not activated, using the &#88DDFFTotemic Staff&7 can toggle the sigils' active state, for decoration only."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"&7Most ritual ranges are centered on the &#FFD700Totem Base&7, except for directional effect blocks. Players holding the &#88DDFFTotemic Staff&7 will display the ritual range."
		""
		"&7Totems of the same Spirit ritual interfere with each other. When a ritual range contains another &#FFD700Totem Base&7, or another totem's ritual range contains this &#FFD700Totem Base&7, the totem activated first will be shut down."
		""
		"&7Blocks crafted from &#888888Tainted Stone&7 and &#9966CCWarped Stone&7 are immune to Spirit rituals."
	]
	quest.6AF6ADCEE5546549.quest_subtitle: "&6A Miracle Appears in the World"
	quest.6AF6ADCEE5546549.title: "Totem Magic"
	quest.6B03AFED832B87A7.quest_desc: [
		"&6Starlit Sea&r"
		"&7is the most common ocean biome in the Starlight Dimension."
		""
		"&7Unlike the Overworld's oceans, the Starlit Sea's seabed is more &aflat&r."
		"&7&#9ACD32Abyssal Fruit&r&7 plants and &#87CEEBSea Ball Flowers&r&7 are the main vegetation of the Starlit Sea."
		"&7Some sea areas bordering land or the Abyss biome generate &FF6B6Bcoral reefs&r&7 in patches (refer to the Overworld's warm ocean)."
		""
		"&7Except for the &#483D8BTower Squid&r&7, other aquatic creatures usually generate in other ocean biomes."
		"&7Non-aquatic creatures can only spawn underground, dozens of blocks deep from the Starlit Sea."
	]
	quest.6B03AFED832B87A7.quest_subtitle: "A bright star falls from heaven!"
	quest.6B03AFED832B87A7.title: "Starlit Sea"
	quest.6B475F80CCD29781.quest_subtitle: "合成用品"
	quest.6B49DEF95C8C0D96.quest_desc: [
		"&7Holding and sprinting consumes durability to increase &#FFAA33movement speed&7. What, not sprinting doesn't consume &#66DDCCdurability&7? What kind of logic is that."
		""
		"&7Movement speed bonus is dynamically determined by &6Silent Gear's&7 &eenchantability&7 attribute. Higher enchantability means higher bonus, up to &c+100%&7."
		"&7Sprinting consumes &c1&7 durability every &c2 seconds&7."
	]
	quest.6B49DEF95C8C0D96.quest_subtitle: "Travel Tool"
	quest.6B5F16B4F3E12902.quest_desc: ["&r&5Arcana (0%~100%):&r&7 Determines the probability of \"rare enchantments\" appearing. When Arcana reaches 100%, some ordinary enchantments (such as Sharpness) become rare."]
	quest.6B82BD57F8A68CEE.quest_subtitle: "Familiar Summoning Ritual"
	quest.6B97738CD8E10A57.quest_desc: [
		"&6Pact of Self-Care"
		"&7Hunger is losing oneself.&r&cHealth drops significantly faster at low hunger"
		"&7Revel, enjoy fine food, cleanse the soul.&r&aFood restores more saturation&r&aEating food clears negative effects"
		""
		"{image:kubejs:textures/gui/malum/pact_of_self_care.png width:160 height:200 align:center}"
	]
	quest.6B97738CD8E10A57.quest_subtitle: "Caring for Oneself"
	quest.6B97738CD8E10A57.title: "Pact of Self-Care"
	quest.6BC39E8AB37961DD.quest_desc: ["朴实无华的属性，可堪一用"]
	quest.6BC39E8AB37961DD.quest_subtitle: "朴实无华"
	quest.6BE787CD7C0F7128.quest_desc: [
		"&7After defeating it, you can craft the following blueprints:"
		""
		"&#66CCFFAncient Spear&7, when the weapon is fully charged, left-click to produce a slightly homing &#66CCFFprojectile&7 that attacks enemies. The projectile's attack power depends on the player's damage (benefits from Strength, etc.)."
		""
		"&#66CCFFTracking Bow,&7 fires homing &#66CCFFghost sandstorms&7 at enemies."
	]
	quest.6BE787CD7C0F7128.quest_subtitle: "Kill kill kill"
	quest.6BE9E4190B1E6A4C.quest_desc: ["Right-click to clear invasions for a period of time, including future ones"]
	quest.6BE9E4190B1E6A4C.quest_subtitle: "Tired of annoying invasions?"
	quest.6BF48D5C9D1B191A.quest_desc: [
		"&7After crafting a &#66DDCCDisk&7, a new storage option is added: the &#66CCFFPortable Terminal&7. This terminal needs to be charged before use. Use a &#FFD700Tesla Coil&7 to charge it."
		""
		"&7Unfortunately, it can only insert one &#66DDCCDisk&7, and its ability to store stackable items is inferior to the &#66DDCCSophisticated Backpack&7, but its performance for storing non-stackable items is decent."
		""
		"&7I mean, just crafting it so you don't have to go get the &#FFAA3364K Disk&7 as a reward is nice too ("
	]
	quest.6BF48D5C9D1B191A.quest_subtitle: "Portable Space"
	quest.6C33A7DFF72E3C76.quest_desc: [
		"Place a Carved Moonmoth Cactus Fruit on top of a Celestial Block to summon"
		""
		"&6Behavior&r"
		"&7An anti-air utility creature that only targets a &csmall number of aerial hostile creatures&r."
		"&7When attacking creatures, its attack speed is &aextremely fast&r, its range is &aextremely long&r, and its damage area is &aextremely large&r. But even so, its attacks still &ccannot harm&r&7 other non-aerial creatures."
		""
		"&7When there are no &emeteorites&r&7 or the above targets around, the &6Celestial Golem&r&7 will not fight back even if attacked by other creatures."
		""
		"&6Intercepting Celestial Meteors&r"
		"&7When the &6Celestial Golem&r&7 is on the surface and the current weather is a &cMeteor Shower&r&7, the Celestial Golem will directly shoot down falling &emeteorites&r&7 in mid-air."
		"&7Shot-down &emeteorites&r&7 still produce the corresponding items."
		"&7&cBitter Comet Fear&r&7 also cannot spawn because the meteorite was shot down."
	]
	quest.6C33A7DFF72E3C76.quest_subtitle: "Planetary Protection Policy"
	quest.6C33A7DFF72E3C76.title: "Celestial Golem"
	quest.6C8EF5FE6AB70D3B.quest_desc: [
		"&7Aircraft—a preferred travel tool. Different models have different performance and suit different scenarios. Some are extremely fast and good for opening up the map and finding ruins, while others are stable and can hover for building. As long as you're willing to invest some materials, there's always one that can help you."
		""
		"&7But be careful not to crash..."
	]
	quest.6C8EF5FE6AB70D3B.quest_subtitle: "Please prepare Feather Falling; there's some turbulence ahead"
	quest.6C8EF5FE6AB70D3B.title: "Set Sail for the Sky"
	quest.6C9DC507DF212214.quest_subtitle: "Quickly create Silent Gear material compatibility"
	quest.6CA6DCCDEB5167BD.quest_desc: [
		"&6&#55AAFFStarlight Dimension&r"
		"&7A realm isomorphic to the Overworld yet differently colored, with &#55AAFFstars hanging low&r&7, lush plants, and &#55AAFFgorgeous celestial phenomena&r&7, as if sunk into a dream that never wakes."
		""
		"&6Dimension Log:&r"
		"&7Terrain height distribution is similar to the Overworld. Most naturally generated blocks correspond to the Overworld, but its surface and vegetation are mostly in &55AAFFblue tones&r&7, and the sky is interwoven with a purple starry sky and &#FFAA00warm orange dusk&r&7."
		"&7Divided by the &cY 0 layer&r&7 into the upper &8Gloomstone Layer&r&7 and the lower &8Voidstone Layer&r&7."
		"&7The variety and splendor of decorative plants far exceed the Overworld, full of vitality."
		"&7Besides regular weather, glorious and unique weather phenomena such as &dMeteor Showers&r&7 and &dAuroras&r&7 also occur."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"&6Basic Laws:&r"
		"&7Teleportation and Coordinates: Coordinate scaling is &a1.0&r&7, corresponding 1:1 with Overworld coordinates."
		""
		"&7Time and Sky: Time is frozen at eternal &#FFAA00dusk&r&7 (12900), with a custom &dpurple starry sky&r&7 and &#FFAA00warm orange canopy&r&7."
		""
		"&7Lighting Rules: No day-night cycle; the sky provides light. Base ambient brightness is &c0&r&7. Monsters can spawn at light levels &c0~7&r&7."
		""
		"&7Building and Respawning: Height range &b-64 to 384&r&7. &aBeds&r&7 and &aRespawn Anchors&r&7 can be used safely."
		""
		"&7Ecology and Threats: Raids cannot be triggered. From the Nether, &cPiglins&r&7, &cPiglin Brutes&r&7, and &cHoglins&r&7 become &8zombified&r here."
	]
	quest.6CA6DCCDEB5167BD.quest_subtitle: "Yesterday Once More No Longer"
	quest.6CA6DCCDEB5167BD.title: "Eternal Starlight"
	quest.6CC1EDF75BF739C0.quest_desc: ["&7同时提升魔力上限与攻速加成，双项属性皆为实战刚需。造价极为廉价"]
	quest.6CC1EDF75BF739C0.quest_subtitle: "我草，冰"
	quest.6CE4032D222E50F3.quest_desc: ["&7Look at these stats—you should be able to tell how &#FF6666overpowered&7 this trait is ( )"]
	quest.6CE4032D222E50F3.quest_subtitle: "Theoretically the Strongest"
	quest.6CF68E9E0A3CB0E7.quest_desc: [
		"&7Natural Quartz, as its name suggests, is a naturally occurring equivalent of &6Nether Quartz&r&7. Its uses are mostly the same as Nether Quartz."
		""
		"&eIt is quite rare&r&7, found deep underground, often forming &6geodes&r&7."
	]
	quest.6D0D20A34E2B3703.quest_desc: [
		"&7After holding and right-clicking to fire in the &bStarlight Dimension&r&7, it can switch the current weather to &cMeteor Shower&r&7 after a short time. Very useful for players wanting to obtain resources such as &eCelestial&r&7."
		""
		"&7Using it in dimensions other than the Starlight Dimension will &cfail&r."
	]
	quest.6D0D20A34E2B3703.quest_subtitle: "Make a Star Wish"
	quest.6D571AC85912D827.quest_desc: [
		"&6Rune Substrate&r"
		"&7The foundation for crafting all other runes. A small amount can be found in some &bvanilla structures&r&7, and it is more common in &cIron's Spells&r&7 structures. Each type of mage drops one rune of the same type upon death (except undead warlocks).&r"
		""
		"&8\"A pale foundation precipitated from the final embers of a mage's soul, used to anchor all rune laws.\""
	]
	quest.6D571AC85912D827.quest_subtitle: "Arcane Materials"
	quest.6D7E037569A98460.quest_desc: [
		"&6Pact of the High Priest"
		"&7An extremely invasive grasp brings harm.&r&cAfter being hit, the interaction distance bonus goes on cooldown&r&cMovement speed reduced while the bonus is on cooldown"
		"&7The whole world is yours.&r&aBlock interaction distance increased by one fifth, entity interaction distance increased by one tenth"
		""
		"{image:kubejs:textures/gui/malum/pact_of_the_high_priest.png width:160 height:200 align:center}"
	]
	quest.6D7E037569A98460.quest_subtitle: "Extending Oneself Thin"
	quest.6D7E037569A98460.title: "Pact of the High Priest"
	quest.6D895DFB1144DF16.quest_desc: [
		"&6Yeti Fur&r&7"
		"&7Kill a Yeti / use shears on a Yeti to obtain &#F5F5DCYeti Fur&r&7;&r"
		""
		"&7Yeti Fur is a flammable building block similar to wool;&r"
		""
		"&7Creatures landing on top of this block also take no fall damage and bounce upward based on fall distance (similar to a slime block);&r"
		""
		"&7Yeti Fur can also block &#8Sculk Sensors&r&7 / &8Sculk Shriekers&r&7 from detecting sound;&r"
		""
		"&7Yetis by default only have white textures and cannot be dyed like sheep. Yeti Fur variants other than white can only be crafted manually.&r"
	]
	quest.6D895DFB1144DF16.title: "Yeti Fur"
	quest.6D937711826032A4.quest_desc: [""]
	quest.6D937711826032A4.quest_subtitle: "绝对的强者！由此而生的孤独，教会他数值的是..."
	quest.6DA0846CF76DCC86.quest_desc: ["If you need to keep a chunk permanently loaded, right-click it on the large map to claim and mark it"]
	quest.6DA0846CF76DCC86.quest_subtitle: "OPAC"
	quest.6DA0846CF76DCC86.title: "Chunk Keep-Loading"
	quest.6DB8BE45F81F4357.title: "Discover the Blaze Arena"
	quest.6E0EE5297B295288.quest_subtitle: "&eAll neutral creatures will become hostile to you"
	quest.6E0EE5297B295288.title: "&e\"No Purity Remains in a Body of Filth\""
	quest.6E25E82DBD18D2C8.quest_subtitle: "&cThe world will fall into eternal night"
	quest.6E25E82DBD18D2C8.title: "&c\"An Eternal Journey Under a Lightless Long Night\""
	quest.6E7D9FC91B09210C.quest_desc: ["需要注意的是虽然有扎实的数值，但是鬼魂形态不能通过常规武器造成伤害，搭配一些特殊攻击手段的武器会很好用"]
	quest.6E7D9FC91B09210C.quest_subtitle: "不死新生"
	quest.6E995B7F0867CE19.quest_subtitle: "Familiar Summoning Ritual"
	quest.6F1B0D7041FBCD4B.quest_desc: [
		"&6Rune of Monolith's Protection&r"
		""
		"&7The Rune of Monolith's Protection functions similarly to the ritual of the same name, granting the wearer a half-strength &bMonolith's Protection&r&7 effect, slightly reducing &adamage&r&7 taken, with increased effect when unarmored.&r"
	]
	quest.6F1B0D7041FBCD4B.quest_subtitle: "Guardian Pulse"
	quest.6F6ACDE9BCEFD6A5.quest_desc: [
		"&6Pact of the Cloudskipper"
		"&7What you rely on will eventually destroy you.&r&cFall damage doubled"
		"&7Gravity—the hardest force to defy.&r&aPropulsion from strong winds increased, and grants Ascension&r&aAscension state enhances aerial mobility"
		"{image:kubejs:textures/gui/malum/pact_of_the_cloudskipper.png width:160 height:200 align:center}"
	]
	quest.6F6ACDE9BCEFD6A5.quest_subtitle: "Flying Over All"
	quest.6F6ACDE9BCEFD6A5.title: "Pact of the Cloudskipper"
	quest.6F7065E85A4EE4DA.quest_desc: ["可用于追溯我已合成过的物品记录，对于时常健忘的我来说相当实用。"]
	quest.6F7065E85A4EE4DA.quest_subtitle: "我会永远石剑你....永远..."
	quest.6F7643BD60F5534F.quest_desc: ["&7Can mine dirt blocks in a &#FFAA333×3×3&7 area."]
	quest.6F7643BD60F5534F.quest_subtitle: "Big Spoon"
	quest.6F7DF3491AA2E9DF.quest_desc: [
		"&6Pact of the Parasite"
		"&7Your vulnerability still cannot be ignored.&r&cHealing received reduced by four tenths"
		"&7Surplus confidence fuses into the mind; pain no longer matters.&r&aHarvesting Spirits grants Absorption"
		""
		"{image:kubejs:textures/gui/malum/pact_of_the_parasite.png width:160 height:200 align:center}"
	]
	quest.6F7DF3491AA2E9DF.quest_subtitle: "Stealing Shields to Sustain Oneself"
	quest.6F7DF3491AA2E9DF.title: "Pact of the Parasite"
	quest.6FA8C31F0875CB8E.quest_desc: [
		"&7The most common use case is restocking Totems of Undying: replenishing Totems of Undying into the off-hand while carrying a full backpack of totems lets you achieve \"why are you still here.\" But don't ask me where a full backpack of Totems of Undying comes from..."
		""
		"&7It can also be used in other situations to automatically fill the hotbar with items for easy use."
	]
	quest.6FA8C31F0875CB8E.quest_subtitle: "I only see endless Totems of Undying"
	quest.6FDF4D8E43BF594B.quest_desc: [
		"&7As a base material, widely used in &#FFAA33Rune Crafting&7, &#66CCFFSpirit Crucible&7 mineral multiplication, &#CC99FFSpirit Altar&7 item crafting, &#88DDFFMending Pylon&7 tool repair, and implementing &#FFD700Totem Rituals&7."
		""
		"&7Use a weapon carrying the &#CC6666#malum:soul_hunter_weapon&7 tag (including but not limited to all kinds of &#FFCC44Scythes&7, &#66DDCCSoulstained Steel series&7 tools and weapons, &#CC6666Malice series&7 weapons) to inflict the &#88DDFFSoul Shatter&7 effect on specific creatures and kill them during this period to obtain &#66FF99Spirits&7."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"&7In most cases, the ways to obtain &#66FF99Spirits&7 are as follows:"
		""
		"&#88DDFFHallowed Spirits&7 can be obtained by killing some passive creatures"
		"Such as &#66DD88Cows&7, &#66DD88Dolphins&7"
		""
		"&#CC6666Malicious Spirits&7 can be obtained by killing some hostile creatures"
		"Such as &#CC6666Zombies&7, &#CC6666Spiders&7"
		""
		"&#CC99FFArcane Spirits&7 can be obtained by killing creatures with special attack patterns"
		"Such as &#CC99FFSkeletons&7, &#CC99FFBlazes&7"
		""
		"&#DDA0DDMalefic Spirits&7 can be obtained by killing some rare creatures, etc."
		"Such as &#DDA0DDEndermen&7, &#DDA0DDEvokers&7, &#DDA0DDAncient Guardians&7"
		""
		"&#66DDCCClear Sky Spirits&7 can be obtained by killing some mounts and flying creatures, etc."
		"Such as &#66DDCCCats&7, &#66DDCCBats&7"
		""
		"&#66BB66Earth Spirits&7 can be obtained by killing some ground creatures, etc."
		"Such as &#66BB66Zombies&7, &#66BB66Iron Golems&7"
		""
		"&#FF6633Hellfire Spirits&7 can be obtained by killing some Nether creatures or special creatures"
		"Such as &#FF6633Blazes&7, &#FF6633Piglins&7, &#FF6633Creepers&7"
		""
		"&#3399FFBilgewater Spirits&7 can be obtained by killing aquatic animals"
		"Such as &#3399FFDolphins&7, &#3399FFDrowned&7"
		""
		"&7You can press R on a Spirit to view which entities drop it"
	]
	quest.6FDF4D8E43BF594B.quest_subtitle: "The Building Blocks of Magic"
	quest.6FE5B91598B5393A.quest_desc: ["在前期，最高贵的就是基础值加成"]
	quest.6FE5B91598B5393A.quest_subtitle: "优秀的基础伤害加成"
	quest.6FF16C84BFDC23B4.quest_desc: ["&7词缀与属性俱为顶级，提供扎实的面板数值与可观增伤。击败受火者后方可入手，是构筑中极具分量的核心组件，可与戈伯锭,下界戈伯锭形成强力连携"]
	quest.6FF16C84BFDC23B4.quest_subtitle: "愿您的旅途充满诅咒与祝福"
	quest.70195B5ED5D18F70.quest_desc: [
		"&6Pact of the Skybreaker"
		"&7A blood feud must be answered with destruction.&r&cKnockback taken doubled"
		"&7Gravity—the strongest force imposed on others.&r&aTaking fall damage automatically attacks nearby creatures&r&aDealing fall damage attacks targets regardless of distance"
		"{image:kubejs:textures/gui/malum/pact_of_the_skybreaker.png width:160 height:200 align:center}"
	]
	quest.70195B5ED5D18F70.quest_subtitle: "Striking Down All Things"
	quest.70195B5ED5D18F70.title: "Pact of the Skybreaker"
	quest.70A16F668336C964.quest_desc: [
		"The enchanting module brings a more powerful and phased enchanting experience to MC."
		"Here, enchantment attributes are no longer affected by a single enchantment level, but by five attributes: &a&lTier&r&r, &4&lQuantization&r&r, &5&lArcana&r&r, &e&lStability&r&r, and &3Enchantment Clues&r."
		""
		"{@pagebreak}"
		""
		"In the current version, the specific values and meanings of the attributes are as follows:"
		"&a&lTier&r&r: Represents the source of power, ranging from 0 to 100, representing the minimum level required for the highest enchantment situation. As in vanilla, higher levels yield better enchantments."
		"&4&lQuantization&r&r: Represents the entropy of chaos, ranging from 0 to 100%, representing the degree of influence on the upper and lower limits of the enchantment result. The higher the value, the greater the fluctuation of the actual enchantment level's upper and lower limits. For example: if the Enchanting Table's &a&lTier&r&r is 100 and &4&lQuantization&r&r is 90%, using the third row level to enchant any enchantable item results in a final enchantment level range of [10, 190] (levels). The default value is 15%."
		"&l&5Arcana&r&r: Represents the gift of mystery, ranging from 0 to 100%, representing the probability of obtaining &brare enchantments&r. Special enchantments require a certain Arcana value to appear (such as Miner's Zeal). To prevent some important vanilla enchantments from being squeezed out by rare enchantments at high Arcana, when Arcana reaches 100%, important enchantments like Sharpness become rare enchantments."
		"&l&eStability&r&r: Represents the world's solidity, provided by the Geode-Sealed Bookshelf, used to eliminate Quantization's effect on the floor. With Stability, the enchantment level range in the above Quantization example becomes [100, 190] (levels)."
		"&3Enchantment Clues&r: Represents the sight of truth. The value represents how many enchantment results you can know in advance during enchanting. Some advanced bookshelves affect this count. Default is 1 clue."
	]
	quest.70A16F668336C964.quest_subtitle: "Enhanced Enchanting Power"
	quest.70A16F668336C964.title: "Apotheosis — Enchanting Module"
	quest.70B6CF3213A607ED.quest_desc: [
		"Never imagined I'd one day find someone in a group chat willing to help with server testing and setup"
		""
		"Helped Codfish with server testing for quite a long time (and thanks also to everyone who played on that server and gave feedback!)"
	]
	quest.70B6CF3213A607ED.quest_subtitle: "Server Testing + Setup"
	quest.70F085FC6F1CAAF2.quest_desc: [
		"&7The modpack has a clear stage progression. Before defeating a stage boss, bosses of unattained stages cannot be challenged."
		""
		"&7Some ores are locked by stage bosses and only appear after defeating the corresponding boss. Otherwise, you won't find them even if you dig through the core of the earth."
	]
	quest.70F085FC6F1CAAF2.quest_subtitle: "It's time..."
	quest.70F085FC6F1CAAF2.title: "Setting Off"
	quest.713CA5306C2B86A2.quest_desc: [
		"&6Connector&r"
		""
		"&7Place two Connectors facing each other. Hold a &eCopper Wire Spool&7 and right-click each of them; an electrified wire forms between them. The Copper Wire Spool is consumed and returns an empty spool. Once connected, energy can flow between them&r"
		""
		"&8If either Connector is removed, the wire breaks, dropping four copper wires.&r"
		""
		"&7One pull, one connection—between the wires, energy flows.&r"
	]
	quest.714645D7B7F4C7BA.quest_desc: [
		"&7Can be crafted into &#A020F0Shade Snail Shell Powder:&r&7"
		""
		"&7Made by decomposing &#A020F0Shade Snail Shells&r&7 in a crafting grid;&r"
		""
		"&7Can be used like bone meal to accelerate crops to the next growth stage;&r"
		"&7Can also be used on saplings, mushrooms, and other plants that can be accelerated by bone meal;&r"
		"&7Can also be further crafted into black dye in a crafting grid.&r"
	]
	quest.714645D7B7F4C7BA.quest_subtitle: "Material dropped after killing a Shade Snail"
	quest.71944D592D710B99.quest_desc: ["{\"text\":\"\",\"extra\":[{\"text\":\"I know you might get a headache seeing this mod's \",\"color\":\"gray\"},{\"text\":\"eyes\",\"color\":\"red\"},{\"text\":\", but now they can all be \",\"color\":\"gray\"},{\"text\":\"crafted\",\"color\":\"green\"},{\"text\":\".\",\"color\":\"gray\"}]}"]
	quest.71944D592D710B99.quest_subtitle: "Craftable"
	quest.71B24EEAADB29F3A.quest_desc: [
		"&7Use a &#FFD700Reforging Hammer&7 to re-hammer the &#CC99FFweapon&7 whose attributes you want to reforge in a &#66DDCCAnvil&7, allowing you to reforge &#FFAA33attributes&7."
		""
		"&7Trading with villagers can obtain three types of &#FFD700Reforging Hammers&7. Of course, you can also craft them yourself, which is far more convenient than trading."
		"&7You can reforge &#CC99FFweapons&7, &#66CCFFarmor&7, tools, and trinkets separately. The best traits for melee &#CC99FFweapons&7 are mostly &#FFD700Legendary&7, for ranged &#CC99FFweapons&7 it's &#66CCFFUnreal&7, and trinket/armor traits cover different aspects."
		""
		"&7Best trinket traits:"
		"&#66FF66Warding&7, increases &#FFAA332&7 armor value"
		"&#FF6666Menacing&7, increases &#FFAA334%&7 attack damage"
		"&#FFD700Lucky&7, increases &#FFAA332%&7 critical strike chance"
		""
		"&7Since the base critical multiplier is only &#FFAA33150%&7, the &#FFD700Lucky&7 bonus is hard to surpass &#FF6666Menacing&7, so it's not recommended."
		""
		"&7Reforging is risky. Don't get carried away in the early game; just make do with what works."
		"&7Reforging often consumes a lot of &#66DDCCAnvil&7 durability. You can use the &#66CCFFSophisticated Backpack's&7 &#FFD700Anvil Upgrade&7 to save iron ingots."
	]
	quest.71B24EEAADB29F3A.quest_subtitle: "Because too many people asked, so it's in the main questline"
	quest.71B24EEAADB29F3A.title: "Obtaining Techniques"
	quest.71C2AB4CCFAA1C59.quest_desc: ["&7Increases the spawner's spawning range. Each one adds 2 blocks, up to 48 blocks. Can be used with quartz to reduce the spawning range and make it more concentrated."]
	quest.71C2AB4CCFAA1C59.quest_subtitle: "The Factory Must Expand"
	quest.71CB5BC6CDEF6271.quest_desc: [
		"Alloy Smelting Furnace construction diagram:"
		""
		"Layer one: must be built using blocks of the same material as the alloy furnace"
		"{image:kubejs:textures/gui/alloy_forgery/alloy_forgery1.png width:160 height:100 align:center}"
		""
		"{@pagebreak}"
		""
		"Layer two: place the Smelting Controller in the red box area shown"
		"{image:kubejs:textures/gui/alloy_forgery/alloy_forgery2.png width:160 height:100 align:center}"
		""
		"{@pagebreak}"
		""
		"Layer three: continue placing bricks"
		"{image:kubejs:textures/gui/alloy_forgery/alloy_forgery3.png width:160 height:120 align:center}"
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"Then right-click the Smelting Controller to open the furnace UI. Place materials in to prepare for automation"
	]
	quest.71CB5BC6CDEF6271.quest_subtitle: "Metal Crafting"
	quest.71CB5BC6CDEF6271.title: "Smelting Controller"
	quest.71EB7660FA903627.quest_subtitle: "Magical Material"
	quest.7220F1709920A6DC.quest_desc: ["&7A base trinket used only to increase &FF8844armor value&7 by a small amount. A necessary prerequisite for crafting its higher-tier material variants."]
	quest.7220F1709920A6DC.quest_subtitle: "Trinket Base"
	quest.72387868BC05D119.quest_desc: ["&7The Nether seems to have undergone some changes... more &#FF6666dangerous&7 than the commonly known Nether... please proceed with caution."]
	quest.72387868BC05D119.quest_subtitle: "Everything is so scary!!!"
	quest.72387868BC05D119.title: "Gate of Purgatory"
	quest.7241681266CB77A7.quest_desc: [
		"&7Now you can really craft a spellbook out of &#66CCFFiron&7."
		""
		"&7Spellbook slots are determined by the material's &#CC99FFspell slots&7."
		"&7Spell power amplification is determined by the material's &bspell power&7."
		"&7Max mana amplification is determined by the material's &dmax mana&7."
	]
	quest.7241681266CB77A7.quest_subtitle: "Iron! Magic"
	quest.727B996FAE26B0BB.quest_desc: [
		"&7Use the &#FFD700Seer's Orb&7 to right-click a portal frame to activate a &#CC99FFRift&7."
		""
		"&7After the chaotic &#CC99FFRifts&7 closed one after another, the power to open &#CC99FFRifts&7 was sealed within the &#FFD700Seer's Orb&7. Only heroes recognized by the Gatekeeper can enter the &#CC99FFRift&7."
		""
		"&7The Gatekeeper gave you some seeds, hoping you can go to the &#66CCFFStarlight Forest&7 and feed the &#FFAA33Spark Birds&7 there. He hasn't returned to the &#66CCFFStarlight Forest&7 for a very, very long time."
		""
		"&7&#FFAA33Spark Bird&7 nests are usually high up in the canopy of the &#66CCFFStarlight Forest&7. Place seeds into the nests and feed nearby &#FFAA33Spark Birds&7 to breed them. &#FFAA33Spark Birds&7 will repay you with some random items as thanks, including special &#66DDCCforging materials&7."
		""
		"[ { \"text\": \"[Click to jump]\", \"underlined\": true, \"clickEvent\": { \"action\": \"change_page\", \"value\": \"6CA6DCCDEB5167BD\" } } ]"
	]
	quest.727B996FAE26B0BB.quest_subtitle: "&mUmbrella swing, step into the mud, open!"
	quest.727B996FAE26B0BB.title: "Open the Door"
	quest.7291BB4AE2E4BA76.quest_desc: ["Before you can quickly obtain a hammer in the early game, the Crude Hammer is clearly the better choice"]
	quest.7291BB4AE2E4BA76.quest_subtitle: "Crude Tool"
	quest.729E08704E144DC7.quest_desc: ["{\"text\":\"\",\"extra\":[{\"text\":\"After holding and \",\"color\":\"gray\"},{\"text\":\"right-clicking\",\"color\":\"yellow\"},{\"text\":\" this item in the \",\"color\":\"gray\"},{\"text\":\"Nether\",\"color\":\"red\"},{\"text\":\", it turns into a \",\"color\":\"gray\"},{\"text\":\"map\",\"color\":\"aqua\"},{\"text\":\" pointing to the \",\"color\":\"gray\"},{\"text\":\"Castle structure\",\"color\":\"gold\"},{\"text\":\".\",\"color\":\"gray\"}]}"]
	quest.729E08704E144DC7.quest_subtitle: "Why can you figure out the castle's location just by mashing materials together"
	quest.72C552BE02BA433D.quest_desc: [
		"&7The Apotheosis Spawner Module brings players more powerful and customizable spawners, as well as convenient solutions for partially automating mob farms."
		""
		"&7The spawner has too many attributes but they are very concise and easy to understand. Here they are introduced by the materials consumed."
	]
	quest.72C552BE02BA433D.quest_subtitle: "Super Monster Factory"
	quest.72C552BE02BA433D.title: "Apotheosis — Spawner Module"
	quest.72EADB2FF95D25B3.quest_desc: [
		"&7A set of spell robes."
		""
		"&7Can obtain &#CC99FFSpell Power&7, &#CC99FFSpell Resistance&7, and &#66FFCCMana Regeneration&7 based on materials."
		"&7Can obtain &#55D5D5pact cap&7, &#55D5D5healing multiplier&7, and &cknockback resistance&7 based on materials."
	]
	quest.72EADB2FF95D25B3.quest_subtitle: "Less defensive than other armor, but specialized against spell-related attributes"
	quest.7306BEC7A3E98304.quest_subtitle: "Undead"
	quest.731473A765D3B6B6.quest_desc: [
		"&7While searching everywhere for traces of &darcane energy&r&7, the most commonly found is &bClear Sky Arcana&r&7."
		"&7All &eweather phenomena&r&7 carry faint imprints of Clear Sky Arcana; but essentially, they do not possess the form of Spirits, only the &8residual memory&r&7 of their influence upon the world."
		"&7Their influence has dissipated, but with just a little effort they can be restored."
		""
		"&7Memories of these &bgales&r&7 remain everywhere. They have lost the power of the gale and can only drift about."
		"&7However, simply infusing them with &eClear Sky Arcana&r&7 allows these memories to be rewoven with the flow of &darcane energy&r&7, restoring them to their original state."
		"&7They can thus once again exert influence upon the world."
		"&7Building on existing uses, with the help of &6Wind Charges&r&7 and &aGalewind Cores&r&7, I have found two new applications of this effect."
		""
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"&6Gale Activator"
		"&7Wind Charges carry scattered memories. They have a chaotic nature and are released upon impact."
		"&7When activated by redstone, the Gale Activator weaves a burst of &bgale&r&7, pushing all surrounding things outward."
		"&7The Artisan's Crook can configure the strength and specific form of this effect."
		""
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"&6Wind Tunnel Device"
		"&7Galewind Cores are captured from strong winds. They are more powerful and have direction."
		"&7When activated by a connected Gale Activator, the Wind Tunnel Device continuously weaves an upward-blowing &ewind column&r&7 that can move most objects and creatures."
		"&7The Artisan's Crook can configure the distance and direction of this effect."
	]
	quest.731473A765D3B6B6.quest_subtitle: "Spurring Airflow"
	quest.731473A765D3B6B6.title: "Gale Weaving"
	quest.732853B6E9D536CC.quest_desc: [
		"&6Aurora Deer Antler&r&7"
		"&7A special drop produced when the Aurora Deer is not killed;&r"
		""
		"&7Players need to &#FFA500attack&r&7 the Aurora Deer to enrage it, making its &#00FFFFcharge attack&r&7 hit the side of a &#808080hard block such as stone&r&7. Only then is there a chance for it to drop an &#FFA500Aurora Deer Antler&r&7.&r"
	]
	quest.734CF87743FF73AB.quest_desc: ["&7A base trinket used only to increase &FF8844armor value&7 by a small amount. A necessary prerequisite for crafting its higher-tier material variants."]
	quest.734CF87743FF73AB.quest_subtitle: "Trinket Base"
	quest.737A6C878749DFB1.quest_desc: [
		"&7&#66FF66Lesser Wisps&7 seek out nearby &#55D5D5Soul Sand&7, hide inside it, and transform it into &#66CCFFSoul-Infused Soul Sand&7;  "
		""
		"&7&#66FF66Lesser Wisps&7 re-emerge after hiding in &#66CCFFSoul-Infused Soul Sand&7 for an extremely long time, and transform that &#66CCFFSoul-Infused Soul Sand&7 into &#FFD700Suspicious Soul Sand&7;  "
		""
		"&7The &#FFD700Suspicious Soul Sand&7 transformed this way inherits the corresponding archaeology loot table based on its biome/structure;"
		""
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"&7&#66CCFFSoul-Infused Soul Sand&7 crafted and placed by players / partially naturally generated does not have the above transformation properties;  "
		""
		"&7&#66CCFFSoul-Infused Soul Sand&7 that has been right-clicked with &#FFD700Honeycomb&7 loses its transformation ability (can no longer become &#FFD700Suspicious Soul Sand&7);  "
		""
		"&7Must be mined with a tool enchanted with &#66CCFFSilk Touch&7 to drop the correct item;  "
		""
		"&7Hold a brush and long-press right-click on &#66CCFFSoul-Infused Soul Sand&7 containing a &#66FF66Lesser Wisp&7 to forcibly expel it from the block, and the &#66CCFFSoul-Infused Soul Sand&7 will turn into &#FFD700Suspicious Soul Sand&7."
	]
	quest.737A6C878749DFB1.quest_subtitle: "Strange Soul"
	quest.737A6C878749DFB1.title: "Observation: Soul-Infused Soul Sand"
	quest.737AC021C2A2CF1D.quest_desc: [
		"&2On journeys, you often encounter well-enchanted weapons you cannot use—what a shame."
		""
		"&6This Salvaging Tome can, through an anvil, transfer half (rounded up) of the random enchantments on equipment into the book, consuming enchantment count × 10 levels of experience to convert into enchanted books. The original equipment is destroyed."
		""
		"&eCan also be repeatedly used on marked equipment to refresh the combination of enchantments to be extracted."
	]
	quest.737AC021C2A2CF1D.quest_subtitle: "Recycle and Reuse"
	quest.73E6FF96B1846AF3.quest_desc: [
		"&6Pact of the Fortress"
		"&7A grand exterior and an indolent nature cannot be separated.&r&cSoul Ward recovery rate halved"
		"&7A compressed form of Soul Ward, grand and precise.&r&aIncreases Soul Ward capacity&r&aSoul Ward firmness increased by half"
		""
		"{image:kubejs:textures/gui/malum/pact_of_the_fortress.png width:160 height:200 align:center}"
	]
	quest.73E6FF96B1846AF3.quest_subtitle: "Standing Firm in Defense"
	quest.73E6FF96B1846AF3.title: "Pact of the Fortress"
	quest.73FCDE97B31913FF.quest_subtitle: "It really does explode!"
	quest.7458C276CADE77AC.quest_desc: ["Functions the same as a vanilla shield"]
	quest.7458C276CADE77AC.quest_subtitle: "A Better Defense Method"
	quest.746B034A029684EA.quest_desc: [
		"&6Smart Filter&r"
		"&7Controls a device's output and input filtering with greater complexity.&r"
		"&7Right-click to open the configuration GUI. You can mark items in the top inventory. The buttons below, from left to right, are: black/whitelist, match/ignore NBT, clear, confirm.&r"
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"&7If a marked List Filter/Attribute Filter with information is placed inside, it reads the internal marked information and generates filtering logic through logical operations. (Different marks in the same filter use OR logic; a filter using the blacklist applies NOT logic.)&r"
		"&7For example: A List Filter marks iron sword and gold sword using the blacklist; B Attribute Filter marks not-full-durability; C List Filter marks filters A and B using the blacklist. Then C's filtering logic is NOT(NOT(iron sword OR gold sword) OR NOT full durability), simplified to (iron sword OR gold sword) AND full durability.&r"
		"&7Filters can be placed inside other filters, allowing more item filtering.&r"
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"&6Attribute Filter&r"
		"&7The Attribute Filter can filter based on some '&eattributes&r&7' of items. It is more flexible than a general filter and achieves smarter results in automated processing than ordinary filters (ordinary filters still cannot be replaced).&r"
		"&7Holding and using the Attribute Filter opens its configuration GUI. To add a filter condition, place a reference item, and the GUI center then displays all '&eattributes&r&7' of that item. Players can use the mouse wheel to select. After selecting, click the [ &a+&r&7 ] or [ &c+!&r&7 ] on the right to add that attribute as a positive filter or negative filter. A positive filter matches items with that attribute; a negative filter matches items without it. Players can add multiple filter conditions in one Attribute Filter, and the bottom-left of the GUI lets you set the matching logic for multiple tags.&r"
	]
	quest.746B034A029684EA.title: "Filter"
	quest.746FA8AC7777829D.quest_desc: [
		"&7&#66CCFFSoul Glass&7 is a block players can pass through;  "
		""
		"&7Except for players, all creatures cannot pass through &#66CCFFSoul Glass&7 (they also avoid &#66CCFFSoul Glass&7 when pathfinding);  "
		""
		"&7&#66CCFFSoul Glass&7 only has collision volume on its top;  "
		""
		"&7Players can stand normally on top of &#66CCFFSoul Glass&7, but sneaking players will still pass through &#66CCFFSoul Glass&7;  "
		""
		"&7The above properties make &#66CCFFSoul Glass&7 very suitable as a door or \"elevator\" in player shelters."
		""
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"&7Players passing into &#66CCFFSoul Glass&7 have their &#FFAA33movement speed&7 reduced. Wearing equipment with the &#66CCFFSoul Speed&7 enchantment can negate this effect;  "
		""
		"&7After right-clicking &#66CCFFSoul Glass&7 with a &#FFD700Flint and Steel&7 / &#FFD700Fire Charge&7:  "
		"&7The &#66CCFFSoul Glass's&7 texture changes and it can emit light (light level: &#FFAA3312&7). All other properties remain unchanged."
	]
	quest.746FA8AC7777829D.quest_subtitle: "Phasmophobia sufferer"
	quest.7494DCB39DEAF4F5.quest_desc: [
		"&7This should count as an improved terminal. I removed its dependency on &#66DDCCDisks&7, sacrificing some functions to obtain maximum storage space."
		""
		"&7It can only be used after charging. Sneak-right-click the &#66CCFFTerminal&7 to bind it. After binding, you can remotely access its contents at any time. Use a &#FFD700Tesla Coil&7 to recharge it."
	]
	quest.7494DCB39DEAF4F5.quest_subtitle: "Remote Storage"
	quest.74F6BCC9482F2FD6.quest_desc: [
		"&6Pact of Reciprocation"
		"&7Only &cstrife&r&7 remains in your heart.&r&cDisables natural Soul Ward recovery"
		"&7A transformation, a brand-new mechanism of refutation."
		"&r&aDealing magic damage restores Soul Ward&r"
		"&aGreatly increases Soul Ward capacity&r"
		"&aSoul Ward recovery amount doubled"
		""
		"{image:kubejs:textures/gui/malum/pact_of_reciprocation.png width:160 height:200 align:center}"
	]
	quest.74F6BCC9482F2FD6.quest_subtitle: "Repaying Double"
	quest.74F6BCC9482F2FD6.title: "Pact of Reciprocation"
	quest.7501056B288C71E1.quest_subtitle: "Food value > 8"
	quest.7535B9010BCF5E06.quest_desc: [
		"&6Rune of Flame's Embrace&r"
		""
		"&7The Rune of Flame's Embrace functions similarly to the ritual of the same name, granting a burning wearer a half-strength &bFlame's Embrace&r&7 effect, extinguishing &cflames&r&7 and providing &anormal healing&r&7.&r"
	]
	quest.7535B9010BCF5E06.quest_subtitle: "Extinguishing Pulse"
	quest.754B74CB9D6E7C5A.quest_desc: [
		"&7Allows the spawner to spawn creatures even when no player is nearby."
		""
		"&7Use with caution..."
	]
	quest.754B74CB9D6E7C5A.quest_subtitle: "Stabbed Through the Unmanned Factory"
	quest.756DE36F8CEBB947.quest_desc: ["&7The Starlight Dimension has many unique ecologies and biomes. While traveling, take a look around."]
	quest.756DE36F8CEBB947.quest_subtitle: "Star Traveler"
	quest.75DF4040BA1F636B.quest_desc: ["&7Spawns in a burning state"]
	quest.75DF4040BA1F636B.quest_subtitle: "Cooking Requires the Right Heat"
	quest.75EB87C487763166.quest_desc: [
		"Inlay all five Runewood Logs above the Totem Base with Arcane Spirits to activate the &bRite of Unbinding&r. This ritual significantly alters the nearby environment and spawns a Soulwood Sapling."
		""
		"&7After further research, I discovered that the &6Soulwood Tree&r&7 produced by the &bRite of Unbinding&r&7 has become another species entirely, completely different from the original &eRunewood Tree&r&7. Its growth process differs, and so do its traits..."
		"&7"
		"&7It seems that the &dSpirit Scar&r&7 that created it does not stop at the level of color and magical properties. The most notable differences are its form and leaf color. The Soulwood Tree is more slender and frail than the Runewood Tree. Unlike the Runewood Tree's vivid orange-yellow leaves, its leaves are a sickly purplish-red. However, their uses are still roughly the same."
		"&7"
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"&6Soulwood Tree Research: Growth"
		"&7Similar to &8Blight&r&7, its sapling also accepts &dSpirit Arcane Energy&r&7 and common fertilizers like bone meal, with roughly similar results."
		"&7"
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"&6Soulwood Tree Research: Blight"
		"&7Another notable difference is its influence on surrounding things. For example, it reproduces the &bDirectionless Ritual&r&7 with the energy of its growth, transmuting surrounding things into Blight. If you want to plant this tree, it is best to designate a safe, controllable area specifically."
		"&7"
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"&6Soulwood Tree Research: Resin"
		"&7The viscous sap veins of the Soulwood Tree seem to gather and fill more easily than those of the Runewood Tree. The resulting resin's effects are also somewhat corrupted. &cCursed Resin&r&7 does not restore my vitality, but instead enhances it, increasing my attack power and providing damage resistance."
	]
	quest.75EB87C487763166.quest_subtitle: "Warped Sapling"
	quest.760AED607B00C7CA.quest_desc: [
		"&6Pact of the Arcanaphage"
		"&7Souls dwell within the form for a reason.&r"
		"&cHalf of all damage taken becomes magic damage&r"
		"&cSoul Ward firmness halved"
		"&7A part of your soul dissipates outside the body to attract arcane energy.&r&aShattering souls produces extra arcane energy&r&aHarvesting Spirits increases most magic attributes"
		""
		"{image:kubejs:textures/gui/malum/pact_of_the_arcanaphage.png width:160 height:200 align:center}"
	]
	quest.760AED607B00C7CA.quest_subtitle: "Detached from Oneself"
	quest.760AED607B00C7CA.title: "Pact of the Arcanaphage"
	quest.761C662C880C3BC3.quest_subtitle: "A handy tool for finding an Ocean Monument"
	quest.76418D5CB8DDA0B1.quest_desc: ["You only realize how many bugs need fixing once the pack actually gets tested..."]
	quest.76418D5CB8DDA0B1.quest_subtitle: "Guinea Pigs"
	quest.7655A85408A81AA1.quest_desc: [
		"If you are fortunate enough to encounter a wild familiar, you may be able to exchange arcane essence for their assistance."
		""
		"&eYou can also use the summoning ritual to summon familiars"
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"&6Familiar Basic Mechanics&r"
		"&7Familiars can be tamed using &bArcane Essence&r&7. Right-click a familiar with a stick to set it to &astay in place&r&7, keeping it stationary and not attacking. Tamed familiars can be &asummoned/dismissed&r&7 by selecting the corresponding familiar in the familiar selection interface. The selection interface can be opened through the corresponding key binding, after which you can use the summon/dismiss hotkeys to control the selected familiar. After obtaining the '&cLearn Necromancy&r&7' advancement, familiars will avoid death at the cost of &emana&r&7, but if your mana runs out, they will still die.&r"
	]
	quest.7655A85408A81AA1.quest_subtitle: "Finding a Familiar"
	quest.7655A85408A81AA1.title: "Eternal Companion"
	quest.768F736B2B18FA1B.quest_desc: [
		"&6Oath of the Overkeen Eye&r"
		""
		"&7The perceptiveness within your soul makes you prepared for what is to come.&r"
		"&7-&cSpell charge&r&7 recovery rate halved&r"
		""
		"&7An arcane-seeking eye fused into the soul.&r"
		"&7-&eStaff projectiles&r&7 will &ahome in&r&7 on targets&r"
		"{image:kubejs:textures/gui/malum/oath_of_the_overkeen_eye.png width:160 height:200 align:center}"
	]
	quest.768F736B2B18FA1B.quest_subtitle: "Piercing a Willow at a Hundred Paces"
	quest.768F736B2B18FA1B.title: "Oath of the Overkeen Eye"
	quest.76B78E211A0AEC85.quest_desc: [
		"&7Determined by &6Silent Gear&7 attributes:"
		"&7• Armor &7→ &cArmor value&7, also provides &cbonus health (armor ÷ 2)"
		"&7• Armor Toughness &7→ &cArmor toughness"
		"&7• Knockback Resistance &7→ &cKnockback resistance"
	]
	quest.76B78E211A0AEC85.quest_subtitle: "Compared to normal armor, its armor value and other attributes are higher, at the cost of losing spell attributes"
	quest.76BD72A25B241E0C.quest_desc: ["&7Using the light of Glowstone, I improved the Nether Bookshelf that symbolizes chaos. While providing extra &4Quantization&7, it also gives a small amount of &5Arcana&7. Although still inferior to the Ocean Bookshelf, a mosquito leg is still meat, right"]
	quest.76BD72A25B241E0C.quest_subtitle: "A More Balanced Nether Bookshelf"
	quest.76BD72A25B241E0C.title: "Disordered Expansion"
	quest.771C9B9ADDCDA5E6.quest_desc: ["一条龙身上浑身都是宝，提供优秀的护甲值加成和基础攻击力加成"]
	quest.771C9B9ADDCDA5E6.quest_subtitle: "你是龙，也好"
	quest.773AC14F2AF8822B.quest_desc: [
		"&7Nether Quartz is the most special adjustment item. It must be used together with other adjustment items and is not consumed itself (similar to a wrench). Quartz reverses the magic of the adjustment item, making it affect the result of using the item alone in the &eopposite&r way."
		""
		"&7When using quartz, place the other adjustment item in the off-hand."
	]
	quest.773AC14F2AF8822B.quest_subtitle: "Reverse Adjustment"
	quest.77437FA5561BE4E6.quest_desc: [""]
	quest.77437FA5561BE4E6.quest_subtitle: "从砍倒一棵树开始"
	quest.77437FA5561BE4E6.title: "开始游玩"
	quest.7779D406142005D6.quest_desc: [
		"&6Research: Void Salt"
		"&7After passing through the &dWeeping Well&r&7, &8Hex Ash&r&7 changed into a substance I call \"&8Void Salt&r&7.\" This dark powder is chemically similar to Hex Ash, but contains no carbon, so it can no longer be called \"ash.\""
		"&7"
		"&7It seems to be composed of an unknown unstable metal, bonded with some caustic substance I cannot identify. It is quite puzzling beyond the physical level as well. Carbon is the basis of life, but this substance with the carbon removed... seems to be moving? I could not confirm this in experiments, but I am almost certain this substance possesses some kind of life, and it moves."
		"&7"
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"&6Re-Examination: Void Salt"
		"&7&cNonexistence&r&7 produced &aexistence&r&7—that is the manifestation of &8Umbral Arcane Energy&r&7. It may &creally&r&7 be alive... but its life is defined by nothingness, rather than the existence of matter. And by extension, perhaps there is even more complex life within the void?"
	]
	quest.7779D406142005D6.quest_subtitle: "A Clue to the Essence of Souls"
	quest.779B259771323E1B.quest_desc: [
		"&7击败死者之王将解锁以下矿物：&r"
		"&7"
		"&#67B1E5戈伯&r&7"
		"&#C9C8E1泽纳莱特&r&7"
		"&#757369符文碎屑&r&7"
		"&#7EE344叶绿矿&r&7"
		"&#770808惧石&r&7"
		"&#DD660A烈阳核心&r"
	]
	quest.779B259771323E1B.quest_subtitle: "亡者力量"
	quest.77A67AF0D408E4DC.quest_desc: [
		"&7Holding the &#66DDCCTuning Fork&7 displays the various attributes of the &#66FF99Spirit Crucible&7."
		"{image:kubejs:textures/gui/malum/tuning_fork.png width:140 height=140 align=center}"
		"&7Right-click the &#66FF99Spirit Crucible&7 to toggle between default and selecting an attribute."
		""
		"&7The selected attribute gains &e20%&7, but all other attributes are reduced by &e10%&7. The Weakest Attribute bonus and Tuning Strength are unaffected. If the &#66FF99Spirit Crucible&7 is equipped with the &#FFAA33Starcore Mechanism&7, the buff and debuff magnitudes are doubled."
		""
		"&7For negative attributes such as &#FF6666Instability Risk&7, the value changes inversely—that is, when the attribute is debuffed by &e10%&7, its value +&e10%&7."
	]
	quest.77A67AF0D408E4DC.quest_subtitle: "Adjusting the Tuner"
	quest.77A67AF0D408E4DC.title: "Crucible Enhancement"
	quest.77CAB89231462E66.quest_subtitle: "Iron's Spells chapter may be reset in 1.3"
	quest.7807160BB2108E79.quest_desc: ["&7Extremely low crafting barrier. &#66CCFFQuartz Ore&7 is available for mining right in the Overworld, and the acquisition path is smooth. Excellent stat performance, and its innate trait \"&#FFAA33Critical Strike&7\" is an outstanding damage-boosting tool. Combat returns are significant—a highly cost-effective offensive material."]
	quest.7807160BB2108E79.quest_subtitle: "The Critical Choice"
	quest.78294B68D04E42A9.quest_desc: [
		"&dA blind brute comes to guard the Ancient City..."
		""
		"&7A symbol of pure strength, possessing extremely violent melee capabilities. Fighting it with long arms or spells is the safer strategy. The Sculk Tendril dropped after killing it is an important material for the Echoing Sculk Bookshelf."
	]
	quest.783683CB8A00E9B7.quest_desc: [
		"&7The &#88DDFFArcana Pylon&7's function is to raise the effect level of simple rituals. Placing it beside a totem and providing the corresponding &#66FF99Spirit&7 for the totem ritual raises the corresponding effect level."
		"{image:kubejs:textures/gui/malum/arcana_pylon.png width:200 height:140 align:center}"
	]
	quest.783683CB8A00E9B7.quest_subtitle: "High Obelisk"
	quest.783683CB8A00E9B7.title: "Aura Enhancement"
	quest.784CD820CEC6F25B.quest_desc: [
		"Move your mouse to the top-left corner of the quest selection box, look for the arrow, and click it to see the following screen:"
		"{image:kubejs:textures/gui/ftb_kjs3.png width:120 height:80 align:center}"
		""
		""
		"{@pagebreak}"
		""
		"Click again to view which prerequisite quests there are. Selecting one automatically jumps to that prerequisite quest"
		"{image:kubejs:textures/gui/ftb_kjs4.png width:120 height:80 align:center}"
		"You can also use the right arrow at the top-right of the quest to view a dropdown menu listing all dependent quests."
	]
	quest.784CD820CEC6F25B.quest_subtitle: "&mHow the hell do I complete this damn quest"
	quest.784CD820CEC6F25B.title: "View Prerequisites"
	quest.786068AC2857F91F.quest_desc: [
		"&7&#FFD700Giant Fossils&7 are common structures in the &#8B4513Soul Sand Valley&7, mainly composed of &#DDDDDDBone Blocks&7 and &#DDDDDDBone Cortex&7;"
		""
		"&7Divided into 5 common variants and 1 rare variant;"
		"&7This structure usually does not generate &#DDDDDDSuspicious Soul Sand&7, but the &#DDDDDDSuspicious Soul Sand&7 transformed from &#66DDCCSoul-Infused Soul Sand&7 within it inherits the archaeology loot table from this structure;"
		""
		"&7&#FFD700Giant Fossil Camps&7 are variants of &#FFD700Giant Fossils (structures)&7 after further decoration, generated in the &#8B4513Soul Sand Valley&7 structure;"
		""
		"&7Comparatively rarer, but still shares the same archaeology loot table as &#FFD700Giant Fossils (structures)&7;"
		"&7This structure usually does not generate &#DDDDDDSuspicious Soul Sand&7, but the &#DDDDDDSuspicious Soul Sand&7 transformed from &#66DDCCSoul-Infused Soul Sand&7 within it inherits the archaeology loot table from this structure."
	]
	quest.786068AC2857F91F.quest_subtitle: "Doo da doo da doo"
	quest.786068AC2857F91F.title: "Find Structure: Giant Fossil"
	quest.789A0AD70CA77553.quest_desc: [
		"&7People often use &6gold&r&7 as a base for mystical research; its natural magical conductivity makes it quite useful. Spirit arcane energy is no exception. And simply using &bHallowed Arcana&r&7 can enhance gold's magical conductivity."
		""
		"&7Hallowed Gold's physical properties are similar to gold. By fusing pure arcane energy into the alloy, it allows other arcane energies to conduct smoothly. &6Hallowed Gold&r&7 with this property is exactly the excellent conductor my research needs. It can also be used to craft several stylish item stands."
	]
	quest.789A0AD70CA77553.quest_subtitle: "In Accord with Rhythm"
	quest.78E0C869F2BB2516.quest_desc: [
		"&7作为顶端升级时可以提供 &#FFAA331&7 幸运值，极端的强大，建议前期在可以打顶端升级的位置 &#FFD700打满&7 青金石，可以巨幅增加战利品宝箱的物资产出。"
		""
		"&7推荐部位：&#66DDCC顶端升级&7"
	]
	quest.78E0C869F2BB2516.quest_subtitle: "我！真！幸！运！"
	quest.78FE7E1CD8810721.quest_subtitle: "Just as the title says"
	quest.791787D97B46619C.quest_desc: ["&7The modpack includes a &#66DDCCNature's Compass&7, which can be used to search for specific biomes, but does not include a &#66DDCCStructure Compass&7. &7When your early-game equipment is poor, it's recommended to explore the Overworld first. It is &#FF6666not recommended&7 to enter the Nether too early."]
	quest.791787D97B46619C.quest_subtitle: "Have you seen the troublemaker? Where?"
	quest.791787D97B46619C.title: "Exploration"
	quest.79244245C1776777.quest_desc: ["&7Pure human power—a stack of steak per 100 kilometers. An aircraft that also has hovering capability, with decent flight speed. No real downsides, no real upsides either."]
	quest.7924CE833E734123.quest_desc: [
		"&7Holding the &#88DDFFTotemic Staff&7 displays the influence range of totem rituals.  "
		"&7Right-clicking an unactivated totem pole toggles the active state of its sigil."
		""
		"&7A totem is a structure composed of a &#FFD700Totem Base&7 and multiple totem poles, capable of performing &#CC99FFSpirit Rituals&7."
		""
		"{image:kubejs:textures/gui/malum/totemic_staff.png width=160 height=160 align=center}"
	]
	quest.7924CE833E734123.quest_subtitle: "Cognition: Ritual"
	quest.7924CE833E734123.title: "Totem Resonance"
	quest.7964EFBEAA0F5D57.quest_desc: ["&7Click &a√&r&7 to unlock the next quest"]
	quest.7964EFBEAA0F5D57.quest_subtitle: "As you can see, this is a quest"
	quest.7964EFBEAA0F5D57.title: "Guidance"
	quest.7995CC0B134AEC55.quest_subtitle: "哇，金色传说"
	quest.799B92FBA8B69A02.quest_desc: [
		"{\"text\":\"\",\"extra\":[{\"text\":\"The \",\"color\":\"gray\"},{\"text\":\"Orichalcum Ingots\",\"color\":\"gold\"},{\"text\":\" dropped by the Skeleton King are very useful, commonly used as an equipment source for crafting various \",\"color\":\"gray\"},{\"text\":\"Silent Gear\",\"color\":\"aqua\"},{\"text\":\" equipment.\",\"color\":\"gray\"}]}"
		""
		"{\"text\":\"\",\"extra\":[{\"text\":\"After obtaining Orichalcum Ingots, \",\"color\":\"gray\"},{\"text\":\"you can also defeat some bosses and obtain their unique weapons to craft some \",\"color\":\"gray\"},{\"text\":\"Silent Gear\",\"color\":\"aqua\"},{\"text\":\" based on those unique weapons.\",\"color\":\"gray\"}]}"
		""
		"&#7EE344Chlorophyte Ore&r&7 generates in the Jungle underground above height 0, replacing dirt blocks"
		""
		"&#770808Dreadstone&r&7 generates in the Overworld at depths from -64 to 0"
		""
		"&#DD660ASun Core&7 generates in the Nether at depths from -64 to 80"
		""
		"&#E9FAFFZenith Ore&r will generate"
		""
		"&#FF1C45Nether Gober&r&7 generates in the Nether"
		""
		"&#7EE344Chlorophyte Ore's&r&7 own traits and values are not outstanding, but it provides spell power and healing received. Consider it if you have spellcasting needs."
		""
		"&#770808Dreadstone&r&7 is used to craft Dread Steel and Shadow Ingots. The former increases Spirit Calamity's oath count and increases healing received, while the latter increases oath count and spell power but reduces healing. Choose according to your needs."
		""
		"&#DD660ASun Core&7 currently has no use."
	]
	quest.799B92FBA8B69A02.quest_subtitle: "All Kinds of Martial Arts"
	quest.799B92FBA8B69A02.title: "It's Time!"
	quest.799C21A4DB6DA05C.quest_desc: [
		"&7Each &#66FF99Spirit&7 harvested while worn grants a &e30&7 * &#CC99FFArcane Resonance&7-second &#FF8844Gluttony&7 effect, or raises an existing &#FF8844Gluttony&7 effect by &e1&7 level (up to level &eX&7)."
		""
		"&7After eating &#FFAA33Gluttony Condensate&7, each &#CC6666Belt of the Starving&7 worn increases the &#FF8844Gluttony&7 effect's level by +&e1&7 and duration by +&e10&7 seconds."
	]
	quest.799C21A4DB6DA05C.quest_subtitle: "Endless Hunger"
	quest.79B7BF074539AA91.quest_desc: [
		"&6Smart Fluid Pipe&r"
		"&7Has a filter slot that can mark items or hold a filter. (Mark with bucketed or bottled fluids.)&r"
		"&7Only fluids meeting the condition are allowed to pass.&r"
		"&7When using Smart Fluid Pipes, try to place them close to the fluid source; otherwise there is a chance of &cclogging&r&7 because other fluid types are expelled first.&r"
	]
	quest.7A1141EE7A34D62F.quest_desc: [
		"&6Oath of Unsighted Resistance&r"
		""
		"&7The Oath dulls the blade of Malice slashes.&r"
		"&7-Reduces &cMalice Critical&r&7 damage when restoring &cMalice Ward&r"
		""
		"&7An etching carved into the malice soul-return.&r"
		"&7-&6Malice Critical&r&7 charges &aMalice Ward&r"
		"{image:kubejs:textures/gui/malum/oath_of_unsighted_resistance.png width:160 height:200 align:center}"
	]
	quest.7A1141EE7A34D62F.quest_subtitle: "Confined to Slaughter"
	quest.7A1141EE7A34D62F.title: "Oath of Unsighted Resistance"
	quest.7A4449338F885205.quest_desc: [
		"Summon it using the Soul-Seeking Ember Bell in the Castle structure; can be located using a Rolled Map, and can also be summoned via the Altar."
		""
		"&7Defeating it unlocks End Gober Ore, and the Castle's special vaults will produce Blaze Gold Ingots."
	]
	quest.7A4449338F885205.quest_subtitle: "Stage 2 - kill to unlock Stage 3"
	quest.7A4D91266571EC0F.quest_desc: ["&7The &#88DDFFSurging&7 enchantment launches targets into the air, but the &#88DDFFSurging&7 cooldown is extended."]
	quest.7A4D91266571EC0F.quest_subtitle: "Scythe Authority"
	quest.7A63B4E0381D9BA4.quest_desc: [
		"&6Pact of Patience Repaid"
		""
		"&7A long ache is worse than a short one.&r&cBuffered damage becomes magic damage, and its intensity increases by one fifth when released"
		"&7Dispersing the impact, slowing the damage.&r&aBuffers half of damage taken, converting it into damage over time&r&aBuffered damage cannot cause death"
		"{image:kubejs:textures/gui/malum/pact_of_patience_repaid.png width:160 height:200 align:center}"
	]
	quest.7A63B4E0381D9BA4.quest_subtitle: "Diluting Pain"
	quest.7A63B4E0381D9BA4.title: "Pact of Patience Repaid"
	quest.7AF763EC94AE76CA.quest_desc: ["&7Increases the level cap of enchantment storage, but provides no other improvements..."]
	quest.7AF763EC94AE76CA.quest_subtitle: "A Bigger Library"
	quest.7AF858E2ECF74FAD.quest_desc: [
		"Can be summoned via the Altar"
		""
		"&7Special drops mainly include: Blood Bead, Brain of Confusion, Molten Eyeball."
		""
		"&7Has a small chance to drop a random Seven Deadly Sins trinket."
	]
	quest.7AF858E2ECF74FAD.quest_subtitle: "Stage 1"
	quest.7B098F5DB49DB51F.title: "Nightfall Spider"
	quest.7B2DD9D8E6237F68.quest_desc: ["The skull representing blood sacrifice is connected to the Nether, providing an extra Quantization attribute"]
	quest.7B2DD9D8E6237F68.quest_subtitle: "Weak Quantization Growth"
	quest.7B2DD9D8E6237F68.title: "Primitive Chaotic Sacrifice"
	quest.7B470F04445F5D8B.quest_desc: [
		"{\"text\":\"\",\"extra\":[{\"text\":\"I can now distinguish the composition of \",\"color\":\"gray\"},{\"text\":\"Malignant Lead\",\"color\":\"red\"},{\"text\":\", making it easier to design uses. Just as \",\"color\":\"gray\"},{\"text\":\"Umbral Arcana\",\"color\":\"dark_gray\"},{\"text\":\" is strange, its alloys with metals also have special properties.\",\"color\":\"gray\"},{\"text\":\"Deeprock Aurum\",\"color\":\"yellow\"},{\"text\":\" becomes lowly, producing Malignant Lead, and this \",\"color\":\"gray\"},{\"text\":\"pewter\",\"color\":\"red\"},{\"text\":\" craves outward action. It craves erosion, dismantling, and eliminating human development.\",\"color\":\"gray\"}]}"
		""
		"{\"text\":\"\",\"extra\":[{\"text\":\"This property does have its mundane uses—as a weapon it further damages armor while harming and shattering souls; its occult uses also cannot be underestimated. Malignant Pewter is not inert at the magical level, nor does it absorb magic. Rather, magic seems simply unable to \",\"color\":\"gray\"},{\"text\":\"form\",\"color\":\"red\"},{\"text\":\" around it, symbolizing the fading of the pursuit of knowledge.\",\"color\":\"gray\"}]}"
		""
		"{\"text\":\"\",\"extra\":[{\"text\":\"This metal is quite tough and quite sharp, but wearing \",\"color\":\"gray\"},{\"text\":\"anti-magic armor\",\"color\":\"red\"},{\"text\":\" will certainly cause problems... and also bring entirely new abilities. I already have a rough idea for crafting an armor set from it; this set can utilize the metal's abilities and should be extremely powerful.\",\"color\":\"gray\"}]}"
		""
		"{@pagebreak}"
		""
		"{\"text\":\"\",\"extra\":[{\"text\":\"Malice Fortress Armor\",\"color\":\"gold\"}]}"
		""
		"{\"text\":\"\",\"extra\":[{\"text\":\"Malignant Pewter\",\"color\":\"red\"},{\"text\":\" repels magic, so from a mage's perspective, wearing it is a strange practice indeed. But I \",\"color\":\"gray\"},{\"text\":\"am also\",\"color\":\"green\"},{\"text\":\" a mage, and the Fortress Armor I created is incomparably powerful.\",\"color\":\"gray\"}]}"
		""
		"{\"text\":\"\",\"extra\":[{\"text\":\"The armor beneath the Malignant Pewter plating is the opposite of \",\"color\":\"gray\"},{\"text\":\"Soulstained Steel Armor\",\"color\":\"gold\"},{\"text\":\"—my soul is not protected; rather, the flow of arcane energy is destroyed by this metal. It distorts arcane energy into flowing outward, thereby disrupting incoming damage. When wearing the full Fortress Armor set, the damage my soul ultimately takes is reduced to half.\",\"color\":\"gray\"}]}"
		""
		"{@pagebreak}"
		""
		"{\"text\":\"\",\"extra\":[{\"text\":\"This armor affects more than just incoming magic. The wearer's own arcane circuits are also affected. Their original paths toward the soul are disrupted, stolen, processed and twisted. And in the dissolution of arcane energy, the energy still remains. The armor reacts to this energy and strengthens accordingly.\",\"color\":\"gray\"}]}"
		""
		"{\"text\":\"\",\"extra\":[{\"text\":\"There are two key points in this effect. First, the armor's magic absorption process should be called \\\"\",\"color\":\"gray\"},{\"text\":\"Malice Conversion\",\"color\":\"red\"},{\"text\":\"\\\". It is the process of intercepting arcane energy flowing toward the soul and absorbing the resulting energy. Second, the armor weaves the stolen energy, giving it entirely new form and intent. The effect of this process should be named \\\"\",\"color\":\"gray\"},{\"text\":\"Malice Ward\",\"color\":\"gold\"},{\"text\":\"\\\".\",\"color\":\"gray\"}]}"
		""
		"{@pagebreak}"
		""
		"{\"text\":\"\",\"extra\":[{\"text\":\"Malice Ward\",\"color\":\"gold\"},{\"text\":\" is effectively a powerful shield that can directly negate almost all types of damage. As the armor continuously absorbs magic, Malice Ward's capacity, recovery rate, and recovery bonuses also grow, varying depending on the absorbed attributes. As far as my research has gone, Malice Fortress Armor's most powerful ability is none other than this.\",\"color\":\"gray\"}]}"
	]
	quest.7B470F04445F5D8B.quest_subtitle: "Evolution Ceases"
	quest.7B6F7BDF000CF379.quest_desc: [
		"&6Fused Consciousness&r"
		""
		"&7The future holds many mysteries... but you can learn some in advance.&r"
		"&7Throwing an iron block into the &eWeeping Well&r&7 crafts a &bAnomalous Construct Part&r&7. Throwing a complete construct part into the &eWeeping Well&r&7 crafts a Fused Consciousness.&r"
	]
	quest.7B6F7BDF000CF379.quest_subtitle: "Blueprints of All Things Past and Future"
	quest.7B8819152EE73E21.quest_desc: [
		"&6Fruit of Life&r"
		"&7A consumable used to increase a familiar's &ahealth&r&7. There are 3 tiers, each with a usage cap&r"
	]
	quest.7B8819152EE73E21.title: "&6Fruit of Life&r"
	quest.7B8A4E62A807BF77.quest_desc: [
		"&7Can switch modes via &#FFD700sneak + right-click&7.  "
		"&7There are four modes:  "
		"&7&#66CCFFSmall Tunnel&7: Mines a &#FFAA331×1×5&7 passage  "
		"&7&#66CCFFLarge Tunnel&7: Mines a &#FFAA333×3×5&7 passage  "
		"&7&#66CCFFMining Tunnel&7 and &#66CCFFEscape Tunnel&7 mine stair-shaped passages"
	]
	quest.7B8A4E62A807BF77.quest_subtitle: "The True Mine Shaft Excavator"
	quest.7B8A4E62A807BF77.title: "Multi-Tool Pickaxe Mold"
	quest.7BACE6601BC4DFED.quest_desc: [
		"&7Can be used to carry items on the go. Use &#66DDCCMineral Upgrades&7 to upgrade upward through &#FFAA33Iron&7-&#FFD700Gold&7-&#66CCFFDiamond&7-&#CC99FFAlloy&7. Each upgrade expands the &#66DDCCstorage space&7. If one backpack isn't enough, you can craft multiple backpacks—no more worrying about not being able to carry away &#FFAA33loot&7. If you can't find a place to settle down for a while, you can even carry a large number of backpacks to store items."
		""
		"&7The top-left corner of the backpack shows the slots available for &#66DDCCupgrades&7. Different upgrades have different uses. Only a few common ones are highlighted here; explore the rest yourself."
		""
		"&7The &#FFD700Settings&7 in the top-right corner of the backpack allow you to modify some specific backpack options, such as &#66CCFFdisplaying a certain slot's item&7 on the backpack, or specifying that a certain slot &#FFAA33can only store one type of item&7. This lets some items you need to carry ignore sorting and only be stored in designated positions, making daily access convenient."
	]
	quest.7BACE6601BC4DFED.quest_subtitle: "Not enough space? Try a Dimensional Pocket"
	quest.7BD83673ECEA9F2E.quest_subtitle: "A handy tool for finding the Castle"
	quest.7BD9DC7DB2278AA5.quest_desc: [
		"&7需要杀死死者之王后在古城战利品箱获取，拥有相当高的攻击伤害，但没有特殊词条，适合用于合金制作武器部件。"
		""
		"推荐部位：武器"
	]
	quest.7BD9DC7DB2278AA5.quest_subtitle: "朴素的高伤害"
	quest.7BF7E53DAB408397.quest_desc: ["{\"text\":\"\",\"extra\":[{\"text\":\"I know you might get a headache seeing this mod's \",\"color\":\"gray\"},{\"text\":\"eyes\",\"color\":\"red\"},{\"text\":\", but now they can all be \",\"color\":\"gray\"},{\"text\":\"crafted\",\"color\":\"green\"},{\"text\":\".\",\"color\":\"gray\"}]}"]
	quest.7BF7E53DAB408397.quest_subtitle: "Craftable"
	quest.7C09F05734B44F6A.quest_desc: [
		"&7Hold right-click to fire a &#CC99FFvoid grenade&7 at enemies, &#FF6666indiscriminate of friend or foe&7."
		"&7Grenade damage = &cranged damage × 1.5&7."
		"&7Cooldown is dynamically determined by &6Silent Gear's&7 &edraw speed&7 attribute."
	]
	quest.7C09F05734B44F6A.quest_subtitle: "Ha~ki~ma~ru~yo~"
	quest.7C19C7795643C67E.quest_desc: [
		"&7The Soul-Bound Flesh Variant is a block that can be sliced to mass-produce &#55D5D5Soul-Bound Flesh&7;  "
		"&7Players can right-click to \"slice\" it;  "
		"&7Each slice drops &#FFAA3316 pieces&7 of Soul-Bound Flesh, up to &#FFAA33four slices&7;  "
		"&7This block is not limited to one-time production;  "
		""
		"&7When the Soul-Bound Flesh Variant still has remaining slices: it will regenerate a slice at an &#66CCFFextremely slow speed&7 for players to harvest again;  "
		"&7After growing back to the &#FFAA33four-slice&7 state, it &#FF6666stops growing&7 (until it is sliced again);  "
		""
		"&7As long as players leave at least one slice, they effectively have a &#66FF66slow but steady&7 source of Soul-Bound Flesh."
	]
	quest.7C19C7795643C67E.quest_subtitle: "Is this meat fresh"
	quest.7C227ABAEC91DA58.quest_desc: [
		"&7A set of spell robes."
		""
		"&7Can obtain &#CC99FFSpell Power&7, &#CC99FFSpell Resistance&7, and &#66FFCCMana Regeneration&7 based on materials."
		"&7Can obtain &#55D5D5pact cap&7, &#55D5D5healing multiplier&7, and &cknockback resistance&7 based on materials."
	]
	quest.7C227ABAEC91DA58.quest_subtitle: "Less defensive than other armor, but specialized against spell-related attributes"
	quest.7C74D47B9ED97737.quest_desc: [
		"&7权限管理器是一个可以存储权限卡的方块"
		""
		"你可以配置每个玩家（这是与权限卡绑定）有什么权限"
		""
		"{@pagebreak}"
		""
		"&e当网络上没有权限卡时，每个玩家都可以访问所有权限。"
		""
		"&6开始插入权限卡来定义玩家的权限。"
		""
		"&e没有配置权限卡的玩家仍然可以在网络中做所有事情（所有权限）。"
		""
		"&6要为所有未配置的玩家配置一套\"全球\"权限，配置不绑定到玩家的权限卡，并将其插入权限管理器中。"
		""
		"&e在服务器上的操作员，有权访问所有权限。"
		""
		"&6权限管理器的放置者始终能够打开它的 GUI 并更改安全设置，无论权限如何。"
	]
	quest.7C74D47B9ED97737.quest_subtitle: "无权访问"
	quest.7C78F44CB8587BCB.quest_desc: ["&7远程特化的棍材，若你的武器无需承担近战输出职责，它便是极为契合的选择。专注增幅远程体系，让每一发投射都更具威胁。"]
	quest.7C78F44CB8587BCB.quest_subtitle: "*哔哔"
	quest.7C7A1613FB9C97E8.quest_subtitle: "How did you know..."
	quest.7C7A1613FB9C97E8.title: "Catch 64 Fish"
	quest.7C7C7734793AB866.quest_desc: [
		"&6Prismarine Focusing Lens&r"
		""
		"&7Sometimes, simplicity is the answer. The Prismarine Focusing Lens refracts not light, but arcane energy, thereby greatly reducing the &cInstability Risk&r&7 of the &eSpirit Focusing&r&7 process. But one thing to note: stability can only prevent extra wear on the Catalyst Charm.&r"
	]
	quest.7C7C7734793AB866.quest_subtitle: "Stabilize"
	quest.7C8FEB4083F60A23.quest_desc: [
		"Hold right-click to spin and attack surrounding enemies"
		""
		"Attack interval is determined by attack speed"
		"Attack radius is half the player's reach distance (not the weapon's)"
	]
	quest.7C8FEB4083F60A23.quest_subtitle: "Spinning in Circles"
	quest.7C8FEB4083F60A23.title: "Whirl Blade Template"
	quest.7CACDAC57F697371.quest_desc: ["&7Right-click consumes some durability to &#66CCFFhighlight&7 nearby &#FFD700ores&7."]
	quest.7CACDAC57F697371.quest_subtitle: "If It's Not Off, It's On?"
	quest.7CB11EBD34BA84FB.quest_desc: [
		"{\"text\":\"\",\"extra\":[{\"text\":\"If you want, you can even\",\"color\":\"gray\"},{\"text\":\"defeat\",\"color\":\"red\"},{\"text\":\"creatures much \",\"color\":\"gray\"},{\"text\":\"weaker\",\"color\":\"green\"},{\"text\":\"than you...\",\"color\":\"gray\"}]}"
		""
		"&7Of course, be careful: as your number of &cBOSS&7 kills grows, your &6Rank&7 will rise as well..."
		""
		""
		"For the vast majority of hard-to-summon BOSSes, you can summon them via the Altar; search &eSpawn: XXX&r in EMI to view the corresponding recipe"
		"{image:kubejs:textures/gui/spawn.png width:150 height:130 align:center}"
		"Note that some BOSSes may leave behind indestructible structures after being defeated, so summoning near your base is not recommended."
	]
	quest.7CB11EBD34BA84FB.quest_subtitle: "Anyway, before facing the BOSSes, let's pick a few unlucky mobs to practice on"
	quest.7CB11EBD34BA84FB.title: "Warm-up"
	quest.7CDF0A87C605E833.quest_subtitle: "Familiar Summoning Ritual"
	quest.7CE0C7EC4D46C170.quest_subtitle: "Familiar Summoning Ritual"
	quest.7CEF4D8E514066A7.quest_desc: [
		"&6Tower Squid&r&7"
		"&7A common aquatic creature in the Starlight Dimension, smaller in size than the vanilla squid;&r"
		""
		"&7Cannot survive out of water (completely loses movement ability and gradually loses health until death after a period of time);&r"
		""
		"&7Hold a water bucket and right-click the Tower Squid: converts it into item form (&#1E90FFBucket of Tower Squid&r&7) for storage.&r"
	]
	quest.7CEF4D8E514066A7.title: "Tower Squid"
	quest.7CF77F3C6D4073BD.quest_desc: [
		"&7Spirits successfully fuse into items, genuinely altering the properties of the objects, and I can indirectly exert the abilities that Spirits possess by manipulating these items."
		""
		"&7Building on these materials, I focused my research on three directions: soul, flesh, and world."
		""
		"{@pagebreak}"
		""
		"&7Spirits are born from souls, so using their power to influence souls can be said to be easy. But likewise, they are born from souls with self-will, so they cannot be fully controlled by my will, meaning the power they bring often has negative effects."
		""
		"I call these negative Authorities granted by Spirits \"&4Oaths&r\""
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"&7Making Spirit creations affect the flesh is a bit more troublesome. After repeated experiments, I concluded that they still need a \"vessel\" to function."
		""
		"I call these vessels that allow Spirits to act upon the flesh \"&4Runes&r\""
		""
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"&7Making Spirits affect the world requires brute force—greatly increasing their output power. Since it does not need to act on living beings, the degree of experimental openness can be increased, and bold experiments have produced quite a lot of results, mostly practical tools."
	]
	quest.7CF77F3C6D4073BD.quest_subtitle: "Inspiration Strikes"
	quest.7CF77F3C6D4073BD.title: "Infinite Possibilities"
	quest.7D0410D74877C78A.quest_desc: [
		"{\"text\":\"\",\"extra\":[{\"text\":\"To use \",\"color\":\"gray\"},{\"text\":\"Refined Storage\",\"color\":\"gold\"},{\"text\":\" to store and retrieve items, you need three components: \",\"color\":\"gray\"},{\"text\":\"Controller, Terminal, and Storage\",\"color\":\"aqua\"},{\"text\":\".\",\"color\":\"gray\"}]}"
		""
		"{\"text\":\"\",\"extra\":[{\"text\":\"The Controller powers all components. The \",\"color\":\"gray\"},{\"text\":\"Alternator\",\"color\":\"yellow\"},{\"text\":\" from quest rewards can power the Controller when placed directly against it, and the generator only needs to be connected to a \",\"color\":\"gray\"},{\"text\":\"Large Water Wheel\",\"color\":\"aqua\"},{\"text\":\" to run.\",\"color\":\"gray\"}]}"
		""
		"{\"text\":\"\",\"extra\":[{\"text\":\"The Terminal is where you access stored contents. You can deposit and withdraw here. The \",\"color\":\"gray\"},{\"text\":\"Crafting Terminal\",\"color\":\"yellow\"},{\"text\":\" also adds crafting functionality. The left side of the terminal page has many additional functions, such as adjusting item sorting order.\",\"color\":\"gray\"}]}"
		""
		"{\"text\":\"\",\"extra\":[{\"text\":\"Storage affects how many items you can store. Each 1 storage unit represents one item, so storing a stack of cobblestone directly takes up 64 storage units.\",\"color\":\"gray\"}]}"
		""
		"{\"text\":\"\",\"extra\":[{\"text\":\"The next page has a more detailed placement example.\",\"color\":\"gray\"}]}"
		""
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"{\"text\":\"\",\"extra\":[{\"text\":\"As shown, you can place the \",\"color\":\"gray\"},{\"text\":\"Controller\",\"color\":\"aqua\"},{\"text\":\", \",\"color\":\"gray\"},{\"text\":\"Storage Terminal\",\"color\":\"aqua\"},{\"text\":\", and \",\"color\":\"gray\"},{\"text\":\"Storage Block\",\"color\":\"aqua\"},{\"text\":\" together to \",\"color\":\"gray\"},{\"text\":\"link\",\"color\":\"green\"},{\"text\":\" them, while also \",\"color\":\"gray\"},{\"text\":\"powering\",\"color\":\"yellow\"},{\"text\":\" the controller.\",\"color\":\"gray\"}]}"
		""
		"{image:kubejs:textures/gui/refinedstorage1.png width:180 height:100 align:center}"
		"{\"text\":\"\",\"extra\":[{\"text\":\"At this point, the linked \",\"color\":\"gray\"},{\"text\":\"Storage Blocks'\",\"color\":\"aqua\"},{\"text\":\" \",\"color\":\"gray\"},{\"text\":\"size\",\"color\":\"yellow\"},{\"text\":\" and \",\"color\":\"gray\"},{\"text\":\"count\",\"color\":\"yellow\"},{\"text\":\" determine the \",\"color\":\"gray\"},{\"text\":\"amount\",\"color\":\"aqua\"},{\"text\":\" of items you can store.\",\"color\":\"gray\"}]}"
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"{\"text\":\"\",\"extra\":[{\"text\":\"You can also use \",\"color\":\"gray\"},{\"text\":\"cables\",\"color\":\"yellow\"},{\"text\":\" to link them, in which case all blocks connected by cables will be counted.\",\"color\":\"gray\"}]}"
		""
		"{image:kubejs:textures/gui/refinedstorage2.png width:180 height:100 align:center}"
	]
	quest.7D0410D74877C78A.quest_subtitle: "Basic Tutorial"
	quest.7D0410D74877C78A.title: "Tips: Basic Usage"
	quest.7D2142146614638C.quest_subtitle: "你为什么在这里"
	quest.7D237676ED4A865D.quest_desc: [
		"&7The Apotheosis Enchanting Module adds a new crafting method to MC—&bInfusion&7. Infusion is similar to normal enchanting, but restricts certain attributes. Almost all items have a lower limit for &aTier&7, and almost no items have an upper limit for &aTier&7 ("
		""
		"&7Special and powerful items will restrict &4Quantization&7 and &5Arcana&7. Some powerful items have &6very strict&7 condition requirements. Therefore, learning how to choose and ratio bookshelves is crucial."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"I will circle my &bInfusion Recommended Bookshelves&r with gear blocks to indicate them"
	]
	quest.7D237676ED4A865D.quest_subtitle: "Strengthening Magic with Magic"
	quest.7D237676ED4A865D.title: "Understanding Infusion Operations"
	quest.7D271783CE2A7614.quest_desc: ["在前期可以提供dot伤害，以及提供毒系伤害加成"]
	quest.7D271783CE2A7614.quest_subtitle: "！？毒毒？！"
	quest.7D2FD37CB2502689.quest_subtitle: "Legendary Tank"
	quest.7D35770E89B19DBE.quest_desc: [
		"&7The &#FFD700Small Chapel&7 is a house structure built from &#8B4513Soul Slate&7. The &#FFD700loot chest&7 generated inside always contains 1 &#66DDCCSanctuary Locator Pointer&7;"
		""
		"&7A small amount of &#FFAA33Misery Melons&7 generates outside, and 2 &#DDDDDDSkeletons&7 spawn alongside it inside."
	]
	quest.7D35770E89B19DBE.quest_subtitle: "This one, don't need it anymore"
	quest.7D35770E89B19DBE.title: "Find Structure: Small Chapel"
	quest.7D61EDF0B7F33C80.quest_desc: ["具有朝向，玩家放置时将面朝点击的方块面，只有朝向方向的网络会和其他面接入的网络分开"]
	quest.7D61EDF0B7F33C80.quest_subtitle: "相当于线缆，但可受红石信号控制"
	quest.7D628BA502AB05E5.quest_desc: [
		"&7The Skeleton King needs to be summoned using Spirit Calamity's Spirit Altar. Remember to summon it at night—during the day it will immediately go berserk and deal massive damage capable of instantly killing players."
		""
		"&7After killing the Skeleton King, you can go defeat various Cataclysm bosses to obtain their unique weapon templates. At the same time, many important minerals have reappeared in the world"
	]
	quest.7D628BA502AB05E5.quest_subtitle: "Doo da doo da doo"
	quest.7D628BA502AB05E5.title: "Target: Skeleton King"
	quest.7D6295CE0F8D8951.quest_desc: [
		"&6Alternator&r"
		""
		"&7A machine that converts rotational stress into electric current, the exact opposite of the &eElectric Motor&7, which converts electrical energy back into rotational force. One end accepts stress input, the other outputs energy.&r"
		""
		"&7Requires at least &c32 RPM&7 to start working and has an internal energy buffer of &c5 kFE&7.&r"
		""
		"&7Through it, you can convert mechanical kinetic energy into &eelectrical energy&7, which is easier to store and transmit over distance, then re-drive machinery via the Electric Motor. Note that energy is always lost in each conversion.&r"
	]
	quest.7D98C82FDB5C8642.quest_desc: [
		"&7&#FF6666Blaze Iron&7 is a rare material, usable only for crafting;  "
		"&7When dropped as an item, it &#FF6666will not be destroyed by fire/lava&7.  "
		""
		"&7Can be produced with a chance from &#FFD700Suspicious Soul Sand&7 found in the &#FFD700Soul Sand Valley&7 biome.  "
		""
		"&8May be used as a Silent Gear material in the future..."
	]
	quest.7D98C82FDB5C8642.quest_subtitle: "Activated"
	quest.7DC30B49569B363E.quest_desc: [
		"&6Rune of Oakwood's Might&r"
		""
		"&7The Rune of Oakwood's Might functions similarly to the ritual of the same name, granting the wearer a half-strength &bOakwood's Might&r&7 effect, providing a fixed amount of &adamage boost&r&7, with increased effect when bare-handed.&r"
	]
	quest.7DC30B49569B363E.quest_subtitle: "Empowerment Pulse"
	quest.7DD3F8C5DB93381B.title: "Bow Weapons"
	quest.7DDA9820D328CC3F.quest_desc: ["&7Functions the same as a vanilla &#66CCFFpickaxe&7. You can place a vanilla &#66CCFFpickaxe&7 in a crafting table to convert it into a &#66DDCCSilent Gear Pickaxe&7."]
	quest.7DDA9820D328CC3F.quest_subtitle: "Beloved Kin and Friends"
	quest.7E59A0E6979C8FF1.quest_desc: [
		"&6Pact of the Blaze&r"
		""
		"&7The nature of fire cannot be denied.&r"
		"&7-After forcibly extinguishing fire, you take a &cHellfire Arcane Impact&r"
		""
		"&7Nothing can rival raging fire.&r"
		"&7-&eFire effects&r&7 inflicted on enemies are more potent&r"
		""
		"{image:kubejs:textures/gui/malum/pact_of_the_prospector.png width:160 height:200 align:center}"
	]
	quest.7E59A0E6979C8FF1.quest_subtitle: "Adding Fuel to the Fire"
	quest.7E59A0E6979C8FF1.title: "Pact of the Blaze"
	quest.7E9B315D76C81C10.quest_desc: [
		"&7Normal attacks extend a tentacle to strike the target."
		"&7When fully charged, left-click extends a tentacle toward the nearest target within &c16 blocks&7 in front."
		"&7Right-click extends a grappling claw to pull yourself forward."
	]
	quest.7E9B315D76C81C10.quest_subtitle: "Tentacle Enthusiast"
	quest.7E9B315D76C81C10.title: "Tidal Claw Template"
	quest.7EB97CBE6483FCF7.quest_desc: ["But I still have to remind you: the Dorm Manager now only spawns when you keep a regular sleep schedule..."]
	quest.7EB97CBE6483FCF7.quest_subtitle: "Sleep Well"
	quest.7EF077D05E3E3B7E.quest_desc: [
		"&6Rune of Unyielding&r"
		""
		"&7The Rune of Unyielding stabilizes the wearer's stance, negating all &cknockback&r&7.&r"
	]
	quest.7EF077D05E3E3B7E.quest_subtitle: "Resisting the Irresistible"
	quest.7EFD778DFD9450E1.quest_desc: ["If you don't want to build up Spirit Calamity infrastructure, you can use Iron's Spells to harvest spirits"]
	quest.7EFD778DFD9450E1.quest_subtitle: "Facility Purchase"
	quest.7EFD778DFD9450E1.title: "Altar Purchase"
	quest.7F0DAB4DB433FC15.quest_desc: ["用于护甲时给予抗性提升效果，虽然也会附带虚弱效果，前期搭配飞剑或许有意想不到的效果"]
	quest.7F0DAB4DB433FC15.quest_subtitle: "高额防护"
	quest.7F0EB703538AF425.quest_subtitle: "我即虚空"
	quest.7F11174C00472167.quest_desc: [
		"&6Starlight Forest&r"
		"&7is one of the surface biomes of the Starlight Dimension, the most ordinary and also the most common."
		""
		"&7The main tree species of the Starlight Forest is the &eMoonlight Tree&r."
		"&7Compared to its variant biome (&8Starlight Thicket&r&7), the Moonlight Trees in this biome generally grow &ataller&r."
		"&7The generation spacing between individual Moonlight Trees is &alonger&r&7, and the ground covered by tree shade appears relatively more &aopen&r."
		""
		"&7Besides the &eMoonlight Berry&r&7 plants hanging from the leaves, the biome's surface also has some unique plants: &8Starlight Flowers, Starlight Torch Flowers, Yellow Ridge Grass, etc&r."
		"&7Some plants capable of &alighting up&r&7 also reduce monster spawning on the biome's surface to a certain extent."
	]
	quest.7F11174C00472167.quest_subtitle: "Very Ordinary"
	quest.7F11174C00472167.title: "Starlight Forest"
	quest.7F2C0291CE6F6B66.quest_desc: [
		"&7&#CC99FFLust&7  "
		"&7When attacking:  "
		"&7Each attack applies 1 stack of &#CC99FF\"Rose\"&7 to the target (at most once per 0.5 seconds)  "
		"&7The attacker themselves &#FF6666takes 1 extra damage&7  "
		""
		"&7When &#CC99FF\"Rose\"&7 reaches &#FFAA337 stacks&7, the effect triggers:  "
		"&7The attacker &#66FF66restores 15% max health&7  "
		"&7Applies a &#FF6666random debuff&7 to the target for &#FFAA3310 seconds&7  "
		"&7All debuffs on the target have their &#FFD700stack count +1&7  "
		""
		"&7Passive: You &#66FF66cannot die from bleed damage&7; bleed damage leaves at least 1 health."
	]
	quest.7F2C0291CE6F6B66.quest_subtitle: "Lust Erosion"
	quest.7F2C0291CE6F6B66.title: "Lust Erosion"
	quest.7F53C2C16D225E49.quest_subtitle: "能够破坏前方的方块或流体，同时也能吸收前方的掉落物"
	quest.7F578E1D8C765465.quest_desc: [
		"&7Most Spirit rituals share commonalities. Simple rituals manifest effects through Seeking &#DDA0DDRite Nodes&7, while more complex rituals—those seeking to influence the world without a specific target—manifest their effects through Formed &#DDA0DDRite Nodes&7."
		""
		"&7A Formed Rite Node, upon forming, wanders in the direction indicated by the totem. I measured its movement speed at exactly four blocks per second, and it can activate its carried effect eight times before dissipating."
		""
		"{@pagebreak}"
		""
		"&7Tainted Stone produces a unique negative effect on magic. It interferes with the flow of arcane energy, ultimately completely dismantling it. And if there is no particular external structure, the only thing to note is its interfering nature. Rite Nodes flying over &#888888Tainted Stone&7 will not activate effects and therefore will not dissipate."
		""
		"&7Finally, Rite Nodes cannot be touched, and therefore have no mass, are unaffected by gravity, and can pass through any solid matter."
		""
		"{@pagebreak}"
		""
		"&7The &#66CCFFRite Anchor&7 is a device that can guide and enhance wandering Rite Nodes. Embedding &#CC99FFSpirit Arcana&7 into it establishes a flight path, thereby affecting all Nodes that fly through. The arcane etching technique used for the path is inherently sensitive, so the &#66CCFFRite Anchor&7 cannot function when affected by redstone."
		"{image:kubejs:textures/gui/malum/rite_anchor.png width=200 height=90 align=center}"
		""
		"{@pagebreak}"
		""
		"&6Node Speed"
		"&7Embedding &#66DDCCClear Sky Spirits&7 into the &#66CCFFRite Anchor&7 grants Nodes a speed boost, accelerating their movement through the world. Each Node can receive this effect twice, doubling its speed each time."
		""
		"{@pagebreak}"
		""
		"&6Node Strength"
		"&7Embedding &#3399FFBilgewater Spirits&7 into the &#66CCFFRite Anchor&7 grants Nodes a strength boost, enhancing their effectiveness when interacting with certain Rite Anchor etching patterns. Each Node can receive this effect twice, doubling its strength each time."
		""
		"{@pagebreak}"
		""
		"&6Node Effect"
		"&7Embedding &#66BB66Earth Spirits&7 into the &#66CCFFRite Anchor&7 grants Nodes an effect boost, enhancing the strength of the effect produced by each activation. Each Node can receive this effect twice, doubling its effect each time."
		""
		"{@pagebreak}"
		""
		"&6Node Range"
		"&7Embedding &#FF6633Hellfire Spirits&7 into the &#66CCFFRite Anchor&7 grants Nodes a range boost, allowing them to reach farther positions before dissipating. Each Node can receive this effect twice, doubling its range each time."
		""
		"{@pagebreak}"
		""
		"&6Node Repair"
		"&7Embedding &#88DDFFHallowed Spirits&7 into the &#66CCFFRite Anchor&7 causes Nodes to continuously repair themselves, extending their own existence time and thus reaching farther positions. Each Node can receive this effect four times."
		""
		"{@pagebreak}"
		""
		"&6Node Revival"
		"&7Embedding &#CC6666Malicious Spirits&7 into the &#66CCFFRite Anchor&7 causes Nodes to sacrifice existing element bonuses to immediately repair themselves. The limit is the same as Hallowed Spirits."
		""
		"{@pagebreak}"
		""
		"&6Node Guiding"
		"&7Embedding &#CC99FFArcane Spirits&7 into the &#66CCFFRite Anchor&7 causes Nodes to change their flight path, with no consumption and no side effects. Arcane Spirits are pure energy without direction, so the effects they produce are naturally relatively plain, but also fitting."
		""
		"{@pagebreak}"
		""
		"&6Node Splitting"
		"&7Embedding &#888888Umbral Spirits&7 into the &#66CCFFRite Anchor&7 causes Nodes to split into two unrelated Nodes with identical functions. Each Node can receive this effect four times. The copied Node has only a single color and cannot be copied again."
		""
		"{@pagebreak}"
		""
		"&6Ritual Research: Elemental Bonuses"
		"&7A Node is a primitive arcane construct with no specialty, so its functions are quite limited. Passing elemental Spirits through the &#66CCFFRite Anchor&7 solves this problem, though I still need to document the specific functions in detail."
		""
		"&7When a Rite Node flies over a Rite Anchor inlaid with &#66DDCCClear Sky&7, &#3399FFBilgewater&7, &#66BB66Earth&7, or &#FF6633Hellfire&7 patterns, it receives an elemental bonus. Within the same category, only the first two receptions take effect. Also, because the Node's own construction is simple, it can receive at most four bonuses total."
		""
		"{@pagebreak}"
		""
		"&6Ritual Research: Node Revival"
		"&7A Node is a primitive arcane construct. The prototype I designed only required the etching to have an effect and the ability to move. Later, a key function was added: self-maintenance. It cannot be said to be self-recovery like a living thing, but it still counts as self-maintenance."
		""
		"&7When receiving the command from a &#CC6666Malicious Spirit&7, a Node forcibly sacrifices itself. It abandons all existing elemental bonuses. Speed is the least important, so the speed bonus is abandoned first. Then the strength bonus, then the effect bonus. Range is the most important and is only abandoned when no other bonuses remain."
	]
	quest.7F578E1D8C765465.quest_subtitle: "Arcane in Motion"
	quest.7F578E1D8C765465.title: "Node Management"
	quest.7F72D5E0DE65AC67.quest_desc: [
		"&7A &#FFAA33Strider&7 killed by a &#CC99FFPhantom&7 will always transform into a &#FF6666Stomp Beast&7;"
		""
		"&7After a &#FF6666Stomp Beast&7 is killed, there is a chance a new &#CC99FFPhantom&7 will spawn in its place (Easy 0%, Normal 25%, Hard 50%);"
		""
		"&7If a docile variant &#CC99FFPhantom&7 approaches a [Trample] gargoyle statue, it will immediately transform into a &#FF6666Stomp Beast&7."
		""
		"&7&#66FF66Immune&7 to fire damage, cold damage, and fall damage, and is not slowed by &#55D5D5Soul Sand&7 and similar blocks when moving;  "
		"&7No longer possesses the &#FFAA33Strider's&7 ability to walk on lava surfaces;"
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"&7The &#FF6666Stomp Beast&7 only deals continuous damage to creatures it passes over while moving, regardless of whether the &#FF6666Stomp Beast&7 itself has that creature as a hatred target;  "
		"&7The &#FF6666Stomp Beast&7 is neutral toward players and will actively attack &#CC99FFSkeletons&7, &#CC99FFStrays&7, &#CC99FFWither Skeletons&7, and Vessels;  "
		"&7When the &#FF6666Stomp Beast&7 actively binds hatred to a creature, each successful attack has a small chance to drop &#FFAA331~4&7 &#FF6666Blaze Iron&7;  "
		"&7The &#FF6666Stomp Beast's&7 attacks inflict extremely long knockback on hit;  "
		"&7This attack can be blocked by a &#FFD700Shield&7: but the &#FF6666Stomp Beast&7 may not only step over the shield block, but blocking its attack with a shield will also rapidly consume durability."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"&7The &#FF6666Stomp Beast&7 will actively seek out and chew on any bones dropped on the ground (with a chewing animation for a period of time);  "
		"&7For every bone eaten, it restores &#FFAA3310&7 health and reduces its \"agitation value\" by &#FFAA3330 seconds&7;  "
		"&7If it picks up and eats &#66DDCCStuffed Roasted Bone&7: the &#FF6666Stomp Beast&7 has a chance to be \"tamed\" (extremely low chance, recommend preparing &#FFAA332~5 stacks&7);"
		""
		"&7Players can place a saddle on it, then right-click to mount it;"
		""
		"&7After mounting, the player also needs to hold a &#66DDCCSkull Fishing Rod&7 to control its movement;  "
		"&7While the player rides the &#FF6666Stomp Beast&7 and moves, the &#FF6666Stomp Beast&7 can deal attack damage to all creatures it passes;  "
		"&7While the player rides the &#FF6666Stomp Beast&7 and moves, its \"agitation value\" rises (maximum cap is &#FFAA335 minutes&7);  "
		"&7Once the \"agitation value\" is full: the &#FF6666Stomp Beast&7 will kick the creature riding it away and treat that creature as a hatred target;  "
		"&7Afterward, the &#FF6666Stomp Beast&7 still needs to pick up and eat bones to reduce its \"agitation value\" before it can be ridden again;"
		""
		"&7When the &#FF6666Stomp Beast&7 touches water (fluid), is exposed to rainy weather, or is hit by a splash/lingering water bottle:  "
		"&7It will immediately transform into a &#FFAA33Strider&7 and gain &#FFAA3310 seconds&7 of Nausea, &#FFAA335 seconds&7 of Weakness II, and &#FFAA335 seconds&7 of Slowness III.  "
		"&7Please note: a \"tamed\" &#FF6666Stomp Beast's&7 initial hatred toward the player is still neutral. It will still fight back against players who attack it;"
		""
		"&7&#FFD700Sneak + right-click&7 to remove the saddle equipped on the &#FF6666Stomp Beast&7."
	]
	quest.7F72D5E0DE65AC67.quest_subtitle: "Oh life~ can't you let me off just this once~"
	quest.7F72D5E0DE65AC67.title: "Observation: Stomp Beast"
	quest.7F921AB47163D20E.quest_desc: [
		"&7此项目会更改最长生成时间，一个物品影响20t的时间，一般与糖配合使用。"
		""
		"&7最长生成时间与最短生成时间结合就是刷怪间隔，间隔时长会在这两个值之间取随机数。"
	]
	quest.7F921AB47163D20E.quest_subtitle: "MADE IN HAVEN"
	quest.7F921AB47163E20E.quest_desc: [
		"&7This item changes the maximum spawn time. One item affects 20 ticks of time, usually used with sugar."
		""
		"&7The maximum spawn time combined with the minimum spawn time forms the spawn interval. The interval duration takes a random number between these two values."
	]
	quest.7F921AB47163E20E.quest_subtitle: "MADE IN HAVEN"
	quest.7FB5C401A36A72B5.quest_desc: ["&7基础数值平平无奇，需依靠 &#FFD700狂宴&7 机制层层叠加。狂宴叠满后加成可观，是值得投入资源叠加的潜力型材料。"]
	quest.7FB5C401A36A72B5.quest_subtitle: "飨宴之核"
	quest.7FBCCBE36CC54CC2.quest_desc: ["Before you can quickly obtain a knife in the early game, the Crude Knife is clearly the better choice"]
	quest.7FBCCBE36CC54CC2.quest_subtitle: "Crude Tool"
	quest.7FD6941949B8C8F4.quest_desc: [
		"&6Mechanical Crafter&r"
		"&7A work component capable of automatically crafting items.&r"
		"&7Stress consumption: &c2 su/RPM&r"
		""
		"&6Purpose&r"
		"&6Item Crafting&r"
		"&7The Mechanical Crafter can execute '&eAuto Crafting&r&7' and '&6Mechanical Crafting&r&7' recipes.&r"
		"&7'Auto Crafting' recipes automatically adapt to all vanilla Crafting Table recipes; 'Mechanical Crafting' recipes are special recipes added by Create.&r"
		""
		"&6Placement and Adjustment&r"
		"&7When crafting items with Mechanical Crafters, multiple crafters must be arranged according to the target item's recipe shape, forming a &ecrafting structure&r&7.&r"
		"&7Then, use a Wrench to adjust the internal paths of the crafting structure, connecting the crafters' crafting paths to each other.&r"
		"&7After connecting the crafting paths, an &aitem output&r&7 must be set, otherwise crafting cannot complete.&r"
		""
		"&6Material Input and Power&r"
		"&7Players can hold items and right-click the front of a Mechanical Crafter to insert directly, or input items from any face via logistics components. The Mechanical Crafter is also one of the Mechanical Arm's usable targets.&r"
		"&7The Mechanical Crafter requires stress input through the gears on its side to operate. It can transmit power itself, so a crafting structure only needs power supplied at one point.&r"
		""
		"&6Operation&r"
		"&6Triggering&r"
		"&7When all Mechanical Crafters in a crafting structure are filled, it automatically begins operating. To force-start an unfilled crafting structure, input a redstone signal to any one crafter.&r"
		"&7Players can install a '&eCrafter Lid&r&7' on a crafter. A crafter with a lid cannot store items but counts as filled, so when the other crafters are filled, the crafting structure starts automatically.&r"
		""
		"&6Starting Crafting&r"
		"&7During operation, materials on the crafting structure move step by step along the path from the end toward the output. Each step takes &c1000/RPM·Tick&r&7.&r"
		"&7When all materials reach the end, it consumes the time of 1 step to craft the product, which is then ejected.&r"
		"&7If the crafter at the end points at a container, the product is stored in that container.&r"
		"&7If the recipe is unavailable, all materials are ejected at the last step.&r"
		""
		"&6Connecting&r"
		"&7Hold a Wrench and right-click the seam between two same-facing Mechanical Crafters to connect them. When items are input to one of them, the items are evenly distributed to all connected crafters.&r"
		"&7Right-click the same seam with a Wrench again to disconnect.&r"
		""
		"&6Crafting Speed&r"
		"&7Crafting speed is mainly determined by the Mechanical Crafter's rotation speed, but that is not the only factor.&r"
		"&7The number of steps required for crafting also affects speed. This depends on the crafting structure's path arrangement; using a more optimized path reduces steps and improves efficiency.&r"
		""
		"&8This manuscript is sticky. You can't help but wonder what its owner crafted it with.&r"
	]
	quest.7FF37718528D1FB5.quest_desc: ["&6Compared to the previous two tomes, the Extraction Tome is particularly precious—it can completely extract the enchantment energy from an item without damaging the item at all.&r"]
	quest.7FF37718528D1FB5.quest_subtitle: "Recycle... Not Recycle! Reuse!"
	quest.7FFEDC8A8DA45A2F.quest_desc: [
		"# &6Font Preferences &r"
		""
		"### &eAvailable Fonts &r"
		"&fThe modpack provides two fonts by default:"
		"&7- Path: &e\\\\kubejs\\\\assets\\\\ &r"
		"&7- &6ChironGoRoundTC &r (default font)"
		"&7- &6Maple_UI.ttf &r"
		""
		"### &bHow to Switch Fonts &r"
		"1. Press &4Ctrl + K &r to open the Modern UI control interface"
		"2. Click &ePreferences &r"
		"3. &eSwipe right &r in the interface"
		"4. Select your preferred font"
		""
		"### &3Custom Fonts &r"
		"&7- You can download other font files yourself"
		"&7- Place the font file in any directory and call it directly"
		"&7- &aAll default fonts are free for commercial use, no copyright risk &r"
		""
		"&7- Default font is &6ChironGoRoundTC .ttf &r"
	]
